\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Senate leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  hails bipartisanship and thanks Mike Johnson as foreign aid bill heads for passage \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Richard Luscombe (earlier) \par \uc2 5,047 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 April 2024\par 20:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our latest stories below:\uc2 US Senate\uc2  close to passing $95bn aid package after key procedural voteTrump lauds House speaker as \u8216\'20\'18good person\u8217\'20\'19 after Ukraine bill passage\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-662802528f0839cf006b12c0#block-662802528f0839cf006b12c0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has taken the key step}}}\uc2  of invoking cloture on the $95b bill that will send military aid to Ukraine, Israel and Taiwan, and could set the stage for social media app TikTok\u8217\'20\'19s ban nationwide. Lawmakers are now debating the legislation, with final passage expected later today or perhaps tomorrow. The chamber earlier in the day rejected an attempt to make amendments to the bill, which already passed the House, thwarting independent \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s plans to tweak the text to stop weapons shipments to Israel in what he called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6628077d8f08f2c421482b6e#block-6628077d8f08f2c421482b6e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ca dark day for democracy\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, GOP senators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627e0388f0839cf006b110d#block-6627e0388f0839cf006b110d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  on the Biden administration to step in to break up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627b9df8f0839cf006b0e53#block-6627b9df8f0839cf006b0e53"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-Palestinian demonstrations}}}\uc2  on college campuses, including \uc2 New York University\uc2  and \uc2 Yale University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-662808ff8f0839cf006b12ef#block-662808ff8f0839cf006b12ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assailed}}}\uc2 Donald Trump \u8217\'20\'19s hand in overturning Roe v Wade in a speech in Florida, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-66280c568f08f2c421482b90#block-66280c568f08f2c421482b90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mocked}}}\uc2  his Bible sales.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627d4518f08c8e126c5d756#block-6627d4518f08c8e126c5d756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans}}}\uc2  to ship $1b in weapons to Ukraine that can be quickly deployed on the battlefield once the foreign aid bill passes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trial on charges of falsifying business records {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627da9f8f08c8e126c5d7ba#block-6627da9f8f08c8e126c5d7ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is continuing}}}\uc2  in New York City, with testimony from former Nation Enquirer publisher David Pecker.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627d9198f08c8e126c5d7ac#block-6627d9198f08c8e126c5d7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took a risk}}}\uc2  by allowing the chamber to pass the bill funding Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defense, but Trump praised him nonetheless.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-662804fe8f08f2c421482b5a#block-662804fe8f08f2c421482b5a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thanked Johnson}}}\uc2  for allowing the House to vote on and pass the foreign aid bill, despite his previous hesitancy towards arming Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back in the Senate, lawmakers continue to debate the foreign aid bill for Israel, Ukraine and Taiwan, which appears headed for passage later today.\par \par \uc2 The speeches will probably go on for a few hours. Shortly after the chamber overwhelmingly took the key legislative step of invoking cloture on the bill, CNN reports Republican minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , an ardent supporter of Ukraine, laid into conservative commentator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  for his support of \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , and the damage it has caused:\par \par \uc2 enltrMitch McConnell, a staunch backer of Ukraine aid, says the anti-Ukraine movement began with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cwho, in my opinion, ended up where he should have been all along, which is interviewing \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Senate just voted 80-19 to break a filibuster on $95B aid\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Gz4aKSxG6L"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Gz4aKSxG6L}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1782846317519135018?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Carlson traveled to Russia in February for an interview with Putin, which did not appear to go the way the conservative commentator hoped:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/09/tucker-carlson-vladimir-putin-interview-analysis-russia-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Talkshow or a serious conversation?\u8217\'20\'19 Tucker Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s interview of Putin offered neither}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Much of what \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told the crowd in Florida was well-trod territory for the president, who has pledged to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access ever since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022.\par \par \uc2 But he did try out a new line, one inspired by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s foray into theology.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump bragged how proud he was to get rid of Roe v Wade \u8230\'20\'26 He took credit for it. He said, there has to be punishment for women exercising their reproductive freedom. His words, not mine,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Then he teed up a zinger: \u8220\'20\'1CHe described {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/dec/15/neil-gorsuch-us-supreme-court-dobbs-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Dobbs decision}}}\uc2  as a miracle. Maybe it\u8217\'20\'19s coming from that Bible he\u8217\'20\'19s trying to sell. I almost wanted to buy one just to see what the hell\u8217\'20\'19s in it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If you haven\u8217\'20\'19t heard about it, yes, Trump is selling a Bible:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/26/trump-selling-bible"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Book of Donald: Trump hawks special \u8216\'20\'18God Bless the USA\u8217\'20\'19 Bibles for $60}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  vowed to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access as president, including vetoing any attempt by Congress to pass a nationwide ban on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 But much of his speech was dedicated to reminding voters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s role in Roe v Wade\u8217\'20\'19s downfall.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who ripped away the right to freedom of women in America. It will be all of us who restore those rights for women in America,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you do that, you\u8217\'20\'19ll teach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and extreme Maga Republicans an extremely valuable lesson: don\u8217\'20\'19t mess with the women of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 In Florida, Biden takes Trump to task for Roe v Wade's downfall\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has made it to Tampa, where he\u8217\'20\'19s laying into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his role in the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe v Wade, which has allowed states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Beginning next week, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be banned in Florida beyond six weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 a point at which many women are not aware they are pregnant. During his presidency, Trump appointed to the supreme court three conservative justices who would go on to vote to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor 50 years, the court ruled that there was a fundamental constitutional right to privacy. But two years ago, that was taken away. Let\u8217\'20\'19s be real clear. There was one person responsible for this nightmare, and he\u8217\'20\'19s acknowledged and he brags about it \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is worried voters are gonna hold him accountable for the cruelty and chaos he created. Folks, the bad news for Trump is we are going to hold them accountable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Independent senator \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  expressed disappointment that the chamber declined to consider amendments to the foreign aid bill he planned to offer that would restore funding to \uc2 UN\uc2  relief agency \uc2 Unrwa\uc2  and remove weapons shipments to Israel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am very disappointed, but not surprised, that my amendment to end offensive military aid to Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s war machine \u8211\'20\'13 which has killed and wounded over 100,000 Palestinians, two-thirds of whom are women and children \u8211\'20\'13 will not be considered,\u8221\'20\'1D the Vermont lawmaker said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPolls show that a majority of Americans, and a very strong majority of Democrats, want to end US taxpayer support for Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s war against the Palestinian people. It is a dark day for democracy when the Senate will not even allow a vote on that issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer hails bipartisanship, thanks Johnson as foreign aid bill heads for passage\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , once again spoke from the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s floor after lawmakers voted overwhelmingly to advance the $95b bill authorizing military aid to Ukraine, Israel and Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 Passing the legislation was a top priority for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , his Democratic allies and some Republicans, including the Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 . It faced resistance from others in the GOP, among them the Republican House speaker, Mike Johnson. But Johnson relented earlier this month, and allowed it to be voted on in the House, where it passed with more Democrats in favor than Republicans.\par \par \uc2 In his remarks, Schumer thanked Johnson and McConnell, while saying the bill\u8217\'20\'19s passage was a sign that bipartisanship is alive and well in a Congress better known for intractable partisan stalemate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s outcome yet confirms another thing we\u8217\'20\'19ve stressed from the beginning of this Congress. In divided government, the only way to ever get things done is bipartisanship,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI thank leader McConnell, as I\u8217\'20\'19ve mentioned before, working hand in hand with us, not letting partisanship get in the way. I thank Speaker Johnson, who rose to the occasion, in his own words, that he had to do the right thing, despite the enormous political pressure on him. And I thank leader Jeffries, who worked so well together in his bipartisan way, with Speaker Johnson.\u8221\'20\'1D The last name is \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , the Democratic House minority leader.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Foreign aid bill on course for passage after key Senate vote\par \par \uc2 The Senate invoked cloture on the $95bn bill to provide military assistance to Israel, Ukraine and Taiwan, an important procedural step that clears the way for a final vote on its passage later today.\par \par \uc2 The bill advanced with 80 votes in favor, and 19 opposed.\par \par \uc2 The measure has already been approved by the House, and will be signed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  after it passes the Senate. Lawmakers are now expected to debate the legislation and offer a limited number of amendments.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back in the Senate, they\u8217\'20\'19re voting on whether to invoke cloture on the foreign aid bill.\par \par \uc2 That will set the stage for its final consideration, after a period of debate.\par \par \uc2 A previous motion by Republican senator \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  that would have blocked the bill\u8217\'20\'19s progress was voted down with 50 senators opposed and 48 in favor.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to assail Trump's record on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Florida address\par \par \uc2 When he speaks in Tampa at 3pm, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will press his message that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is responsible for the spread of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans across the country, his re-election campaign announced.\par \par \uc2 The president will arrive in Florida one week before a law banning abortions after six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 a point at which many women are not yet aware they are pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 goes into effect. In a memo, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager, Julie Ch \u225\'00\'E1vez Rodriguez, said such laws were out of step with the American public.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is hoping that Americans will somehow forget that he\u8217\'20\'19s responsible for the horror women are facing in this country every single day because of him. It\u8217\'20\'19s a bad bet,\u8221\'20\'1D Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez Rodriguez wrote.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 When President Biden speaks out against attacks on reproductive freedom across the country and yet another extreme Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban taking effect in Florida, it will resonate with voters across every battleground state. Women and their families do not want Trump and MAGA Republicans continuing to dismantle their fundamental freedoms. An overwhelming majority of voters have rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans every time they\u8217\'20\'19ve been on the ballot, and this November, they\u8217\'20\'19ll reject Trump too.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will shortly arrive in Tampa, where he is scheduled to give an address this afternoon on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, including attacking Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban that is set to take effect on 1 May.\par \par \uc2 Reporters on the ground in Tampa say Biden will be faced by several dozen people who have gathered to protest the president\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 enltrAbout 75 demonstrators outside Biden event in Tampa criticizing Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza and saying Biden is complicit in \u8220\'20\'1Cgenocide\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chants of \u8220\'20\'1CBiden, Biden you can\u8217\'20\'19t hide. You\u8217\'20\'19re committing genocide.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YvMtsjNvvB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YvMtsjNvvB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Zac Anderson (@zacjanderson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/zacjanderson/status/1782822962892071227?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate procedural vote delayed as Republicans complain they can't offer amendments\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s procedural vote on the foreign aid bill is being delayed by Republicans complaining they can\u8217\'20\'19t offer amendments to it.\par \par \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2 , of Missouri, and Utah\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  are accusing the Democratic majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , of effectively railroading through his version of the bill \u8220\'20\'1Cwith minimal debate and perhaps no amendments\u8221\'20\'1D, Lee said.\par \par \uc2 He insists, as extremist House Republicans who opposed the bill last week did, that money for Ukraine is unpopular.\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , independent senator for Vermont, says he agrees with Lee.\par \par \uc2 He says he wants to offer two amendments, one to ensure there\u8217\'20\'19s no money for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cwar machine\u8221\'20\'1D. The second is removing a block on aid money for the \uc2 United Nations Relief and Works Agency\uc2  (\uc2 Unrwa\uc2 ), which Israel says has been infiltrated by \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Hamas\uc2  terrorists\u8221\'20\'1D stealing funds.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMembers can agree with me or disagree with me on the issues, but they should be voted upon,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said.\par \par \uc2 Senators are voting now whether to adopt a motion by \uc2 Lee\uc2  to table (kill) Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s motion to move forward with the foreign aid bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , will visit Saudi Arabia this weekend in pursuit of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s ambitious goal of helping to restore that nation\u8217\'20\'19s relations with Israel, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/04/23/blinken-saudi-arabia-israel-trip"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19ll be attending the special meeting of the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  in Riyadh on Sunday, and meeting the Saudi crown prince, \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 , and other regional leaders, the outlet said.\par \par \uc2 Axios, citing US officials, adds that Blinken \u8220\'20\'1Cis considering\u8221\'20\'1D visiting Israel and its prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , as part of his trip, but has not yet finalized an itinerary.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senators are inching towards a procedural vote on the $95.3bn foreign aid package, expected close to the top of the hour.\par \par \uc2 Arizona Democrat Mark Kelly has just been on the chamber floor, lamenting that it took so long for Congress to pass a bill he said 71% of members ultimately voted for.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of delays, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s fighters are desperately low [on weapons and ammunition],\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s tying the hands of their commanders at the same time Russia is revitalizing its war effort.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But, he says, \u8220\'20\'1CUkraine can win this war. Passing this bill will allow the transfer to them more of what Ukraine needs to turn the tide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republican Maine senator \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  concurs. \u8220\'20\'1C[This is] a volatile and dangerous time in world history,\u8221\'20\'1D she says:\par \par \uc2 If [Russia\u8217\'20\'19s president Vladimir] Putin is allowed to succeed in Ukraine, he will continue to pursue his goal of recreating the Soviet Union. He\u8217\'20\'19s made no bones about that.\par \par \uc2 She fears Moldova, Georgia, the Baltic nations and Poland are in Putin\u8217\'20\'19s sights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThen our troops would be involved in a much larger war,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The Senate will soon begin voting on a $95bn foreign aid bill for Israel, Ukraine and other US allies, ending {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627a6778f08e572db1259b5#block-6627a6778f08e572db1259b5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 months of negotiations}}}\uc2  over one of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s top priorities and giving Kyiv another lifeline in its defense against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion. But the drama isn\u8217\'20\'19t over yet. Independent senator \uc2 Bernie Sanders{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627b4e38f08c8e126c5d4eb#block-6627b4e38f08c8e126c5d4eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has vowed}}}\uc2  to offer amendments stripping from the bill funds to send Israel weapons, while Republicans opposed to arming Ukraine may make their own stand. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627ca3c8f08f2c4214827fb#block-6627ca3c8f08f2c4214827fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Voting begins at 1pm}}}\uc2  with a procedural motion. Meanwhile, GOP senators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627e0388f0839cf006b110d#block-6627e0388f0839cf006b110d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are calling}}}\uc2  on the Biden administration to step in to break up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627b9df8f0839cf006b0e53#block-6627b9df8f0839cf006b0e53"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-Palestinian demonstrations}}}\uc2  on college campuses, including \uc2 New York University\uc2  and \uc2 Yale University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627d4518f08c8e126c5d756#block-6627d4518f08c8e126c5d756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans}}}\uc2  to ship $1b in weapons to Ukraine that can be quickly deployed on the battlefield once the foreign aid bill passes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s trial on charges of falsifying business records {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627da9f8f08c8e126c5d7ba#block-6627da9f8f08c8e126c5d7ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is continuing}}}\uc2  in New York City, with testimony from former Nation Enquirer publisher David Pecker.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/senate-ukraine-israel-aid-vote-biden-trump-latest-updates?page=with:block-6627d9198f08c8e126c5d7ac#block-6627d9198f08c8e126c5d7ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took a risk}}}\uc2  by allowing the chamber to pass the bill funding Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defense, but Trump continued to praise him, raising his chances of keeping his job.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican senators demand Biden administration 'restore order' on campuses hit by pro-Palestinian protests\par \par \uc2 Twenty-five Republican senators have demanded that the Biden administration send federal law enforcement to respond to college campuses where pro-Palestinian protests have occurred, and called the demonstrators \u8220\'20\'1Canti-Semitic, pro-terrorist mobs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Department of Education and federal law enforcement must act immediately to restore order, prosecute the mobs who have perpetuated violence and threats against Jewish students, revoke the visas of all foreign nationals (such as exchange students) who have taken part in promoting terrorism, and hold accountable school administrators who have stood by instead of protecting their students,\u8221\'20\'1D the group wrote in a letter addressed to the US attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , and the education secretary, \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among the signatories is the party\u8217\'20\'19s Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , and his deputy, \uc2 John Thune\uc2 . \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , the Missouri senator who separately demanded the president deploy national guard troops to college campuses, also signed the letter.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the campus protests:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/23/university-protests-arrests-yale-nyu-columbia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tensions rise as police arrest 150 pro-Palestinian protesters at Yale and NYU }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , what\u8217\'20\'19s he up to today?\par \par \uc2 The answer is sitting in a New York City courtroom where he is on trial for allegedly falsifying business records to cover up hush-money payments before his 2016 election victory. On the witness stand now is David Pecker, a former ally and longtime publisher of the National Enquirer.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re blogging his testimony live, and you can follow it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/trump-hush-money-trial-new-york-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump hush-money trial: David Pecker takes witness stand again after gag order hearing \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 That the House passed the foreign aid bill is somewhat of a surprise. Anti-Ukraine sentiment is rife and growing among the Republicans who hold a slim majority in that chamber, and speaker Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s decision to put the foreign aid bill up for a vote \u8211\'20\'13 and passing it with the help of more Democrats than Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 puts him in peril of losing his job. But though \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  counts himself as a skeptic of funding Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s defenses, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports that he recently praised Johnson \u8211\'20\'13 a bad sign for the nascent attempt to remove the speaker:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Johnson }}}\uc2  is a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood person\u8221\'20\'1D and is \u8220\'20\'1Ctrying very hard\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said, after the US House speaker oversaw passage of military aid to Ukraine, long opposed by Trump, in the face of fierce opposition from the right of the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, look, we have a majority of one, OK?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.johnfredericksradio.com/listen-live/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a radio interview}}}\uc2  on Monday night, after a day in court in his New York hush-money trial.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not like he can go and do whatever he wants to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of Johnson. \u8220\'20\'1CI think he\u8217\'20\'19s a very good person. You know, he stood very strongly with me on Nato when I said \uc2 Nato\uc2  has to pay up \u8230\'20\'26 I think he\u8217\'20\'19s a very good man. I think he\u8217\'20\'19s trying very hard. And again, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to have a big election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Johnson faces {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/16/house-republican-effort-oust-speaker-mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposition from rightwingers in his party}}}\uc2 , in particular from \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , a fervent Trump ally who has threatened to trigger a motion to vacate, the mechanism by which a speaker can be removed, and called for Johnson to quit.\par \par \uc2 No less than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/04/20/us/politics/ukraine-israel-foreign-aid-vote.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 112 House Republicans}}}\uc2  voted against Ukraine aid, leaving Johnson reliant on Democratic support. A similar scenario saw his predecessor, Kevin McCarthy, removed last year, but with an election looming, many see Johnson as safe for now.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/23/trump-mike-johnson-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump lauds House speaker as a \u8216\'20\'18good person\u8217\'20\'19 after Ukraine aid bill passage}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 US plans to quickly ship $1b to Ukraine once aid bill passes\par \par \uc2 The United States will send $1b in weapons to Ukraine once the foreign aid bill is approved by Congress and signed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , with an emphasis on munitions that can quickly be deployed on the battlefield, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The weapons will arrive in Ukraine amid warnings of a looming offensive by Russia, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/08/russia-ukraine-forces-struggle-enemy-mariinka"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has made some gains}}}\uc2  on the battlefield in recent months.\par \par \uc2 Citing US officials, Reuters reports the weapons to be delivered will include Stinger air defense munitions, vehicles, anti-tank munitions and ammunition for artillery systems the United States has already provided.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Just what exactly is in the foreign aid package the Senate is expected to approve later today? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/yang-tian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yang Tian}}}\uc2  breaks down the massive bill:\par \par \uc2 The US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2  has approved $95bn in foreign aid for Ukraine, Israel and other US allies in a rare Saturday session as Democrats and Republicans banded together after months of hard-right resistance over renewed American support for repelling Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 With an overwhelming vote, the $61bn in aid for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  passed in a matter of minutes, a strong showing as American lawmakers race to deliver a fresh round of US support to the war-torn ally. Many Democrats cheered on the House floor and waved Ukraine flags.\par \par \uc2 The speaker, Mike Johnson, who helped marshal the package to passage, said after the vote: \u8220\'20\'1CWe did our work here, and I think history will judge it well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/21/house-approves-61bn-aid-for-ukraine-what-we-know-so-far-and-what-happens-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House approves $61bn aid for Ukraine \u8211\'20\'13 what we know so far, and what happens next}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer says Senate should 'finish the job' with foreign aid vote\par \par \uc2 In brief remarks on the Senate floor, the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , called for lawmakers to pass the foreign aid bill \u8220\'20\'1Cas expeditiously as possible\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe time has come to finish the job to help our friends abroad once and for all,\u8221\'20\'1D the New Yorker said. He continued:\par \par \uc2 I ask my colleagues to join together to pass the supplemental today as expeditiously as possible, send our friends abroad the aid they have long been waiting for.\par \par \uc2 Let us not delay this. Let us not prolong this. Let us not keep out friends around the world waiting for a moment longer.\par \par \uc2 He noted that voting will begin at 1pm, starting with a procedural vote and then a motion to invoke cloture.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Republican McConnell calls foreign aid vote 'a test of American resolve'\par \par \uc2 In remarks on the Senate floor, the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , said today\u8217\'20\'19s vote on the foreign aid bill for Ukraine, Israel and other US allies was \u8220\'20\'1Ca test\u8221\'20\'1D of America\u8217\'20\'19s leadership on the global stage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, the Senate sits for a test on behalf of the entire nation. It is a test of American resolve, our readiness and our willingness to lead, and the stakes of failure are abundantly clear,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFailure to help Ukraine stand against Russian aggression now means inviting escalation against our closest treaty allies and trading partners. It means greater risk that American forces would become involved in conflict.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While conservative Republicans, many of whom are in the House, oppose further aid to Ukraine, McConnell has been a steadfast ally of Kyiv. That created a rift with the House speaker, Mike Johnson, until he relented last week and allowed Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber to approve the military aid package the Senate will vote on later today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 GOP senator demands Biden deploy national guard against pro-Palestinian protesters on college campuses\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  has asked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to deploy the national guard against pro-Palestinian protesters at college campuses, accusing them of \u8220\'20\'1Cshocking displays of antisemitism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/23/university-protests-arrests-yale-nyu-columbia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The protests}}}\uc2  at \uc2 New York University\uc2  and \uc2 Yale University\uc2  in Connecticut have resulted in dozens of arrests. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hawley.senate.gov/sites/default/files/2024-04/Hawley-Letter-to-Biden-re-Columbia_0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his letter}}}\uc2 , Hawley, who represents Missouri and was one of the most prominent backers in the Senate of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims of fraud in the 2020 election, warned : \u8220\'20\'1COn college campuses across the United States, Jewish Americans are at risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At Columbia, Hawley said that \u8220\'20\'1Cdemonstrators have illegally established a \u8216\'20\'18Gaza Solidarity Encampment\u8217\'20\'19 on the university\u8217\'20\'19s campus and engaged in shocking displays of antisemitism \u8211\'20\'13 assaults on Jewish students, the theft and attempted burning of an Israeli flag, and violent, genocidal rhetoric\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He likened deploying the national guard to actions taken during school desegregation in the south decades ago:\par \par \uc2 In 1957, pursuant to Executive Order 10730, President \uc2 Dwight Eisenhower\uc2  deployed the national guard and 101st airborne division to ensure the safety of black students attending Central High in Little Rock, Arkansas. I urge you to similarly mobilize the national guard and other necessary authorities to protect Jewish American students on \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campus, and any other campus where Jewish students are at risk. \u8216\'20\'18Never again\u8217\'20\'19 means never again.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Beyond Congress, opposition to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza has intensified on several college campuses, where police were called in to make dozens of arrests. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the demonstrations, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/erum-salam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Erum Salam}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Police arrested dozens of people at pro-Palestinian demonstrations at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/yale-university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yale University}}}\uc2  in Connecticut and \uc2 New York University\uc2  in Manhattan, as student protests over Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza continue to roil US campuses.\par \par \uc2 On the \uc2 Yale University\uc2  campus in New Haven, Connecticut, authorities arrested at least 47 protesters on Monday evening, the university said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yale.edu/2024/04/22/statement-regarding-campus-protests-beinecke-plaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2 . Students who were arrested will be referred for disciplinary action.\par \par \uc2 The police crackdowns came after \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  canceled in-person classes on Monday in response to protesters setting up tent encampments at its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  City campus last week.\par \par \uc2 Several hundred people had been protesting on the Yale university campus, demanding the university divest from military weapons manufacturers. Yale said it had repeatedly asked students to leave, and warned them they could face law enforcement and disciplinary action if they didn\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/23/yale-nyu-uni-college-arrests-pro-palestine-protest-israel-gaza-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dozens arrested at Yale and NYU as pro-Palestinian student protests spread}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sanders seeks to strip funding for Israel's 'offensive military' operations from foreign aid bill\par \par \uc2 Much has changed since October, when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  first proposed pairing another round of military assistance to Ukraine with new aid to Israel, as well as other American allies. Many of the president\u8217\'20\'19s allies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/14/biden-israel-backing-israel-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are today in open revolt}}}\uc2  over his support for the country\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza, which Biden has continued even as he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/04/israel-us-gaza-joe-biden-benjamin-netanyahu-phone-call#:~:text=Joe%20Biden%20calls%20for%20'immediate,Israel%2DGaza%20war%20%7C%20The%20Guardian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 publicly worried}}}\uc2  over its humanitarian impact and called for a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 The foreign aid bill that Senate is expected to approve today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/20/us-house-approves-61bn-aid-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will include}}}\uc2  about $4.4bn to replenish depleted US supplies given to Israel, $3.5bn to help Israel buy weapons, and more than $5bn for its missile defense systems. It will also make it easier for Israel to buy US weapons from other countries.\par \par \uc2 Independent senator \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , a progressive who caucuses with the Democrats, plans to make a stand against that funding by offering an amendment that would strip the aid for offensive weapons from the package. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the Vermont lawmaker had to say:\par \par \uc2 I look forward to offering amendments tomorrow to cut billions in offensive military funding to Israel from the proposed national security supplemental package and protect essential humanitarian operations. The Senate should have a chance to debate and vote on the key components of such a massive package.\par \par \uc2 In poll after poll, Americans have showed their increasing disgust for Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s war machine and the humanitarian disaster it has caused in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Enough is enough. We cannot continue to fund this horrific war.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine, Israel aid, TikTok ban saga nears end as Senate plans vote\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The long and winding road of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s proposal to send tens of billions of dollars in foreign aid to Ukraine, Israel and other US allies may finally reach its conclusion today. Beginning at 1pm ET, the Senate is set to vote on a bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/20/us-house-approves-61bn-aid-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved by the House of Representatives}}}\uc2  last week that authorizes the assistance \u8211\'20\'13 and forces TikTok\u8217\'20\'19s parent company ByteDance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/apr/20/us-house-tiktok-byte-dance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to divest from the social media app}}}\uc2  in a year, or face a nationwide ban. The legislation is expected to pass, but not without some drama \u8211\'20\'13 independent senator \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  says he will offer amendments to cut funding for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s offensive operations, citing the humanitarian impact of its invasion of Gaza, and you may see other amendments offered by Republicans wary of backing Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Assuming none of the amendments manage to stall its progress, and the bill makes it through the Senate, today will cap an odyssey that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/20/joe-biden-tv-address-to-nation-oval-office-speech-vladimir-putin-hamas-aid-for-israel-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began in October}}}\uc2  when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  paired another round of funding for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defense against Russia with aid for Israel that he said was necessary in the wake of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s October 7 attack. For months, the bill had no clear path to passage, largely due to Republican resistance to funding Ukraine, and their demands for strict border security measures. But that resistance crumbled last week when House speaker Mike Johnson decided to allow a vote on the aid despite not getting the immigration changes he wanted, handing Biden and Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s supporters in the GOP, notably top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , an important foreign policy victory. We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know how it\u8217\'20\'19s looking as the Senate convenes later today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is heading to Tampa, Florida, to campaign in a state he hopes to win in November, even though it hasn\u8217\'20\'19t voted for a Democratic president since 2012. The president will condemn the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/02/florida-abortion-ban-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 , which takes effect next week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Primaries are happening all over the country today, including in Pennsylvania, where progressive Democrat Summer Lee{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/22/summer-lee-progressive-congress-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faces a challenger}}}\uc2  backed by a pro-Israel group.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s criminal trial in Manhattan continues, with judge Juan Merchan considering whether the former president violated a gag order. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/23/trump-hush-money-trial-new-york-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Follow our live blog}}}\uc2  for more.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240423ek4n001uw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
