\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 California readies itself as \u8216\'20\'18 \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  sanctuary\u8217\'20\'19 while Arizona gears up for ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell in Oakland \par \uc2 1,108 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 April 2024\par 16:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Golden state expanded \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access after Roe was repealed in 2022 while neighboring state is set to enact near-total ban\par \par \uc2 As Arizona prepares for a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to go into effect in the coming months, providers in California are getting ready to welcome a surge of out-of-state clients and live up to the state\u8217\'20\'19s reputation as an \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  sanctuary\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 California clinics have been treating patients confused by the legal framework in neighboring Arizona ever since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 law enshrining a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 Arizona has had a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on its books since 1864, but that law hadn\u8217\'20\'19t been enforced since the Roe decision in 1973. After the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling to overturn Roe, the Arizona supreme court allowed enforcement of the 1864 ban to go back into effect. At {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/24/arizona-abortion-ban-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the same time}}}\uc2 , however, Republican lawmakers in the statehouse passed a newer law banning abortions after 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 After Roe was overturned, \u8220\'20\'1Cthere was a lot of confusion both on the part of patients and providers in terms of what they could and could not do to be adhering to the law,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pratima Gupta, an OB-GYN who provides \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in San Diego and a fellow with Physicians for Reproductive Health. She remembers clinics closing their doors, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/12/30/1146437034/abortion-ban-arizona-ruling-doctors-prosecution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just to be told}}}\uc2  that the 1864 total ban wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be enforced after all.\par \par \uc2 The need was urgent, Gupta recalled. She particularly remembered one patient who had driven hours by herself from Arizona for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . After the procedure, \u8220\'20\'1Cshe literally jumped off the table, started to get dressed and asked: \u8216\'20\'18Can I go home now?\u8217\'20\'19 Because she had arranged childcare for a certain amount of time.\u8221\'20\'1D Gupta and her colleagues begged her to stay just 10 minutes so they could observe her before she drove the four hours home.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is the level of motivation that we are seeing,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 California law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/maps/state/california/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guaranteed \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  before Roe and voters further enshrined those rights in the state constitution in November 2022. When Roe was overturned, the California governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://calmatters.org/health/2022/09/california-abortion-bills/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a package of 12 laws}}}\uc2  protecting and expanding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/01/25/california-post-roe-abortion-00078804#:~:text=More%20than%20%24200%20million%20in,hire%20and%20train%20more%20providers."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 directed $200m}}}\uc2  in state funding to supporting out-of-state patients, including $20m to help those patients pay for travel, lodging and other logistical expenses. Clinics across California saw a surge in out-of-state patients.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  of the Pacific Southwest (PPPSW), for example, which operates 20 clinics across the California border in San Diego, Los Angeles and Imperial county, said roughly 10% of all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients at its clinics today come from states outside California.\par \par \uc2 Today, California providers are preparing for another surge in Arizona patients. On 9 April, the Arizona supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  that the 1864 total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 which had wound its way through the local courts \u8211\'20\'13 could take effect. The ban will become enforceable {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kjzz.org/content/1877268/abortions-can-continue-arizona-until-least-june-8-ag-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this June}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 meaning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still legal in Arizona before 15 weeks until then. Kris Mayes, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, has said her office {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azag.gov/press-release/attorney-general-mayes-statement-planned-parenthood-az-v-mayes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will not prosecute}}}\uc2  patients or physicians who provide abortions, and Democratic lawmakers in the state have vowed to try to repeal the ban (including by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/battle-abortion-heats-arizona-2024-ballot-rcna141347"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introducing an amendment}}}\uc2  that voters will get to consider this November guaranteeing the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in the state constitution). Still, providers expect the legal limbo will move many people seeking abortions to seek care elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis ruling places patients in Arizona in an even more precarious position,\u8221\'20\'1D said Darrah DiGiorgio Johnson, president and CEO of PPPSW. The organization {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthood.org/planned-parenthood-pacific-southwest/campaigns/abortion-arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that it has appointments available for Arizona patients \u8220\'20\'1Cin days not weeks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Organizations such Access Reproductive Justice, a California-based \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund, are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/C5jdSq7yWZj/?img_index=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offering}}}\uc2  to connect people seeking abortions and other reproductive healthcare with providers in the state, and provide logistical and financial support.\par \par \uc2 Still, there are challenges. Many patients needing care struggle to make the journey out of state, said Gupta, especially youth, members of the LGBTQ+ community and undocumented patients.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the majority of southern California\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics are located in the San Diego and Los Angeles metro areas. Those are crucial, and convenient for patients to fly in to from out of state.\par \par \uc2 But there are far fewer providers in rural areas, including near the California-Arizona border, and a growing number of hospitals in those regions have made significant cuts in maternal and reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  does operate one clinic in El Centro, just an hour\u8217\'20\'19s drive from the Arizona border. That clinic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kpbs.org/news/local/2023/08/16/planned-parenthood-officials-say-they-will-rebuild-torched-facility-in-el-centro"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 burned down}}}\uc2  in August 2023. The organization opened a temporary facility to continue seeing patients there and is scheduled to open a new permanent health center this summer, said Sandra Duran, communications director of PPPSW. Before it caught fire, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kpbs.org/news/local/2023/08/15/fire-planned-parenthood-in-el-centro"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 up to half}}}\uc2  of the patients seeking care at the El Centro clinic came from out of state or Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Although she\u8217\'20\'19s hopeful that advanced practice clinicians will be able to expand access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in rural California, Gupta notes that the continued closure of obstetrics units in rural hospitals across the state is worrisome. It means that backup can be increasingly far away for those providers.\par \par \uc2 The 2022 bills have provided some relief, she said, in particular a law that allowed nurse practitioners and nurse midwives to perform first-trimester aspiration abortions without a doctor present. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s been tremendously helpful, especially in expanding care to our more rural communities in California,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gupta. She adds that although California \u8220\'20\'1Cis welcoming trainees from other states\u8221\'20\'1D, it\u8217\'20\'19s difficult to convince new providers to move to California because it\u8217\'20\'19s one of the most expensive states to live in.\par \par \uc2 Researchers are also examining whether allowing California pharmacists to prescribe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to out-of-state patients would be another way to expand care. Pharmacists in California and in many other states can prescribe contraception, but prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication is out of their scope, explained Cathren Cohen, a staff attorney at the UCLA Law Center on Reproductive Health, Law and Policy and the author of a recent paper on the topic. She and her colleagues found that 69% of California pharmacists would be willing to prescribe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills if they were allowed to.\par \par \uc2 Researchers are still studying how effective a legislative change making that happen would be \u8211\'20\'13 and whether such laws could be implemented will depend on a supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2  expected this summer that could limit access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240419ek4j001xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
