\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Arizona Republicans again block effort to repeal near-total  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Jem Bartholomew \par \uc2 1,157 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 April 2024\par 11:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Only 28% of Arizona voters approve of the 1864 law. Plus, Israeli media reports weapons deployments for Rafah offensiveDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 After days of nationwide debate over the Arizona supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent}}}\uc2  decision to uphold a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from the 19th century, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-controlled statehouse has again {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/17/arizona-republicans-block-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quashed an effort to}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/17/arizona-republicans-block-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeal the ban}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans, who hold a one-seat majority in both the Arizona house and senate, shot down a procedural measure in the statehouse on Wednesday that would have enabled the chamber to vote on a bill to repeal the ban.\par \par \uc2 It was the second attempt at repeal since the court ruling. The ban, passed before Arizona became a state, permits abortions only to save a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life. Due to legal delays, it is not yet in effect. Instead, Arizona currently bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 With or without repealing the 1864 law, Arizona Democrats are also attempting to place a ballot measure before voters in November that would restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How was the vote split? Just one Republican voted with the house\u8217\'20\'19s 29 Democrats, but the 30-30 split was not enough to move forward.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What do people in Arizona think? When polled in 2022, only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.noblepredictiveinsights.com/post/voting-impact-of-supreme-court-ruling-on-abortion-in-arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 28% of voters}}}\uc2  approved of the 1864 law.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How is the GOP approaching \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationally? Republicans have long been opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe v Wade in 2022 has complicated their stance. Anger over Roe\u8217\'20\'19s fall was credited with poor results in the 2022 midterms, and now many Republicans are attempting to moderate their previously hardline views.\par \par \uc2 Israel reportedly deploys extra weapons for assumed Rafah offensive\par \par \uc2 Israel has reportedly deployed extra artillery and armoured personnel carriers to the Gaza Strip periphery, suggesting that the military is preparing for its long-threatened {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/17/israel-reportedly-deploys-extra-weapons-for-assumed-rafah-offensive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ground offensive on Rafah}}}\uc2 , the only place of relative safety for at least 1.4 million displaced Palestinian civilians.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli daily Ma\u8217\'20\'19ariv also said on Wednesday that troops had been put on alert and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe governing principle of the operation\u8221\'20\'1D had been approved by the \uc2 IDF\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IDF\uc2  confirmed on Tuesday it was buying 40,000 tents to prepare for the evacuation of hundreds of thousands of displaced civilians in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on Israeli tensions with Iran? Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war cabinet is still focused on weighing up how to respond to Iran. The \uc2 UK government\uc2 , according to Politico, is now expecting an imminent Israeli strike on Iran.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on the humanitarian toll in Gaza? After \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacked Israel, killing about 1,200 and taking more than 200 hostage, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s air and ground assault on Gaza has killed at least 34,000 people, health officials say.\par \par \uc2 Trump to return to court for third day of jury selection in hush-money trial\par \par \uc2 The former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will return to a Manhattan courtroom on Thursday for the third day of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/18/trump-day-three-juror-hush-money-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hush-money trial}}}\uc2 , which could finalise jury selection for one of the most high-profile criminal cases in US history.\par \par \uc2 So far, seven people have been selected after intense grilling of a jury pool that has examined prospective jurors\u8217\'20\'19 political views, personal lives and social media posts.\par \par \uc2 The judge on Tuesday rebuked Trump, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI won\u8217\'20\'19t have any jurors intimidated in this courtroom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s expected today? Five more jurors and six alternates are still to be chosen.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who has been selected so far? An information technology worker, an English teacher, an oncology nurse, a sales professional, a software engineer and two lawyers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Which case is this one again? Trump is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/15/trump-hush-money-trial-key-arguments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged}}}\uc2  with 34 counts of falsifying business records over an alleged $130,000 hush-money scheme involving Stormy Daniels and Karen McDougal.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Philippine and US forces will carry out their first ever military {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/18/china-warning-balikatan-exercise-2024-philippines-us-military-drills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exercises}}}\uc2  outside the south-east Asian country\u8217\'20\'19s territorial waters. China said it would lead to greater insecurity in the South China Sea.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US reimposed oil {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/17/us-reimposes-venezuela-sanctions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sanctions}}}\uc2  on Venezuela after President Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to consolidate rule. It comes six months after the US eased restrictions in hopes of a democratic opening.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A woman in Brazil was arrested and charged with violating a corpse and attempted theft through fraud. The woman is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/17/brazil-woman-corpse-bank-fraud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alleged}}}\uc2  to have brought her uncle\u8217\'20\'19s cadaver to a bank to sign a $3,250 loan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Three Russian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/18/ukraine-war-briefing-dont-stockpile-your-patriots-put-ukrainian-needs-first-allies-told"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 missiles}}}\uc2  hit downtown Chernihiv in Ukraine on Wednesday. Authorities said at least 17 people were killed as Ukraine urges the US to approve further aid.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: incarcerated people suffered 3.5 times more frequent deaths during Covid peak\par \par \uc2 A University of California study found that at the peak of the pandemic in 2020, people inside prisons died almost three-and-a-half times more frequently than the free population. More than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/18/incarcerated-people-covid-death-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 6,000 incarcerated people died}}}\uc2  in the first year of the pandemic. A Marshall Project analysis of data found roughly 50 or more people dying per 10,000 in prison in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: the inside story of the biggest art fraud in American history\par \par \uc2 Orlando Whitfield was a student when he became best friends with Inigo Philbrick. A few years later, Philbrick had led investors to part with about $86m, and stood accused of identity theft, forging documents, selling paintings without their owner\u8217\'20\'19s knowledge and more. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2024/apr/17/inside-story-of-the-biggest-art-fraud-in-american-history-orlando-whitfield"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Whitfield talks}}}\uc2  about their decade of hustling \u8211\'20\'13 and Philbrick\u8217\'20\'19s route to jail.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: average world incomes\par \par \uc2 will drop by nearly a fifth by 2050\par \par \uc2 as result of crisis\par \par \uc2 Average incomes will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/apr/17/climate-crisis-average-world-incomes-to-drop-by-nearly-a-fifth-by-2050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fall by almost a fifth}}}\uc2  within the next 26 years as a result of the climate crisis, according to a study published in Nature. It predicts the costs of damage will be six times higher than the price of limiting global heating to 2C. Rising temperatures, heavier rainfall and more frequent and intense extreme weather are projected to cause $38tn of destruction each year by mid-century.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: \u8216\'20\'18At my first archery class, there\u8217\'20\'19s so much tension it\u8217\'20\'19s like a romantic comedy\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hold the bow with my left arm and place the three middle fingers of my right hand on the string,\u8217\'20\'19 the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2024/apr/18/jennifer-wong-fitness-wellbeing-reviews-archery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comedian Jennifer Wong writes}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I pull my right arm all the way back there\u8217\'20\'19s a fair bit of resistance. There\u8217\'20\'19s so much tension it\u8217\'20\'19s like a romantic comedy! I aim. I release. And the arrow goes flying to the left of the target.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240418ek4i001ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
