\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Arizona Republicans again block effort to repeal 1864 near-total  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 483 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 April 2024\par 01:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 After decrying state supreme court ruling on ban with no exceptions for rape or incest, lawmakers ensure its potential to take effect\par \par \uc2 After days of nationwide debate over the Arizona supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent}}}\uc2  decision to uphold a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from the 19th century, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-controlled statehouse has again quashed an effort to repeal the ban.\par \par \uc2 Republicans, who hold a one-seat majority in both the Arizona house and senate, on Wednesday shot down a procedural measure in the statehouse that would have enabled the chamber to vote on a bill to repeal the ban. Just one Republican, the representative Matt Gress, voted with the house\u8217\'20\'19s 29 Democrats, but the 30-30 split was not enough to move forward.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday marked the second time that state legislators have tried to repeal the ban, which was first passed in 1864, since the state supreme court ruling. Last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/arizona-republicans-block-repeal-state-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gress tried to bring forth}}}\uc2  a vote on the repeal bill. However, he then voted with other Republicans to recess until Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The ban, passed before Arizona became a state, only permits abortions to save a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life. It does not have exceptions for rape or incest. Due to legal delays, it is not yet in effect; instead, Arizona currently bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The GOP has long been opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe v Wade in 2022 has complicated their stance. Anger over Roe\u8217\'20\'19s fall was credited with slowing a much-promised \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D in the 2022 midterms, as well as helping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters win a string of ballot measures in red and purple states. Now, before the 2024 elections, many Republicans are attempting to moderate their previously hardline views.\par \par \uc2 After the Arizona supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision last week, multiple Republicans with a history of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  beliefs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/arizona-republicans-against-state-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denounced the ruling}}}\uc2  and the ban. Shawnna Bolick, a Republican state senator married to one of the justices who sided with the majority to uphold the 1864 ban, called on her colleagues to repeal it, as did Gress. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who appointed three of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices who overturned Roe and has said he believes each state should decide its own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, indicated that he believes the 1864 ban goes too far. Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s ban, he suggested, will be \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/trump-arizona-abortion-ban-#:~:text=Trump%20says%20Arizona%20supreme%20court's,'%20%7C%20Donald%20Trump%20%7C%20The%20Guardian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 straightened out}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hours after the scuttled effort in the state house, Anna Hernandez, a Democratic state senator, successfully introduced a senate version of the repeal bill, which senate Democrats will now seek to advance. Due to the senate\u8217\'20\'19s procedural rules, passing that bill will take multiple days.\par \par \uc2 Arizona \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters are continuing to gather signatures for a November ballot measure that would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240417ek4h002xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
