\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Senators kill first article of impeachment against Alejandro Mayorkas \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe (now) and Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 5,907 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 April 2024\par 20:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on Mayorkas impeachment, read our story here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing our US live politics blog after an eventful day in both chambers of Congress. Thanks for joining us.\par \par \uc2 In the Senate: The impeachment trial against Alejandro Mayorkas, the homeland security secretary, was crawling towards a close after Democrats killed off one of the two articles against him, and were poised to dismiss the second. A campaign of delay and obfuscation by Republican members, in the form of a succession of points of order, motions to adjourn or calling for private session, slowed proceedings to a snail\u8217\'20\'19s pace. Ultimately, the second charge, that Mayorkas broke the law by enacting \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s immigration policies, was set for a similar fate as the first: dismissal on a party-line vote.\par \par \uc2 In the House: Members will vote Saturday on a package of foreign aid for Israel, Ukraine and Taiwan after Mike Johnson, the beleaguered Republican speaker, finally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/17/mike-johnson-oust-foreign-aid-ukraine-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unveiled details of four bills}}}\uc2  he hopes will appease hard-liners in his party seeking to oust him. Three of the bills provide aid funding, while the fourth, the text of which is forthcoming, is expected to include measures to redirect seized Russian assets toward Ukraine and force the sale of TikTok.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we were following:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he was considering tripling tariffs on Chinese steel, with indications that he wants to go to 25%. \u8220\'20\'1CChina is cheating, not competing on steel,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said at an event at the \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  union headquarters in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Arizona again blocked an effort by Democrats to overturn an 1864 rule outlawing almost all abortions, enacted by a ruling earlier this month by the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court. Respected pollster \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2  says November\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race in the key swing state now \u8220\'20\'1Cleans Democratic\u8221\'20\'1D following the controversy, a change from \u8220\'20\'1Ctoss-up\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and Jeb Bush, current and former Florida governors, led tributes to Bob Graham, a two-term governor of the state, three-term US senator and Democratic political heavyweight who has died aged 87.\par \par \uc2 Please join us again on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two more Republican points of order are stalling the vote to kill the second and final article of impeachment against Alejandro Mayorkas.\par \par \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  of Florida wanted an adjournment until 30 April, repeating an earlier motion that failed. It met the same fate, a 51-49 defeat.\par \par \uc2 Now John Kennedy of Louisiana is back again. He wants an adjournment until 1 May. No prizes for guessing how that motion will turn out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas impeachment articles\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve been talking a lot about the two articles of impeachment filed against Alejandro Mayorkas, the homeland security secretary , but what exactly do they charge him with?\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-resolution/863/text"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 text from congress.gov}}}\uc2 . Both articles were introduced by \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the firebrand Republican representative, in November 2023, and passed the House in February after a first vote to impeach failed.\par \par \uc2 Article 1 alleges Mayorkas \u8220\'20\'1Cwillfully and systemically refused to comply with the law\u8221\'20\'1D. It says he ignored congressional law and that \u8220\'20\'1Cin large part because of his unlawful conduct, millions of aliens have illegally entered the US on an annual basis with many unlawfully remaining in the US\u8221\'20\'1D. It tries to pin the border crisis firmly on the shoulders of the Biden administration, and Mayorkas for delivering it.\par \par \uc2 Article 2 alleges \u8220\'20\'1Cbreach of public trust\u8221\'20\'1D. It says Mayorkas \u8220\'20\'1Cknowingly made false statements, and knowingly obstructed lawful oversight of the department of homeland security, principally to obfuscate the results of his willful and systemic refusal to comply with the law\u8221\'20\'1D. One of the alleged \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse statements\u8221\'20\'1D was telling Congress he believed the border was secure, which Greene and others insisted rose to the threshold of being a \u8220\'20\'1Chigh crime or misdemeanor\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senators kill first impeachment article against Mayorkas\par \par \uc2 The Senate has voted to kill the first article of impeachment \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cwillful and systemic refusal to comply with the law\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 against Alejandro Mayorkas.\par \par \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2 , a Republican from Alaska, voted \u8220\'20\'1Cpresent\u8221\'20\'1D, neither for nor against, but all other senators voted along party lines, resulting in a 51-48 vote.\par \par \uc2 On to the second article, \u8220\'20\'1Cbreach of public trust\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 US Steel\uc2  should stay a US-owned company, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said on Wednesday during remarks to steelworkers at an event in Pittsburgh, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 US Steel\uc2 , he said at a campaign event:\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 should remain a totally American company. And that\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen, I promise you.\par \par \uc2 US Steel Corp\uc2  has agreed to be bought by Japan\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  for $14.9bn.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican tactics to handle the Mayorkas impeachment trial in the Senate this afternoon are becoming clear: delay proceedings as much as they can.\par \par \uc2 Each motion, or point of order, a Republican makes must be subjected to a roll call of all 100 members. Ted Cruz, the Texas senator, made a motion to debate the articles of impeachment in closed session. Senators voted along party lines and the motion failed 49-51.\par \par \uc2 Next up, John Kennedy of Louisiana made a point of order to adjourn the hearing until 30 April. One more roll call later, it also fell.\par \par \uc2 Now \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Kentucky Senate minority leader, has tabled a point of order to try to block a first vote to dismiss the first article of impeachment. The roll call on that is under way.\par \par \uc2 It too will fail on straight party lines, but each of these Republican efforts soaks up more and more time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden just drew laughs from the steel union members watching his campaign event in Pittsburgh, when he made several mentions of \u8220\'20\'1Cmy predecessor\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , saying he \u8220\'20\'1Cis busy right now\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He was referring to the fact that his rival is standing trial in New York, the first-ever criminal trial of a former US president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden floats ramping up tariffs on Chinese steel\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just confirmed what had been flagged before his trip \u8211\'20\'13 that he is considering tripling tariffs on Chinese steel, with indications that he wants to go to 25%.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChina is cheating, not competing on steel,\u8221\'20\'1D the US president said, at an event at the \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  union headquarters in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 He protested that \u8220\'20\'1Cfor too long, the Chinese state has poured money into their steel industry\u8221\'20\'1D and that it was not fair competition.\par \par \uc2 He also said that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cand the Maga\u8221\'20\'1D Republicans want to impose tariffs across the board on all imports, which the president said will hurt American consumers. He referred to the Make America Great Again slogan of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election campaign, which has come to signify the hard right of the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump simply does not get it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 "I'm president because of you guys" \u8211\'20\'13 Biden\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now speaking at the steelworkers\u8217\'20\'19 union headquarters in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 The US president is 45 minutes behind schedule. Pro-Palestinian protesters are demonstrating outside the event.\par \par \uc2 Biden is on a three-day swing through the vital battleground state of Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 He was in his home town of Scranton yesterday, where he contrasted how his roots have kept him humble while presidential rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  trades on his rich man\u8217\'20\'19s persona.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow, Biden will visit Philadelphia again; it has been a frequent stop on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 Biden just raised cheers and claps from the gathered union members when he said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m president because of you guys.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  has now made a motion to dismiss the first article of impeachment on the grounds it \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not allege conduct that rises to the level of a high crime or misdemeanor\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A formal vote will follow shortly, unless there are any efforts or motions to delay it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 It could be at least an hour or two before any vote to dismiss the articles of impeachment against Alejandro Mayorkas, the homeland security secretary. Or it could all be over very quickly.\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , a Democrat, has just told the chamber he wants to allow up to 60 minutes of debate on each article before he calls a vote to dismiss.\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2  of Missouri isn\u8217\'20\'19t happy. He says Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to kill the impeachment are unprecedented:\par \par \uc2 Never before in the history of our republic has the Senate dismissed or tabled articles of impeachment when the impeached individual was alive and did not resign.\par \par \uc2 I will not assist Senator Schumer in setting our constitution ablaze, bulldozing 200 years of precedent.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s now a debate about whether the articles of impeachment actually meet the high bar of \u8220\'20\'1Chigh crimes and misdemeanors\u8221\'20\'1D required, which would make them invalid if it\u8217\'20\'19s found they don\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 If it is determined the articles are unconstitutional, then the vote to kill will likely follow in short order, and without the need for more debate.\par \par \uc2 Watch this space \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas impeachment trial under way\par \par \uc2 Senators are lining up to sign the oath book in the chamber, the opening formalities of the impeachment trial that\u8217\'20\'19s just got under way against Alejandro Mayorkas, the homeland security secretary.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a slow process, as each of the 100 members must sign individually. But things are expected to pick up pretty quickly at its conclusion, with opening statements.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear at what point \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Democratic Senate majority leader, will call a vote to dismiss the two articles of impeachment received from the Republican-controlled House yesterday.\par \par \uc2 But Schumer says he will do so after \u8220\'20\'1Ca period of debate\u8221\'20\'1D. Such a vote will effectively kill the impeachment outright.\par \par \uc2 There is no chance of Mayorkas being convicted, even if the trial were allowed to conclude. Prosecutors would need 60 votes in a chamber controlled by Democrats, and several Republicans have already indicated they would acquit him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has signed a bill mandating that kindergartners in the state learn \u8220\'20\'1Cthe truths about the evils of communism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The hard-right Republican, who frequently touts an agenda promoting \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom\u8221\'20\'1D in education, and giving parents rights over choices for their children\u8217\'20\'19s curriculum, has made it compulsory for students up to 12th grade to attend the \u8220\'20\'1Chistory of communism\u8221\'20\'1D class, beginning in the 2026 school year.\par \par \uc2 Lessons must be \u8220\'20\'1Cage appropriate and developmentally appropriate\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the bill. The state\u8217\'20\'19s board of education will draw up academic standards for the lessons.\par \par \uc2 Florida high schoolers are already required to attend a 45-minute instruction class about \u8220\'20\'1CVictims of Communism Day\u8221\'20\'1D before they can graduate.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s bill-signing took place at the Assault Brigade 2506 museum in Hialeah Gardens, near Miami. DeSantis was flanked by former Cuban rebels who took part in the failed 1961 Bay of Pigs invasion, which took place 63 years ago today against the island\u8217\'20\'19s communist dictator, \uc2 Fidel Castro\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The voting-equipment company \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  has agreed to settle a defamation lawsuit with the far-right One America News Network (OAN) over lies broadcast on the network about the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Erik Connolly, a lawyer for \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2 , confirmed the case had been settled, but said the details were confidential. Attorneys for \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  and OAN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.237087/gov.uscourts.dcd.237087.201.0_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notified a federal judge}}}\uc2  in Washington on Tuesday that they were agreeing to dismiss the case, which \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  filed in 2021.\par \par \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  sued OAN in November 2021, saying the relatively small company was a victim of OAN\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdecision to increase its viewership and influence by spreading disinformation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  was only involved in the 2020 election in a single US county, Los Angeles, but OAN repeatedly broadcast false claims that its equipment had flipped the election for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  allies \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2  played a key role in advancing the outlandish claims.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/17/smartmatic-oan-voting-settlement-defamation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Voting equipment company Smartmatic settles defamation lawsuit with far-right network}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The extent of the opposition by hardline Republicans to speaker Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s foreign aid bills unveiled Wednesday is becoming clear, with some promising to block their passage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republican Speaker of the House is seeking a rule to pass almost $100bn in foreign aid - while unquestionably, dangerous criminals, terrorists, & fentanyl pour across our border,\u8221\'20\'1D Chip Roy, the Texas representative, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/chiproytx/status/1780617487849025932"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Republican Speaker of the House is seeking a rule to pass almost $100 billion in foreign aid - while unquestionably, dangerous criminals, terrorists, & fentanyl pour across our border. The border \u8220\'20\'1Cvote\u8221\'20\'1D in this package is a watered-down dangerous cover vote. I will oppose. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8LHlnZlgjd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/8LHlnZlgjd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chip Roy (@chiproytx) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/chiproytx/status/1780617487849025932?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe border \u8216\'20\'18vote\u8217\'20\'19 in this package is a watered-down dangerous cover vote. I will oppose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Roy is among those refusing to consider US aid for Israel, and particularly Ukraine, without massive investments in border security, which he and others say isn\u8217\'20\'19t included in Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s just-released package.\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the extremist Georgia representative who has threatened to call a vote to oust Johnson, is also furious.\par \par \uc2 enltrNews flash for Speaker Johnson, we have already passed HR2, the Senate has it and refuses to secure our border, they want 5,000 illegals per day to come in.\par \par \uc2 The House passed $14 Billion for Israel aid in November and the Senate refuses to pass it.\par \par \uc2 You, Speaker Johnson, voted\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 ???? (@RepMTG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1780621984142971114?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou are seriously out of step with Republicans by continuing to pass bills dependent on Democrats. Everyone sees through this,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1780621984142971114"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she wrote}}}\uc2 , also on X.\par \par \uc2 Johnson says the House will vote on the bills on Saturday night. There\u8217\'20\'19s no guarantee he will still be speaker at that point if Greene, or others, deliver on their threat to call a \u8220\'20\'1Cmotion to vacate\u8221\'20\'1D vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy morning in US politics on several fronts. An impeachment trial in the Senate is about to get under way for homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas, and there have been developments in efforts to progress funding for Israel and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19ve been following:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is preparing to hold a vote that could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/17/dismiss-impeachment-charges-mayorkas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismiss the two articles of impeachment}}}\uc2  filed by House Republicans on Tuesday alleging that Mayorkas broke the law in enacting \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s immigration policies. Schumer called the charges an \u8220\'20\'1Cillegitimate and profane abuse of the US Constitution\u8221\'20\'1D and said the votes would come after a brief \u8220\'20\'1Cperiod of debate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Embattled speaker Mike Johnson said the House would vote Saturday evening on three foreign aid bills, including money for Ukraine and Israel. The Louisiana Republican has been walking a fine line trying to find a solution that will appease rightwingers seeking to oust him, while standing a chance of passing the Democratic-controlled Senate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Arizona are resurrecting an effort to overturn an 1864 rule outlawing almost all abortions, enacted by a ruling earlier this month by the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court. Respected pollster \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2  says November\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race in the key swing state now \u8220\'20\'1Cleans Democratic\u8221\'20\'1D following the controversy, a change from \u8220\'20\'1Ctoss-up\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and Jeb Bush, current and former Florida governors, led tributes to Bob Graham, a two-term governor of the state, three-term US senator and Democratic political heavyweight who has died aged 87.\par \par \uc2 And still to come this afternoon:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  meets with steelworkers in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, as he touts his fair tax plan for workers and high earners. The president is due to deliver remarks at 1.45pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 McConnell: Democrats failing obligations to assess evidence by tanking Mayorkas impeachment\par \par \uc2 In response, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican Senate minority leader, is not happy that the impeachment trial is about to be tanked.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s accusing Democrats of failing to live up to their obligations to assess the evidence and render a verdict, and taking potshots at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s border policies:\par \par \uc2 Today it falls to the Senate to determine whether and to what extent Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas enabled and inflamed this crisis. Under the Constitution and the rules of impeachment, it is the job of this body to consider the articles of impeachment brought before us and to render judgment.\par \par \uc2 The question right now should be how best to ensure that the charges on the table receive thorough consideration. But instead, the more pressing question is whether our Democratic colleagues intend to let the Senate work its will, at all.\par \par \uc2 Tabling articles of impeachment would be unprecedented in the history of the Senate. Tabling would mean declining to discharge our duties as jurors.\par \par \uc2 It would mean running both from our fundamental responsibility and from the glaring truth of the record-breaking crisis at our southern border.\par \par \uc2 Absent from McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s statement blaming Democrats for the border crisis is any mention that his own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/07/us-senate-vote-bipartisan-border-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican senators negotiated, then sank, bipartisan legislation to address it}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The about-face came apparently at the urging of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presumptive opponent in November, who did not want Republicans to hand the president a pre-election victory on a campaign issue.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  has released a lengthy statement about the commencement (and presumably very swift termination) of the impeachment trial of homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 It is the \u8220\'20\'1Cleast legitimate, least substantive, and most politicized impeachment trial in the history of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic Senate majority leader said, encapsulating remarks he made in the chamber just now and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/watch/live/?ref=watch_permalink&v=1446080922926702"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted to Facebook}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The charges brought against Secretary Mayorkas fail to meet the high standard of high crimes and misdemeanors. To validate this gross abuse by the House would be a grave mistake and could set a dangerous precedent for the future.\par \par \uc2 For the sake of the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s integrity, and to protect impeachment for those rare cases we truly need it, Senators should dismiss today\u8217\'20\'19s charges.\par \par \uc2 So, when we convene in trial today, to accommodate the wishes of our Republican Senate colleagues, I will seek an agreement for a period of debate time that would allow Republicans to offer a vote on trial resolutions, allow for Republicans to offer points of order, and then move to dismiss.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s not kid ourselves about what\u8217\'20\'19s going on today: the impeachment of Alejandro Mayorkas has nothing to do with high crimes and misdemeanors and everything to do with helping \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 The votes could come in very short order, once Republicans have had their (very brief) say. The chamber has just convened to begin the proceedings.\par \par \uc2 Schumer concludes:\par \par \uc2 It is beneath the dignity of the Senate to entertain this nakedly partisan exercise.\par \par \uc2 Impeachment should never be used to settle policy disagreements. That would set a disastrous precedent for the Congress and could throw our system of checks and balances into endless cycles of chaos.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 House to vote Saturday on foreign aid packages\par \par \uc2 Speaker Mike Johnson has announced the House will vote on Saturday evening on a foreign aid package, including money for Ukraine and Israel.\par \par \uc2 It looks like Congress members will vote on three separate bills, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s chief congressional correspondent Manu Raju reports, even though their text has not yet been released.\par \par \uc2 enltrSaturday evening vote on foreign aid package, Johnson tells members in message {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Wuwx6mOb56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Wuwx6mOb56}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1780616668743414153?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter significant member feedback and discussion, the House rules committee will be posting soon today the text of three bills that will fund America\u8217\'20\'19s national security interests and allies in Israel, the Indo-Pacific, and Ukraine, including a loan structure for aid, and enhanced strategy and accountability,\u8221\'20\'1D a message from Johnson to colleagues states.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , have said they will not accept standalone bills, although Republican sources have said Johnson could wrap up whatever passes the House into a single package.\par \par \uc2 We await reaction from Republican rightwingers, who have indicated disapproval of any measure that includes money for Ukraine, and have threatened to remove Johnson as speaker over it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer: Mayorkas impeachment 'illegitimate and profane abuse of constitution'\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s looking increasingly likely that Senate Democrats will move to kill the impeachment trial of homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas in the coming few hours.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an illegitimate and profane abuse of the US constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  just told colleagues, according to reporting from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Lauren Gambino.\par \par \uc2 He said he would move to dismiss the two articles of impeachment after a \u8220\'20\'1Cperiod of debate time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 We reported earlier that Schumer was primed to call for a dismissal vote soon after senators were sworn in as jurors at lunchtime. It would deny Republican House impeachment managers an opportunity to present their case that Mayorkas is guilty of \u8220\'20\'1Chigh crimes and misdemeanors\u8221\'20\'1D for defying US law in pursuing immigration policies.\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans are already accusing Schumer of a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhitewash\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ccover-up\u8221\'20\'1D even before the trial has begun. Democrats, meanwhile, say the impeachment is \u8220\'20\'1Can embarrassing political stunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Developments in Arizona over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court paving the way for an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1864 act outlawing the procedure}}}\uc2  to take effect, have prompted a significant change in prospects for Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 fortunes in November elections.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/rating-changes-arizona-senate-and-az-6/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sabato\u8217\'20\'19s Crystal Ball}}}\uc2 , the website of the \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s respected pollster \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2 , Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s open Senate race between Republican Kari Lake (if she wins her primary race, as expected) and challenger \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  has shifted from \u8220\'20\'1Ctoss-up\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Cleans Democratic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrCrystal Ball rating changes this morning in ARIZONA --\par \par \uc2 AZ-SEN Toss-up to Leans D\par \par \uc2 Juan Ciscomani (R, AZ-6) Leans R to Toss-up\par \par \uc2 Explained here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7v9T3h4Ivs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7v9T3h4Ivs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Kondik (@kkondik) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kkondik/status/1780558021476659328?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Similarly, the congressional race in AZ district six, currently held by Republican Juan Ciscomani, has moved from \u8220\'20\'1Cleans Republican\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Ctoss-up\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Arizona Republicans have faced a huge backlash over the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, and particularly after they blocked Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 early efforts to repeal the 1864 law.\par \par \uc2 Terry Greene Sterling{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/17/arizona-abortion-ban-doctors-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes for the Guardian}}}\uc2  today about how Democrats in Arizona expect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fuel a \u8220\'20\'1Cblue wave\u8221\'20\'1D in November:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/17/arizona-abortion-ban-doctors-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers hope 1864 ban will spark change: \u8216\'20\'18A blue wave is coming\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a day off in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s criminal hush money trial in New York, but the Republican presumptive presidential nominee is keeping busy.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s meeting Poland\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Andrzej Duda\uc2 , who once proposed naming a military base in his country Fort Trump, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 The pair will meet over dinner, the AP says, citing \u8220\'20\'1Ca person familiar with the matter\u8221\'20\'1D. The agency states European leaders are preparing for the possibility of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House, with \uc2 Nato\uc2  leaders especially concerned given his support of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s leader \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some in Poland fear the get-together could hurt the country\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with the Biden administration, the AP says, while others welcome the prospect of Duda leveraging ties with Trump to make the case for backing Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trial for covering up a payment to an adult film star resumes on Thursday, with seven jurors already seated, and five more, plus six alternates, still needed. Judge Juan Merchan has said opening arguments could begin as early as Monday.\par \par \uc2 Have a read of the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest Trump on Trial newsletter here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/16/trump-on-trial-six-jurors-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump on Trial: seven jurors \u8211\'20\'13 and a warning for Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bob Graham, a veteran Democratic politician who served two terms as Florida governor, three terms in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , and ran for president in 2004, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/17/bob-graham-death-us-senator-florida-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 died at the age of 87}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Known for his dislike of partisan politics, Graham enjoyed a career that spanned five decades. He was massively popular with Florida\u8217\'20\'19s voters, and founded the concept of \u8220\'20\'1Cworkdays\u8221\'20\'1D, where he would join citizens in their daily life and talk to them about the issues that concerned them.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Bob Graham Center community is deeply saddened by the death of our beloved founder, former Florida Governor and U.S. Senator Bob Graham. We honor his historic legacy and life of service: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/522qmA9Aoc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/522qmA9Aoc}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YwMEo9e3ko"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YwMEo9e3ko}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bob Graham Center (@GrahamCenter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GrahamCenter/status/1780434237264650429?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 During 408 such days, Graham enjoyed stints as a housewife, boxing ring announcer, flight attendant and arson investigator.\par \par \uc2 He gained national prominence as chairman of the Senate intelligence committee in the aftermath of the September 2001 terrorist attacks, and as an early critic of the Iraq war that followed. He ran unsuccessfully for the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination in 2004.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are deeply saddened to report the passing of a visionary leader, dedicated public servant, and even more importantly, a loving husband, father, grandfather, and great-grandfather,\u8221\'20\'1D Graham\u8217\'20\'19s family said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Republicans \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the current Florida governor, and Jeb Bush, governor from 1999 to 2007, were among those paying tribute on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 enltrFlorida mourns the loss of former Governor and U.S. Senator Bob Graham today.\par \par \uc2 He was a devoted public servant who, among other important work, made enormous achievements in conserving Florida's natural resources.\par \par \uc2 We are grateful for his service to our state and nation. May he\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (@GovRonDeSantis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovRonDeSantis/status/1780584048055783465?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFlorida and our country has lost a great public servant. Bob Graham served Floridians with a servants heart, with integrity and with civility. Columba and I are praying for the Graham family. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vbvWd58Mn0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vbvWd58Mn0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeb Bush (@JebBush) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JebBush/status/1780546252221923456?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s news from Michigan, where the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman}}}\uc2  reports on Democrats seizing control of the state\u8217\'20\'19s lower house following special elections there:\par \par \uc2 Special elections for two vacant seats in the Michigan house of representatives flipped control back to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2 , who organizers say could use their restored trifecta in the state to pass legislation protecting voting rights and election administration.\par \par \uc2 A push to codify voter protections stalled after two Democratic lawmakers resigned and the party lost their majority in the house of representatives last November. With the election on Tuesday of Mai Xiong and Peter Herzberg, who represent sections of Detroit and its suburbs, legislators could use their newfound majorities to renew those efforts.\par \par \uc2 roltrMichigan state house\par \par \uc2 ?? 56\par \par \uc2 ?? 54\par \par \uc2 Michigan state senate\par \par \uc2 ?? 20\par \par \uc2 ?? 18\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 umichvoter ?????? (@umichvoter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/umichvoter/status/1780421758304018893?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 In November 2022, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2  voters passed a constitutional amendment enacting sweeping election reforms, including establishing early voting, expanding absentee voting and pre-empting the creation of stringent voter ID laws. The following year, the Democratic-controlled state legislature passed legislation to enact the amendment, setting aside more than $40m in the state budget to fund a measure to expand early and absentee voting, which was adopted by election clerks across the state.\par \par \uc2 Despite some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/michigan-officials-struggle-implementing-citizen-voting-changes-2024-rcna104107"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hiccups}}}\uc2  along the way, election offices across the state have succeeded in enacting the newly guaranteed nine days of early voting. Ahead of the 27 February presidential primary, more than 1 million voters cast their ballots early and absentee \u8211\'20\'13 a record, according to the state. The secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.michigan.gov/sos/resources/news/2024/02/26/over-one-million-early-and-absentee-votes-cast-ahead-of-michigans-presidential-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attributed}}}\uc2  the high turnout to the expanded early voting measure.\par \par \uc2 In their last legislative session, Michigan lawmakers introduced other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.michigan.gov/sos/elections/mvra"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 measures}}}\uc2  to protect voting rights \u8211\'20\'13 including establishing, through a package of bills, a state-level Voting Rights Act and a ban on prison gerrymandering. The Michigan Voting Rights Act forms part of a slew of measures states have taken to fill in the gaps left by weakened federal voting rights protections: New York, Connecticut, Virginia, Oregon, Washington and California have already passed such legislation.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/17/michigan-special-elections-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan special elections flip control of lower house in Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 favor}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats plot to squash Mayorkas impeachment trial\par \par \uc2 The Senate impeachment trial of homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas could be over before it even begins on Wednesday, as Democrats advance a plan to smother it.\par \par \uc2 According to the Associated Press, Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is expected to call votes to dismiss two articles of impeachment against Mayorkas after senators are sworn in as jurors at lunchtime.\par \par \uc2 Such a move could scuttle the trial, and frustrate Republicans who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/16/alejandro-mayorkas-impeachment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presented the articles}}}\uc2  and announced impeachment managers on Tuesday in expectation of being able to make their case that Mayorkas repeatedly ignored the law in pursuing immigration policy.\par \par \uc2 Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/13/mayorkas-house-impeachment-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 needed a second House vote}}}\uc2  in February to narrowly impeach Mayorkas after the first one ended in humiliation, and Democrats seized on it as \u8220\'20\'1Can embarrassing political stunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrNo one should take the extreme MAGA Republican impeachment effort against the Homeland Security Secretary seriously.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s an embarrassing political stunt led by \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Good riddance.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  (@hakeemjeffries) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hakeemjeffries/status/1780362614519767416?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Some Senate Republicans are also skeptical. Utah\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  is open to voting with Democrats to dismiss the impeachment, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/04/16/mayorkas-impeachment-dismiss-vote-mitt-romney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports}}}\uc2 . Romney was among six moderate Republican senators who did not sign a letter from colleagues to Schumer demanding a trial, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/list-gop-senators-who-didnt-sign-call-mayorkas-impeachment-trial-1889568"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Newsweek}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas, meanwhile, says he\u8217\'20\'19s focused on running the homeland security department.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs they work on impeachment, I work on advancing the mission of the department. That\u8217\'20\'19s what I\u8217\'20\'19ve done throughout this process,\u8221\'20\'1D he told CBS Mornings.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/16/alejandro-mayorkas-impeachment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Republicans present Mayorkas impeachment articles to Senate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican dysfunction overshadows Ukraine funding effort\par \par \uc2 The Republican infighting that has both stalled and overshadowed efforts to pass funding packages for Israel and Ukraine is still raging today, as speaker Mike Johnson clings to his job in the face of a growing rightwing rebellion.\par \par \uc2 So far, there\u8217\'20\'19s no sign of a formal plan for the urgently needed aid as Johnson mulls his best approach. Kentucky extremist \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2  on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/16/house-republican-effort-oust-speaker-mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave his support}}}\uc2  to a threat by Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  to invoke a \u8220\'20\'1Cmotion to vacate\u8221\'20\'1D if Johnson follows through with a plan to tie tens of billions of dollars in funding for Ukraine to money for Israel and Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 But standalone bills, which Johnson is also said to be considering, won\u8217\'20\'19t cut it in the Democratic-controlled Senate, or with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who has indicated he won\u8217\'20\'19t sign anything other than an all-in-one package.\par \par \uc2 And a number of Republican congress members insist they cannot support anything that would help Ukraine unless legislation includes money for strengthening the border.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a delicate dance, with no predictable outcome. Johnson, who can only afford to lose two Republican votes in any push to remove him, says he won\u8217\'20\'19t resign, calling moves to oust him \u8220\'20\'1Cabsurd\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, some Democrats are ready to step in to try to save him. Florida congressman \uc2 Jared Moskowitz\uc2  is among those who says he\u8217\'20\'19s ready to keep Johnson in place in any House vote in order to secure the advancement of US aid for overseas allies.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy position hasn\u8217\'20\'19t changed. Massie wants the world to burn, I won\u8217\'20\'19t stand by and watch. I have a bucket of water. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bn61J6N2y3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/bn61J6N2y3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jared Moskowitz\uc2  (@JaredEMoskowitz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JaredEMoskowitz/status/1780240051877589367?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 16, 2024}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2024/04/17/johnson-second-guesses-his-plan-00152720?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=ef9757b7-1c82-4c99-8e9a-082111707afd&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Politico Playbook}}}\uc2 , Johnson is \u8220\'20\'1Csecond guessing\u8221\'20\'1D his approach, resulting in a delay to publication of his plan, and growing unease among Republican leadership at the increasing dysfunction and chaos.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll keep an eye on developments and bring you news of any proposals as they\u8217\'20\'19re published.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/16/house-republican-effort-oust-speaker-mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Second House Republican joins far-right effort to oust Mike Johnson}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans spar over foreign aid bill as Senate Democrats plot to crush Mayorkas impeachment\par \par \uc2 Good morning and happy hump day to US politics readers. Wednesday could finally see the publication of speaker Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s long-awaited plan to save his job, quell Republican infighting and advance urgent foreign aid for Israel and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s been plenty of talk, and little action so far, on how the Republican leader plans to present solutions for the funding impasse that has further highlighted fractures in his divided caucus.\par \par \uc2 Any misstep could trigger a \u8220\'20\'1Cmotion to vacate\u8221\'20\'1D by rebel-rousers \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2 , and potentially see Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s departure from the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s chair, unless Democrats step in to save him.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you news of any firm proposals as we get them.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere today, the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic majority is plotting to sink the impeachment of homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas, following Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presentation of two articles by the Republican House majority.\par \par \uc2 Majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  has a plan to bring votes to dismiss the charges, after senators are sworn in as jurors on Wednesday, but before arguments can begin, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is on the campaign trail with steelworkers in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, this afternoon. The president is pitching a plan to increase taxes on high earners, and is expected to continue bashing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , whose hush-money trial in New York has an off-day today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re following:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Arizona are preparing to try to repeal the controversial 1864 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill that has prompted huge blowback and poses a threat to Republican candidates in November\u8217\'20\'19s elections.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  and energy secretary \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2  are testifying before the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s appropriations subcommittee this morning.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Long-serving Florida governor and US senator Bob Graham, a Democratic political heavyweight who also ran for president in 2004, has died aged 87.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240417ek4h001ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
