\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Arizona  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling is a win Kari Lake didn\u8217\'20\'19t need in key Senate race\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Sun City West and Goodyear \par \uc2 2,457 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2024\par 15:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Republican former TV anchor is trying to soften her election-denying image against the Democratic congressman \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  in one of the year\u8217\'20\'19s most closely watched races\par \par \uc2 On a recent Tuesday morning, at a retirement community on the western edge of Phoenix\u8217\'20\'19s sprawling desert metropolis, Kari Lake beamed at the graying crowd and introduced her guest, the Montana senator Steve Daines, the Republican charged with winning back the party\u8217\'20\'19s Senate majority in Washington.\par \par \uc2 His presence sent the message that establishment Republicans were fully behind Lake, a former TV news anchor in Phoenix whose embrace of election denialism and fealty to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made her a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/politics-arizona-state-government-us-republican-party-united-states-2022-midterm-elections-83b69ddc64c94aad9f5cfb63d0af4f5a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 darling of his Maga movement }}}\uc2  but probably {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/15/us/politics/election-denial-republicans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cost}}}\uc2  her the 2022 race for Arizona governor, a loss she has never formally conceded.\par \par \uc2 Now, as the likely Republican nominee for an open Senate seat in Arizona, Lake, 54, is attempting something of a rebrand, vowing to be less {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KariLake/status/1732068833396199426?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdivisive\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  as she strains to win back the very voters she alienated with her scorched-earth campaign for governor two years ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet me be clear, we win Arizona, we win the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Daines told attendees, a mix of local Republican officials and sun-seeking transplants. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s as simple as that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The race, however, is not simple at all. The contest to replace \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/09/kyrsten-sinema-independent-days-after-democrats-secure-senate-majority"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left the Democratic party last year}}}\uc2  to become an independent before deciding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/05/kyrsten-sinema-not-running-reelection-senate-arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not to seek re-election}}}\uc2 , is expected to be one of the most competitive \u8211\'20\'13 and expensive \u8211\'20\'13 of the election cycle.\par \par \uc2 Lake\u8217\'20\'19s likely opponent, the Democratic congressman \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 , is also courting voters in the political center, softening the combative approach that made him popular with the constituents of his liberal Phoenix district. With just under seven months until election day, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/senate/2024/arizona/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most surveys}}}\uc2  show Gallego, 44, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4542446-ruben-gallego-kari-lake-arizona-senate-poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with a narrow lead}}}\uc2  over Lake.\par \par \uc2 The Senate race was roiled this week by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision}}}\uc2  to uphold a territorial-era law that bans nearly all abortions in the state, all-but ensuring the issue will dominate the political debate in an electoral battleground with a strong libertarian bent.\par \par \uc2 A court-the-center playbook has powered sweeping statewide victories for Democrats in the years since Trump won the 2016 election. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s 11 electoral votes in 2020 while the state sent two Democrats to the Senate and elected a Democratic governor, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , who defeated Lake in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Even knowing the risks of running to the right in a purple state, Lake has not sought to distance herself from Trump \u8211\'20\'13 she has promised, as her first act in the Senate, to introduce legislation to \u8220\'20\'1Cbuild the wall\u8221\'20\'1D. But she has attempted to move her message beyond her baseless claims of election fraud, despite ongoing litigation related to her effort to overturn her defeat in 2022. She has also sought to walk back her position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which she once called the \u8220\'20\'1Cultimate sin\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Gallego, speaking to a crowd of retirees in the Phoenix suburb of Goodyear last week, is hoping his efforts to work across the aisle in Congress and a yet-to-be-unveiled roster of Republican and independent endorsements will end in a decisive victory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have to explain to them who Kari Lake is,\u8221\'20\'1D Gallego said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to explain to them who I am.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Democrats hope to harness outrage over the decision to allow enforcement of the pre-statehood \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.On Friday Gallego appeared alongside Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at an event in Tucson to hammer Republicans for their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  record.\par \par \uc2 The ruling was so seismic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/arizona-republicans-against-state-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  even staunchly anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  Republicans}}}\uc2  like Lake {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/11/kari-lake-arizona-abortion-reversal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raced to distance themselves}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, fury over the 160-year-old law, which has not yet taken effect, amplified signature-gathering efforts to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on the ballot this year, a move Democrats hope will mobilize young and otherwise disengaged liberal voters.\par \par \uc2 Gallego, meanwhile, has made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a centerpiece of his Senate campaign since its onset. At the Goodyear event, the Democrat vowed as senator to abolish the Senate filibuster to codify Roe v Wade, which the supreme court overturned in 2022, eliminating the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we believe it\u8217\'20\'19s right, then we need to do everything we can to enshrine that right,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Strategists in the state believe Lake will probably have a harder time than Gallego appealing to Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s coveted slice of independent voters and moderates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongressman Gallego has to introduce himself to voters and talk about his legacy of service,\u8221\'20\'1D said Stacy Pearson, an Arizona-based Democratic strategist. \u8220\'20\'1C[Lake] has to convince voters that she was just kidding 12 months ago, and isn\u8217\'20\'19t really supportive of a ban that predates light bulbs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard for a candidate to shake off the stench of death after a statewide loss,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, \u8220\'20\'1Cmuch less when that candidate was supporting the very \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that has women\u8217\'20\'19s hair on fire in Phoenix today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lake, like Trump, has spent the days since the decision trying to find safe political ground on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue. She quickly denounced the 1864 law as \u8220\'20\'1Cout of line\u8221\'20\'1D with the people of Arizona and called on the legislature to \u8220\'20\'1Ccome up\u8221\'20\'1D with a solution.\par \par \uc2 But Democrats are unwilling to let voters forget Lake\u8217\'20\'19s words from 2022, when she told a conservative podcast host: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m incredibly thrilled that we are going to have a great law that\u8217\'20\'19s already on the books\u8221\'20\'1D and referred to the civil war-era ban by its number in Arizona state code.\par \par \uc2 With a spotlight on her retreat, Lake on Thursday released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vPl_hyizHMU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five-and-a-half-minute video}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe issue is less about banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and more about saving babies,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, as she emphasized her support for policies that would support mothers and reduce taxes on families.\par \par \uc2 On her website, Lake says she opposes a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Lake\u8217\'20\'19s spectacular jump from the anchor desk into the heart of Trumpworld politics shocked many viewers \u8211\'20\'13 and voters. And it is part of her pitch. In Sun City West, the ex-journalist told attendees they were being \u8220\'20\'1Clied to\u8221\'20\'1D by an \u8220\'20\'1CunAmerican\u8221\'20\'1D press corps. Instead, she asked them to trust her. After years of reporting across Arizona, Lake said she was uniquely qualified to represent the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI understand the people of Arizona probably better than anybody in politics right now in this state because I\u8217\'20\'19ve had the opportunity to be invited into your homes to cover the big issues,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Attendee Donna Burrell, 70, of Sun City Grand, said she was torn over who to support in the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican primary in July. Burrell had been leaning toward Lake\u8217\'20\'19s main primary opponent, a conservative county sheriff, Mark Lamb, but Lake impressed her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem so angry and in-your-face,\u8221\'20\'1D Burrell said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I came here today, I really liked her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Republican base is firmly behind Lake, who leads Lamb by a wide margin. But Mike Noble, a Phoenix-based pollster who is tracking public opinion on the race, predicted Lake would struggle to broaden her appeal , especially with independent voters, a significant share of whom, he said, place stolen election claims in the same category as the \u8220\'20\'1Cearth is flat\u8221\'20\'1D conspiracy.\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19re not a leader, if you\u8217\'20\'19re exploiting people\u8217\'20\'19s fear. That\u8217\'20\'19s what she\u8217\'20\'19s doing right now\par \par \uc2 Ruben Gallego\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Lake {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/27/kari-lake-defamation-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  chose not to defend}}}\uc2  her claims of a stolen election, asking an Arizona court to move directly to the damages phase of a defamation lawsuit. The case was brought by Maricopa county\u8217\'20\'19s top election official, Stephen Richer, a Republican whom Lake accused of allowing fraud to taint the results of the 2022 gubernatorial election she lost, claims he said unleashed a barrage of threats against him and his family.\par \par \uc2 Richer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://protectdemocracy.org/work/kari-lake-and-other-defendants-capitulate-in-richer-defamation-suit/#:~:text=%E2%80%9CKari%20Lake%20and%20the%20other,and%20Rule%20of%20Law%20Clinic."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Lake\u8217\'20\'19s decision amounted to an admission that her \u8220\'20\'1Clies were just that: lies\u8221\'20\'1D. Lake said she conceded nothing and compared herself to Trump, casting them as twin victims of a legal system that will \u8220\'20\'1C stop at nothing to destroy us\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail, Gallego presents himself to voters as a results-driven veteran committed to the defense of America\u8217\'20\'19s democratic institutions.\par \par \uc2 In Goodyear, he recalled being on the House floor when a mob of Trump supporters breached the US Capitol. He said his combat instincts kicked in and he began instructing lawmakers how to put gas masks on and prepare to fight if it came to that. Lake, he warned, was only fueling those forces.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re not a leader, if you\u8217\'20\'19re exploiting people\u8217\'20\'19s fear,\u8221\'20\'1D Gallego said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what she\u8217\'20\'19s doing right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Lake\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to reconcile with Republicans she attacked during her 2022 race have been mixed. Outreach to \uc2 Meghan McCain\uc2 , the daughter of Senator \uc2 John McCain\uc2 , the popular Arizona Republican senator who died in 2018, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MeghanMcCain/status/1760346193630990352?lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was met with the response \u8220\'20\'1Cno peace bitch\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . At a campaign rally during her run for governor, she told the late senator\u8217\'20\'19s supporters to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/11/15/opinions/kari-lake-mccain-arizona-republicans-gabriel/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cget the hell out\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , a comment Lake later said was made \u8220\'20\'1Cin jest\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 And at the end of the event in Sun City West, a woman waved a piece of paper which she claimed provided evidence of ballot-rigging in the 2020 election. \u8220\'20\'1CI need your help,\u8221\'20\'1D she shouted as Lake and Daines quickly left the stage.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 At Gallego\u8217\'20\'19s town hall, held earlier this month in a traditionally Republican part of Phoenix\u8217\'20\'19s West Valley that has experienced soaring growth in the past decade, Democrats scrounged for extra seating to accommodate the crowd.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was pleasantly, pleasantly surprised that we could get this big of a turnout in a very red part of the county,\u8221\'20\'1D said Barbara Valencia, a member of the local Democratic party who has known Gallego since the early days of his political career. She was confident Arizonans would gravitate toward Gallego the more they learned about his story \u8211\'20\'13 a Harvard-educated combat veteran raised by a single mother from Colombia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s very grassroots, from the ground up,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Since launching his campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/23/ruben-gallego-arizona-senate-kyrsten-sinema-democrat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than a year ago}}}\uc2 , Gallego has made his goal to visit every corner of the state, including each of Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s nearly two dozen federally recognized tribal nations, to reach voters outside of the Phoenix metropolitan area. Before the West Valley event, Gallego {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rubengallego/status/1775331008818397536?s=46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visited}}}\uc2  leaders of the Kaibab Paiute Indian Tribe in northern Arizona, which required flying into southern Utah and driving two hours south.\par \par \uc2 Yet despite recent Democratic successes, Gallego must also contend with stormy presidential-year politics. Biden, who will be at the top of the ballot, is unpopular in Arizona, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/2024/arizona/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trailing}}}\uc2  Trump in several swing state surveys. Inflation has proven an intractable problem for the president, while his handling of record migration at the US-Mexico border has drawn bipartisan criticism.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats in the state are worried about the party\u8217\'20\'19s outreach to Latino voters, a critical part of their electoral coalition that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/01/trump-biden-latino-voters-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has shifted}}}\uc2  toward Trump in recent years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to mobilize the Hispanic vote,\u8221\'20\'1D said Judy Phillips, a Democrat who attended Gallego\u8217\'20\'19s town hall in Goodyear and is Hispanic. \u8220\'20\'1CIf they don\u8217\'20\'19t hear the good things from the candidates, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to get sucked in by the lies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s not running against an astronaut, Mark Kelly \u8230\'20\'26 She\u8217\'20\'19s running against a true radical far-left activist\par \par \uc2 Steve Daines\par \par \uc2 But early indicators are on his side. A poll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://7453540.fs1.hubspotusercontent-na1.net/hubfs/7453540/AZPOP/2024/240205_AZPOP/240205_AZPOP%20Senate%20poll%20report.xlsx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conducted}}}\uc2  by Noble\u8217\'20\'19s firm in February, before Sinema bowed out of the race, found that Gallego led Lake by double digits with suburbanites, independents and Hispanic voters. Sinema has not made an endorsement in the Senate race.\par \par \uc2 Arizona Republicans, Noble quipped, choose to nominate unpopular candidates who cannot win general elections \u8220\'20\'1Cnot because it is easy, but because it is hard\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 At her event, Lake sought to scare off moderate Republicans from defecting with a warning about her opponent. Gallego, she said, was trying to \u8220\'20\'1Ctrick the people of Arizona\u8221\'20\'1D into believing he was a consensus-building, \u8220\'20\'1Cmiddle-of-the-road\u8221\'20\'1D Democrat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be further from the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, citing his past criticism of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s border wall. Daines, the Montana senator, chimed: \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s not running against an astronaut, Mark Kelly. She\u8217\'20\'19s not running against \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 . She\u8217\'20\'19s running against a true radical far-left activist.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Defining Gallego while also trying to change her own reputation in the state will require considerable resources, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLake\u8217\'20\'19s miniscule war chest isn\u8217\'20\'19t enough to really let that sink into voters,\u8221\'20\'1D said Barrett Marson, an Arizona-based Republican consultant. \u8220\'20\'1CShe will need the help of national groups to really paint Ruben as a liberal lion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gallego\u8217\'20\'19s campaign is already running biographical ads on local and cable TV, including one focused on his deployment to Iraq with a Marine Corps unit that sustained some of the highest casualties of the war. With his record, the Democrat is targeting the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/11/10/map-where-veterans-live-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 large veteran population}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is an open question whether her support from Republicans in Washington will translate into a significant financial investment. But her core supporters are giving. Last week, Lake\u8217\'20\'19s campaign announced that she raised what it claimed was a record $1m at a fundraising event at Mar-a-Lago, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Florida resort.\par \par \uc2 It is yet another sign, Marson said, that Lake and Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwill live or die together\u8221\'20\'1D in Arizona this November.\par \par \uc2 Gallego, meanwhile, announced that his campaign raised $7.5m in the first three months of 2024, a notable haul that leaves him with $9.6m cash on hand. Lake has yet to announce her first-quarter fundraising numbers, but the stakes are high. She began the year with much less money than Gallego and it remains unclear what, if any, damages she will have to pay in the defamation suit.\par \par \uc2 Much can \u8211\'20\'13 and almost certainly will \u8211\'20\'13 change before election day. But as the contours of the high-profile Senate race come into focus, political observers now believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be a defining issue of the Arizona election. And here, they say, Gallego has the advantage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got those crossover voters that will never register as Democrats but who are also not Maga,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pearson, the Democratic strategist, referring to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing movement. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd this is an issue that takes those voters \u8211\'20\'13 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s defiant, libertarian, Republican voting bloc \u8211\'20\'13 and pulls them right over to the Democrats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240414ek4e001mj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
