\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Jimmy Kimmel on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trials: \u8216\'20\'18Seems like quite a lot of due process for a witch-hunt to me\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff \par \uc2 986 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par 14:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Late-night hosts discuss Trump\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming hush-money trial, his \uc2 Chick-fil-A\uc2  appearance and Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s 1864 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Late-night hosts talk Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s banter at \uc2 Chick-fil-A\uc2 , his delay tactics in court and Republican hypocrisy with outrage over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban from 1864}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jimmy Kimmel\par \par \uc2 From Los Angeles, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2024/apr/05/jimmy-kimmel-trump-hush-money-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jimmy Kimmel}}}\uc2  looked forward to the start of Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hush-money trial next Monday in New York. \u8220\'20\'1CAll his many efforts to delay it have failed,\u8221\'20\'1D he remarked on Thursday evening. \u8220\'20\'1CHis only move left is to have sex with everyone in the court and pay them $130,000 to keep their mouths shut.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has lost three appeals in as many days to delay the trial. \u8220\'20\'1CHe does this in every trial to gum up the mechanism. He keeps challenging and challenging, and it works,\u8221\'20\'1D Kimmel explained. \u8220\'20\'1CAll these trials are behind schedule, and most won\u8217\'20\'19t likely happen until after the election, if at all.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhich, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know, it seems like quite a lot of due process for a witch-hunt to me,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like, \u8216\'20\'18We can\u8217\'20\'19t burn this witch yet, her attorneys are saying the water we use to see if she floats wasn\u8217\'20\'19t distilled.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut you know what they say: if at first, second, third, fourth, fifth, sixth, seventh, eighth, ninth or tenth you don\u8217\'20\'19t succeed, cry, cry again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other GOP news, the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , has reportedly started telling donors that he will fundraise for Trump, his former bitter rival in the Republican primary. \u8220\'20\'1CWhich should be easy, given his natural magnetism and charm,\u8221\'20\'1D Kimmel deadpanned.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis \u8220\'20\'1Cspent the better part of a year trashing Trump. Now he wants to raise money for him,\u8221\'20\'1D Kimmel explained. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd there\u8217\'20\'19s actually a very good reason why: he\u8217\'20\'19s a little bitch. It\u8217\'20\'19s another chicken with his backbone removed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Seth Meyers\par \par \uc2 Amid all his legal troubles \u8211\'20\'13 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Save America Pac spent $230,000 a day on legal bills in February \u8211\'20\'13 the former president attempted to drum up popular support this week with a visit to a \uc2 Chick-fil-A\uc2  in Atlanta, where he bought 30 milkshakes and bantered with employees by asking if they were getting rich. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like he\u8217\'20\'19s never talked to normal human beings in his life,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/seth-meyers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Seth Meyers}}}\uc2  on Late Night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you ask me, they deserve to be rich,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CCertainly richer than Donald Trump. And they deserve a raise for working that shift, because he for sure did not pay.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meyers also targeted fawning coverage of the stunt on Fox News, where one host argued: \u8220\'20\'1CThis idea that Democrats try to sell that Trump is an awful human being, that he\u8217\'20\'19s Adolf Hitler \u8211\'20\'13 I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if Hitler was regularly buying journalists milkshakes or walking in \uc2 Chick-fil-A\uc2  or Dairy Queen like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sorry, you don\u8217\'20\'19t know that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t? I know \u8211\'20\'13 he didn\u8217\'20\'19t,\u8221\'20\'1D Meyers responded. \u8220\'20\'1CThey say crazy shit all the time on Fox News but they\u8217\'20\'19re not willing to go out on a limb to say for certain that Hitler didn\u8217\'20\'19t buy milkshakes for journalists?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat are you even talking about Hitler for?!\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one else brought him up. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a good rule for your life: you never want to be the first person in a conversation to bring up Hitler.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Daily Show\par \par \uc2 Arizona's anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law is being received as well as O.J. Simpson at the Pearly Gates. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/michaelkosta?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @michaelkosta}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MiQSd7AmOq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MiQSd7AmOq}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 The Daily Show (@TheDailyShow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheDailyShow/status/1778604197774311785?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And on The Daily Show, guest host Michael Kosta went in on the Arizona supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to uphold a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban first enacted in 1864, before Arizona was even a state. \u8220\'20\'1CThis anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law is being received as well as OJ Simpson at the pearly gates,\u8221\'20\'1D Kosta joked, citing statements from several Republican lawmakers opposing the decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven far-right Republican Kari Lake hates it!\u8221\'20\'1D he said of the extremist Arizona Senate candidate. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that can\u8217\'20\'19t just be because she\u8217\'20\'19s in a tight Senate race. Surely she\u8217\'20\'19s always hated it, right?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kosta quoted Lake from less than two years ago: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m incredibly thrilled that we are going to have a great law that\u8217\'20\'19s already on the books,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to the ban by its bill number.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHave you ever loved a law so much that you memorized it?\u8221\'20\'1D Kosta wondered. \u8220\'20\'1CEven the person who wrote the law in 1864 would be like, \u8216\'20\'18My lady, thou art a weirdo.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pretty sure if you find Kari Lake\u8217\'20\'19s iPhone, you\u8217\'20\'19ll be able to unlock it,\u8221\'20\'1D he quipped.\par \par \uc2 Yet despite outcry even from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republicans, the same GOP lawmakers in Arizona voted down a measure to overturn the ruling. \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys say you don\u8217\'20\'19t want an insane \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, but then you voted to keep it,\u8221\'20\'1D Kosta mused. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s almost like you\u8217\'20\'19re just \u8230\'20\'26 totally full of shit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Arizona women are going to be forced to live under this law from 1864, then all of Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s lawmakers should be forced to get their healthcare from 1864 standards too,\u8221\'20\'1D he proposed. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got back pain? Put some leeches on it! Migraine? More leeches. Feeling depressed? You can see a therapist! Your therapist is a leech.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 2024-04-12T14:43:10Z 2024-04-12T15:06:52Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/39dc57e61273aa12bb6229a412bbe0b2a690d876/206_117_2548_1529/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/39dc57e61273aa12bb6229a412bbe0b2a690d876/206_117_2548_1529/500.jpg}}}\uc2  Jimmy Kimmel on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to delay his hush-money trial: \u8216\'20\'18He does this in every trial to gum up the mechanism. He keeps challenging and challenging, and it works.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240412ek4c0020a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
