\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  calls Trump \u8216\'20\'18architect of healthcare crisis\u8217\'20\'19 in Arizona  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  speech \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin (now); Maya Yang and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 5,400 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par 23:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all the live coverage for today, thanks for following along. Some highlights and links from the day:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House lawmakers voted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/fisa-surveillance-act-reauthorized"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reauthorize section 702 of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act}}}\uc2  (Fisa), including a key measure that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/12/what-is-fisa-warrant-surveillance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allows for warrantless surveillance of Americans}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The reauthorization of Fisa was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/12/politics-updates-kamala-harris-trump-mike-johnson?page=with:block-661977698f08f961ba5a8227#block-661977698f08f961ba5a8227"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considered}}}\uc2  a win for the embattled House speaker, Mike Johnson.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/sterilizations-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research}}}\uc2  showed that rates of people seeking permanent contraception \u8211\'20\'13 such as tubal ligation or vasectomies \u8211\'20\'13 jumped after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Mike Johnson held a joint press conference {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/12/politics-updates-kamala-harris-trump-mike-johnson?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6619a4048f0806742af9755a#block-6619a4048f0806742af9755a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promoting legislation}}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Crequire proof of citizenship to vote\u8221\'20\'1D despite federal law already prohibiting non-citizen voting and a lack of evidence of migrants casting ballots.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said he would \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/12/politics-updates-kamala-harris-trump-mike-johnson?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6619a80f8f087ec9b85349d8#block-6619a80f8f087ec9b85349d8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 absolutely}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D testify at his upcoming New York criminal trial.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/12/politics-updates-kamala-harris-trump-mike-johnson?page=with:block-6619a6358f087ec9b85349c9#block-6619a6358f087ec9b85349c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took credit for eroding \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 , saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe broke Roe v Wade \u8230\'20\'26 and we gave it back to the states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  condemned Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban at a rally in Tucson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/12/politics-updates-kamala-harris-trump-mike-johnson?page=with:block-6619acdd8f08f961ba5a83bd#block-6619acdd8f08f961ba5a83bd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwants to take America back to the 1800s\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/12/politics-updates-kamala-harris-trump-mike-johnson?page=with:block-6619ae908f0806742af975a8#block-6619ae908f0806742af975a8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blaming the former president}}}\uc2  for state bans across the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Arizona's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban: '\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did this'\par \par \uc2 Speaking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at a campaign rally in Tucson, vice -president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1Cmomentum is on our side\u8221\'20\'1D, citing voters\u8217\'20\'19 support for reproductive rights in ballot measures across the US:\par \par \uc2 From Kansas to California to Kentucky, in Michigan, Montana, Vermont, and Ohio, the people of America have voted for freedom and not just by a little, but often by overwhelming margins, proving also that this is not just a partisan issue, proving that the voice of the people has been heard.\par \par \uc2 Harris was speaking days after Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruled that a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban law dating back to 1864 could go into effect. Of that law, she said:\par \par \uc2 Women here live under one of the most extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in our nation. No exception for rape or incest, prison time for doctors and nurses and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  made illegal before most women even know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant. The overturning of Roe was without any question a seismic event, and this ban here in Arizona is one of the biggest aftershocks yet \u8230\'20\'26 this law was passed in the 1800s before Arizona was even a state, before women could even vote. What has happened here in Arizona is a new inflection point \u8230\'20\'26 overturning Roe was just the opening act of a larger strategy to take women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and freedoms \u8230\'20\'26 we all must understand who is to blame. Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : 'Trump wants to take America back to the 1800s'\par \par \uc2 Vice -president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is strongly condemning Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and tying the policy and other state bans directly to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the architect of this healthcare crisis, and that is not a fact that he hides. Just this week, he said he was \u8216\'20\'18proudly\u8217\'20\'19 responsible for overturning Roe.\par \par \uc2 Harris summarized Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks from minutes earlier in Mar-a-Lago: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump just said the collection of state bans is working the way it\u8217\'20\'19s supposed to.\u8221\'20\'1D On Trump\u8217\'20\'19s backtracking of support of a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Harris said, \u8220\'20\'1CEnough with the gaslighting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A second Trump term, she said, would mean \u8220\'20\'1Cmore bans, more suffering and less freedom. He basically wants to take America back to the 1800s,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we are not going to let that happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  condemns \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Arizona speech\par \par \uc2 Vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is now speaking in Tucson, Arizona to condemn the 1800s-era ban supported by the state supreme court this week:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Arizona Supreme Court ruled an extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from the 1800s with no exceptions for health, rape, or incest will go into effect. Trump is responsible for this.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m in Tucson to discuss the fight ahead for our reproductive freedom. Tune in.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ocUnZWa18Z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ocUnZWa18Z}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1778901134104580312?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump: I would 'absolutely' testify at New York criminal trial\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told reporters at Mar-a-Lago he would \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely\u8221\'20\'1D testify at his New York criminal trial, which is set to start next week. It is not, however, clear if he will actually do so.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Trump vows to testify at his New York criminal trial that starts next week -- "Yeah I would testify absolutely" -- though whether he will actually testify remains to be seen given his track record of self-incrimination\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1778899041415242167?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Asked if it was \u8220\'20\'1Crisky\u8221\'20\'1D for him to testify, the former president responded, \u8220\'20\'1CI tell the truth.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s testimony has previously hurt him in court, and he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/26/e-jean-carroll-damages-trump-defamation-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2  by a jury earlier this year to pay millions to E Jean Carroll for defamation.\par \par \uc2 Trump shared familiar grievances about his various criminal ongoing criminal trials before his \u8220\'20\'1Celection integrity\u8221\'20\'1D press conference with House speaker Mike Johnson came to an end.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , speaking at Mar-a-Lago, was asked why voters should trust he will not sign a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, when he had previously indicated support. He responded:\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t need it any longer, because we broke Roe v Wade \u8230\'20\'26 and we gave it back to the states.\par \par \uc2 He claimed he does not support the unpopular Arizona state supreme court ruling this week supporting a near total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ban dating back to 1864. When asked whether he is \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D, he gave a meandering, unclear response.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson promotes legislation to 'require proof of citizenship to vote'\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson says Republicans are introducing legislation to \u8220\'20\'1Crequire proof of citizenship to vote\u8221\'20\'1D despite the fact that it is already illegal for non-citizens to vote and there is no evidence of widespread migrant voting (or even many specific examples of this happening).\par \par \uc2 Johnson hasn\u8217\'20\'19t shared a ton of details about the mechanics of the legislation, but claimed that if \u8220\'20\'1Chundreds of thousands\u8221\'20\'1D of migrants cast votes, it could impact the result of the elections. Research has repeatedly shown that the systems in place have not allowed non-citizens to register or cast ballots.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s press conference at Mar-a-Lago has begun\par \par \uc2 The former president has started his presser with his signature xenophobic rhetoric on immigration, which has become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/06/donald-trump-speech-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasingly dehumanizing}}}\uc2  and viscous on the campaign trail. He has frequently called migrants \u8220\'20\'1Canimals\u8221\'20\'1D and has said they are \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/16/trump-immigrants-new-hampshire-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poisoning the blood}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D of the US, echoing Nazi speech and the racist, far-right Great Replacement Theory suggesting the left is promoting migration to replace white people.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s introductory remarks included {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-focuses-migrants-crime-here-is-what-research-shows-2024-04-11/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 misinformation}}}\uc2  tying migrants to crime.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we await the joint press conference of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and House speaker Mike Johnson at Mar-a-Lago, here\u8217\'20\'19s a refresher on some of the misleading and false information they have been promoting about non-citizens and voting:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The two have said they are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/11/trump-mike-johnson-migrant-voting-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing legislation}}}\uc2  to ban non-citizens from voting \u8211\'20\'13 despite the fact that it is already illegal under federal law for people without US citizenship to cast a ballot.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has spread racist conspiracy theories on the campaign trail \u8211\'20\'13 claiming without evidence that migrants will try to illegally vote and steal the election for him, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThey can\u8217\'20\'19t speak a word of English for the most part, but they\u8217\'20\'19re signing them up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s democracy reporter Rachel Leingang {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no evidence of widespread non-citizen voting, nor are there even many examples of individual instances of the practice, despite strenuous efforts in some states to find these cases.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/noncitizen-voting-missing-millions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  by the Brennan Center of the 2016 election found just 0.0001% of votes across 42 jurisdictions, with 23.5m votes, were suspected to be non-citizens voting, 30 incidents in total.\par \par \uc2 The press conference is scheduled for 4.30pm local time. For more background, check out Leingang\u8217\'20\'19s coverage from earlier this week:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/11/trump-mike-johnson-migrant-voting-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump and Mike Johnson push for redundant ban on non-citizens voting}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Mike Johnson to hold 'election integrity' press conference\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to meet House Republican speaker Mike Johnson in Mar-a-Lago on Friday where the two will hold a press conference on \u8220\'20\'1Celection integrity \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Friday, Johnson told reporters, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t ever comment on my private conversations with President Trump, but I\u8217\'20\'19m looking forward to going to Florida and spend some time with him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a senior Trump adviser {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/04/12/politics/mike-johnson-trump-mar-a-lago/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  CNN that the two will \u8220\'20\'1Cdraw attention to\u8221\'20\'1D state proposals and lawsuits that would allow non-citizens to vote.\par \par \uc2 Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s meeting with Trump comes after the Republican speaker secured a crucial win in the House earlier on Friday after the Republican-led chamber voted to pass Fisa reauthorization. The legislation, which allows for warrantless surveillance of Americans by intelligence officials, is supported by Johnson but heavily opposed by hard-right Republicans and Democrats alike.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Wyoming Republican representative Harriet Hageman has also released a video address following the House\u8217\'20\'19s passage of Fisa\u8217\'20\'19s reauthorization.\par \par \uc2 In her address, Hageman, who voted no, said:\par \par \uc2 I was a no vote for the reason that the amendment that would have required the intelligence agencies to obtain a warrant to search the records of American citizens was not adopted.\par \par \uc2 I truly believe that as members of Congress, it is our responsibility to ensure that all of these agencies are following the constitution and the protecting the civil liberties of American citizens yet that\u8217\'20\'19s not what happened today.\par \par \uc2 enltrI voted NO on FISA 702 reauthorization today. It is a violation of the Fourth Amendment to our Constitution for the government to conduct warrantless searches of American citizens. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UoUP0hSso3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UoUP0hSso3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Harriet Hageman (@RepHageman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepHageman/status/1778854300266926470?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Colorado Republican representative \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  has released a video address following the House\u8217\'20\'19s passage of Fisa\u8217\'20\'19s reauthorization.\par \par \uc2 In her address, Boebert said:\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 86 Republicans betrayed you, the American people, today, saying the federal government does not need a warrant to start a query or illegally spy on you or tap your phones or whatever they want to do.\par \par \uc2 Boebert went on to point to the Florida Republican representative Anna Paulina Luna, who objected to the legislation\u8217\'20\'19s passage and requested a vote to reconsider the legislation. As a result, the bill will not be able to head to the Senate until the House votes on the motion.\par \par \uc2 That bill cannot be sent to the Senate until we take another vote on the warrant amendment for Fisa on Monday. That means we need you, the American people, putting pressure on these 86 Republicans who sold you out today,\u8221\'20\'1D said Boebert.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Uniparty just voted to allow the Deep State to violate your Fourth Amendment rights and spy on millions of Americans for two more years. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepLuna?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepLuna}}}\uc2  just forced an additional procedural vote to stop them.\par \par \uc2 GET. A. WARRANT. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FISA?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FISA}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JoWrYm2CQA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JoWrYm2CQA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  (@RepBoebert) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepBoebert/status/1778849804967088377?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the list of the 86 House Republicans who voted against Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Republican representative Andy Biggs\u8217\'20\'19 amendment to Fisa\u8217\'20\'19s section 702 which called for the prohibition of warrantless surveillance:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: 86 Republicans just voted against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAndyBiggsAZ?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepAndyBiggsAZ}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s amendment to require a warrant to spy on Americans under FISA causing it to fail.\par \par \uc2 Here are the names: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6mAoJfnlac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6mAoJfnlac}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Price (@greg_price11) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/greg_price11/status/1778827570240159772?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota Democratic representative \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  has criticized the House\u8217\'20\'19s passage of the reauthorization of Fisa.\par \par \uc2 In a series of tweets on Friday, Omar, who voted against the legislation, wrote:\par \par \uc2 Section 702 still allows the government to collect communications of non-Americans abroad without a warrant. This has enabled warrantless surveillance that disproportionately targets Muslim Americans, African Americans, and other minority communities.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis has enabled warrantless surveillance that disproportionately targets Muslim Americans, African Americans, and other minority communities.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  exploited Section 702 more than 200,000 times to search for Americans' data.\par \par \uc2 This raises serious 4th Amendment\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  (@Ilhan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Ilhan/status/1778846273526730831?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 She went on to add:\par \par \uc2 True reform of surveillance powers needs warrants for searches of Americans, strict rules against racial and religious profiling [and] oversight to protect civil liberties.\par \par \uc2 Anything less continues a system used to unfairly target Americans under the guise of counterterrorism.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fisa bill's House passage proves a crucial victory for Mike Johnson\par \par \uc2 The 273-147 bipartisan vote reauthorizing Fisa is a win for the embattled House speaker, Mike Johnson, and comes at a time when he faces direct challenges to his leadership.\par \par \uc2 Johnson was seen on the House floor speaking to the far-right Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , who last month filed a motion to remove Johnson from the speakership.\par \par \uc2 Greene later told reporters she and Johnson spoke about \u8220\'20\'1Call sorts of things\u8221\'20\'1D, CNN reported.\par \par \uc2 Johnson said he and Greene \u8220\'20\'1Cagree on our conservative philosophy\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 We just have different ideas sometimes on strategy. The important part of governing in a time of divided government like we have is communication with members and understanding the thought process behind it, that they have a say in it.\par \par \uc2 Johnson is also scheduled to meet with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Florida later on Friday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act, or Fisa, which gives the government expansive powers to view emails, calls and texts, has long been divisive and resulted in allegations from civil liberties groups that it violates privacy rights.\par \par \uc2 Section 702 has faced opposition before, but it became especially fraught in the past year after court documents revealed that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2023/05/19/fbi-digital-surveillance-misuse-jan6-blm/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the FBI had improperly used it}}}\uc2  almost 300,000 times \u8211\'20\'13 targeting racial justice protesters, January 6 suspects and others. That overreach emboldened resistance to the law, especially among far-right Republicans who view intelligence services like the \uc2 FBI\uc2  as their opponent.\par \par \uc2 Debate over Section 702 pitted Republicans who alleged that the law was a tool for spying on American citizens against others in the GOP who sided with intelligence officials and deemed it a necessary measure to stop foreign terrorist groups.\par \par \uc2 One proposed amendment called for requiring authorities to secure a warrant before using section 702 to view US citizens\u8217\'20\'19 communications, an idea that intelligence officials oppose as limiting their ability to act quickly.\par \par \uc2 Another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rollcall.com/2024/04/09/house-again-tees-up-reauthorization-of-powerful-spy-authority/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sticking point}}}\uc2  in the debate was whether law enforcement should be prohibited from buying information on American citizens from data broker firms, which amass and sell personal data on tens of millions of people, including phone numbers and email addresses.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservatives strike deal with Johnson to get Fisa bill passed\par \par \uc2 House conservatives who had blocked the Fisa bill earlier this week amid a push from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  allowed it to move forward on Friday after striking a deal with the speaker, Mike Johnson.\par \par \uc2 Under the agreement, the new version of the bill would be a two-year reauthorization of section 702 of Fisa, cut down from the original proposed five years.\par \par \uc2 This would mean that if Trump won the presidential election this year, the legislation would be up in time for Trump to overhaul Fisa laws next time around.\par \par \uc2 The far-right Florida Republican \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , speaking to CNN earlier today, said:\par \par \uc2 We just bought President Trump an at bat. The previous version of this bill would have kicked reauthorization beyond the Trump presidency. Now President Trump gets an at bat to fix the system that victimized him more than any other American.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two-year reauthorization of Fisa passes in House, 273-147\par \par \uc2 The House passed a two-year reauthorization of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s warrantless surveillance program that had stalled earlier this week amid Republican resistance and after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had urged GOP members to \u8220\'20\'1Ckill\u8221\'20\'1D the law.\par \par \uc2 In a 273 to 147 vote, lawmakers renewed section 702 of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (Fisa), which is set to expire on 19 April, through 2026. The bill now heads to the Senate, which is expected to give it bipartisan approval.\par \par \uc2 Section 702 allows the \uc2 US government\uc2  to collect the communications of targeted foreigners abroad by compelling service providers to produce copies of messages and internet data, or networks to intercept and turn over phone call and message data.\par \par \uc2 But the law is controversial because it allows the government to incidentally collect messages and phone data of Americans without a court order if they interacted with the foreign target, even though the law prohibits section 702 from being used by the NSA to specifically target US citizens.\par \par \uc2 The White House, intelligence chiefs and top lawmakers on the House intelligence committee have warned of potentially catastrophic effects of not reauthorizing the program.\par \par \uc2 Friday\u8217\'20\'19s vote marks the fourth attempt to pass the bill, which was blocked three times in the past five months by House Republicans bucking their party. Earlier this week, House conservatives refused to support the bill that the speaker, Mike Johnson, put forward.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican Ohio congressman Warren Davidson, has responded to the House vote to reauthorize Fisa, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Csad day\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 From Punchbowl news\u8217\'20\'19 Mica Soellner:\par \par \uc2 enltrReacting to FISA bill passing without warrant, Rep. Warren Davidson says \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s a pretty sad day\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Davidson led support on getting a warrant provision included and handed out buttons to members to express support\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mica Soellner (@MicaSoellnerDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MicaSoellnerDC/status/1778830244205547879?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fisa reauthorization passes in House\par \par \uc2 The House\u8217\'20\'19s vote to reauthorize the Foreign Intelligence Service Act has passed.\par \par \uc2 Following days of Republican infighting that has put House Republican speaker Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s leadership in a precarious position, Fisa passed with a vote of 273 yays and 147 nays in the Republican-led chamber.\par \par \uc2 The vote marks a win for Johnson who has come under fire from hard-right Republicans including Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s representative \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  over his support for Fisa. Greene, who is opposed to Fisa, has repeatedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-661541bb8f08cbf8b1ee9c5c#block-661541bb8f08cbf8b1ee9c5c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened}}}\uc2  to oust Johnson as he has \u8220\'20\'1Cnot lived up to a single one of his self-imposed tenets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 With the vote\u8217\'20\'19s passage, the reauthorization of Fisa, specifically its amendments to section 702, allows for intelligence officials to extend their warrantless surveillance on electronic communications between Americans and foreigners abroad.\par \par \uc2 Despite intelligence officials including the \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/what-is-fisa-surveillance-law-in-spotlight/story?id=109138345#:~:text=The%20federal%20law%20sets%20out,searches%2C%20pen%20registers%20and%20more."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arguing}}}\uc2  that a warrant requirement would \u8220\'20\'1Cblind ourselves to intelligence in our holdings\u8221\'20\'1D, civil rights organizations such as the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  have criticized the legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGiven our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history of abusing its surveillance authorities, and the secrecy surrounding the program, we should be concerned that section 702 is and will be used to disproportionately target disfavored groups, whether minority communities, political activists, or even journalists,\u8221\'20\'1D it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu.org/issues/national-security/warrantless-surveillance-under-section-702-fisa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 A vote to amend Fisa\u8217\'20\'19s section 702 to update the definition of foreign intelligence to help target international narcotics trafficking has passed.\par \par \uc2 The amendment, introduced by Texas Republican representative Daniel Crenshaw, passed after 268 yays and 152 nays.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 A vote to amend Fisa\u8217\'20\'19s section 702 to require the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to report to Congress on the number of queries conducted on Americans has passed.\par \par \uc2 The amendment, introduced by Texas Republican representative Chip Roy, passed after 269 yays and 153 nays.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 A vote to amend Fisa\u8217\'20\'19s section 702 to prohibit warrantless surveillance in the House has failed.\par \par \uc2 The amendment, introduced by Arizona Republican representative Andy Biggs, failed after the yays and nays votes tied at 212-212.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 House votes on Fisa reauthorization\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led House is voting on the reauthorization of section 702 of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act, controversial legislation that is also being seen as a crucial test for the House speaker, Mike Johnson.\par \par \uc2 The House\u8217\'20\'19s vote comes after rightwing Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 and Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 blocked the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s consideration of the bill on Wednesday, which seeks to expand intelligence officials\u8217\'20\'19 warrantless surveillance of communications between Americans and foreigners abroad.\par \par \uc2 With House Republicans divided over Fisa, Johnson, who supports it, is currently in a precarious position surrounding his leadership.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot allow Section 702 of Fisa to expire. It\u8217\'20\'19s too important to national security. I think most of the members understand that,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/10/us/politics/fisa-trump-johnson-house.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said.}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has thrown his support behind hard-right Republicans, writing on Truth Social on Wednesday, \u8220\'20\'1CKILL FISA.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sterilization rates rise following overturning of Roe v Wade - study\par \par \uc2 With \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  set to visit Tucson, Arizona, on Friday to explicitly blame \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the \u8220\'20\'1Carchitect\u8221\'20\'1D of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights crisis, a new study has revealed that the rate of sterilizations in the US has jumped following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturn of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Jessica Glenza reports:\par \par \uc2 Rates of people seeking permanent contraception \u8211\'20\'13 such as tubal ligation or vasectomies \u8211\'20\'13 shot up after the supreme court overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 2022, in the Dobbs decision.\par \par \uc2 Although both procedures increased, the rate of increase was double for tubal ligations, commonly known as a woman getting her \u8220\'20\'1Ctubes tied\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe major difference in patterns of these two procedures likely reflects the fact that young women are overwhelmingly responsible for preventing pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D Jacqueline Ellison, assistant professor in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sph.pitt.edu/hpm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 department of health policy and management}}}\uc2  at the Pitt School of Public Health in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, said in a release.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/sterilizations-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rate of sterilizations in US jumped after overturning of Roe v Wade, study shows}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Evan Corcoran, a longtime lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has reportedly quit the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team and could now become an important witness for the prosecution in the federal criminal case against Trump for hoarding and hiding classified documents after he left office, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/04/11/politics/evan-corcoran-trump-legal/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  last night.\par \par \uc2 The report calls it a quiet exit, in recent months, but a significant one, citing unnamed sources familiar with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal circle.\par \par \uc2 The outlet reports:\par \par \uc2 Corcoran was brought on to help Trump fend off charges in the classified documents investigation, but instead turned into a central witness after Trump allegedly misled him about the whereabouts of the documents at his Mar-a-Lago club and encouraged him to lie to the justice department and withhold those documents.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 DNC covered Biden legal bills - report\par \par \uc2 Democratic party election campaign donations were used to pay for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal bills when a special counsel was investigating the fact that he hung on to classified documents after his time as US vice -president, Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/04/12/dnc-covered-biden-legal-bills-special-counsel-probe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports today}}}\uc2 , citing two unnamed sources and the outlet\u8217\'20\'19s own analysis of finance records.\par \par \uc2 Axios immediately points out the bitter irony for Republicans, in that Democrats have been fiercely critical of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for spending his election coffers on his massive legal bills, which amounted to more than $50m last year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/02/01/trump-legal-fees-campaign-donations-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  the outlet.\par \par \uc2 Filings by the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  showed it paid more than $1.5m to lawyers or firms representing Biden during Robert Hur\u8217\'20\'19s investigation, Axios said and the Guardian US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/biden-election-dnc-campaign-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now reports here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/16/donald-trump-financial-fraud-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fined and sanctioned}}}\uc2  in a huge civil fraud case in New York involving his family business empire the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , as well as fined in his civil case with writer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/e-jean-carroll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 E Jean Carroll}}}\uc2  , whom he was found liable to have sexually abused in the past.\par \par \uc2 The former president is also facing four criminal cases, with the first one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/trump-new-york-business-records-trial-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 going to trial}}}\uc2  in an unprecedented event for an ex-US president, in New York on Monday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 With the spotlight on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to take aim at him today as the \u8220\'20\'1Carchitect\u8221\'20\'1D of the country\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights crisis, the former president is reported to have once thought Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cmust be part of Russia \u8221\'20\'1D during his presidency.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Martin Pengelly reports:\par \par \uc2 As president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cmade it very clear\u8221\'20\'1D that he thought Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cmust be part of Russia\u8221\'20\'1D, his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/12/fiona-hill-trump-putin-populism-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former adviser Fiona Hill}}}\uc2  says in a new book about US national security under threat from Russia and China.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump made it very clear that he thought, you know, that Ukraine, and certainly Crimea, must be part of Russia,\u8221\'20\'1D Hill, senior director for European and Russian affairs on the \uc2 US National Security Council\uc2  between 2017 and 2019, tells David Sanger, a \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reporter and author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/710053/new-cold-wars-by-david-e-sanger-with-mary-k-brooks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Cold Wars: China\u8217\'20\'19s Rise, Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Invasion, and America\u8217\'20\'19s Struggle to Defend the West}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe really could not get his head around the idea that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  was an independent state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This, Sanger writes, meant Trump\u8217\'20\'19s view of Ukraine was \u8220\'20\'1Cessentially identical\u8221\'20\'1D to that of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/vladimir-putin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vladimir Putin}}}\uc2 , the Russian president who would order an invasion of Ukraine in February 2022, a year after Trump left office.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/trump-russia-ukraine-book-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump thought Ukraine \u8216\'20\'18must be part of Russia\u8217\'20\'19 during presidency, book says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona congressman on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban: 'It is a dark day in Arizona'\par \par \uc2 In a new interview with Forbes Women, the Democratic Arizona US representative Greg Stanton condemned the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban : \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a dark day in Arizona. A dark day that will hurt women across our state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stanton went on to add:\par \par \uc2 The Arizona supreme court \u8230\'20\'26 [on Tuesday] issued its ruling saying this territorial law that was passed even before Arizona became a state, at a time when women could not even vote, when Native Americans were not considered fully human under law in the United States, a law from that time period is now the law of the land again in the state of Arizona. And that\u8217\'20\'19s why it\u8217\'20\'19s a dark day in our state \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 First time in America, we\u8217\'20\'19ve gone backwards on constitutional rights. We\u8217\'20\'19re going restore that right and send a message that in our country, we go forward on civil and constitutional rights, not backwards.\par \par \uc2 enltr"It is a dark day in Arizona. A dark day that will hurt women across our state." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepGregStanton?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepGregStanton}}}\uc2  joins {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ForbesWomen?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ForbesWomen}}}\uc2  's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mcgrathmag?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mcgrathmag}}}\uc2  on "Forbes Newsroom" to discuss the Arizona Supreme Court reinstating a 1864 law that bans nearly all abortions Tuesday. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/E1nSxeJzXu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/E1nSxeJzXu}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/R23OTaSTQu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/R23OTaSTQu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Forbes (@Forbes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Forbes/status/1778777888449343626?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s far-right \uc2 US Senate\uc2  candidate, has also condemned the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that she once supported.\par \par \uc2 In a video address released on Thursday evening, Lake said:\par \par \uc2 This total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  the Arizona supreme court just ruled on is out of line with where the people of this state are \u8230\'20\'26 I agree with President Trump \u8211\'20\'13 this is such a personal and private issue.\par \par \uc2 enltrAbortion is a very sensitive issue & voters deserve to know where every candidate stands.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s my position: ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EjxtaOZXF6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EjxtaOZXF6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kari Lake (@KariLake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KariLake/status/1778494973824151896?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 In 2022, Lake hailed the 1864 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law which makes no exceptions for cases of rape or incest, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2022/oct/12/katie-hobbs/az-gop-governor-hopeful-lake-called-near-total-abo/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m incredibly thrilled that we are going to have a great law that\u8217\'20\'19s already on the books \u8230\'20\'26 I believe it\u8217\'20\'19s ARS 13-3603, so it will prohibit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Arizona except to save the life of a mother. And I think we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be paving the way and setting course for other states to follow.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/11/kari-lake-arizona-abortion-reversal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kari Lake denounces Arizona \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban that she once supported}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of her campaign trip to Tuscon, Arizona, on Friday, where she is expected to blame \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the country\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights crisis, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  tweeted:\par \par \uc2 Women across our country are suffering at the hands of extremists who say they\u8217\'20\'19re motivated by the well-being of women and children but ignore the crisis of maternal mortality.\par \par \uc2 enltrWomen across our country are suffering at the hands of extremists who say they\u8217\'20\'19re motivated by the well-being of women and children but ignore the crisis of maternal mortality. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xU4qM81aE3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xU4qM81aE3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1778576352217592169?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  expected to blame Trump for US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights crisis on Arizona visit\par \par \uc2 Good morning,\par \par \uc2 The vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , is set to travel to Tucson, Arizona, for a campaign event where she is expected to explicitly blame \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the \u8220\'20\'1Carchitect\u8221\'20\'1D of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights crisis in the US.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s trip to Arizona comes after the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/arizona-republicans-block-repeal-state-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  on Wednesday that a 1864 law with no exceptions for rape or incest can go into effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the architect of this healthcare crisis. And that\u8217\'20\'19s not a fact he hides. In fact, he brags about it,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris is expected to say, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/playbook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe all must understand who is to blame. It is the former president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . It is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who, during his campaign in 2016, said women should be punished for seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/04/10/abortion-arizona-law-ban-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 instructing}}}\uc2  her team to designate the trip as a campaign event, one senior Harris aide told Politico that she is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot subject to the Hatch Act and she can say whatever the heck she wants \u8230\'20\'26 we could really be unencumbered in how we tell the story.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in 2022, Harris has repeatedly gone after anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  conservatives as she and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  cement \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a key campaign issue in this year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election campaign.\par \par \uc2 Here are other developments in US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House Republican speaker, Mike Johnson, will meet with Trump in Mar-a-Lago, where they plan to deliver remarks on \u8220\'20\'1Celection integrity\u8221\'20\'1D, NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/speaker-mike-johnson-meet-donald-trump-threats-job-rcna147424"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House is set to vote on the reauthorization of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act, the controversial legislation that failed two days ago in the Republican-led chamber.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is set to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-civil-rights-black-america-sharpton-conference-1142ce622a42c5b6cf96aeb301d53a71"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deliver}}}\uc2  a virtual keynote address at Rev \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual racial justice conference in New York.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240412ek4c001s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
