\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Rate of sterilizations in US jumped after overturning of Roe v Wade, study shows\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 473 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par 17:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Number of people seeking permanent contraception increased after 2022 decision, in particular among women, research reveals\par \par \uc2 Rates of people seeking permanent contraception \u8211\'20\'13 such as tubal ligation or vasectomies \u8211\'20\'13 shot up after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022, in the Dobbs decision.\par \par \uc2 Although both procedures increased, the rate of increase was double for tubal ligations, commonly known as a woman getting her \u8220\'20\'1Ctubes tied\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe major difference in patterns of these two procedures likely reflects the fact that young women are overwhelmingly responsible for preventing pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D Jacqueline Ellison, assistant professor in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sph.pitt.edu/hpm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 department of health policy and management}}}\uc2  at the Pitt School of Public Health in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, said in a release.\par \par \uc2 People capable of getting pregnant \u8220\'20\'1Cdisproportionately experience the health, social and economic consequences of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans\u8221\'20\'1D, she said.\par \par \uc2 Researchers are only beginning to grapple with the health effects of the Dobbs decision, which has allowed 21 US states to severely restrict or almost entirely ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/25/abortion-after-rape-laws-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Another research letter}}}\uc2  in Jama Internal Medicine found that more than 65,000 US rape victims could not get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their own state because of bans. Some experts also expect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans to increase the rates of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/03/28/health/trisomy-18-abortion.html#:~:text=And%20the%20number%20of%20babies,prohibit%20it%20after%2012%20weeks."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 babies born with severe genetic abnormalities}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10728320/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worsen maternal mortality rates}}}\uc2 , particularly among Black women and especially in many deep south states that have among the worst rates in the nation.\par \par \uc2 The new research letter was published in the journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jama-health-forum/fullarticle/2817438"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jama Health Forum}}}\uc2 . Ellison and her co-authors used the TriNetX platform, which gathers data largely from major academic medical centers, to perform an analysis of de-identified patient records that contained the procedure codes for tubal ligations and vasectomies.\par \par \uc2 Researchers studied the period leading up to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, from 2019 to 2022, and then afterward from 2022 to 2023. They focused specifically on people aged 18-30 \u8211\'20\'13 a group in their prime reproductive years. This group is also more likely to regret undergoing sterilization compared with people older than 30.\par \par \uc2 Researchers found an increase of 58 tubal ligations or five procedures a month after Dobbs. They also found an increase of about 27 vasectomies after Dobbs, but no significant increase per month.\par \par \uc2 The study was unable to look at specific regions of the country, because TriNetX does not collect identifying information about facilities. Similarly, researchers were unable to explore the experiences of racial minorities, low-income and disabled people through the data. Those groups are known to suffer worse health outcomes overall, and are likely to be more susceptible to the coercion of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Researchers said the higher rate among women and people capable of getting pregnant may \u8220\'20\'1Creflect the disproportionate health, social and economic consequences of compulsory pregnancy\u8221\'20\'1D on them.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240412ek4c002ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
