\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Kari Lake denounces Arizona  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban that she once supported\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano in Los Angeles \par \uc2 708 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par 17:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Far-right \uc2 US Senate\uc2  candidate joins Republicans who have decried state supreme court ruling but who blocked appeal effort\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, the far-right \uc2 US Senate\uc2  candidate and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ally, denounced Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on Thursday, arguing that the strict legislation she previously praised does not have the support of the state\u8217\'20\'19s residents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  the Arizona supreme court just ruled on is out of line with where the people of this state are,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a video on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CI agree with President Trump \u8211\'20\'13 this is such a personal and private issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a sudden and apparently strategic reversal, Lake and other Republicans in the state have come out against a ruling from the court on Tuesday declaring that a civil war-era law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state is now enforceable. The law, which predates Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s statehood, does not provide exceptions for rape or incest and abortions are permitted only if the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life is at risk.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said the court went too far: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19ll be straightened out, and as you know, it\u8217\'20\'19s all about states\u8217\'20\'19 rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans in the statehouse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/arizona-republicans-block-repeal-state-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked an effort}}}\uc2  by Democrats on Wednesday to repeal the ban, highlighting the disunity within the party over how to handle an issue that will probably define the 2024 race.\par \par \uc2 Lake, an unsuccessful candidate for governor in the state and election denier, expressed her support for the law in 2022 after the supreme court voted to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m incredibly thrilled that we are going to have a great law that\u8217\'20\'19s already on the books,\u8221\'20\'1D she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2022/oct/12/katie-hobbs/az-gop-governor-hopeful-lake-called-near-total-abo/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a June 2022 radio interview. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe it\u8217\'20\'19s ARS 13-3603, so it will prohibit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Arizona except to save the life of a mother. And I think we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be paving the way and setting course for other states to follow.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An adviser to Lake on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CarolineWren/status/1777836529429221835"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  she was referring to a different law, despite the fact that she cited the number of the 1864 code.\par \par \uc2 While Republicans celebrated the decision to overturn Roe, the issue has become a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/trump-arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political nightmare}}}\uc2  for the party. Political strategists have said that the near-total ban would draw moderate voters to Democrats and mobilize young voters and voters of color.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was an earthquake of epic proportions in Arizona politics,\u8221\'20\'1D Barrett Marson, a Phoenix-based Republican strategist, said this week. \u8220\'20\'1CAnytime Republicans are talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they\u8217\'20\'19re losing. Now, I think the only issue is going to be \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2 , the Republican former governor who expanded the state supreme court and appointed the four conservative justices who ruled the ban is enforceable, has said the court went too far. He said the ruling was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot the outcome I would have preferred\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/15/gallup-survey-abortion-support-united-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Support}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US remains strong. A survey last year found that 69% of Americans, a record high, believed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should generally be legal in the first three months of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Lake has sought to distance herself from her past comments on Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s law and urged lawmakers to \u8220\'20\'1Ccome up with an immediate commonsense solution that Arizonans can support\u8221\'20\'1D. Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/04/11/kari-lake-arizona-abortion-ban-00151835"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico}}}\uc2  reported on Thursday that Lake was personally lobbying lawmakers to repeal the law.\par \par \uc2 In a five-minute video released on Thursday in which she lavished praise on Trump and expressed her agreement with his position no less than three times, Lake said that while she personally opposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she supported exceptions for rape and incest. \u8220\'20\'1CA full ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not where the people are,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She reiterated her support for the decision to overturn Roe, and insisted that if elected to the Senate she would oppose federal funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as a federal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to Washington DC to impose federal restrictions on something that\u8217\'20\'19s already been sent back to the states,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to Washington DC to secure our borders, strengthen our families and help President Trump make America great again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240412ek4c0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
