\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban is a political nightmare for Republicans in the 2024 election\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 868 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par 01:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republicans are trying to slow down the car whose brakes they cut \u8211\'20\'13 and to convince voters that, if it crashes, they had nothing to do with it\par \par \uc2 When the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 2022, Republicans across the country cheered. Freed from Roe\u8217\'20\'19s regulations, GOP lawmakers promptly blanketed the US south and midwest in near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 But today, after a string of electoral losses, stories of women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/16/abortion-ban-lawsuits-pregnancy-complication-emergency-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being denied abortions}}}\uc2  and polls that confirm \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans remain wildly unpopular, the political calculus has changed. Republicans are now trying to slow down the car whose brakes they cut \u8211\'20\'13 and to convince voters that, if the car crashes, they had nothing to do with it anyway.\par \par \uc2 Nowhere encapsulates the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s backpedal on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  better than Arizona, whose state supreme court on Tuesday ruled to let an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1864 near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  go into effect. That ban, which outlaws \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all cases except to save the life of a woman, was passed before Arizona became a state, before the end of the civil war and before women gained the right to vote.\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, a Republican running to represent Arizona in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  and a diehard ally of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , once called that ban \u8220\'20\'1Ca great law\u8221\'20\'1D. But on Tuesday, the inflammatory politician {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/arizona-republicans-against-state-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became one of several}}}\uc2  GOP officials to denounce the ruling, urging the state legislature to \u8220\'20\'1Ccome up with an immediate commonsense solution that Arizonans can support\u8221\'20\'1D. On Wednesday, Trump also indicated that he thought Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban \u8211\'20\'13 whose revival was enabled by a \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling he has repeatedly taken credit for \u8211\'20\'13 had gone too far. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19ll be straightened out and, as you know, it\u8217\'20\'19s all about states\u8217\'20\'19 rights,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-abortion-arizona-law-florida-ban-7cdd6d2e3c320a89ec7a7c037824e7cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republican state lawmakers denounced the decision, but halted an effort by Democrats on Wednesday to repeal the law, instead voting to move to a recess to prevent a vote on the matter.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains banned past 15 weeks in Arizona, since the 1864 ban is being held up by legal delays. But Arizona is expected to be a key battleground state in the 2024 elections, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters have gathered more than half a million signatures in support of a ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution. Democrats are hoping that measure will boost turnout and bring their candidates \u8211\'20\'13 including \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to victory.\par \par \uc2 In other words, this ban threatens to become a political nightmare for Republicans come November.\par \par \uc2 Lake and Trump are caught in the quandary that is now facing Republicans in Arizona and beyond its borders. For 50 years, the GOP became increasingly wedded to the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, passing restrictions that cut off access to the procedure and littering the courts with lawsuits to overturn Roe. These restrictions won them votes from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates, as well as cash from influential advocacy groups. But because Roe stopped many of these restrictions from taking effect, it shielded Republicans from reckoning with the real-world consequences of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies \u8211\'20\'13 or with the outrage of voters. Since Roe was overturned, and those real-world consequences have come into focus, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights-related ballot measures have succeeded in several Republican strongholds, including Kansas and Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 Lake didn\u8217\'20\'19t say what that \u8220\'20\'1Ccommonsense solution\u8221\'20\'1D might be, but other Republicans have tried to take a stab at it. Juan Ciscomani, who represents Arizona in the US House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepCiscomani/status/1777757519504380389/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called the decision}}}\uc2  no less than \u8220\'20\'1Ca disaster\u8221\'20\'1D and claimed he was a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong supporter of empowering women to make their own healthcare choices\u8221\'20\'1D. He also, in the same statement, said the 15-week ban \u8220\'20\'1Cprotected the rights of women and new life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This seems to be the party line that many Arizona Republicans are now congealing around: they will support a 15-week ban, which the state legislature first passed in 2022, but not a near-total ban. This, too, is a gamble. Last year, when Virginia Republicans tried to take control of the state legislature by proposing to \u8220\'20\'1Ccompromise\u8221\'20\'1D and ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 15 weeks of pregnancy, they fell short.\par \par \uc2 Yet the post-Roe electoral firepower of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has never been tested in a presidential election. Biden has spent months trying to blame \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans on Trump, since Trump appointed three of the justices who overturned Roe. Trump, meanwhile, alternates between congratulating himself for overturning Roe, both rebuking and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/16/trump-16-week-abortion-ban-exceptions-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flirting with the idea}}}\uc2  of a national ban, and claiming, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he did earlier this week}}}\uc2 , that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access should now be left up to the states.\par \par \uc2 For Republicans, the only option may be to take a cue from their party\u8217\'20\'19s leader and rewrite their own history. When asked about Lake\u8217\'20\'19s previous support for the 1864 ban, her campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/10/us/politics/kari-lake-abortion-arizona.html?unlocked_article_code=1.jU0.fTe_.6J2Z9I2gKPU0&smid=url-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested to the New York Times}}}\uc2  that Lake was referring to a different law.\par \par \uc2 But in the comments praising it, Lake even referred to the 1864 ban by its statute number, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azleg.gov/ars/13/03603.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13-3603}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m incredibly thrilled that we are going to have a great law that\u8217\'20\'19s already on the books,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240410ek4a00339\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
