\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump campaign calls for more presidential debates \u8216\'20\'18much earlier\u8217\'20\'19 in election race \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong \par \uc2 5,806 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par 20:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read more of our US politics coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign wrote to the commission on presidential debates asking for this year\u8217\'20\'19s general election debates between him and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to take place \u8220\'20\'1Cmuch earlier\u8221\'20\'1D and calling for more to be added to the schedule.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign letter comes after five of the major TV news networks banded together to prepare a letter urging Biden and Trump to participate in televised debates ahead the November general election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign launched a seven-figure ad buy in Arizona on Thursday focusing on reproductive rights, just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/trump-arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two days after}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court upheld a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban dating to 1864.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, called on Americans to overcome their \u8220\'20\'1Cself-doubt\u8221\'20\'1D as he offered a paean to US global leadership before a bitterly divided Congress.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the far-right congresswoman of Georgia who has filed a motion to remove Mike Johnson, said the House speaker offered her a spot on a proposed \u8220\'20\'1Ckitchen cabinet\u8221\'20\'1D of advisers after a meeting at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 SenatorTim Kaine, a former vice-presidential nominee and leading foreign policy voice in the Democratic party, has said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  now understands that \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cplayed\u8221\'20\'1D him during the early months of the war in Gaza but \u8220\'20\'1Cthat ain\u8217\'20\'19t going to happen any more\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The joint press conference between Mike Johnson and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at Mar-a-Lago tomorrow will come just two days after the former president called on Republicans to kill legislation the speaker put forward to extend a controversial surveillance law. Trump had urged House GOP members to reject a reauthorization of the law, Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (Fisa), ahead of the key procedural vote on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Johnson is dashing to Florida to meet with Trump, where the pair are expected to appear tomorrow at an event at the former president\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate for a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor announcement on election integrity\u8221\'20\'1D. Friday\u8217\'20\'19s appearance will mark their first public event together since Johnson was elected to the speakership last fall.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  director \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  is currently speaking before the House appropriations committee, where he is expected to warn lawmakers of his concerns over potential bad actors carrying out attacks on US soil.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur most immediate concern has been that individuals or small groups will draw twisted inspiration from the events in the Middle East to carry out attacks here at home,\u8221\'20\'1D a transcript of Wray\u8217\'20\'19s opening statement obtained by ABC News reads.\par \par \uc2 But now increasingly concerning is the potential for a coordinated attack here in the homeland, akin to the ISIS-K attack we saw at the Russia Concert Hall a couple weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 Wray said he was \u8220\'20\'1Chard pressed to think of a time where so many threats to our public safety and national security were so elevated all at once,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the transcript.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 While he was careful not to touch on US domestic politics, the address by Japanese prime minister, \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , today comes amid a deadlock in Congress on approving billions of dollars in additional military aid to Ukraine, due to pressure from hard-right Republicans aligned with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kishida warned that the biggest challenge the world faces comes from China:\par \par \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s current external stance and military actions present an unprecedented and the greatest strategic challenge, not only to the peace and security of Japan but to the peace and stability of the international community at large.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUkraine of today may be East Asia of tomorrow,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 enltrKishida decries Russian war against Ukraine as \u8220\'20\'1Cunprovoked, unjust, and brutal.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CAs I often say, Ukraine of today may be East Asia of tomorrow,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. That gets a standing ovation from most (\uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  among the few in the chamber who remain seated).\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Morgan Chalfant (@mchalfant16) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mchalfant16/status/1778444374755446835?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , on Thursday called on Americans to overcome their \u8220\'20\'1Cself-doubt\u8221\'20\'1D as he offered a paean to US global leadership before a bitterly divided Congress.\par \par \uc2 Warning of risks from the rise of China, Kishida said that Japan \u8211\'20\'13 stripped of its right to a military after the second world war \u8211\'20\'13 was determined to do more to share responsibility with its ally the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we meet here today, I detect an undercurrent of self-doubt among some Americans about what your role in the world should be,\u8221\'20\'1D Kishida told a joint session of the House of Representatives and Senate during a state visit to Washington.\par \par \uc2 The international order that the US worked for generations to build is facing new challenges, challenges from those with values and principles very different from ours.\par \par \uc2 Kishida said he understood \u8220\'20\'1Cthe exhaustion of being the country that has upheld the international order almost single-handedly\u8221\'20\'1D but added:\par \par \uc2 The leadership of the United States is indispensable. Without US support, how long before the hopes of Ukraine would collapse under the onslaught from Moscow? Without the presence of the United States, how long before the Indo-Pacific would face even harsher realities?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 A majority of voters in Florida say they believe a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is too strict, but only 42% said they will vote in favor of a ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections into the state constitution, according to a new poll.\par \par \uc2 The study by Emerson College Polling found that 57% of respondents said the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/02/florida-abortion-ban-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  that will become state law}}}\uc2  next month is \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo strict\u8221\'20\'1D, compared with 15% who said it is not strict enough.\par \par \uc2 Spencer Kimball, executive director of Emerson College Polling, said:\par \par \uc2 Fifty-six percent of Democrats and 44% of independents plan to vote in favor of a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability. Republicans are more split: 36% plan to vote no, 30% yes, and 34% are unsure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin Republicans have hit the state election commission with complaints alleging that officials in the state\u8217\'20\'19s two largest cities illegally rejected Republican applicants for poll worker positions for the primary election.\par \par \uc2 The complaints, filed by the Milwaukee county Republican party and Dane county Republican party, claim officials in Milwaukee and Madison violated state law by not contacting eligible Republicans nominated by their party to work the polls. The move furthers the GOP strategy of questioning election processes in key battleground states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the kind of misconduct that drives down faith in elections,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) chairman, Michael Whatley, said in a statement on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Republican Party is filing these complaints to compel election officials to follow the law and guarantee bipartisan access to important election administration positions in the Badger state.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/11/wisconsin-republican-primary-poll-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin Republicans allege anti-GOP bias in latest election challenge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Burt Jones, Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s state senator turned lieutenant governor, will be investigated for his role as a fake elector for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Pete Skandalakis, director of the prosecuting attorneys\u8217\'20\'19 council of Georgia, said he will look into whether Jones should face criminal charges over efforts to overturn the 2020 presidential election in the state.\par \par \uc2 Jones was one of 16 state Republicans who signed a certificate stating that Trump had won Georgia and declaring themselves the state\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cduly elected and qualified\u8221\'20\'1D electors even though \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had been declared the winner in the state.\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , was barred from prosecuting Jones in 2022 as part of her election interference case against Trump and others, after she hosted a campaign fundraiser for his Democratic opponent in the lieutenant governor\u8217\'20\'19s race.\par \par \uc2 Skandalakis announced on Thursday that he would appoint himself to spearhead a potential case against Jones, after facing criticism for not moving more quickly to find a prosecutor to replace Willis.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign letter comes after five of the major TV news networks banded together to prepare a letter urging \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to participate in televised debates ahead the November general election.\par \par \uc2 The letter, endorsed by ABC, \uc2 CBS\uc2 , CNN, NBC and Fox News, urged the presumptive presidential nominees \u8220\'20\'1Cto publicly commit to participating in general election debates before November\u8217\'20\'19s election\u8221\'20\'1D, according to CNN.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a statement responding to the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s letter asking for more presidential debates, Republican national committee Michael Whatley and co-chair \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 Election calendars have become longer than ever before \u8211\'20\'13 and scheduling debates after millions of Americans have already cast their ballots does a grave disservice to voters who want to hear solutions to the economic, border, and crime crises created by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign calls for more presidential debates\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign wrote to the commission on presidential debates asking for this year\u8217\'20\'19s general election debates between him and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to take place \u8220\'20\'1Cmuch earlier\u8221\'20\'1D and calling for more to be added to the schedule.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cdn.nucleusfiles.com/63/63f29f01-e38e-4157-8d1d-6b73a08ed3f7/final-debate-commission-letter-4-11-24.pdf?utm_medium=email&utm_source=ncl_amplify&utm_campaign=240411-icymi_trump_campaign_demands_biden_debate_him_much_earlier_and_more_often&utm_content=ncl-GSehQjdam9&_nlid=GSehQjdam9&_nhids=EGo1txbeb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  to the commission, Trump co-campaign managers Susie Wiles and Chris LaCivita wrote:\par \par \uc2 The Commission must move up the timetable of its proposed 2024 debates to ensure more Americans have a full chance to see the candidates before they start voting, and we would argue for adding more debates in addition to those on the currently proposed schedule.\par \par \uc2 The first presidential debate is scheduled to take place on 16 September in San Marcos, Texas. There are three presidential debates and one vice presidential debate scheduled.\par \par \uc2 Wiles and LaCivita noted that by the date of the first proposed debate, more than a million Americans are likely to have already voted, and three million may have cast their ballot by 1 October, when the second proposed debate is scheduled. They added:\par \par \uc2 We have already indicated President Trump is willing to debate anytime, anyplace, and anywhere \u8211\'20\'13 and the time to start these debates is now.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who did not participate in any of the Republican primary debates, made similar requests during the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  sent out a scripted robocall on behalf of its new co-chair \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 , falsely claiming Democrats were guilty of \u8220\'20\'1Cmassive fraud\u8221\'20\'1D in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all know the problems,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://soundcloud.com/user-735086019/rnc-call-spreads-false-claims-about-massive-fraud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the RNC call said}}}\uc2 , according to CNN, which also said the call was sent 145,000 times in the first week of April.\par \par \uc2 No photo IDs, unsecured ballot drop boxes, mass mailing of ballots and voter rolls chock full of deceased people and non-citizens are just a few examples of the massive fraud that took place. If Democrats have their way, your vote could be canceled out by someone who isn\u8217\'20\'19t even an American citizen.\par \par \uc2 Marc Elias, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commoncause.org/clip/time-marc-elias-fought-trumps-2020-election-lawsuits-can-he-win-the-battle-over-voting-rights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic lawyer}}}\uc2  who repeatedly defeated Trump in court after the 2020 election, said the \uc2 RNC\uc2  robocall {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marceelias/status/1778412061459906921"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showed}}}\uc2  the Republican party to be \u8220\'20\'1Cmore committed to the big lie than ever\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who installed his daughter-in-law at the \uc2 RNC\uc2  last month, lost the 2020 election conclusively to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and was told by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/01/trump-lawyer-joe-digenova-election-security-chief-chris-krebs-shot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 close}}}\uc2  aides {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/01/william-barr-no-evidence-voter-fraud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including}}}\uc2 William Barr\uc2 , his attorney general, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/01/trump-lawyer-joe-digenova-election-security-chief-chris-krebs-shot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris Krebs}}}\uc2 , his head of cybersecurity, that there was no widespread fraud.\par \par \uc2 Regardless, Trump pursued his fraud lie through the courts \u8211\'20\'13 losing every case \u8211\'20\'13 and ultimately by inciting the deadly attack on Congress on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/11/lara-trump-rnc-election-robocalls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lara Trump\u8217\'20\'19s RNC robocall falsely claims \u8216\'20\'18massive fraud\u8217\'20\'19 in 2020 election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The daily media briefing in the west wing at the White House is overdue, so we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you highlights when it happens.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary Karine-Jean-Pierre was scheduled to begin the briefing at 1.30pm ET, then it was put back to 1.45pm, but no sign yet.\par \par \uc2 These events often run late and it\u8217\'20\'19s nothing we\u8217\'20\'19re not used to, it often partly depends on whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is running on or behind schedule (usually behind).\par \par \uc2 No-one else is listed as attending the briefing today. Jean-Pierre is sometimes accompanied, increasingly of late with so much international news involving the US, especially in Gaza, by national security adviser Jake Sullivan or national security spokesman John Kirby.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Amid the Biden-Harris campaign ad buy in Arizona focusing on reproductive rights, just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/trump-arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two days after}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court upheld a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban dating to 1864, US vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will visit the state tomorrow, for an official campaign event {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/arizona/2024/04/09/kamala-harris-to-visit-arizona-for-abortion-campaign-event/73261920007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 focused on}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Creproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris had already planned to be in Arizona but now will make the visit to Tucson a key campaign trail stop as she leads the administration and the election campaign\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to bolster reproductive choice.\par \par \uc2 Also she\u8217\'20\'19s marking Black Maternal Health Week.\par \par \uc2 And she\u8217\'20\'19s been posting.\par \par \uc2 enltrBlack women are 3x times as likely to die because of pregnancy-related complications than their white counterparts.\par \par \uc2 As we begin Black Maternal Health Week, we must ensure Black women get the care they deserve throughout pregnancy, childbirth, and postpartum. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RC0stq3Hag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/RC0stq3Hag}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1778413969050320929?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And re-posted this from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrVice President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  has been a leader on the issue of maternal mortality for years.\par \par \uc2 She has led the charge to improve maternal health outcomes and continues to elevate the issue so all mothers can access the care they need.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m proud to have her on my team. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ntYAYeBOiG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ntYAYeBOiG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1778474368567333092?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively day so far of political jostling between Democratic and Republican leaders and within the Republican top echelons, on Capitol Hill and on the presidential election campaign trail. There\u8217\'20\'19s more to come and we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you the news as it happens.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign launched a seven-figure ad buy in Arizona on Thursday focusing on reproductive rights, just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/trump-arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two days after}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court upheld a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban dating to 1864.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the far-right congresswoman of Georgia who has filed a motion to remove Mike Johnson, said the House speaker offered her a spot on a proposed \u8220\'20\'1Ckitchen cabinet\u8221\'20\'1D of advisers after a meeting at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 SenatorTim Kaine, a former vice-presidential nominee and leading foreign policy voice in the Democratic party, has said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  now understands that \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cplayed\u8221\'20\'1D him during the early months of the war in Gaza but \u8220\'20\'1Cthat ain\u8217\'20\'19t going to happen any more\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The joint press conference betweenMike Johnson and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at Mar-a-Lago tomorrow will come just two days after the former president called on Republicans to kill legislation the speaker put forward to extend a controversial surveillance law. Trump had urged House GOP members to reject a reauthorization of the law, Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (Fisa), ahead of the key procedural vote on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speakerMike Johnson is dashing to Florida to meet with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , where the pair are expected to appear tomorrow at an event at the former president\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate for a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor announcement on election integrity\u8221\'20\'1D. Friday\u8217\'20\'19s appearance will mark their first public event together since Johnson was elected to the speakership last fall.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is due to brief the media at 1.30pm ET. At 3.15pm \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet with Philippine president \uc2 Ferdinand R Marcos Jr\uc2  and at 4.15pm Biden will hold a trilateral meeting with Marcos and Japanese prime minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , which US vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will attend.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jon Stone, a New Hampshire Republican state representative and county chair for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign, who once presented Trump with an AR-15 assault rifle, lost his job as a police officer in 2006 after a suspension over a relationship with a teenage girl prompted him to threaten to kill colleagues and rape the police chief\u8217\'20\'19s wife and children.\par \par \uc2 The extraordinary story was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://indepthnh.org/2024/04/05/documents-rep-jon-stone-threatened-mass-shooting-and-rape-after-investigation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported}}}\uc2  by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://indepthnh.org/about/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 InDepthNH.org}}}\uc2  , a \u8220\'20\'1Cnonprofit watchdog news website published by the New Hampshire Center for Public Interest Journalism \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Its story, by Damien Fisher, begins:\par \par \uc2 Republican representative Jon Stone\u8217\'20\'19s New Hampshire law enforcement career ended when he threatened to kill fellow police officers in a shooting spree, and murder his chief after raping the chief\u8217\'20\'19s wife and children, all while he was already under scrutiny for his inappropriate relationship with a teen girl, according to the internal investigation reports finally released this week.\par \par \uc2 Stone, a twice-elected Republican state representative for Claremont, has been fighting to keep those reports secret for years. Last month, the New Hampshire supreme court ruled that Stone could not block their release in response to this reporter\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 right-to-know request, ending years of legal challenges.\par \par \uc2 Stone and his attorney did not comment.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, HuffPost {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/trump-fired-police-officer-new-hampshire_n_6616de8ce4b0999df35397ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed to}}}\uc2  Stone\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 presentation to Trump of an assault rifle engraved with the New Hampshire state motto, \u8220\'20\'1CLive free or die\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1C1-4-5\u8221\'20\'1D, indicating Trump was his No 1 choice to be the 45th president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was very nice to meet Mr Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D Stone, a co-owner of Black Op Arms, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wmur.com/article/claremont-business-gives-custom-made-rifle-to-trump/5207421"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told WMUR-9}}}\uc2 , an ABC News affiliate.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Stepanek, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 New Hampshire campaign chair, told HuffPost: \u8220\'20\'1CI just found out about it this morning. [Stone has] been a Trump supporter for a long time, and he\u8217\'20\'19s been a state representative, and he had, as far as we were concerned, what looked like a great background.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe haven\u8217\'20\'19t made any decisions at this point,\u8221\'20\'1D Stepanek said, adding that he expected aides close to Trump at his Florida home would decide what to do. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it will be handled by Mar-a-Lago, in consultation with me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chris LaCivita and Susie Wiles, co-managers of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, did not comment to HuffPost.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has contacted Steven Cheung, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign spokesperson, for comment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona state senator Eva Burch, a Democrat, shared her recent experience of getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as she condemned the state supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling earlier this week that a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could be enforced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomebody took care of me,\u8221\'20\'1D Burch, who earned national attention last month after announcing she would get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because her pregnancy is no longer viable, said today.\par \par \uc2 Now we\u8217\'20\'19re talking about whether or not we should put that doctor in jail. This is outrageous that we would even dignify the consideration of this type of ban.\par \par \uc2 enltrArizona State Sen. Eva Burch (D): "A couple weeks ago, I had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 a safe, legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  here in Arizona for a pregnancy that I very much wanted."\par \par \uc2 "Somebody took care of me," she continues. "And now we're talking about whether or not we should put that doctor in jail." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/znACed4wB2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/znACed4wB2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1778435617220612410?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona \u8217\'20\'19s state Republican leadership halted an effort by Democrats on Wednesday to repeal an 1864 law banning almost all abortions, which the state supreme court this week ruled could go into effect.\par \par \uc2 Democrats and one Republican lawmaker sought to repeal the law, but GOP leaders, who command the majority, cut it off twice and quickly adjourned for the week. Outraged Democrats erupted in finger-waving chants of \u8220\'20\'1CShame! Shame!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republican state Rep Teresa Martinez, of Casa Grande, said there was no reason to rush the debate. She accused Democrats of \u8220\'20\'1Cscreaming at us and engaging in extremist and insurrectionist behaviour on the House floor\u8221\'20\'1D. The GOP-led senate briefly convened without debate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democratic legislators seized on national interest in the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got the eyes of the world watching Arizona right now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Democratic state Rep Stephanie Stahl Hamilton, of Tucson.\par \par \uc2 We know that the supreme court decision yesterday is extreme. And we know that should the 1864 ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain a law in Arizona, people will die.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign launches seven-figure ad buy on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Arizona\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign launched a seven-figure ad buy in Arizona on Thursday focusing on reproductive rights, just two days after the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court upheld a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban dating to 1864.\par \par \uc2 The ad buy focuses on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s latest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance, in which he said laws should be left to individual states, many of which have enacted new restrictions since he appointed supreme court justices who were instrumental in the 2022 Dobbs decision that overturned Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , millions of women lost the fundamental freedom to control their own bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden narrates in the 30-second ad.\par \par \uc2 And now, women\u8217\'20\'19s lives are in danger because of that. The question is, if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  gets back in power, what freedom will you lose next?\par \par \uc2 The ad, dubbed \u8220\'20\'1CPower Back\u8221\'20\'1D, will run this month on targeted television programs and target key young, female and Latino voters both on television and online, according to the campaign.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, campaign manager Julie Chavez Rodriguez said:\par \par \uc2 This week, women across the state of Arizona are watching in horror as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from 1864 with no exceptions for rape, incest, or the health of a woman will soon become the law of the land for Arizonans. This nightmare is only possible because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  said she had recently spoken to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  but did not say how the former president felt about her threats to force a vote to remove Mike Johnson as House speaker.\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t speak for the president,\u8221\'20\'1D Greene said after her meeting with Johnson on Wednesday, CNN reported.\par \par \uc2 Asked about Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming appearance with Trump at his Mar-a-Lago club, Greene said:\par \par \uc2 Things like that don\u8217\'20\'19t bother me.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 MTG says she does not support Johnson despite 'kitchen cabinet' adviser offer\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the far-right congresswoman of Georgia who has filed a motion to remove Mike Johnson, said the House speaker offered her a spot on a proposed \u8220\'20\'1Ckitchen cabinet\u8221\'20\'1D of advisers after a meeting at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Johnson met with Greene for nearly an hour on Wednesday to discuss their disagreements, after which she described the exchange as \u8220\'20\'1Cdirect and passionate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Johnson \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscussed having a kitchen cabinet group that would be a group of advisers for him, asked me if I was interested,\u8221\'20\'1D she told reporters on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 She said she would \u8220\'20\'1Cwait and see\u8221\'20\'1D about Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s offer, but that she was more interested in how he handles several issues before Congress, particularly aid for Ukraine and the Fisa vote. She added:\par \par \uc2 I explained to him, this isn\u8217\'20\'19t personal. But he has not done the job that we elected him to do.\par \par \uc2 She added:\par \par \uc2 He does not have my support and I\u8217\'20\'19m watching what happens with Fisa and Ukraine. Those are the two things that we\u8217\'20\'19ll all be watching.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic senator for Virginia, Tim Kaine, is best known nationally as Hillary Clinton \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/jul/22/tim-kaine-vice-president-running-mate-hillary-clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  running mate}}}\uc2  in the 2016 presidential election, a race they lost to Republicans \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 . The Biden ally is a member of the Senate foreign relations and armed services committees.\par \par \uc2 Kaine has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kaine.senate.gov/press-releases/kaine-statement-on-hamas-acts-of-terror-against-israeli-civilians"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly reiterated his backing}}}\uc2  for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  following the terrorist attack six months ago that killed 1,200 people, mostly civilians, and took about 250 people hostage. But he has joined other Democrats in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kaine.senate.gov/press-releases/kaine-issues-statement-on-latest-developments-in-israel-hamas-conflict#:~:text=%E2%80%9CLike%20so%20many%20Virginians%2C%20I,Americans%E2%80%94have%20not%20been%20released."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressing growing consternation}}}\uc2  over a hardline military response that has killed more than 33,000 Palestinians, according to the Gaza health ministry, and spurred a looming famine.\par \par \uc2 In a 30-minute phone call last week, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  issued a stark warning to \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  that future American support for the war depends on the swift implementation of new steps to protect civilians and aid workers. Netanyahu subsequently approved measures to increase the flow of humanitarian aid into Gaza, including the reopening of a key crossing destroyed in the 7 October attack. Kaine noted:\par \par \uc2 They turned water back on in northern Gaza. They allow bakeries to start to operate again in Palestine. They announced they\u8217\'20\'19re pulling troops back in southern Gaza, and there\u8217\'20\'19s probably more that they\u8217\'20\'19re going to do, because I think he finally heard in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s voice, \u8216\'20\'18Yeah, I\u8217\'20\'19m a friend but you played me and I know you played me; that ain\u8217\'20\'19t going to happen any more.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 I feel strongly that \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  has made Israel less safe in dramatic ways and is now hurting the US-Israel relationship, which has been fairly steady and easy to be counted upon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden knows Netanyahu \u8216\'20\'18played\u8217\'20\'19 him in early months of Gaza war, says Tim Kaine\par \par \uc2 Senator Tim Kaine, a former vice-presidential nominee and leading foreign policy voice in the Democratic party, has said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  now understands that \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cplayed\u8221\'20\'1D him during the early months of the war in Gaza but \u8220\'20\'1Cthat ain\u8217\'20\'19t going to happen any more\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/11/tim-kaine-interview-biden-israel-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with the Guardian}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, Kaine accused the prime minister of making Israel \u8220\'20\'1Cdramatically less safe\u8221\'20\'1D and hurting its longstanding relationship with the US, and said the US president had come to realise the limits of his influence.\par \par \uc2 Biden embraced Netanyahu early in the conflict but had little to show for it as Israel continued to rain bombs on Gaza, causing mass displacement, threats of famine and disease and, last week, the deaths of seven \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  aid workers. Protesters have condemned Biden for miscalculating the extent of his sway over Netanyahu. Kaine reflected:\par \par \uc2 I do believe he felt like that relationship and the true compassion that he had for Israel over his career would lead him to be listened to by the Israeli leadership. I think he is enormously frustrated that he\u8217\'20\'19s been trying to give advice, not like a foe would give it \u8211\'20\'13 \u8216\'20\'18I think this is better for you if you listen to me. I\u8217\'20\'19m not just saying this is better for me; I\u8217\'20\'19m saying this will be better for you.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House is expected to vote again on renewing section 702 of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (Fisa) today after the bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/11/trump-biden-mike-johnson-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-6617ed308f08b0a35c23cc26#block-6617ed308f08b0a35c23cc26"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was blocked }}}\uc2  on Wednesday by a small faction of House Republicans backed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republican congressman French Hill of Arkansas told Reuters:\par \par \uc2 What I\u8217\'20\'19ve been told is that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do the same thing we were doing yesterday today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/11/trump-biden-mike-johnson-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-6617ed308f08b0a35c23cc26#block-6617ed308f08b0a35c23cc26"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embarrassing defeat}}}\uc2  over the Fisa bill and the threat of an intra-party revolt over a Ukraine aid package leaves Johnson, six months into his speakership, in a similar place as his predecessor Kevin McCarthy, who was unceremoniously voted out last fall.\par \par \uc2 After the Fisa vote on Wednesday, Johnson held a closed-door meeting of House Republicans but there was no breakthrough after more than an hour, NBC News reported. The speaker later told reporters:\par \par \uc2 We will regroup and reformulate another plan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson suffered embarrassing defeat over surveillance bill after Trump calls to 'kill' it\par \par \uc2 The joint press conference between Mike Johnson and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at Mar-a-Lago tomorrow will come just two days after the former president called on Republicans to kill legislation the speaker put forward to extend a controversial surveillance law.\par \par \uc2 Trump had urged House GOP members to reject a reauthorization of the law, Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (Fisa), ahead of the key procedural vote on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CKILL FISA,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump posted to Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 As a result, a faction of far-right House conservatives banded together to block the law from coming to the House floor, throwing the chamber into chaos once again. The Fisa vote was an embarrassing defeat for Johnson, and the fourth time in his tenure that the House has defeated a rule vote.\par \par \uc2 Asked about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s role in the reauthorization process, Johnson told reporters:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll just say that it\u8217\'20\'19s never helpful for the majority party to take down its own rules. What it does ultimately is it weakens our hand in negotiations with the Senate and the White House, so it\u8217\'20\'19s not a good development.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the House adjourned last month, Mike Johnson vowed that the chamber would soon \u8220\'20\'1Ctake the necessary steps to address the supplemental funding request\u8221\'20\'1D, which includes money for Ukraine, Israel and Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 The Senate passed a $95bn foreign aid package in February, but Johnson indicated that the House would consider an amended proposal when members returned to Washington this week.\par \par \uc2 Even as Johnson faces a challenge from the hard-right flank of his conference including congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  of Georgia, other House Republicans insist the chamber must take action to assist Ukraine. They warn that further inaction, after months of ignoring the White House\u8217\'20\'19s demands to approve more funding, will only embolden Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are at a critical juncture on the ground that is beginning to be able to impact not only morale of the Ukrainians that are fighting, but also their ability to fight,\u8221\'20\'1D congressman \uc2 Mike Turner\uc2 , the Republican chair of the House intelligence committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/face-the-nation-full-transcript-03-31-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CBS News}}}\uc2  last Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Putin knows this. This is obviously an area where we cannot allow Putin to win.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Allies of Mike Johnson have reached out to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to ask him to publicly support the speaker, sources told CNN. Johnson has also been advised to keep the former president in the loop on a vote on funding for Ukraine could be imminent in the chamber, it writes.\par \par \uc2 The specter of Trump has loomed large over the wrangling for a Ukraine deal; he was instrumental in Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to call a House vote on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/12/senate-procedural-vote-ukraine-israel-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $95bn wartime funding bill}}}\uc2  that passed the Democratic-led Senate in February, which also included aid for Israel in its war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Trump has also demanded Republicans reject any Ukraine funding measure that ties in money for US border security in order to deny \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cwin\u8221\'20\'1D on immigration ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s election. The friction has led to rightwingers, such as \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , threatening Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s position.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson and Trump to hold joint press conference on Friday\par \par \uc2 The joint appearance at Mar-a-Lago tomorrow was pitched by Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s office to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s team, but the event is being viewed as a win by both camps, according to Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Playbook.\par \par \uc2 Johnson gets to stand onstage with the King of MAGA himself right as he faces a hard-right revolt, while Trump gets the country\u8217\'20\'19s highest-ranking Republican to lend credence to his voting concerns as many in the GOP beg him to move past the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The event on Friday comes as discussions are under way about holding regular meetings between the Trump campaign and Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s team, it writes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Those around \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are growing weary of the constant motion-to-vacate threats and fearful that an election-year speakership battle could risk Republicans losing the House, Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Playbook writes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe internal fighting is not appreciated by [Trump],\u8221\'20\'1D one person close to the former president said, adding:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s no way to run a party; it\u8217\'20\'19s no way to run a House. You can\u8217\'20\'19t work in that environment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump and Johnson grow closer amid frustration over 'stupid' threat to speakership\par \par \uc2 The embattled House speaker, Mike Johnson, is dashing to Florida to meet with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  this week where the pair are expected to appear tomorrow at an event at the former president\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate for a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor announcement on election integrity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Friday\u8217\'20\'19s appearance will mark their first public event together since Johnson was elected to the speakership last fall, and comes as he and Trump have begun to develop a rapport and engaging in more frequent phone calls, Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Playbook reports. It also comes at a precarious time for Johnson, who faces a threat for his ouster from one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most loyal allies in Congress, the far-right Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Just before the spring recess last month, Greene filed a motion to vacate, and has since warned Johnson that passing Ukraine aid would put his position in peril. Johnson warned on Wednesday that an effort to oust him would not be helpful for the Republican majority and \u8220\'20\'1Cwould be chaos in the House\u8221\'20\'1D, and Trump insiders reportedly agree. \u8220\'20\'1C100 percent distraction. Unwanted. And just stupid,\u8221\'20\'1D one Trump insider told Playbook.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re not going to get trapped into this cycle of bullshit that comes out of members of the House.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am ET: Japanese prime minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2  will meet with Speaker Mike Johnson, Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  and House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10.35am: Kishida will address a joint meeting of Congress.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1.30pm: Jeffries will hold his weekly news conference.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1.30pm: White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will brief.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 3.15pm: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet with Philippine president \uc2 Ferdinand R Marcos Jr.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 4.15pm: Biden will hold a trilateral meeting with Marcos and Kishida. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will attend.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240411ek4b001y6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
