\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge imposes gag order on Trump in hush-money trial \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 6,822 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par 14:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For more on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s gag order, read our full report:Judge imposes gag order on Trump in upcoming hush-money trial\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The supreme court heard arguments in a case brought by a conservative group that sought to restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone. The justices seemed skeptical of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602e3ab8f08c746a2490068#block-6602e3ab8f08c746a2490068"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  that the drug should be restricted due to its health risks and the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s regulatory decisions, after an attorney representing the drug\u8217\'20\'19s manufacturer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602e0208f08c746a2490046#block-6602e0208f08c746a2490046"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that a court ruling against it could have ripple effects across the entire pharmaceutical industry. Meanwhile, an attorney for the Biden administration said cutting off access would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602d6d18f084fdcfd85d621#block-6602d6d18f084fdcfd85d621"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cinflict grave harm on women across the nation\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . By {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602ec338f08c746a24900fd#block-6602ec338f08c746a24900fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the hearing\u8217\'20\'19s end}}}\uc2 , only conservative justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  sounded open to the challenge, and a ruling in the case is expected this summer.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-660319038f08c746a24903a7#block-660319038f08c746a24903a7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is reportedly prohibited}}}\uc2  from attacking witnesses, prosecutors or jurors in his trial on hush money-related charges under a gag order handed down by judge Juan Merchan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-660320da8f08aa6adb8dc31e#block-660320da8f08aa6adb8dc31e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  attorney and philanthropist Nicole Shanahan as his running mate in an event in Oakland, California.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the federal government will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602fce98f0891b675f761db#block-6602fce98f0891b675f761db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cmove heaven and earth\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to reopen the port of Baltimore and rebuild the Francis Scott Key Bridge, which collapsed early this morning after being struck by a container ship.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , Texas\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general and a force in the conservative legal world, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602f6f28f08c746a24901cd#block-6602f6f28f08c746a24901cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached a deal}}}\uc2  with prosecutors to resolve securities fraud charges.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals judge who ruled against mifepristone last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602d0c58f08e9df71ad72c5#block-6602d0c58f08e9df71ad72c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has ties}}}\uc2  to one of the groups trying to keep it off the market.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 -supporting Super Pac Make America Great Again Inc unleashed an attack on \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , after he announces Nicole Shanahan as his running mate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  is a far-left radical that supports reparations, backs the Green New Deal, and wants to ban fracking. It\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise he would pick a Biden donor leftist as his running mate,\u8221\'20\'1D said spokesperson Alex Pfeiffer.\par \par \uc2 Third party candidates with dedicated followings can add an element of unpredictability to tight presidential races \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2000/nov/10/uselections2000.usa8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just ask }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2000/nov/10/uselections2000.usa8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Al Gore}}}\uc2  . But despite Team Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vitriol, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/biden-vs-trump-would-be-close-rematch-with-rfk-jr-threat-biden-reutersipsos-poll-2023-12-12/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls have shown}}}\uc2  Kennedy may sap support from Biden in states where he\u8217\'20\'19s on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  has gone on the attack against Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, including by filing a complaint accusing him of improperly coordinating with a political action committee:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/10/robert-kennedy-jr-campaign-super-pac-collusion-allegations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic party accuses RFK Jr campaign of colluding with Super Pac}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  announces Nicole Shanahan as running mate in presidential campaign\par \par \uc2 Independent presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  has announced attorney and wealthy philanthropist Nicole Shanahan as his running mate.\par \par \uc2 He made the announcement in Oakland, California, at an event attended by hundreds of supporters, as well as protesters outraged by his opposition to vaccines.\par \par \uc2 Wendy Bloom, a registered nurse who has worked in pediatric cancer units for 37 years, said she disagrees with many of Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s ideas, and was particularly enraged by his opposition to vaccines.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBesides being anti-vaccines, he\u8217\'20\'19s not pro-science, and anti-research,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. She also dismissed the choice of Shanahan as a running mate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis choice of VP tells us everything we need to know,\u8221\'20\'1D Bloom said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe has no experience. She\u8217\'20\'19s just a wealthy individual can help raise money. Voters deserve someone with experience.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy supporter Marilyn Chin, 71, said she voted Democrat for most of her life, but is now supporting Kennedy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGet out of the duopoly,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t vote Republican, don\u8217\'20\'19t vote Democrat, start looking for something else.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/26/rfk-jr-vp-nicole-shanahan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr names tech lawyer Nicole Shanahan as 2024 running mate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In seeking a gag order against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office argued the former president had a \u8220\'20\'1Clongstanding history of attacking witnesses, investigators, prosecutors, judges, and others involved in legal proceedings against him\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/03/26/nyregion/trump-trial-gag-order.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Judge Juan Merchan agreed, writing in the order that, \u8220\'20\'1Chis statements were threatening, inflammatory, denigrating.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Times notes that earlier today, Trump called his former fixer \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath\u8221\'20\'1D, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112162726199012291"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a post on Truth Social}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 just the sort of statement that Merchan\u8217\'20\'19s gag order is meant to prohibit.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The supreme court heard arguments in a case that sought to restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone, and seemed skeptical of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602e3ab8f08c746a2490068#block-6602e3ab8f08c746a2490068"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  that the drug should be restricted due to its risks and the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s regulatory decisions. An attorney representing the drug\u8217\'20\'19s manufacturer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602e0208f08c746a2490046#block-6602e0208f08c746a2490046"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that a court ruling against the drug could have ripple effects across the entire pharmaceutical industry, while an attorney for the Biden administration said cutting off access would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602d6d18f084fdcfd85d621#block-6602d6d18f084fdcfd85d621"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cinflict grave harm on women across the nation\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . By {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602ec338f08c746a24900fd#block-6602ec338f08c746a24900fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the hearing\u8217\'20\'19s end}}}\uc2 , only conservative justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  sounded open to the challenge, and a ruling in the case is expected this summer.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the federal government will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602fce98f0891b675f761db#block-6602fce98f0891b675f761db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cmove heaven and earth\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to reopen the port of Baltimore and rebuild the Francis Scott Key Bridge, which collapsed early this morning after being struck by a container ship.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , Texas\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general and a force in the conservative legal world, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602f6f28f08c746a24901cd#block-6602f6f28f08c746a24901cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached a deal}}}\uc2  with prosecutors to resolve securities fraud charges.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals judge who ruled against mifepristone last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates?page=with:block-6602d0c58f08e9df71ad72c5#block-6602d0c58f08e9df71ad72c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has ties}}}\uc2  to one of the groups trying to keep it off the market.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York judge imposes gag order in Trump hush money case - report\par \par \uc2 The judge in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s hush money criminal case has imposed a gag order that forbids him to attack witnesses, prosecutors or jurors involved in the criminal trial that\u8217\'20\'19s due to begin next month, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  has just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/03/26/nyregion/trump-trial-gag-order.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/03/26/nyregion/trump-trial-gag-order.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alvin Bragg}}}\uc2  , asked the judge, Juan Merchan, to impose the order.\par \par \uc2 The trial in New York is scheduled to begin on 15 April.\par \par \uc2 More details soon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  foe who ended up being forced out of Congress due to her opposition to the former president, also described NBC\u8217\'20\'19s elevation of McDaniel as a danger, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  chair turned NBC politics analyst \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cenabled criminality and depravity\u8221\'20\'1D in her support for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overturn the 2020 election, the former congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Liz_Cheney/status/1771916401726705757?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  as controversy swirled over McDaniel\u8217\'20\'19s media role.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRonna facilitated Trump\u8217\'20\'19s corrupt fake elector plot and his effort to pressure Michigan officials not to certify the legitimate election outcome,\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney, a Republican who was vice-chair of the House January 6 committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Liz_Cheney/status/1771916401726705757?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on social media.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe spread his lies and called January 6 \u8216\'20\'18legitimate political discourse\u8217\'20\'19. That\u8217\'20\'19s not \u8216\'20\'18taking one for the team\u8217\'20\'19. It\u8217\'20\'19s enabling criminality and depravity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McDaniel rose in Republican politics as a member of the powerful Romney family before reportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/364060-trump-asked-rnc-chairwoman-to-stop-using-romney-in-her-name-report/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropping}}}\uc2  the name at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s behest and becoming RNC chair in 2017.\par \par \uc2 In February 2022, the RNC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jdawsey1/status/1489434467617755138"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Cheney and \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , the other anti-Trump Republican on the committee that investigated the deadly attack on Congress on 6 January 2021, were engaged in the \u8220\'20\'1Cpersecution of ordinary citizens engaged in legitimate political discourse\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Cheney lost her seat in Congress that year. Kinzinger chose to retire. McDaniel was eased out of the RNC last month, to be replaced in part by \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 , the former president\u8217\'20\'19s daughter-in-law.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/25/liz-cheney-ronna-mcdaniel-trump-rnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney: controversial NBC hire Ronna McDaniel enabled Trump \u8216\'20\'18depravity\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House said that meetings over the last two days between the US national security adviser, Jake Sullivan, and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s defense minister, Yoav Gallant, have been \u8220\'20\'1Cproductive\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , yesterday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/un-gaza-ceasefire-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 canceled}}}\uc2  a high-level delegation from Israel to the White House to discuss Rafah, with the visit meant to take place today. He withdrew his agreement for talks after the US abstained from \u8211\'20\'13 rather than vetoed \u8211\'20\'13 a \uc2 UN\uc2  security council resolution calling for an immediate ceasefire in Gaza and the release of hostages held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gallant was already in Washington for longer-planned talks at a lower level. Meanwhile, in the Middle East earlier today, Israel recalled its negotiators from Doha, in Qatar, after deeming mediated talks on a Gaza truce \u8220\'20\'1Cat a dead end\u8221\'20\'1D due to demands by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , Reuters reported earlier, citing an Israeli official.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said to reporters board Air Force One moments ago: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are committed to supporting Israel in its fight against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 We cannot expect Israel to live under active threat.\u8221\'20\'1D She added that it was critical for Israel to do \u8220\'20\'1Cwhatever is possible\u8221\'20\'1D to protect civilians in Rafah.\par \par \uc2 There, about 1.7 million Palestinians are trapped under Israeli siege and suffering bombardment and food deprivation as international talks about a ceasefire and access for more aid founder.\par \par \uc2 Aid agencies and international bodies including United Nations officials have said that people stranded further north in Gaza are on the brink of famine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , has just been speaking with reporters aboard Air Force One, on the way to Raleigh, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , are holding a joint event there to talk about healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Reporters were firing off their questions, in a short gaggle on a short flight. Jean-Pierre is confirming the US president\u8217\'20\'19s position is he will \u8220\'20\'1Cmove heaven and earth\u8221\'20\'1D to reopen the port and rebuild the bridge.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s being asked about the state of US infrastructure but emphasizes that although the government pledges to work with Congress for funding to rebuild the bridge, the search and rescue effort that\u8217\'20\'19s still under way in Baltimore is the main focus.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what \uc2 Yale University\uc2  historian Timothy Snyder had to say about the danger of NBC News hiring former RNC chair \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 , as told by the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The former \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  chair {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/25/republican-national-committee-chair-ronna-mcdaniel-biden-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned NBC politics analyst}}}\uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ctried to disassemble our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D by supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s electoral fraud lies and should not be given such a media role, a leading historian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/media/msnbc-guest-flames-nbc-news-for-hiring-ronna-mcdaniel-this-is-pretty-bad/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  amid uproar over the appointment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat NBC has done is they\u8217\'20\'19ve invited into what should be a normal framework someone who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t believe that framework should exist at all,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://history.yale.edu/people/timothy-snyder"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Timothy Snyder}}}\uc2 , a Yale professor and author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2017/mar/08/on-tyranny-timothy-snyder-review-trump-twenty-lessons-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 On Tyranny}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/media/msnbc-guest-flames-nbc-news-for-hiring-ronna-mcdaniel-this-is-pretty-bad/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  MSNBC, part of the network now employing McDaniel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/nbc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC}}}\uc2  has done of its own volition is bring into a very important conversation about democracy, one which is going to take place for the next seven months or so, someone who \u8230\'20\'26 tried to disassemble our democracy. Who personally took part in an attempt to undo the American system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 NBC announced the hire on Friday. Carrie Budoff Brown, the senior vice-president for politics, said McDaniel would contribute analysis \u8220\'20\'1Cacross all NBC News platforms\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, McDaniel told Meet the Press \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the 2020 election \u8220\'20\'1Cfair and square\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that she did \u8220\'20\'1Cnot think violence should be in our political discourse\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/26/nbc-condemned-by-top-us-historian-over-ronna-mcdaniel-appointment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Pretty bad\u8217\'20\'19: NBC condemned by top US historian over role for Ronna McDaniel}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 NBC News will cut ties with former RNC chair \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  after outcry \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 NBC News will drop former \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  chair \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  after an outcry from its top talent over her promotion of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s false claims of fraud in the 2020 election, Puck reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrSCOOP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PuckNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PuckNews}}}\uc2  : NBC NEWS plans to drop ex RNC-chair \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  as a paid contributor following on-air revolt from NBC/MSNBC talent. Execs are deliberating over details; announcement pending. Meanwhile, McDaniel is seeking legal representation.\par \par \uc2 Full details, scoops &\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dylan Byers (@DylanByers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DylanByers/status/1772672463790547271?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 McDaniel\u8217\'20\'19s hiring by the network attracted criticism from former lawmakers and historians, who argued they were elevating a voice who had helped Trump attack US democracy. On Sunday, McDaniel acknowledged that the 2020 election had not been stolen, though maintained it was acceptable to say there were \u8220\'20\'1Cproblems\u8221\'20\'1D with the vote:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/25/republican-national-committee-chair-ronna-mcdaniel-biden-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Ex-RNC chair Ronna McDaniel: Biden won 2020 election \u8216\'20\'18fair and square\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did not say when he expected the Francis Scott Key Bridge to be rebuilt or, more crucially for the nation\u8217\'20\'19s economy, the port of Baltimore to be able to resume operations.\par \par \uc2 The president also gave no update on the six people still missing from the collapse, but said the search and rescue operation to find them is a \u8220\'20\'1Ctop priority\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 For the latest on this developing story, follow our live blog:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/26/baltimore-bridge-collapse-ship-collision-francis-scott-key-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden says Baltimore rescue effort \u8216\'20\'18top priority\u8217\'20\'19 with people still missing and says bridge collapse was \u8216\'20\'18terrible accident\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden says government will 'move heaven and earth' to rebuild collapsed Baltimore bridge, reopen port\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says he has instructed the federal government to \u8220\'20\'1Cmove heaven and earth\u8221\'20\'1D to rebuild the Francis Scott Key Bridge in Baltimore and reopen its economically vital port.\par \par \uc2 The government will also cover the cost of the reconstruction, the president added in a speech from the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m directing my team to move heaven and earth to reopen the port and rebuild the bridge as soon as humanly possible,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to work with our partners in Congress to make sure the state gets the support it needs. It\u8217\'20\'19s my intention that federal government will pay for the entire cost of reconstructing that bridge, and I expect the Congress to support my effort. It\u8217\'20\'19s gonna take some time, and people of Baltimore can count on us so to stick with them at every step of the way till the port is reopened and the bridge is rebuilt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The port is currently closed due to the span\u8217\'20\'19s collapse, which occurred early this morning after the cargo ship Dali collided with it. The president noted that 15,000 workers rely on the its operations, and \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re gonna do everything we can to protect those jobs and help those workers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As we wait for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to begin his speech on the collapse of the Francis Scott Key Bridge, here are some scenes from earlier today in Baltimore:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , reaches deal to resolve securities fraud charges\par \par \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , Texas\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general and a key player in the world of conservative legal theory, has reached a deal with special prosecutors to resolve longstanding securities fraud charges against him, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 However, Paxton is still under investigation by federal prosecutors, though it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if they will bring charges.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on this breaking story, from the AP:\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors on Tuesday announced an agreement with the Texas attorney general, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ken-paxton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ken Paxton}}}\uc2 , that would ultimately dismiss securities fraud charges he has been facing for nearly a decade.\par \par \uc2 Under the 18-month, pre-trial agreement, the special prosecutors in the case would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/16/ken-paxton-texas-republican-attorney-general-acquitted"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drop three felony counts against Paxton}}}\uc2 . As part of the deal, Paxton must pay full restitution to victims \u8211\'20\'13 roughly $300,000 \u8211\'20\'13 and must also complete 100 hours of community service as well as 15 hours of legal ethics education.\par \par \uc2 The resolution lets Paxton avoid a trial, which had been set to begin in less than three weeks on 15 April. Paxton was first indicted in 2015 after being accused of duping investors in a tech startup near Dallas before he was elected attorney general.\par \par \uc2 If he had been convicted at trial, Paxton could have been sentenced to life in prison.\par \par \uc2 The agreement with prosecutors, which lets Paxton remain in his elected position and doesn\u8217\'20\'19t affect his law license, is another huge legal and political victory for one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most visible Republican state attorneys general. The end of the case comes six months after Paxton was acquitted of corruption charges in an impeachment trial in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  senate.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/26/texas-ag-ken-paxton-fraud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas attorney general reaches deal to dismiss securities fraud charges}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to address Baltimore bridge collapse in White House speech\par \par \uc2 The White House just announced that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will at 12.30pm speak about the collapse of the Francis Scott Key Bridge in Baltimore, which has left six people missing and threatens to cause long-term disruptions to one of the biggest ports on the east coast.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll cover the remarks live on this blog. For more on the disaster, follow our separate live blog:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/26/baltimore-bridge-collapse-ship-collision-francis-scott-key-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Francis Scott Key bridge collapse: six people still missing in Baltimore, officials say \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The just-concluded supreme court arguments over mifepristone were a deep dive into the technicalities of how the \uc2 US government\uc2  approves and regulates medication. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  has taken a close look at what the case entails, and when the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court may rule:\par \par \uc2 Less than two years after it overturned Roe v Wade and ended the national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  is back on the frontlines of the American \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the court will hear oral arguments in one of the most highly watched cases of the session, which could dramatically curtail access to mifepristone, a drug typically used in medication abortions. The court is reviewing decisions made by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) to loosen restrictions on the drug, such as allowing non-physicians to prescribe it, as well as letting providers prescribe it through telehealth rather than in-person appointments.\par \par \uc2 Any decision to restrict mifepristone will affect everyone in the US, not only those who live in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 16 states}}}\uc2  that have banned nearly all abortions. This case could also have wide-ranging consequences for the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s future decision-making.\par \par \uc2 A decision from the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court in the case will probably arrive by summer 2024.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/17/what-abortion-pill-supreme-court-case-access-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What is the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  case in front of the US supreme court right now?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court appears skeptical of challenge to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill as oral arguments conclude\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has just wrapped up more than an hour and a half of oral arguments in the case challenging access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 The last third of the hearing was dominated by the justices, liberal and conservative alike, peppering anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  attorney Erin Hawley with questions that signaled skepticism with her case. \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2 , who argued before the court under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , said that based on their inquiries, all the justices appear ready to turn down the challenge, perhaps with the exception of \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrJustice Kagan really pierces the probabilistic nature of this. Ms. Hawley is doing a good job with what she has to work with, but it's not nearly enough I would think. The Court appears very very skeptical about this theory of a lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2  (@neal_katyal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neal_katyal/status/1772643261024219161?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrJustice Alito now tries to shore up standing, pointing to census case which he says was probabilistic. Ms. Hawley agrees. This is the only standing point I've heard so far that is helpful to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug challengers.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2  (@neal_katyal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neal_katyal/status/1772644018742083922?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMy thread covering the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug argument that my fabulous law partner Jess Ellsworth is arguing is below. The argument is close to over and right now it appears there is a wide consensus on the Court that the challenge to the drug will fail. Only Justice Alito appeared to\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PSs4wYP65y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/PSs4wYP65y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2  (@neal_katyal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neal_katyal/status/1772645863682093410?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The arguments have repeatedly returned to the question of emergency abortions and the role of a federal law known as the Emergency Medical Treatment and Active Labor Act, or Emtala, which broadly requires hospitals to stabilize patients who are facing medical emergencies rather than turning them away.\par \par \uc2 Erin Hawley, a lawyer representing the Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine, has said that in emergency situations, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors she represents do not have the time or ability to turn down cases that involve complications from abortions -even though working on such a case could run counter to their objections to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (More than 100 studies have concluded that mifepristone is a safe and effective way to end a pregnancy.)\par \par \uc2 Solicitor general \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2 , however, has contended that hospitals prepare and protect doctors from being forced to work on cases to which they object. \u8220\'20\'1CThe federal government has never taken the position that Emtala would override an individual doctor\u8217\'20\'19s conscience objections,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 As for Emtala, the court will turn to that law next month, when the justices consider if it requires doctors to perform emergency abortions. Oral arguments are set for 24 April.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  gave Danco\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Jessica Ellsworth some air to explain why pharmaceutical companies have lined up in opposition to undermining the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo you have concerns about judges parsing medical and scientific studies?\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson asked.\par \par \uc2 Ellsworth, the lawyer for the manufacturer of mifepristone, said pharmaceutical companies have \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant concerns\u8221\'20\'1D and rely on the \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s gold standard review process\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reality is \u8230\'20\'26 you have a district court that, among other things, relied on one study that was an analysis of anonymous blog posts,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ellsworth. Other studies \u8220\'20\'1Chave since been retracted for lack of scientific rigor and misleading data\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPrecisely because judges are not experts in statistics and the methodologies used for studies in clinical trials \u8211\'20\'13 that is why \uc2 FDA\uc2  has many hundreds of pages of analysis in the record of what the scientific data showed, and courts are just not in a position to parse and second-guess\u8221\'20\'1D that, she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Lawyer for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group argues \uc2 FDA\uc2  downplayed danger of mifepristone\par \par \uc2 Now arguing before the court is Erin Hawley, who represents the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine. In her opening arguments to the justices, she characterized mifepristone as posing risks that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has not done enough to manage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe lower court\u8217\'20\'19s decision merely restored longstanding and crucial protections under which millions of women used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to earlier rulings in the case. \u8220\'20\'1CThat respondent doctors will be forced to manage \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug harm is not a bug in \uc2 FDA\uc2  system, but part of its very design.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hawley is married to Republican senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  of Missouri, a longtime \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foe:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/josh-hawley-anti-abortion-arguments-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican Josh Hawley\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  arguments echoed in Alabama IVF case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s question about complications from mifepristone goes to the heart of why the medical and pharmaceutical industry considers it so scary for judges to decide questions of science.\par \par \uc2 Alito asked whether the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have provided a more extensive explanation of why telehealth prescribing of mifepristone could lead to an increase in emergency room visits.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe increase in ER visits is just of no consequence? It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t even merit some comment?\u8221\'20\'1D Alito asked \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2 , the US solicitor general.\par \par \uc2 Defending the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , Prelogar said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt fully explained its decision-making and I think it falls well within the realm of reasonableness.\u8221\'20\'1D To researchers, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  comment in question made an obvious point: an increase in emergency room visits does not denote greater risk for adverse events. An emergency room visit is a proxy measure \u8211\'20\'13 in other words, it might indicate the possibility of adverse events, but it may also indicate only an increase in women seeking reassurance, particularly in connection with a drug like mifepristone, which induces bleeding.\par \par \uc2 This is exactly the kind of complicated parsing of science that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  considers every day when looking at studies on the safety and efficacy of drugs.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ruling in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes would threaten 'virtually every drug approval', attorney for mifepristone maker warns\par \par \uc2 Up now before the supreme court is Jessica Ellsworth, an attorney for Danco Laboratories, which manufactures mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 She warned the justices that if they allowed anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors\u8217\'20\'19 challenge to mifepristone to stand, it could have unpredictable ripple effects across the pharmaceutical industry:\par \par \uc2 Respondents\u8217\'20\'19 view of the Food Drug and Cosmetic Act is so inflexible it would upend not just mifepristone, but virtually every drug approval \u8230\'20\'26 \uc2 FDA\uc2  has made for decades.\par \par \uc2 Ellsworth argued that \u8220\'20\'1Crespondents lack standing under every prong of the analysis\u8221\'20\'1D, and added that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cexhaustively\u8221\'20\'1D studied the drug to ensure it\u8217\'20\'19s safe.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking of the Comstock Act, Mr Comstock himself turned up outside the court:\par \par \uc2 enltrMr. Comstock of the eponymous Comstock Act came back to \u8220\'20\'1Csupport my fellow brethren.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lY2CwwLjKa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lY2CwwLjKa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1772635399057186940?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 That would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthony_Comstock"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anthony Comstock}}}\uc2  , the former US postal service inspector and 19th century anti-vice crusader. Outside of Washington DC, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes have seized on the legislation bearing his name to attempt to get the procedure banned:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/13/abortion-ban-comstock-act-new-mexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Mexico supreme court to consider obscure 1873 law used to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The conservative justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  also asked about the role of the Comstock Act, a 19th-century anti-obscenity law that bans the mailing of all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related materials.\par \par \uc2 He suggested that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  should have considered the Comstock Act when it changed the rules around the availability of mifepristone, which can now be sent in the mail.\par \par \uc2 Before the overturning of Roe v Wade, the Comstock Act was long regarded as a relic that no longer applied in the modern world.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has issued guidance declaring that the Comstock Act only applies in situations where people intend to break the law. However, since Roe fell, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have tried to argue that Comstock is good law and should block the mailing of at least \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 If the federal government enforced the Comstock Act, it would result in a de facto nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics rely so heavily on receiving equipment and other materials through the mail to perform abortions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The liberal justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  posed a hypothetical about mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s safety to \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2 , the US solicitor general who is defending the government\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the drug.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven if there is some increase in emergency room visits, the question of when that rises to a sufficient safety risk is up to the\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration (FDA)\uc2 , Sotomayor said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s right,\u8221\'20\'1D Prelogar replied, and noted that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  studied the drug\u8217\'20\'19s safety during the Covid-19 pandemic, when it was even easier to get, and noticed no change in adverse reactions:\par \par \uc2 I also want to emphasize, Justice Sotomayor, that the studies were far from the only evidence \uc2 FDA\uc2  consulted at the time it acted in 2021. It had real world experience during the Covid-19 pandemic, a period of time when the in-person dispensing requirement was not enforced. And \uc2 FDA\uc2  started by looking at, as a comparative analysis, the two periods of time when you had in-person dispensing and when you didn\u8217\'20\'19t, and saw that there was no relevant increase in serious adverse events or difference between those two timeframes.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s significant because a federal appeals court last summer ruled against \uc2 FDA\uc2  decisions in 2016 and 2021 that made mifepristone easier to access. Those are now being challenged by the government in this hearing.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/25/abortion-pill-case-fda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill case at the supreme court could undo the FDA}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The oral arguments began with a debate on whether the doctors have standing, or the right to bring the case in the first place.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors claim they will suffer harm if they have to treat women who experience complications from mifepristone, an argument the Biden administration, which appealed the case to the court, has rejected as too speculative, especially given mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s proven safety record.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has historically rejected standing arguments based on such potential harm, which the solicitor general, \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2 , said rested on a \u8220\'20\'1Clong chain of remote contingencies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But conservative justices \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , both \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents, seemed skeptical of Prelogar \u8217\'20\'19s arguments against standing, with Thomas even suggesting that theories of standing should be reconsidered if they don\u8217\'20\'19t allow the case to move forward.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIs there anybody who can sue and get a judicial ruling on whether what \uc2 FDA\uc2  did was lawful?\u8221\'20\'1D Alito asked. \u8220\'20\'1CShouldn\u8217\'20\'19t somebody be able to challenge that in court?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ruling against mifepristone would 'inflict grave harm on women across the nation' - Biden administration lawyer\par \par \uc2 In her opening statement, the US solicitor general, \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2 , asked the supreme court to keep mifepristone available.\par \par \uc2 A ruling in favor of conservative groups challenging the medication \u8220\'20\'1Cwould severely disrupt the federal system for developing and approving drugs, harming the agency and the pharmaceutical industry. It would also inflict grave harm on women across the nation,\u8221\'20\'1D Prelogar said.\par \par \uc2 She continued:\par \par \uc2 Rolling back \uc2 FDA\uc2  changes would unnecessarily restrict access to mifepristone with no safety justification. Some women could be forced to undergo more invasive surgical abortions, others might not be able to access the drug at all. And all of this could happen at the request of plaintiffs who have no certain injury of their own. The court should reject that profoundly inequitable result.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court begins hearing conservative challenge to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has kicked off oral arguments as it weighs a conservative group\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to restrict access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 Arguments are expected to take an hour. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be covering them live.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As we await the start of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s oral arguments in the conservative challenge to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone, here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  with a rundown of what we can expect in today\u8217\'20\'19s hearing:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is back at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2 , with arguments on Tuesday in the first major case on the issue since a 6-3 majority ruled in 2022 to overturn Roe v Wade and end the national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a decision that unleashed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans throughout the country as well as a political backlash that Democrats hope will serve them in the coming presidential election.\par \par \uc2 At issue in the case is the future of mifepristone, a drug typically used in US medication abortions. The rightwing groups that brought the case are seeking to roll back measures taken by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) to expand the drug\u8217\'20\'19s availability in recent years.\par \par \uc2 A decision in their favor would apply nationwide, including in states that protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, and would likely make the drug more difficult to acquire. The loosening of restrictions on mifepristone have helped mitigate the impact of post-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans; if those restrictions are reimposed, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups anticipate it will become significantly more difficult to access abortions in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMore than 60% of abortions in the US are medication abortions, so that would impact a substantial number of people, whether you live in a protective state or a restricted state,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nicole Huberfeld, a health law professor at Boston University\u8217\'20\'19s School of Public {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Health}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court to hear first major \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  case since Roe decision}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A key moment in the conservative challenge to mifepristone occurred last year, when a federal appeals court issued a ruling to restrict access to the drug. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Melissa Segura reports on the connections between one of the judges who issued that decision, and a group opposing the drug:\par \par \uc2 When the former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointed the Texas attorney James Ho to the fifth circuit court of appeals in 2017, lawyers at the prominent law firm Gibson Dunn \u8211\'20\'13 where Ho worked before his appointment \u8211\'20\'13 had a problem: how to replace the politically connected Ho. Turns out, they didn\u8217\'20\'19t even need to change the home address for his replacement. Ho\u8217\'20\'19s wife, Allyson, moved into her husband\u8217\'20\'19s position and his old office.\par \par \uc2 Meet the Hos.\par \par \uc2 Few people outside of legal circles have heard of the Hos, yet the couple is tied to the case before the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  that will determine women\u8217\'20\'19s access to mifepristone, a drug commonly used in medication abortions. The court hears arguments in the case on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Ho served on the three-judge panel last summer that ruled to restrict access to mifepristone. The legal group behind the mifepristone case, \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , made at least six payments from 2018 through 2022 to his wife, Allyson, a powerhouse federal appellate lawyer who has argued in front of the supreme court and has deep connections to the conservative legal movement that has led the attack on the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/judge-james-ho-wife-mifepristone-abortion-pill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The next Clarence Thomas? \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill case spotlights rightwing judge and his wife\u8217\'20\'19s shadowy connections}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Protesters have gathered outside the supreme court ahead of the 10am kickoff of oral arguments in the conservative challenges against mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 Both sides of the debate are well represented:\par \par \uc2 enltrProtestors chanting \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6ockkqnDQu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6ockkqnDQu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1772610443279827442?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrA speaker who said they are with Alliance for Defending Freedom is speaking to a collection of antiabortion activists holding signs that say \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 FDA\uc2  do your job\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/d9p3Xc15tE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/d9p3Xc15tE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1772614446596186119?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Robots included:\par \par \uc2 esltrMifepristone dispensing robots {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FfMXj2d5Xe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FfMXj2d5Xe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1772615258252726450?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ruling tightening mifepristone access could upend US pharmaceutical industry\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could be upended by a supreme court ruling tightening access to mifepristone. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/26/supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jessica Glenza}}}\uc2  reports, the conservative challengers to the drug have targeted decisions made by the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration (FDA)\uc2  to make it easier to prescribe.\par \par \uc2 But if the supreme court agrees with their complaint, it opens up the possibility of a wave of challenges to other medications that treat a range of issues. Doctors and pharmaceutical companies have become so concerned about the case that they have filed briefs defending the \uc2 FDA\uc2  against the conservative challenge.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on why the stakes in the case are so high:\par \par \uc2 A supreme court case about one little pill \u8211\'20\'13 mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 has the medical and pharmaceutical world on edge. The pill, at the heart of a case that will be argued on Tuesday, is part of a two-drug regimen used to treat miscarriage and end early pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Despite a more than 20-year track record of safe real-world use, backed up by more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/01/health/abortion-pill-safety.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 100 peer-reviewed studies}}}\uc2 , a group of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors is seeking to roll back \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration (FDA)\uc2  decisions that changed and relaxed some prescribing rules.\par \par \uc2 If the doctors succeed, despite contested and in some cases {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://retractionwatch.com/2024/02/06/papers-used-by-judge-to-justify-abortion-pill-suspension-retracted/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now-retracted evidence of harm}}}\uc2 , the case could reshape \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US and have enormous and unpredictable consequences for how drugs are prescribed, regulated and developed.\par \par \uc2 A ruling in favor of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors could threaten everything from trust in medicine to specific drugs to the US\u8217\'20\'19s position as the world\u8217\'20\'19s foremost drug innovator.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am terrified,\u8221\'20\'1D said Juan Hincapie-Castillo, a drug policy researcher, licensed pharmacist and assistant professor of epidemiology at the University of North Carolina. \u8220\'20\'1CThis case is shifting the whole paradigm of how things could go moving forward\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone was approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in 2000 with stringent requirements for how it should be prescribed: only up to seven weeks gestation, dispensed in-person with mandatory follow-up appointments, and with enhanced risk-reporting requirements for doctors. Along with misoprostol, the second drug in the regimen, it is, in effect, designed to induce the equivalent of a miscarriage at home.\par \par \uc2 After more than 20 years and scientific articles spanning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/01/health/abortion-pill-safety.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 countries}}}\uc2 , the scientific consensus is that the \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill\u8221\'20\'1D has a remarkable track record of safety and effectiveness that, in the media, is often compared to that of Tylenol or Viagra.\par \par \uc2 But following the fall of Roe v Wade in 2022, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors initiated a lawsuit against the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in Amarillo, Texas, arguing that the drug\u8217\'20\'19s approval should be withdrawn. The Trump-appointed judge Matthew Kacsmaryk ruled in favor of the doctors. Were his decision not appealed, it would have resulted in a de facto nationwide ban on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/25/abortion-pill-case-fda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill case at the supreme court could undo the FDA}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to weigh conservative challenge to key \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Nearly two years after overturning Roe v Wade and allowing states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the supreme court will today at 10am ET hear arguments in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a case that could limit}}}\uc2  the availability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone. It\u8217\'20\'19s the first time the justices will address reproductive rights since the Dobbs decision in 2022, and will be argued before a court that is ideologically quite similar to the one that decided that case. Conservative justices, including the same five who voted to strike down Roe, dominate the court with a six-seat majority, while liberals hold a three-seat minority.\par \par \uc2 The arguments come {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/self-managed-abortions-avoid-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as evidence emerges}}}\uc2  that usage of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication has soared among Americans. A decision limiting access to mifepristone could also cause tumult in the presidential race, and is sure to be seized on by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to argue that it\u8217\'20\'19s a sign of what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would do if put back in the White House. Trump did, after all, appoint three justices to the court and tip it decisively to the conservatives \u8211\'20\'13 all of whom voted to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been briefed on the collapse of the Francis Scott Key Bridge in Baltimore. We {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/26/baltimore-bridge-collapse-ship-collision-francis-scott-key-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have a live blog}}}\uc2  covering the latest news on the disaster, and you can find it here.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Is the GOP surrendering in their push to impeach Biden? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ArthurDelaneyHP/status/1772369951669563588"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reports}}}\uc2  have emerged that the Republican architect of the attempt to bring charges against the president now says he\u8217\'20\'19ll settle for a criminal referral to the justice department.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House press briefing will take place on Air Force One as Biden heads to campaign in North Carolina, sometime after 1pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240411ek4b002gz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
