\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump to sue judge in effort to avert hush-money trial \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 4,514 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par 14:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our latest full report here:Trump prepares to sue judge in Stormy Daniels hush-money case\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 That concludes today\u8217\'20\'19s US politics live blog.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden announced several student loan forgiveness proposals during remarks in Madison, Wisconsin. One of his biggest proposals will cancel debt for those with more than $20,000 in interest or anyone who started paying off student loans more than two decades ago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  criticized Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cslap in the face\u8221\'20\'1D to the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. In a lengthy post to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X, Pence said that Trump had previously sent Roe v Wade \u8220\'20\'1Cto the ash heap\u8221\'20\'1D by securing supreme court judges who were anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but criticized his \u8220\'20\'1Cretreat\u8221\'20\'1D from \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life Americans\u8221\'20\'1D with his latest decision.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jake Sullivan will host a meeting at the White House on Monday for families of US hostages held in Gaza, Punchbowl News reported. The latest meeting comes amid ongoing attempts to bring hostages home.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump indicated that he will sue the judge overseeing his hush money trial in New York City, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  first reported. Trump is accused of forging financial records to cover up a sex scandal. The trial is set to begin 15 April.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  denounced Trump\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and vowed to continue advocating for a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. In a statement Monday, Graham said he \u8220\'20\'1Crespectfully [disagrees]\u8221\'20\'1D on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stance that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an issue of states\u8217\'20\'19 rights.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for following along.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said that Trump would sign off on a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, when asked about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statement that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access should be left up to the states.\par \par \uc2 While talking with reporters before boarding Air Force 2, Harris said:\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s all be very clear \u8211\'20\'13 if he were to be put back in a position where he could sign off on a law, he would sign off on a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Let\u8217\'20\'19s be very clear about that.\par \par \uc2 From CBS News:\par \par \uc2 enltrBefore boarding Air Force 2 heading to Philadelphia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2  responded to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s video posted this morning indicating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy should be left to states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s all be very clear - if he were to be put back in a position where he could sign off on a law, he would sign off on\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xrD2izyM6v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/xrD2izyM6v}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nidia (@NidiaCavazosTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NidiaCavazosTV/status/1777404123769454771?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Polls, polls, polls\par \par \uc2 Americans \u8211\'20\'13 and the rest of the world \u8211\'20\'13 are keeping an eye on the state of the US presidential race. Almost every day multiple new polls emerge and they nearly all agree \u8211\'20\'13 this race is close. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/president/general/2024/trump-vs-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Two more polls}}}\uc2  came on Monday, one (from I&I/TIPP) had \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  up by three points, while the other (from Emerson) had Trump winning by one.\par \par \uc2 Go back a little further and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/president/general/2024/trump-vs-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over the last nine polls }}}\uc2  Biden has been winning in five of them, three of them had Trump ahead and one was a tie. The overall average still has Trump slightly ahead by just 0.3 points. That seems to represent a pattern of the last few weeks \u8211\'20\'13 Biden is ticking very slowly up. Of course, the vagaries of the US election system and its electoral college mean the polls are no straight predictor of a winner. Trump has (recently) been stronger in core battleground states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pence blasts Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  position\par \par \uc2 Former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4581182-pence-calls-trumps-abortion-stance-a-slap-in-the-face-to-supporters/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blasted}}}\uc2  his old boss\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying that it is a \u8220\'20\'1Ca slap in the face\u8221\'20\'1D of many anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigners.\par \par \uc2 The Hill reports that Pence tweeted in the wake of Trump saying the issue should be decided by individual states \u8211\'20\'13 a blow to those who hoped he might back some form of more national ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump\u8217\'20\'19s retreat on the Right to Life is a slap in the face to the millions of pro-life Americans who voted for him in 2016 and 2020,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence wrote in his post, before praising the steps their administration took to further the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  effort.\par \par \uc2 Pence tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1CBy nominating and standing by the confirmation of conservative justices, the Trump-Pence Administration helped send Roe v. Wade to the ash heap of history where it belongs and gave the pro-life movement the opportunity to compassionately support women and unborn children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden commented on attempts from Republican lawmakers and the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to end his loan forgiveness program.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut then some of my Republican friends and elected officials [in] special interest sued us. And the supreme court blocked us,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, as the crowd booed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut that didn\u8217\'20\'19t stop us,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden added.\par \par \uc2 Read about the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s actions against student loan forgiveness {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/30/student-loan-forgiveness-supreme-court-ruling-biden#:~:text=In%20a%206%2D3%20decision,authorize%20Biden's%20debt%20forgiveness%20plan."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2023/jul/05/us-student-debt-supreme-court-biden-loan-relief-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This decision is a slap in the face\u8217\'20\'19: the real cost of the US student debt ruling}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s student loan forgiveness proposals have already gotten a nod of endorsement from top Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders of Vermont called the proposals a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig deal\u8221\'20\'1D, emphasizing that millions of Americans face \u8220\'20\'1Coutrageous [levels] of student debt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrAt a time when young people across the country are struggling economically, President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision to reduce the outrageous level of student debt they face will be extremely helpful. Millions will now be in a better position to start families & buy homes. This is a big deal.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bernie Sanders (@SenSanders) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSanders/status/1777399336290152618?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden announced several major actions with regards to student loans during his speech.\par \par \uc2 Biden said his administration will propose a new rule to cancel up to $20,000 in interest for people who owe more than when they began paying their off loan.\par \par \uc2 Biden will also cancel student debt for those who started paying their student loans more than two decades ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis relief can be life-changing,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has begun his remarks on student loan forgiveness, discussing the impact that it has on millions of Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot can\u8217\'20\'19t repay for even decades after being [out of] school,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToo many people feel the strain and stress \u8230\'20\'26 because even if they get by, they still have this crushing, crushing debt,\u8221\'20\'1D he added\par \par \uc2 Biden added that student debt also negatively impacts the local economy, as many people are unable to afford homes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks on student loan forgiveness are set to begin shortly in Madison, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned for updates!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 More Democrats have warned that Trump will sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if elected president in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren said Trump bragged he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cproudly the person responsible\u8221\'20\'1D for overturning Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19d sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as president, & his allies plan to get it done even without Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D the Massachusetts senator added.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump just bragged he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cproudly the person responsible\u8221\'20\'1D for overturning Roe. He\u8217\'20\'19d sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as president, & his allies plan to get it done even without Congress. But if we re-elect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JoeBiden}}}\uc2  with a Democratic Congress, we can secure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@ewarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ewarren/status/1777397052445430153?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, noted that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has frequently changed, alluding that it could become more hard line.\par \par \uc2 enltrLet\u8217\'20\'19s wait a few weeks and see what his new position will be. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UNZBznv78Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/UNZBznv78Y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1777375661700563306?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has not been briefed on the date of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Rafah, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 State department spokesperson \uc2 Matthew Miller\uc2  said on Monday that the White House has not received a date for the military operation after Israel\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  said that a day has been chosen.\par \par \uc2 Miller emphasized that the US does not support an invasion of Rafah, where many people in Gaza are currently displaced amid the ongoing genocide in the territory.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jake Sullivan will host a meeting at the White House on Monday for families of US hostages held in Gaza, Punchbowl News reported.\par \par \uc2 The national security adviser will also meet with Israeli opposition Yair Lipid, who is visiting Washington this week.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, White House spokesperson John Kirby said that \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is currently considering a deal that could release more hostages and lead to a six-week ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 enltrNational Security Adviser Jake Sullivan will be meeting tonight at the White House with family members of U.S. hostages in Gaza, per NSC spokesman John Kirby\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 John Bresnahan (@bresreports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bresreports/status/1777360963454292050?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked a myriad of reactions from both sides of the political aisle. On Monday, Trump said that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an issue of states\u8217\'20\'19 rights, refusing to back a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that is popular amid Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have warned that Trump will sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, further limiting reproductive rigts. Meanwhile, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates and GOP members have publicly criticized Trump for refusing to support an national limit.\par \par \uc2 Biden squarely blamed Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cfor creating the cruelty and the chaos that has enveloped America since the Dobbs decision\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is on route to Madison Wisconsin, where he will deliver remarks on his latest student loan forgiveness plan. White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said that Biden will continue \u8220\'20\'1Cfighting on behalf of borrowers\u8221\'20\'1D despite pushback from \u8220\'20\'1CRepublican officials\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has indicated that he will sue the judge overseeing his hush money trial in New York City, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  first reported. Trump is accused of forging financial records to cover up a sex scandal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House announced that \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is reviewing a proposal that could lead to the release of hostages and a six-week ceasefire amid the ongoing genocide in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech on student loans, Jean-Pierre said that Biden will continue to pursue student loan forgiveness despite pushback from \u8220\'20\'1CRepublican officials\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we can\u8217\'20\'19t prevent them from filing lawsuits against this plan, the president will never stop fighting on behalf of borrowers,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 Republican states have previously tried to fight Biden\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to wipe student loan debt, even falsely claiming that they would be financially impacted by the loan forgiveness scheme.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2023/may/02/student-loan-forgiveness-supreme-court-us-states-false-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US states opposing student loan forgiveness made false claims, files reveal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre had choice words for Trump and Senate Republicans about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  following Trump clarifying his position.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre blamed Republicans for \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans\u8221\'20\'1D happening in GOP-led states, during Monday\u8217\'20\'19s gaggle.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only reason that extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are now in effect all over the country is because of the judges the previous president and Senate republicans put in the court,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only reason that women are being [denied] life saving and even unrelated procedures and turned away from emergency rooms\u8230\'20\'26is because of the judges the previous president and Senate republicans put in the court,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre added that bans on IVF, a consequence of the Alabama state supreme court ruling, are because of judges selected by Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to be clear eyed here,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre added, regarding the potential impact on reproductive rights if Trump is elected.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is hosting a gaggle aboard Air Force One, as Biden travels to Wisconsin to give remarks on student loan forgiveness.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned for further updates.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to sue judge in effort to avert hush-money trial\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will sue the judge overseeing his hush money trial, which is over allegations that Trump forged financial records in an attempt to cover up a sex scandal, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/08/nyregion/trump-hush-money-trial-delay.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times first reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The latest lawsuit from Trump is a last-minute attempt to delay the trial, which is set to begin 15 April in New York City.\par \par \uc2 According to the Times, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team has now filed an action against Judge Juan Merchan, though the lawsuit itself is not public.\par \par \uc2 Two sources with knowledge on the suit told the Times on Monday that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys are asking an appeals court to delay the trial and also attacking a gag order that Merchan placed on Trump.\par \par \uc2 Merchan previously denied Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request to delay the trial until the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  reviews his claims around presidential immunity involving a separate criminal case.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/03/donald-trump-hush-money-trial-delay-denied"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s bid to delay hush-money trial denied by New York judge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House: Hamas reviewing latest ceasefire proposal\par \par \uc2 A White House spokesperson said that \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is reviewing a new proposal that could secure the release of hostages and a ceasefire, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Spokesperson John Kirby said that the US is taking current negotiations seriously and hopeful about a possible release deal, which would lead to a six-week ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 Kirby added that 300 aid trucks entered Gaza on Sunday, but that the US is pressing Israel to allow more aid into the territory.\par \par \uc2 The latest negotiations come four days after Biden and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, spoke on the phone after an Israeli air strike killing seven aid workers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Madison, \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  said that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s response to Gaza will hurt his popularity among young voters ahead of the 2024 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4580503-wisconsin-should-be-of-concern-for-biden-because-of-gaza-says-progressive-democrat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Hill reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an interview with MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Ayman Mohyeldin on Sunday, the progressive representative said:\par \par \uc2 Yes, because we\u8217\'20\'19ve always had a problem engaging voters of color, young people and certain demographics\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be harder now because of how we respond \u8212\'20\'14 have pretty much not responded very well to what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Gaza\par \par \uc2 Nearly 50,000 Democrats cast \u8220\'20\'1Cuninstructed\u8221\'20\'1D votes in the Wisconsin primary versus voting for Biden due to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s response to the ongoing genocide in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Graham 'respectfully disagrees' on Trump's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  criticized Trump\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and vows to continue advocating for a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 In a statement Monday, Graham said he \u8220\'20\'1Crespectfully [disagrees]\u8221\'20\'1D on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stance that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an issue of states\u8217\'20\'19 rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will continue to advocate that there should be a national minimum standard limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at fifteen weeks because the child is capable of feeling pain, with exceptions for rape, incest and life of the mother,\u8221\'20\'1D Graham added.\par \par \uc2 Graham said earlier this year that he would introduce legislation for a 15-week ban, but may not pursue the policy in Congress at this time, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4580756-graham-trump-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Hill reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Graham\u8217\'20\'19s split with Trump comes as Republicans are contending with how to handle \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is more of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s statement on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  position.\par \par \uc2 The statement is among Biden\u8217\'20\'19s longer ones as Democrats work to establish that Republicans will further destroy \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t understand: When he ripped away Roe v. Wade, he ripped away a fundamental right for the women of America that the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2  had affirmed and reaffirmed for 50 years.\par \par \uc2 As a fundamental right, it didn\u8217\'20\'19t matter where you lived. It was granted to you as an American, not as a resident of any state. Generations of women had come to rely on that right. Now we\u8217\'20\'19re in the extraordinary position where women today have fewer rights than their mothers and grandmothers.\par \par \uc2 That has never happened before in America. And it cannot be allowed to stand. I am determined to restore the federal protections of Roe v. Wade. So it won\u8217\'20\'19t matter where you live in America: The fundamental right to choose for women will once again be the law of the land. If you give me and Vice President Harris a Democratic Congress, that is exactly what we will do.\par \par \uc2 Trump is simply lying. There was no groundswell of support in America for overturning Roe. In fact, support for Roe is higher today in America than it has ever been. The real truth is Trump made a political deal in 2016. He promised to appoint a Court that would get rid of Roe. And he had to make good on that debt. So he did. It was never about public policy or what was right or what Trump believed. It was always about politics.\par \par \uc2 Trump admits as much in his statement today. Having created the chaos of overturning Roe, he\u8217\'20\'19s trying to say, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, never mind. Don\u8217\'20\'19t punish me for that. I just want to win.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Trump is scrambling. He\u8217\'20\'19s worried that since he\u8217\'20\'19s the one responsible for overturning Roe the voters will hold him accountable in 2024. Well, I have news for Donald. They will. America was built on personal freedom and liberty. So, there is nothing more un-American than having our personal freedoms taken away. And that is what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has done.\par \par \uc2 As I have said many times since the Dobbs decision, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and all those responsible for overturning Roe don\u8217\'20\'19t have a clue about the power of women in America. But they are about to find out.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden warns Trump will sign national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if elected\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  cautioned that Trump will sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if elected, following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s latest remarks on his \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance.\par \par \uc2 In a Monday statement, Biden said that Trump is \u8220\'20\'1Cresponsible for creating the cruelty and the chaos that has enveloped America since the Dobbs decision\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden said:\par \par \uc2 Trump once said women must be punished for seeking reproductive health care \u8211\'20\'13 and he\u8217\'20\'19s gotten his wish. Women are being turned away from emergency rooms, forced to go to court to seek permission for the medical attention they need, and left to travel hundreds of miles for health care\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 With all his empty words on fertility treatments, Trump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t tell you the Maga Republicans he controls in Congress have put forward bills that could ban fertility treatments and that the Speaker of the House he empowered is one of the strongest supporters for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in the nation.\par \par \uc2 Let there be no illusion. If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is elected and the MAGA Republicans in Congress put a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on the Resolute Desk, Trump will sign it into law.\par \par \uc2 Biden added that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermined\u8221\'20\'1D to restore federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections if him and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  get a \u8220\'20\'1CDemocratic Congress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Defending Democracy Together, a conservative anti-Trump group, is mounting a new effort to stave off a change to Nebraska presidential election rules which pro-Trumpers hope will take a potentially crucial electoral college vote away from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With Maine, Nebraska is one of two US states which splits its electoral college vote.\par \par \uc2 Under Nebraska law, two of five electoral college votes go to the candidate with most votes statewide, the others to the winners of three electoral districts.\par \par \uc2 That means that though Nebraska skews heavily Republican, it can split its vote.\par \par \uc2 It did so in 2008 and 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.270towin.com/states/Nebraska"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  taking one electoral vote in the district centered on Omaha, the biggest city in the state.\par \par \uc2 In 2024, as Biden and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  square off in a tightly fought rematch, there is a scenario in which that one Nebraska vote could decide the whole election.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/03/nebraska-electoral-system"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Exhorted}}}\uc2  by the hard-right podcaster Charlie Kirk, therefore, Trump supporters are trying to switch to a winner-takes-all model. The push failed to clear one legislative hurdle last week but it could be revived by \uc2 Jim Pillen\uc2 , the Republican Nebraska governor, in time to affect the November election.\par \par \uc2 Defending Democracy Together, which has strong links to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thebulwark.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Bulwark}}}\uc2  , a never-Trump conservative news site, will therefore this week launch the first tranche of an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL8d1s-rXBFJNNezIPnvwXYYwAx-qsyX5g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ad campaign}}}\uc2  meant to persuade Nebraskans to oppose the change. Targeting Nebraska Republican lawmakers, the ads say:\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in Lincoln want to change Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s independent electoral college vote and destroy your ability to decide the next president.\par \par \uc2 Viewers are then encouraged to call their local Republican and voice their opposition.\par \par \uc2 Gunner Ramer, national spokesperson for Defending Democracy Together, said: \u8220\'20\'1CNebraskans take pride in their ability to exercise their voting power to make their congressional district\u8217\'20\'19s voice heard. When voters feel that their presidential vote truly matters, our democracy is better for it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what makes Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s current system so powerful. Lawmakers in Lincoln need to uphold that pro-democratic principle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  come as Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is set to take effect in May.\par \par \uc2 The near-total ban will take place starting 1 May, but could be overturned by voters in November. Trump previously denounced near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in several GOP-led states.\par \par \uc2 Read more on Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Florida, the last bastion of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the south-eastern United States, will ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past six weeks of pregnancy starting next month, leaving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and their supporters in the state and across the country scrambling to deal with the fallout for patients.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the Florida state supreme court upheld a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, a move that removed the barriers for a separate, six-week ban that takes effect on 1 May. In a separate ruling, the court also agreed to let Florida residents weigh in on the issue through a November ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution \u8211\'20\'13 a decision that opens a new front in an election that is already sure to be dominated by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re all holding out hope for November, but realizing that from May to November, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be turning patients away at unprecedented rates,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Chelsea Daniels, a family medicine physician and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in Miami, Florida. \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels like a punch to the gut.\u8221\'20\'1D\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/02/florida-abortion-ban-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups 'deeply disappointed' by Trump's position\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups have slammed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , signaling the stark divide on the issue in GOP circles.\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of the Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America, said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply disappointed\u8221\'20\'1D in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s position, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/finnygo/status/1777313609544007712"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a statement to X}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We are deeply disappointed in President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s position. Unborn children and their mothers deserve national protections and national advocacy from the brutality of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Saying the issue is \u8216\'20\'18back to the states\u8217\'20\'19 cedes the national debate to Democrats who are working relentless to enact legislation mandating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout all nine months of pregnancy\u8230\'20\'26.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, prominent Democrats have warned that Trump will pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban into law if elected president.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/timkaine/status/1777319975100764289"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a statement to X}}}\uc2 , Senator Tim Kaine of Virginia said that Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Csingularly responsible\u8221\'20\'1D for the end of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections:\par \par \uc2 An old saying goes: \u8220\'20\'1Cwatch what they do, not what they say.\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is singularly responsible for the overturning of Roe & ripping away women\u8217\'20\'19s freedoms\u8212\'20\'14& he \u8220\'20\'1Cproudly\u8221\'20\'1D takes credit for it. He\u8217\'20\'19d sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban into law\u8212\'20\'14no matter how much he tries to deny it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes after he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously suggested}}}\uc2  that he would support a 15-week ban with exceptions for rape, incest, or if the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life was in danger.\par \par \uc2 In Monday\u8217\'20\'19s video, Trump said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly in favor of exceptions for rape, incest and life of the mother.\u8221\'20\'1D He did not say at what number of weeks into pregnancy he would support a ban.\par \par \uc2 Trump previously criticized near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans passed in several Republican-led states as \u8220\'20\'1Cterrible\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His latest comments come as several GOP candidates struggle with the issue, particularly in competitive states.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump says each US state should determine different \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says states and 'will of the people' should determine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  said that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights should be determined by states and the \u8220\'20\'1Cwill of the people\u8221\'20\'1D, dodging calls for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Trump, the Republican nominee for the 2024 presidential election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted a video clarifying his position}}}\uc2  to his social media platform Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy view is now that we have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  where everybody wanted it from a legal standpoint, the states will determine by vote or legislation, or perhaps both, and whatever they decide must be the law of the land. In this case, the law of the state,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the end of the day, this is all about the will of the people. You must follow your heart, or in many cases, your religion or your faith,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Trump noted that he also supports the availability of fertility treatments. His latest remarks comes after the Alabama supreme court ruled that frozen embryos are \u8220\'20\'1Cchildren\u8221\'20\'1D, a win for the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement that forced many Republicans to explain their position on the popular procedure.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  will speak in Madison, Wisconsin about student loan forgiveness for 23 million borrowers.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240408ek48001jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
