\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Shame! Shame!\u8217\'20\'19: Arizona Republican leaders block effort to repeal  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano \par \uc2 656 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par 13:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats stymied after state supreme court rules that 1864 law with no exceptions for rape or incest can go into effect\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s state Republican leadership halted an effort by Democrats on Wednesday to repeal an 1864 law banning almost all abortions, which the state supreme court this week ruled could go into effect.\par \par \uc2 The move came after Republican lawmakers in the state had denounced the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, including some who previously expressed support for the law. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and other high-profile Republicans, such as the Senate candidate Kari Lake, had also declared their opposition to the ruling with Lake urging lawmakers to \u8220\'20\'1Ccome up with an immediate commonsense solution that Arizonans can support\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Arizona supreme court ruled on Tuesday that the 1864 law can go into effect \u8211\'20\'13 though it may not happen for weeks. Under the law, which predates Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s statehood, there are no exceptions for rape or incest and abortions are permitted only if the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life is at risk.\par \par \uc2 Democrats and one Republican lawmaker sought to repeal the law, but GOP leaders, who command the majority, cut it off twice and quickly adjourned for the week. Outraged Democrats erupted in finger-waving chants of \u8220\'20\'1CShame! Shame!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republican state Rep Teresa Martinez, of Casa Grande, said there was no reason to rush the debate. She accused Democrats of \u8220\'20\'1Cscreaming at us and engaging in extremist and insurrectionist behaviour on the House floor\u8221\'20\'1D. The GOP-led senate briefly convened without debate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democratic legislators seized on national interest in the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got the eyes of the world watching Arizona right now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Democratic state Rep Stephanie Stahl Hamilton, of Tucson. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that the supreme court decision yesterday is extreme. And we know that should the 1864 ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain a law in Arizona, people will die.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The state supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision is expected to have major repercussions in the state and could significantly impact \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access across the US south-west. Political strategists have said that the near total ban would draw moderate voters to Democrats and mobilize young voters and voters of color.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was an earthquake of epic proportions in Arizona politics,\u8221\'20\'1D said Barrett Marson, a Phoenix-based Republican strategist. \u8220\'20\'1CAnytime Republicans are talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they\u8217\'20\'19re losing. Now, I think the only issue is going to be \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  called inaction on the proposed repeal unconscionable. \u8220\'20\'1CRadical legislators protected a Civil War-era total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that jails doctors, strips women of our bodily autonomy and puts our lives at risk,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans in the state had, surprisingly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/arizona-republicans-against-state-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 come out against}}}\uc2  the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision. \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision cannot stand,\u8221\'20\'1D Matt Gress, a Republican state representative, said. \u8220\'20\'1CI categorically reject rolling back the clock to a time when slavery was still legal and we could lock up women and doctors because of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gress had tried to bring forth a bill to repeal the ban but then voted with other Republicans to move to recess.\par \par \uc2 The Republican speaker of the Arizona state house and the president of the state senate, said in a joint statement they would be \u8220\'20\'1Clistening to our constituents to determine the best course of action for the legislature\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Democrats, who have made Arizona a top priority in 2024, hope to flip both the state house and senate and have seized on Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am disgusted by the actions of my peers, both lying about their stance on this issue so important to Arizonans, and refusing to repeal the 1864 ban,\u8221\'20\'1D said Priya Sundareshan, a Democratic senator and Arizona Democratic Legislative Campaign Committee co-chair.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is why we need to flip the legislature, pass the ballot initiative and stop Republicans from taking away this right ever again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240410ek4a003s6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
