\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Appeal court judge denies Trump\u8217\'20\'19s third attempt this week to delay hush money trial \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Joanna Walters (now); L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 8,028 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par 14:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our latest reporting on Trump and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  here:Judge denies Trump\u8217\'20\'19s third attempt this week to delay hush-money trialArizona Republicans block \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ban repeal after denouncing court ruling\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An appeals court judge in New York denied \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s third attempt in three days to delay his hush-money criminal trial. Trump was denied his attempt to push back the 15 April trial on charges stemming from hush money paid to porn star Stormy Daniels, paving the way for the first-ever criminal trial of a former US president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616bd558f08e55cb7cf358c#block-6616bd558f08e55cb7cf358c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he believes the Arizona supreme court went too far with its ruling upholding a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Asked if he would sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if elected president in 2024, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616c26d8f08e55cb7cf35f2#block-6616c26d8f08e55cb7cf35f2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CNo.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In response, the Biden campaign{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616cafc8f08a1e6c6fcd132#block-6616cafc8f08a1e6c6fcd132"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cowns the suffering and chaos happening right now\u8221\'20\'1D and warned that he has banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cevery chance he gets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asked what he would say to the people of Arizona, Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616d63a8f08a1e6c6fcd1de#block-6616d63a8f08a1e6c6fcd1de"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CElect me. I\u8217\'20\'19m in the \u8230\'20\'26 21st century, not back then.\u8221\'20\'1D Biden also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616bae38f08a1e6c6fcd021#block-6616bae38f08a1e6c6fcd021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he is \u8220\'20\'1Cconsidering\u8221\'20\'1D a request from Australia to end the prosecution of \uc2 WikiLeaks\uc2  founder Julian Assange.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will visit Arizona on Friday as part of her nationwide reproductive freedoms tour. The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616aa918f0812ef07685a36#block-6616aa918f0812ef07685a36"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Harris would highlight \u8220\'20\'1Cextremists\u8221\'20\'1D in the state who are pushing for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans during her visit.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Florida are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/florida-democrats-abortion-ban-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 teaming up}}}\uc2  with operatives from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign in an all-out assault on Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 extremist positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , believing it will bring victory in presidential and Senate races in November.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616d8928f0851e4c4fbd77d#block-6616d8928f0851e4c4fbd77d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  to block the reauthorization of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act, a high-profile warrantless surveillance program that is now in limbo before a 19 April expiration date.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson will meet on Friday with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for a press conference on \u8220\'20\'1Celection integrity\u8221\'20\'1D at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago club, a Trump campaign official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616e3a78f08e55cb7cf3784#block-6616e3a78f08e55cb7cf3784"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 . Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616b5cc8f082302bf6c003e#block-6616b5cc8f082302bf6c003e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 met with}}}\uc2  Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  on Wednesday, marking the first time the two have spoken since Greene filed a motion to vacate the speakership late last month. Greene {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616c5e88f0851e4c4fbd68d#block-6616c5e88f0851e4c4fbd68d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described}}}\uc2  the meeting as \u8220\'20\'1Cpassionate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The independent presidential candidate Cornel West{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616cfe68f08a1e6c6fcd18c#block-6616cfe68f08a1e6c6fcd18c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that Melina Abdullah would serve as his running mate, joining the former Harvard professor\u8217\'20\'19s long-shot bid in the US presidential race.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616eb9d8f0851e4c4fbd844#block-6616eb9d8f0851e4c4fbd844"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  donors and supporters last weekend that he would help raise money for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the Republican presidential candidate, is accused of covering up a $130,000 hush-money payment his former lawyer \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2  made to porn star Stormy Daniels for her silence before the 2016 election about a sexual encounter she says she had with Trump in 2006, Reuters neatly recaps.\par \par \uc2 Trump has pleaded not guilty to 34 counts of falsifying business records and denies any such encounter with Daniels.\par \par \uc2 Judge Juan Merchan has not yet ruled on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s motion for him to recuse himself. The defense has argued that the judge\u8217\'20\'19s daughter\u8217\'20\'19s work for a political consulting firm with Democratic clients poses a conflict of interest.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, a judge at the appellate division denied Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request to delay the case while he pursues a challenge to the trial being held in heavily Democratic Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, another judge rejected his bid to pause the trial while he appeals Merchan\u8217\'20\'19s decision to impose a gag order restricting his public statements about potential witnesses, court staff, lawyers and family members of the judge and district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 . Those appeals will still be heard by a full panel.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Appeals court judge denies Trump's third attempt this week to delay hush-money trial\par \par \uc2 The appeals court judge, just moments after the hearing wrapped up in New York this afternoon, has ruled against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s third attempt this week to delay his hush-money criminal trial\par \par \uc2 Trump was denied his attempt to push back his 15 April trial on charges stemming from hush money paid to porn star Stormy Daniels, paving the way for the first-ever criminal trial of a former US president, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 During an earlier hearing, Trump lawyer Emil Bove said the trial should be delayed because justice Juan Merchan, who is overseeing the case, has not yet ruled on their request for him to recuse himself.\par \par \uc2 Bove also said Merchan was wrong to deny their request to bar prosecutors from presenting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tweets during his 2017-2021 presidential term as evidence. Bove said presidential immunity should prevent the prosecutors from presenting those posts as evidence. At the hearing before associate justice Ellen Gesmer at a mid-level state appeals court called the appellate division, Bove said:\par \par \uc2 We are scheduled to begin trial under circumstances that will violate President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rights.\par \par \uc2 Steven Wu, a lawyer for Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s office, said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers had brought the requests too late, saying:\par \par \uc2 There is a powerful public interest in ensuring that this criminal trial go forward.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 The hearing is over at the appeals court in New York where lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are making the argument for the third time in three days that his hush-money criminal trial should be delayed.\par \par \uc2 Jury selection will begin on Monday, so time is running out for Trump. We await the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 As colleague Cameron Joseph wrote earlier today, this follows a longstanding pattern of Trump freaking out as major threats approach, and his team responding with frenetic energy.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team throws everything it can at the wall, while Trump continues his tirade against presiding judge Juan Merchan \u8211\'20\'13 while pushing the bounds of the judge\u8217\'20\'19s gag order.\par \par \uc2 To get the latest court developments delivered to your inbox, in the Guardian US\u8217\'20\'19s free Trump on Trial newsletter put together by Cameron, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.HesXJ57d0x1owJZ-aZPL3dMFWr92HeUFQk2v_wBSJ_UtgE-pwHb4UgXNOWZZo0YVZJBNA466czTQIHYkKVqTI9FbndSRgUGOn_atIxvHB4OIEEz2m_wGI6wjCftko7YSqEiNbPmSrZeejTR1-VB51WwuNYiT94UB2UJ_xzEXAF5QSlAFlxhKFpiBF8svGcZq7wMrBaIz0ReV5u4mAqGqo4kANeIwLN42wnceS5UTJMGjjUkWemmUd8utPl0YdtJatU65_UySZS8AfkWRKOpWIig8R8crx72fvwppIrhzKafnoGtpmcf8chy9GyYkldyWEsHKigejQbhGnfEtGGbmr_ocBHEATc8xu1hgpCwMAbyTQSB_asDAcZmyahGn5jpuHCguxIfdbdETJU5t1Jj-CEIbLc7KIV9N3FixySwT1Iia-QHmqAys52IsBO4SazxpFlT5oXUwFUn5bg74VXMWdtZgT7PEmyFAvfadHHvIU4TiRf1pUdTYidVomGJl8cVQHbwGT2qbyIYdXJUYzK4848DxigRlE9kK-IsZyyQkUFzc2ej2Y7vQLwDdNs8eKaIFZUpOXdhKRFg5oeI-4C35-m3tFSLNA-x5FmsG2ulx628rMUGct6YIPUbnznFSY29orLmYucD7MT8CbZDvmdX3uF9G9wxCT2e32jgwpVhHHJqbhRSELDIm8BmtIGvcn_MyWeAo5Z_hwko6xPhphUXH5OFGWoHjxFjqgfZEHI77V44qZld_9K_Nzi-KTY8Y77TU/457/PrVEqngtR7-sD-CZoKsWXA/h12/h001.LcdGdO515U7BtrdbPZcRlvVkmJpxxUZNi4FZQvOmeqY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And you can read today\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/trump-on-trial-the-scramble-before-the-storm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have been back in court for almost the last hour trying to stave off the first-ever criminal trial of a former US president, which begins on Monday.\par \par \uc2 In a more technical legal take from NBC, the TV network explains the following:\par \par \uc2 The court docket for the state Appellate Division shows Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys filed the challenge as a lawsuit invoking a provision of New York law known as Article 78. Article 78 challenges allow litigants, whether in ongoing litigation or otherwise, to seek relief from allegedly unlawful state or local government action.\par \par \uc2 The documents were filed under seal. The Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office, which is prosecuting the case, said it involved Judge Juan Merchan \u8217\'20\'19s refusal to step aside from presiding over the case.\par \par \uc2 enltrLawyers for former President Trump head back to a New York appeals court with their third legal challenge involving his impending criminal trial in three days. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kBDIs74KWC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/kBDIs74KWC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NBC News (@NBCNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNews/status/1778117013430235477?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump is a defendant in four criminal cases, two federal and two state. The hush-money case in New York is first up. The Georgia election interference case, the federal election interference case and the federal classified documents case do not have trial dates yet. The presidential election is on 5 November and Trump is the presumptive Republican nominee, prior to his expected anointment at the Republican National Convention this summer.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump tries to delay hush-money trial for third time this week\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers told a New York appeals court judge on Wednesday that the former US president\u8217\'20\'19s 15 April trial should be delayed because the judge has not yet ruled on their motion for him to recuse himself, in his third last-ditch attempt so far this week to delay the case, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The Republican presidential candidate is accused of covering up a $130,000 hush-money payment his former lawyer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michael-cohen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Cohen}}}\uc2  made to porn star {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/stormy-daniels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stormy Daniels}}}\uc2  for her silence ahead of the 2016 election about a sexual encounter she says she had with Trump in 2006.\par \par \uc2 Trump has pleaded not guilty to 34 counts of falsifying business records and denies any such encounter with Daniels.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, a judge at a mid-level state appeals court known as the appellate division denied Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request to delay the case while he pursues a challenge to the trial being held in heavily Democratic Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 And on Tuesday, another judge rejected his bid to pause the trial while he appeals Judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/02/trump-hush-money-trial-judge-removal-attempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Juan Merchan}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision to impose a gag order restricting his public statements about potential witnesses, court staff, lawyers, and family members of the judge and the Manhattan district attorney, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/who-is-alvin-bragg-donald-trump-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alvin Bragg}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Those appeals will still be heard by a full panel. Jury selection is scheduled to begin in the trial on Monday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , told donors and supporters last weekend that he would help raise money for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, who dropped out of the Republican presidential race in January, told his allies about his plans to help his former rival during a private gathering at the Hard Rock Hotel in south Florida, a DeSantis adviser told NBC News.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is \u8220\'20\'1Ccommitted to helping Trump in any and every way\u8221\'20\'1D, said Texas businessman Roy Bailey, who attended the retreat. He said:\par \par \uc2 I will follow the governor\u8217\'20\'19s lead and I will do anything that he or President Trump ask me to do to help him win this election.\par \par \uc2 A Trump campaign adviser said they were not aware that the Florida governor was going to start raising money for them but added that \u8220\'20\'1Ceveryone should be working towards defeating \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and electing President Trump\u8221\'20\'1D, NBC reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , during a joint press conference with the Japanese prime minister, \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , at the White House, said Japan\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to set up a leader-to-leader summit with North Korea is \u8220\'20\'1Ca good thing\u8221\'20\'1D as he reiterated his administration\u8217\'20\'19s willingness for its own talks without preconditions.\par \par \uc2 Biden said:\par \par \uc2 We welcome the opportunity of our allies to initiate dialogue with the Democratic People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of Korea. As I\u8217\'20\'19ve said many times, we\u8217\'20\'19re open to dialogue ourselves without preconditions with the DPRK.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has repeatedly expressed openness to talks with North Korean leader Kim Jong-un, but has never received a response.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson will meet on Friday with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for a press conference on \u8220\'20\'1Celection integrity\u8221\'20\'1D, a Trump campaign official said.\par \par \uc2 The press conference is scheduled to take place at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago club, AP reported, citing a source as saying that Johnson and Trump will have a \u8220\'20\'1Cjoint announcement\u8221\'20\'1D on Friday.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS w/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KristenhCNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KristenhCNN}}}\uc2  : Speaker Mike Johnson is making plans to deliver a joint press conference with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at Mar-a-Lago on Friday, focused on "election integrity," per sources.\par \par \uc2 Plans still fluid, but comes as Johnson is facing a threat to his speakership from MTG.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Melanie Zanona (@MZanona) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MZanona/status/1778099268542255405?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 When the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022, Republicans across the country cheered. Freed from Roe\u8217\'20\'19s regulations, GOP lawmakers promptly blanketed the US south and midwest in near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 But today, after a string of electoral losses, stories of women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/16/abortion-ban-lawsuits-pregnancy-complication-emergency-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being denied abortions}}}\uc2  and polls that confirm \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans remain wildly unpopular, the political calculus has changed. Republicans are now trying to slow down the car whose brakes they cut \u8211\'20\'13 and to convince voters that, if the car crashes, they had nothing to do with it anyway.\par \par \uc2 Nowhere encapsulates the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s backpedal on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  better than Arizona, whose state supreme court on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled to let an 1864 near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban go into effect}}}\uc2 . That ban, which outlaws \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all cases except to save the life of a woman, was passed before Arizona became a state, before the end of the civil war and before women gained the right to vote.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/trump-arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full analysis by the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive health and justice reporter: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/trump-arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban is a political nightmare for Republicans in the 2024 election}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/trump-arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban is a political nightmare for Republicans in the 2024 election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House has voted to block the reauthorization of section 702 of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act, a high-profile warrantless surveillance program that is now in limbo ahead of a 19 April expiration date.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have been fiercely divided over how to handle the issue, and Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s vote comes months after a similar process to reform and reauthorize the program fell apart before it even reached the House floor.\par \par \uc2 The law allows the \uc2 US government\uc2  to collect the communications of targeted foreigners abroad by compelling service providers to produce copies of messages and internet data, or networks to intercept and turn over phone call and message data.\par \par \uc2 It is controversial because it allows the government to incidentally collect messages and phone data of Americans without a court order if they interacted with the foreign target, even though the law prohibits section 702 from being used by the \uc2 National Security Agency\uc2  to specifically target US citizens.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was asked what he would say to the people of Arizona following the state supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling to let a law banning almost all abortions in the state go into effect.\par \par \uc2 The president, referring to the 1864 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban which passed when Arizona was still a territory, replied:\par \par \uc2 Elect me. I\u8217\'20\'19m in the 20th century \u8230\'20\'26 21st century \u8230\'20\'26 not back then. They weren\u8217\'20\'19t even a state.\par \par \uc2 From the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s JM Rieger:\par \par \uc2 enltrREPORTER: On the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , what do you say to the people of Arizona right now...?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Elect me. I'm in the 20th century \u8212\'20\'14 21st century, not back then. They weren't even a state. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0T2ASk1E0w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0T2ASk1E0w}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 JM Rieger (@RiegerReport) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RiegerReport/status/1778120318650810716?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cornel West \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that Melina Abdullah would serve as his running mate comes as West, an author and leftwing activist, continues his efforts to get on the ballot in every US state.\par \par \uc2 West\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said he had already secured ballot access in Alaska, Oregon, South Carolina and Utah, but some states require a running mate for independent candidates to get on the ballot. As part of his 50-state campaign, West announced in January that he would launch a new political party, called the Justice for All party, to help ease his path to ballot access in some states.\par \par \uc2 West has no path to victory, as national polls show his support languishing in the low single digits. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.marquette.edu/poll/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/MLSPSC19ToplinesLV.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  conducted last month by the Marquette Law School found that just 4% of likely US voters named West as their preferred candidate.\par \par \uc2 But West\u8217\'20\'19s presence on the ballot in key battleground states could draw support away from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , raising concerns among Democrats that the independent candidate might serve as a spoiler for the incumbent president.\par \par \uc2 According to a \uc2 Quinnipiac University{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poll.qu.edu/images/polling/us/us03272024_regvoter_uyex26.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  of US voters conducted last month, Biden leads \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by three points, 48% to 45%, in a head-to-head match-up, but the president\u8217\'20\'19s support dipped down to 38% (compared with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 39%) when third-party candidates such as West, \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  and Jill Stein of the Green party were listed as options.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cornel West announces running mate for independent presidential bid\par \par \uc2 The independent presidential candidat e Cornel West announced on Wednesday that Melina Abdullah would serve as his running mate, joining the former Harvard professor\u8217\'20\'19s long-shot bid in the US presidential race.\par \par \uc2 Abdullah, a professor of Pan-African Studies at California State University, Los Angeles, helped to form the LA chapter of the group \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2 , and West praised her as \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the great freedom fighters of her generation\u8221\'20\'1D. West told the talkshow host Tavis Smiley on Wednesday":\par \par \uc2 I wanted somebody whose heart, mind and soul is committed to the empowerment of poor and working peoples of all colors. And Melina has a history of longevity, of putting her heart, mind, soul and body in the struggle.\par \par \uc2 Abdullah told Smiley that West\u8217\'20\'19s offer took her by surprise, but she quickly accepted because of her belief in his \u8220\'20\'1Cplatform of truth, love and justice\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CHow can you not get behind that platform?\u8221\'20\'1D Abdullah said.\par \par \uc2 So I\u8217\'20\'19ve been following him and had been really enthusiastic about his candidacy and just was excited to be able to share space with him.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Florida are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/florida-democrats-abortion-ban-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 teaming up with }}}\uc2  operatives from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign in an all-out assault on Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 extremist positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , believing it will bring victory in presidential and Senate races in November.\par \par \uc2 They fired an opening salvo on Tuesday, tearing into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cboasting\u8221\'20\'1D about overturning federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a day earlier}}}\uc2 , and assailing the incumbent Republican senator \uc2 Rick Scott{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/3949607-rick-scott-on-6-week-abortion-ban-if-i-was-still-governor-i-would-sign-this-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for supporting}}}\uc2  Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban that takes effect next month.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Republican Florida governor and former candidate for the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed the ban into law}}}\uc2 , also found himself under fire.\par \par \uc2 The Florida supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/01/florida-abortion-right-constitution-vote-november-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled last week}}}\uc2  that the six-week ban will take effect on 1 May, as well as allowing a ballot measure for November that could see voters enshrine the right to the procedure into law.\par \par \uc2 The moves instantly propelled the state to the forefront of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate, and allowed Democrats, all but wiped out in Florida in successive national elections, to seize on the issue as vote-winner.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/florida-democrats-abortion-ban-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida Democrats bet \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  will motivate swell of voters who feel bans go \u8216\'20\'18too far\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump 'owns suffering and chaos happening right now', says Biden campaign on Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has released a statement following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s criticism of the Arizona \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, warning that he has previously \u8220\'20\'1C[banned] \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  every chance he gets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the Biden campaign said that Trump will enact a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban given his track record, adding that the former president \u8220\'20\'1Cproudly overturned Roe\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  owns the suffering and chaos happening right now, including in Arizona, because he proudly overturned Roe \u8211\'20\'13 something he called \u8216\'20\'18\u8220\'20\'1Can incredible thing\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8216\'20\'18\u8220\'20\'1Cpretty amazing\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D just today.\par \par \uc2 Trump lies constantly \u8211\'20\'13 about everything \u8211\'20\'13 but has one track record: banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  every chance he gets. The guy who wants to be a dictator on day one will use every tool at his disposal to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, with or without Congress, and running away from reporters to his private jet like a coward doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change that reality.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Greene added that Johnson asked if she was \u8220\'20\'1Cinterested\u8221\'20\'1D in being apart of a group of advisers for him.\par \par \uc2 Green said:\par \par \uc2 I said, \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19ll wait and see what his proposal is on that.\u8217\'20\'19 Right now. he does not have my support, and I\u8217\'20\'19m watching what happens with FISA and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Greene added that she told Johnson he \u8220\'20\'1Cfailed\u8221\'20\'1D on the latest government spending dealing and received \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot of excuses\u8221\'20\'1D in return.\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. MTG after Johnson meeting says she explained her positions on FISA, Ukraine aid and how he \u8220\'20\'1Cfailed\u8221\'20\'1D them on the govt spending deal\par \par \uc2 Says she got a \u8220\'20\'1Clot of excuses\u8221\'20\'1D of how that happened\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1778101680044908554?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrGreene said he discussed having a kitchen cabinet group that would be a group of advisers for him and asked her if she \u8220\'20\'1Cwas interested.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI said, \u8216\'20\'18I'll wait and see what his proposal is on that.\u8217\'20\'19 Right now. he does not have my support, and I'm watching what happens with FISA\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/V7LMlxGCTt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/V7LMlxGCTt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1778102618776281239?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, Mike Johnson, and Congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  have concluded their meeting, with varying descriptions on how it went.\par \par \uc2 The meeting, which lasted over an hour, came after Greene filed a motion to vacate the speakership.\par \par \uc2 Greene described the meeting as \u8220\'20\'1Cpassionate\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JulieNBCNews/status/1778104290692735274"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reported}}}\uc2 . When asked if the meeting was \u8220\'20\'1Cproductive\u8221\'20\'1D, Greene said:\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19d have to completely change everything he\u8217\'20\'19s done to be productive.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Johnson gave a more diplomatic answer, calling Greene a \u8220\'20\'1Cfriend\u8221\'20\'1D even as the two Republicans have differed on \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s a colleague. I\u8217\'20\'19ve always considered her a friend \u8230\'20\'26 Marjorie and I don\u8217\'20\'19t disagree on philosophy. We\u8217\'20\'19re both conservatives. Sometimes we disagree on strategy.\par \par \uc2 From Punchbowl News\u8217\'20\'19 Mica Soellner:\par \par \uc2 enltrMTG on if she would describe the Johnson meeting as productive: "He'd have to completely change everything he's done to be productive."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mica Soellner (@MicaSoellnerDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MicaSoellnerDC/status/1778105552901489021?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrJOHNSON on MTG meeting today: "She's a colleague. I've always considered her a friend... Marjorie and I don't disagree on philosophy. We're both conservatives. Sometimes we disagree on strategy."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mica Soellner (@MicaSoellnerDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MicaSoellnerDC/status/1778071429507936498?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says 'no' when asked if he would sign national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as president\par \par \uc2 Trump also said that he would not sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if elected president in 2024, ABC News reported.\par \par \uc2 Trump further clarified his position while speaking with reporters on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In response to the question of if he would sign an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Trump said \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D and shook his head.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump says that Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling went too far: \u8220\'20\'1CYeah they did, and that will be straightened out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Also tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ABC}}}\uc2  he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as president. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wQdByVodtv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wQdByVodtv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lalee Ibssa (@LaleeIbssa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LaleeIbssa/status/1778096064853168414?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The latest remarks from Trump come as Democrats have warned that he would authorize an extreme ban if elected, noting how federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights were overturned due to supreme court judges secured during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says Arizona \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went too far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/10/trump-biden-campaign-election-abortion-ban-latest-updates?page=with:block-6616b97c8f08400b17aa820b#block-6616b97c8f08400b17aa820b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more }}}\uc2  from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comments to reporters while at a campaign event in Atlanta after the Arizona state supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling upholding a 1864 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 Asked if Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s ruling went too far, Trump replied:\par \par \uc2 Yeah, they did. That will be straightened out. As you know, it\u8217\'20\'19s all about state\u8217\'20\'19s rights. It will be straightened out. I\u8217\'20\'19m sure the governor and everybody else are going to bring it back into reason and that it will be taken care of, I think, very quickly.\par \par \uc2 enltrQ: "Did Arizona go too far?"\par \par \uc2 Former President Trump: "Yeah, they did. That'll be straightened out. As you know it's all about state's rights. It'll be straightened out. I'm sure that the governor and everybody else are going bring it back to within reason..." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Dc9qluxemc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Dc9qluxemc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1778092841484333298?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden 'considering' dropping prosecution of Julian Assange\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he is considering a request from Australia to end the prosecution of \uc2 WikiLeaks\uc2  founder Julian Assange.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the request as he hosted the Japanese prime minister, \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , Biden replied:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re considering it.\par \par \uc2 Assange, an Australian citizen, faces 18 charges over \uc2 WikiLeaks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 publication of classified documents, largely the result of a leak by the former US army intelligence analyst \uc2 Chelsea Manning\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Assange, 52, has been fighting US extradition efforts from the UK\u8217\'20\'19s Belmarsh prison, where he has been since 2019 for skipping bail during a separate legal battle.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has told reporters he believes the Arizona supreme court went too far with its ruling, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Alayna Treene reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump, 2 days after saying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy should be left to the states, tells reporters he thinks the Arizona Supreme Court went too far in their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, they did, and that\u8217\'20\'19ll be straightened out and as you know it\u8217\'20\'19s all about states\u8217\'20\'19 rights"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alayna Treene (@alaynatreene) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alaynatreene/status/1778089969006825824?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 A closely watched measure of US inflation picked up in March, rising to an annual rate of 3.5%, the Department of Labor announced on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The consumer-price index (CPI) \u8211\'20\'13 which measures a broad range of goods and services \u8211\'20\'13 rose 0.4% from February, higher than the 0.3% expected. Core CPI, which removes the volatile food and energy categories, rose 0.4% from February in contrast to an expected 0.3%.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the report showed his administration has \u8220\'20\'1Cmore to do to lower costs for hardworking families\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 Fighting inflation remains my top economic priority. We\u8217\'20\'19re making progress: wages are rising faster than prices, incomes are higher than before the pandemic, and unemployment has remained below 4% for the longest stretch in 50 years. But we have more to do.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/apr/10/us-inflation-march-cpi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rising home and gas costs pushed US inflation higher than expected in March}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson and \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  to meet today\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, Mike Johnson, is expected to meet with fellow Republican Congress member \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  today, marking the first time the two have spoken since Greene filed a motion to vacate the speakership late last month.\par \par \uc2 Johnson and Greene were slated to speak last Friday, but that plan reportedly fell through. Asked about the upcoming meeting during a press conference alongside other House GOP leaders, Johnson described Greene as \u8220\'20\'1Ca friend\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 Marjorie and I don\u8217\'20\'19t disagree, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think, on any matter of philosophy. We\u8217\'20\'19re both conservatives. But we do disagree sometimes on strategy and with regard to what we put on the floor and when and those things.\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Speaker Mike Johnson (R-LA) says he will meet with Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  (R-GA) \u8212\'20\'14 who filed a motion to vacate him as Speaker \u8212\'20\'14 later today:\par \par \uc2 "I consider her a friend... Marjorie is frustrated by the last set of appropriations bills... And you know what? So am I." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/isvdSihq2u"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/isvdSihq2u}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1778091877645856860?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The meeting comes a day after Greene escalated her criticism against Johnson in a scathing memo to colleagues in which she accused him of a \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplete and total surrender\u8221\'20\'1D to the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 agenda.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The far-right Florida Republican \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  forced Kevin McCarthy out as House speaker last year \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause he slept with a 17-year-old\u8221\'20\'1D and wanted a congressional ethics investigation to end, McCarthy charged on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll give you the truth why I\u8217\'20\'19m not speaker,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HowardMortman/status/1778025391304691957"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , at an event at \uc2 Georgetown University in Washington\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Because one person, a member of Congress, wanted me to stop an ethics complaint because he slept with a 17-year-old, an ethics complaint that started before I ever became speaker. And that\u8217\'20\'19s illegal and I\u8217\'20\'19m not gonna get in the middle of it. Now, did he do it or not? I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. But ethics was looking at it. There\u8217\'20\'19s other people in jail because of it. And he wanted me to influence it.\par \par \uc2 The House ethics investigation of allegations against Gaetz opened in 2021, when \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , a Democrat, was speaker. The House investigation was paused when Gaetz was investigated by the Department of Justice for sex trafficking, over allegations that he paid for sex and had sex with an underage woman. In December 2022, \uc2 Joel Greenberg\uc2 , a former Florida tax collector whose arrest led to the investigation of Gaetz, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/joel-greenberg-sentenced-sex-crimes-freind-matt-gaetz/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sentenced}}}\uc2  to 11 years in prison for offences including sex trafficking a minor.\par \par \uc2 In February 2023, prosecutors said they would not issue charges. The House ethics investigation then restarted. Gaetz denies wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is learning the hard way that there is no middle ground on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  inside the Republican party, NBC News\u8217\'20\'19 Chuck Todd {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/elections/chuck-todd-politicians-need-middle-win-s-getting-harder-find-rcna147129?cid=eml_mrd_20240410"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president is hoping that he can separate himself from the most restrictive positions on the issue, he says.\par \par \uc2 Ironically, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s controversial position shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t, in theory, be controversial in the GOP. Trump is simply espousing what the party said it supported for decades before the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 2022 Dobbs decision: Leave it to the states. But \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  conservatives want to go further with a federal limit. As is now fairly clear, simply returning the decision over reproductive rights to the states wasn\u8217\'20\'19t really the goal of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement pre-Dobbs. The goal was to roll back access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in whatever expedient way they could find.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Arizona \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is even dividing Republican families, according to Politico Playbook.\par \par \uc2 Clint Bolick is one of the four Arizona supreme court justices who supported reinstating the 1864 law.\par \par \uc2 His wife, Arizona state senator Shawnna Bolick, who faces a tough re-election this year, repudiated the effect of the court decision, posting to social media on Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 Considering today\u8217\'20\'19s Arizona Supreme Court ruling to uphold Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s 1864 territorial \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, it is time for my legislative colleagues to find common ground of common sense: the first step is to repeal the territorial law.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs a state legislator, I have worked on protecting all lives, especially the most vulnerable, from the earliest moments of life to protecting women's health by providing safe housing and a nurturing community for homeless pregnant women. Considering today\u8217\'20\'19s Arizona Supreme Court\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9kV9rmvuFP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9kV9rmvuFP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shawnna LM Bolick (@ShawnnaLMBolick) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ShawnnaLMBolick/status/1777780212748738731?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to visit Arizona as part of reproductive freedoms tour\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will visit Arizona as part of her nationwide reproductive freedoms tour, just days after the state supreme court upheld a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president will appear in Tucson on Friday, her office announced on Tuesday after the court decision, although her visit had reportedly already been scheduled.\par \par \uc2 The White House said Harris would highlight \u8220\'20\'1Cextremists\u8221\'20\'1D in the state who were pushing for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans during her visit.\par \par \uc2 Harris issued a statement following the Arizona ruling, laying the blame on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for rolling \u8220\'20\'1Cthe clock to a time before women could vote\u8221\'20\'1D. Last month she said the former president had handpicked three members of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause he intended for them to overturn Roe \u8230\'20\'26 He intended for them to take your freedoms, and he brags about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Arizona Supreme Court ruling allows an 1864 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to go into effect. There are no exceptions for rape and incest, and it threatens doctors and nurses with prison time.\par \par \uc2 It does not have to be this way. Congress must restore the protections of Roe. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JGdA7RNI2W"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JGdA7RNI2W}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@VP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP/status/1777778284438118621?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden hails 'unbreakable' US-Japanese ties as he welcomes Kishida to White House\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  welcomed Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , to the White House this morning as he hailed \u8220\'20\'1Cunbreakable\u8221\'20\'1D US-Japanese ties and lauded the Japanese leader\u8217\'20\'19s quick \u8220\'20\'1Ccourageous\u8221\'20\'1D opposition to \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s full-fledged invasion of Ukraine and for improving relations with South Korea\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COurs is truly a global partnership. For that, Mr Prime Minister Kishida, I thank you,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Now our two countries are building a stronger defense partnership and a strong Indo-Pacific than ever before.\par \par \uc2 Kishida will address Congress on Thursday and join Biden and the president of the Philippines, \uc2 Ferdinand Marcos Jr\uc2 , for a meeting expected to focus on Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s South China Sea incursions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Arizona supreme court decision upended \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s gambit on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a day after the former president sought to neutralize the political issue by declining to support a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Trump had hoped that his announcement on Monday would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights mostly out of the conversation ahead of the November elections, but Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling showed just how difficult it will be to do that, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Dan Balz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/04/09/trump-abortion-arizona-court-decision/?email=620bb4708d235157723d480a0d8d4c265e55ec14&emaila=0ec8b2addfecba6de47e145bbfa10867&emailb=fa17fe37520b9c9752208dccf233e286aef975565778b97fc6ff23ae2388d5a7&utm_source=Sailthru&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=4.10.24%20BN%20Morning%20Wednesday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 All \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics are national, not local. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  developments \u8211\'20\'13 new laws, new restrictions, new stories of women caught up in heart-wrenching and sometimes life-threatening decisions \u8211\'20\'13 are no longer confined to the geography where they take place. They are instantly part of the larger debate.\par \par \uc2 Trump is correct about the dangers to Republicans of continuing the debate about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, Balz says, but the former president has abandoned those whose interests he once vowed to serve.\par \par \uc2 There is no safe harbor for Trump and the Republicans at this point. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue is no less complex and no less difficult for many Americans than it was while Roe was in force. But politically the winds have shifted, and done so dramatically.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 For more than a year, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  declined to say when in a pregnancy he would try to draw the line, even as Republican-led states have ushered in a wave of new restrictions and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups pressured him and other Republican presidential candidates to endorse a federal ban on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 In his statement on Monday, Trump did not say whether he would sign into law a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if he were president and Congress passed a federal limit. Neither did he say how he, as a resident of Florida, would vote on a ballot measure that would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into that state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 Democrats, who have made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a central issue of the election, said Trump supported laws in the more than two dozens states that have imposed outright bans or restrictions on the procedure since Roe v Wade was overturned.\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail, Trump has been ambivalent on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He routinely takes credit for appointing the supreme court justices who set the stage for the elimination of Roe v Wade, which he has called a \u8220\'20\'1Cmoral and unconstitutional atrocity\u8221\'20\'1D. He has also called himself the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost pro-life president in American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But he has repeatedly dismissed as too extreme fellow Republicans who oppose exceptions to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in cases of rape, incest and when the life of the pregnant person is at risk. And he has said being too hardline on the issue cost Republicans at the polls in the 2022 midterms and could do so again when he challenges Biden in November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Arizona state supreme court decision came a day after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  declined to endorse a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying that it should be left up to individual states.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stated position}}}\uc2  on Monday dashed hopes of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, which want a federal ban, and drew the ire of Democrats, who blame Trump for outright bans and severe restrictions already in place across the south and midwest.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112235238031827342"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a four-minute video post}}}\uc2  on Truth Social, Trump said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cup to the states to do the right thing\u8221\'20\'1D while also touting his work to confirm the conservative supreme court justices who ultimately overturned Roe v Wade in 2022. \u8220\'20\'1CStates will determine by vote or legislation, or perhaps both,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Whatever they decide must be the law of the land, or in this case the law of the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany states will be different, many will have a different number of weeks, some will be more conservative than others,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 At the end of the day this is all about the will of the people. You must follow your heart, or in many cases your religion or faith.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 Do what\u8217\'20\'19s right for your family, and do what\u8217\'20\'19s right for yourself.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  CFO \uc2 Allen Weisselberg\uc2  sentenced to five months for perjury\par \par \uc2 Allen Weisselberg\uc2 , a longtime lieutenant to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has been sentenced to five months in jail after pleading guilty last month to perjury in the former president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/16/donald-trump-financial-fraud-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent civil fraud trial}}}\uc2  charges.\par \par \uc2 As the former chief financial officer in the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , Weisselberg was key in helping Trump record his net worth. A defendant in the fraud trial, Weisselberg was accused of helping to inflate Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/02/16/nyregion/engoron-judge-highlights.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 net worth}}}\uc2  on government financial documents, misleading lenders.\par \par \uc2 On the witness stand in October, Weisselberg, 76, was evasive, often saying he did not recall the real-estate valuations that were at the center of the trial. But a key moment of his testimony came when Weisselberg insisted he did not notice a discrepancy on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s financial statements: that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s triplex apartment was listed as being 30,000 sq ft when, in reality, it was closer to 11,000 sq ft.\par \par \uc2 Forbes\uc2  magazine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/danalexander/2023/10/12/trumps-longtime-cfo-lied-under-oath-about-trump-tower-penthouse/?sh=6c72eda7db29"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disputed}}}\uc2  the claim he made on the stand, saying it had emails and notes that proved Weisselberg had actively tried to convince the magazine for years that the triplex was bigger than it actually was, denying what was listed on real-estate documents. Weisselberg abruptly ended his testimony after Forbes published an article accusing him of lying on the stand.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 'We are not closing. Ever': Arizona \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers react to ban\par \par \uc2 While the long-term impact of the decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Arizona is not yet clear, a number of providers said on Tuesday that they will stay open as long as they can.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Arizona, which operates multiple locations in the state, intends to continue providing abortions as long as the procedure is legal. Thanks to a court order in a separate case, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  appears to be able to legally provide abortions beyond the 14-day window and potentially as late as into May.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRegardless of today\u8217\'20\'19s decision, what I can tell you is that our doors will remain open,\u8221\'20\'1D Angela Florez, president and CEO of Planned Parenthood Arizona, told reporters on a call after the supreme court decision.\par \par \uc2 We will continue to provide what essential healthcare we can within the limitations of the law, and we hope that supporters will continue to support and that patients will still continue to feel safe in our care.\par \par \uc2 Dr Gabrielle Goodrick, a longtime \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in Phoenix, also told the Guardian that her clinic will continue offering abortions, at least through the 14-day window. Goodrick said.\par \par \uc2 We are not closing. Ever. That\u8217\'20\'19s not a question. I have reassurances from the governor and the attorney general that they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to prosecute, but I need to investigate that further.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Voters in Arizona may be able to weigh in on the issue in November: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters in the state have spent months gathering signatures for a ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution, and the Tuesday decision raises the stakes for their efforts significantly.\par \par \uc2 If it succeeds, the ballot measure would declare that people in Arizona have a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.arizona.vote/electioninfo/assets/47/0/BallotMeasures/I-05-2024%20Arizona%20for%20Abortion%20Access.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fundamental right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and that the state will not try to curb that right before a pregnancy reaches fetal viability, which is generally pegged to about 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Although ballot measures need to amass 383,923 signatures by July to get on the ballot, the organizers behind the Arizona measure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/arizona-abortion-rights-amendment-backers-says-gathered-signatures-nee-rcna145922"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced last week}}}\uc2  that they have gathered more than 500,000 signatures, and plan to collect more.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans who embraced Roe v Wade reversal criticize Arizona ruling\par \par \uc2 Hours after the Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruling, Republicans in the state took a surprising stance for a party that has historically championed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions \u8211\'20\'13 they denounced the decision.\par \par \uc2 Some of the criticisms of the Tuesday ruling came from politicians who had previously supported the 1864 ban or cheered the end of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, a Republican and loyalist of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  running to represent Arizona in the Senate, previously called the ban a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat law\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2022/oct/12/katie-hobbs/az-gop-governor-hopeful-lake-called-near-total-abo/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to PolitiFact}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 David Schweikert\uc2 , an Arizona congressman who is facing one of the most competitive House races in the country this November, said he does not support the ruling, but in 2022 said the fall of Roe \u8220\'20\'1Cpleased\u8221\'20\'1D him.\par \par \uc2 enltrI do not support today\u8217\'20\'19s ruling from the AZ Supreme Court. This issue should be decided by Arizonans, not legislated from the bench. I encourage the state legislature to address this issue immediately.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 David Schweikert\uc2  (@RepDavid) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepDavid/status/1777778129483780533?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Juan Ciscomani, another Republican congressman for Arizona, said the ruling was \u8220\'20\'1Ca disaster for women and providers\u8221\'20\'1D and that the law was \u8220\'20\'1Carchaic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on the Arizona Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling today. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A1Do8AjYlb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/A1Do8AjYlb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congressman Juan Ciscomani (@RepCiscomani) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepCiscomani/status/1777757519504380389?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The speaker of the Arizona house, Ben Toma, and the president of the state senate, Warren Petersen, who are both Republicans, also released a joint statement saying that they would be \u8220\'20\'1Clistening to our constituents to determine the best course of action for the legislature\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, on the day Roe fell, the Republican-controlled state senate released a statement declaring that the 1864 ban was in effect immediately. That statement unleashed confusion and chaos among \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in Arizona, prompting them to stop offering the procedure out of an abundance of caution.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona's Democratic attorney general vows not to prosecute doctors or women under ban\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic attorney general, Kris Mayes, vowed not to prosecute any doctors or women under the 1864 ban.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in a news conference after the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision was published, Mayes said:\par \par \uc2 No woman or doctor will be prosecuted under this draconian law \u8230\'20\'26 as long as I am attorney general. Not by me, nor by any county attorney serving in our state. Not on my watch.\par \par \uc2 Her office is looking to pursue options available to ensure the law is not implemented in the state, she added.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azag.gov/press-release/attorney-general-mayes-statement-planned-parenthood-az-v-mayes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  statement}}}\uc2 , Mayes described the state supreme court decision as \u8220\'20\'1Cunconscionable\u8221\'20\'1D and an \u8220\'20\'1Caffront to freedom\u8221\'20\'1D, and said the court had \u8220\'20\'1Crisked the health and lives of Arizonans\u8221\'20\'1D. She continued:\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s decision to reimpose a law from a time when Arizona wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a state, the Civil War was raging, and women couldn\u8217\'20\'19t even vote will go down in history as a stain on our state.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Arizona governor, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , a Democrat, said Tuesday was a \u8220\'20\'1Cdark day\u8221\'20\'1D for the state following the ruling and implored \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters to make their voices heard in November.\par \par \uc2 Hobbs said the court decision was a sign that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe fight for our reproductive freedoms is far from over\u8221\'20\'1D. In a statement on Tuesday, she said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve personally experienced the anguish of losing a pregnancy and I know it\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous to have the government tell you that the best decision for your health or future could now be considered a crime. I will not stop fighting until we have fully secured the right to reproductive healthcare in our state.\par \par \uc2 The governor last year issued a sweeping executive order banning county attorneys from prosecuting women who seek abortions and doctors who perform them.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to CNN hours after the court ruling, Hobbs said she was confident that voters will have the opportunity to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in November and reverse the decision. She added:\par \par \uc2 This is a commonsense measure that is supported by the vast majority of Arizonans in terms of protecting access. And you know, certainly it\u8217\'20\'19s going to motivate voters in November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans rush to distance themselves from 1864 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics/all"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  readers. The Arizona supreme court \u8217\'20\'19s decision on Tuesday to let {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 160-year-old \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  in the state go into effect pushed Republicans into a new political dilemma, coming as it did just a day after \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared that}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left to individual states.\par \par \uc2 First passed when Arizona was still a territory, the ban only permits abortions to save a patient\u8217\'20\'19s life and does not have exceptions for rape or incest. \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision cannot stand,\u8221\'20\'1D said Matt Gress, a Republican state representative.\par \par \uc2 I categorically reject rolling back the clock to a time when slavery was still legal and we could lock up women and doctors because of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI oppose today\u8217\'20\'19s ruling,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kari Lake, a Republican running to represent Arizona in the Senate and a Trump loyalist. Lake called on the state legislature to \u8220\'20\'1Ccome up with an immediate commonsense solution that Arizonans can support\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 David Schweikert\uc2 , the most vulnerable Republican in the state, also denounced the ruling and said the issue \u8220\'20\'1Cshould be decided by Arizonans, not legislated from the bench\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have struggled to find a way to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, leading the GOP to stumble in the 2022 midterms and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters to win a string of ballot measures. Their latest response to the Arizona ruling may mark their fastest and strongest rebuke of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans since Roe fell. Some of the criticisms of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling came from politicians who had previously supported the 1864 ban or cheered the end of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am ET. \uc2 USAID\uc2  administrator \uc2 Samantha Power\uc2  will testify before the foreign relations committee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the first lady, Jill Biden, will welcome the Japanese prime minister, FumioKishida, and his wife, Yuko Kishida, on the South Lawn.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 12.30pm. Biden and Kishida will hold a joint press conference in the Rose Garden.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240410ek4a00231\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
