\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Florida Democrats bet  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  will motivate swell of voters who feel bans go \u8216\'20\'18too far\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe in Miami \par \uc2 801 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par 21:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats team up with Biden campaign on issue, believing it will bring victory in presidential and Senate races in November\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Florida are teaming up with operatives from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign in an all-out assault on Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 extremist positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , believing it will bring victory in presidential and \uc2 US Senate\uc2  races in November.\par \par \uc2 They fired an opening salvo on Tuesday, tearing into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cboasting\u8221\'20\'1D about overturning federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a day earlier}}}\uc2 , and assailing the incumbent Republican senator \uc2 Rick Scott{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/3949607-rick-scott-on-6-week-abortion-ban-if-i-was-still-governor-i-would-sign-this-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for supporting}}}\uc2  Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban that takes effect next month.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Republican Florida governor and former candidate for the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed the ban into law}}}\uc2 , also found himself under fire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe word is accountability,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2 , chair of the Florida Democratic party, told an online launch meeting attended by Jasmine Burney-Clark, state director of the Biden-Harris campaign, and Democratic state representative \uc2 Anna Eskamani\uc2 , a former regional senior director of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  bragged about overturning Roe v Wade. Then we got here in Florida because we had an individual who wanted to run for president and wanted to take our state into extremism, the Republican legislature who voted for it, and \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 who said on the national stage he will push for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s incumbent on all of us, the party, the candidates, the campaigns, to make sure that we are making that very distinct link.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Florida supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/01/florida-abortion-right-constitution-vote-november-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled last week}}}\uc2  that the six-week ban will take effect on 1 May, as well as allowing a ballot measure for November that could see voters enshrine the right to the procedure into law.\par \par \uc2 The moves instantly propelled the state to the forefront of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate, and allowed Democrats, all but wiped out in Florida in successive national elections, to seize on the issue as vote-winner.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen across our state, since the falling of Roe, is a very broad coalition of Republicans, independents, Democrats, coming together to make sure we had the requisite signatures to get in front of the supreme court and ultimately on to the ballot,\u8221\'20\'1D Fried said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is the kind of coalition that you\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue to see, people across the spectrum, in Key West or Pensacola, different demographics coming from different backgrounds \u8230\'20\'26 the coalition is broad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fried and Eskamani were both careful to point out that the Democratic party was independent of the campaign supporting the ballot initiative, but Eskamani said they could provide information for voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven Republicans agree what has happened in Florida, and across the country, is too far, and in fact 35% of those who signed the petition to help codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are Republican,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo these are completely separate campaigns, but I do think we\u8217\'20\'19re going to see a continuation of a broad coalition of support for reproductive rights and holding all these different bad actors accountable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Burney-Clark\u8217\'20\'19s presence, meanwhile, was further indication that Democrats believe Florida, won comfortably by Trump in 2020, could be back in play for Biden this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  owns Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and he owns every single thing that happens as a result,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/08/trump-truth-social-abortion-ban-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6613fdc58f089151b4b25ffb#block-6613fdc58f089151b4b25ffb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said it best}}}\uc2 , if Trump is elected, and Republicans in Congress put a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on the Resolute Desk, Trump will sign it into law. Trump is endorsing dangerous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans across the country like Florida\u8217\'20\'19s that are only possible because of him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBans that go into effect before women know they are pregnant, like the one that will soon happen here in Florida; women turned away from emergency rooms, forced to go to court to seek permission for medical attention they need to survive; doctors threatened with criminal charges for doing their jobs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden and Vice-President Harris are the only choice for Floridians who want to make sure they get to make their own reproductive decisions. It is just that simple.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The next broadside of the Florida Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 campaign will come on Wednesday, when former congresswoman \uc2 Debbie Mucarsel-Powell\uc2 , who is challenging Scott for his Senate seat, launches her statewide, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -themed \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida freedom tour\u8221\'20\'1D in West Palm Beach.\par \par \uc2 Her campaign believes Scott, who ousted the incumbent Democrat \uc2 Bill Nelson\uc2  by only 10,033 votes from the 8.2m cast in 2018, is vulnerable. \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  thinks that he can push a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in the Senate and back a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Florida without facing any consequences, he has another thing coming,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240410ek4a0028q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
