\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Arizona supreme court upholds near-total  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Vivian Ho \par \uc2 1,135 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par 11:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ruling opens door for law from 1864 that went unenforced after Roe v Wade. Plus: who is \u8216\'20\'18worthy\u8217\'20\'19 of a Herm\u232\'00\'E8s Birkin bag?\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The Arizona supreme court ruled on Tuesday to allow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a law banning almost all abortions}}}\uc2  to go into effect. The law was passed in 1864, before Arizona became a state, but went unenforced for decades after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide in its 1973 decision in Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s decision to reimpose a law from a time when Arizona wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a state, the civil war was raging, and women couldn\u8217\'20\'19t even vote will go down in history as a stain on our state,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kris Mayes, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic attorney general, who also vowed not to prosecute any doctors or women under the 1864 ban.\par \par \uc2 The justices ruled to hold off on requiring the state to enforce the ban for 14 days, giving advocates time to ask a lower court to pause it again.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What does this ruling mean nationally? The decision could curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US south-west and make Arizona one of the biggest battlefields in the 2024 electoral fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates been doing to counteract this ruling? Supporters of reproductive rights in Arizona are gathering signatures for a ballot measure to enshrine those rights into the state constitution. The rules require 383,923 signatures by July for a measure to get on the ballot; organizers said they have more than 500,000.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How have Arizona conservatives reacted to the ruling? With a surprising stance for a party that has historically championed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/arizona-republicans-against-state-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denouncing the decision}}}\uc2  after some had initially supported it.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  urges Israel to call for a ceasefire in Gaza\par \par \uc2 In an interview that aired on Tuesday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the approach taken by the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , on Gaza was a \u8220\'20\'1Cmistake\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/10/benjamin-netanyahu-joe-biden-gaza-mistake-ceasefire-israel-war-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged Israel to call for a ceasefire}}}\uc2 . Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments to Univision were some of his strongest criticism yet of Netanyahu amid growing tensions over the civilian death toll from Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and dire conditions inside Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I\u8217\'20\'19m calling for is for the Israelis to just call for a ceasefire, allow for the next six, eight weeks, total access to all food and medicine going into the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no excuse to not provide for the medical and the food needs of those people. It should be done now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Aimee Harris, a Florida woman, was sentenced on Tuesday to a month in prison and three months of home confinement for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/biden-diary-project-veritas-sentenced"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stealing and selling Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s daughter\u8217\'20\'19s diary}}}\uc2  to the conservative group Project Veritas.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The president of Micronesia said the US\par \par \uc2 was beefing up military capabilities in the country, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/10/micronesia-president-wesley-simina-military-capabilities-us-airport-upgrade-yap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considering additional military projects}}}\uc2  as it pushed ahead with plans for a $400m airport upgrade.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Missouri death row inmate was executed on Tuesday, despite an extraordinary effort by corrections officials and his appeals judge to have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/missouri-executes-death-row-inmate-despite-clemency-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his capital sentence commuted}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: swapping red meat for herring, sardines and anchovies could save 750,000 lives\par \par \uc2 Red meat consumption has been linked with a higher risk of disease in humans as well as significant harm to the environment. However, forage fish such as herring, sardines and anchovies are highly nutritious, environmentally friendly and the most abundant fish species in the world\u8217\'20\'19s oceans. A new study has found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/food/2024/apr/09/swapping-red-meat-for-herring-sardines-and-anchovies-could-save-75000-lives-study-suggests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swapping red meat for forage fish}}}\uc2  could prevent 750,000 deaths a year and significantly reduce the prevalence of disability as a result of diet-related disease \u8211\'20\'13 in particular in low- and middle-income countries, where these fish are cheap and plentiful, and where the toll taken by heart disease in particular is high.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Bolivia\u8217\'20\'19s hunt for gas\par \par \uc2 Bolivia\u8217\'20\'19s gas production from ageing fields has been failing for years, against a backdrop of fluctuating global commodity prices. These fossil fuel exports were meant to fund a revolutionary leftist agenda. Now the government is scouring the country for gas reserves that could keep its fossil-fuel model of development running, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2024/apr/10/bolivias-hunt-for-gas-targets-national-parks-and-divides-communities-tariquia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opening up protected areas such as the Tariqu\u237\'00\'EDa reserve}}}\uc2  for oil and gas exploration. \u8220\'20\'1CProtected areas are the new extractive frontier,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Penelope Anthias, a Durham University geographer.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or this: the racial abuse of Romeo and Juliet star\par \par \uc2 Francesca Amewudah-Rivers was targeted online with racial abuse after the announcement of her casting of Juliet in a new production of Romeo and Juliet, alongside Tom Holland as Romeo. More than 800 predominantly Black female and non-binary actors \u8211\'20\'13 including Lashana Lynch, Sheila Atim, Marianne Jean-Baptiste and Lolly Adefope \u8211\'20\'13 have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/apr/10/too-much-to-bear-black-actors-condemn-racial-abuse-of-romeo-juliet-star"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed an open letter in solidarity}}}\uc2  with the actor, condemning the \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo familiar horror\u8221\'20\'1D of racial abuse that Amewudah-Rivers has faced. \u8220\'20\'1CThe racist and misogynistic abuse directed at such a sweet soul has been too much to bear,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter reads. \u8220\'20\'1CFor a casting announcement of a play to ignite such twisted ugly abuse is truly embarrassing for those so empty and barren in their own lives that they must meddle in hateful abuse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Biden requires chemical plants to reduce toxic emissions\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration announced a new mandate on Tuesday requiring more than 200 of the US\u8217\'20\'19s chemical plants to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/apr/09/epa-chemical-plants-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reduce toxic emissions}}}\uc2  linked to cancer and to better protect communities from hazardous pollution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis rule will reduce a lot of hazardous air pollutants. There will be less cancer based on these emissions, there will be lives saved,\u8221\'20\'1D said Adam Kron, a senior attorney with \uc2 Earthjustice\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: \u8216\'20\'18Hell hath no fury like a wealthy person being told no\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A Herm\u232\'00\'E8s Birkin is fashion\u8217\'20\'19s most high-status handbag. While the price tag of $10,000 or more is enough to make the bag unattainable for most people, even those with the cash can\u8217\'20\'19t just pop up to a shop and buy one over the counter. Now two California residents are suing the French brand after being thwarted from buying the bag, accusing \uc2 Herm\u232\'00\'E8s\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Cunlawful tying\u8221\'20\'1D: forcing customers to buy other pricey \uc2 Herm\u232\'00\'E8s\uc2  items in order to prove themselves \u8220\'20\'1Cworthy\u8221\'20\'1D of a Birkin. The suit is raising questions about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/2024/apr/10/birkin-bag-hermes-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 how Herm\u232\'00\'E8s cultivates an air of exclusivity}}}\uc2  in an age of resale \u8211\'20\'13 and shining a light on the extreme lengths some customers will go to convince \uc2 Herm\u232\'00\'E8s\uc2  that they are Birkin material.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240410ek4a001rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
