\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Arizona supreme court upholds 1864 law banning almost all abortions\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,156 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par 16:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Justices rule to hold off on requiring state to enforce ban for 14 days, to allow advocates to ask lower court to pause it again\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  supreme court ruled on Tuesday to let a law banning almost all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abortions}}}\uc2  in the state go into effect, a decision that could curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US south-west and could make Arizona one of the biggest battlefields in the 2024 electoral fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The justices said Arizona could enforce an 1864 near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, first passed before Arizona became a state, that went unenforced for decades after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide in the 1973 decision Roe v Wade. However, the justices also ruled to hold off on requiring the state to enforce the ban for 14 days, in order to allow advocates to ask a lower court to pause it again.\par \par \uc2 The ban can only be enforced \u8220\'20\'1Cprospectively\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the 4-2 ruling. Minutes after the ruling Kris Mayes, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic attorney general, vowed not to prosecute any doctors or women under the 1864 ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s decision to reimpose a law from a time when Arizona wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a state, the civil war was raging, and women couldn\u8217\'20\'19t even vote will go down in history as a stain on our state,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayes said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Voters may be able to weigh in on the issue in November: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters in Arizona have spent months gathering signatures for a ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution, and the Tuesday decision raises the stakes for their efforts significantly. If it succeeds, the ballot measure would declare that people in Arizona have a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.arizona.vote/electioninfo/assets/47/0/BallotMeasures/I-05-2024%20Arizona%20for%20Abortion%20Access.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fundamental right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and that the state will not try to curb that right before a pregnancy reaches fetal viability, which is generally pegged to about 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Although ballot measures need to amass 383,923 signatures by July to get on the ballot, the organizers behind the Arizona measure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/arizona-abortion-rights-amendment-backers-says-gathered-signatures-nee-rcna145922"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced last week}}}\uc2  that they have gathered more than 500,000 signatures, and plan to collect more.\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , a Democrat, said Tuesday was a \u8220\'20\'1Cdark day\u8221\'20\'1D for the state and implored \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters to make their voices heard in November.\par \par \uc2 Hobbs vowed to do everything in her power to preserve access to reproductive care in the state. The governor last year issued a sweeping executive order banning county attorneys from prosecuting women who seek abortions and doctors who perform them.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the possibility that her directive could be challenged in court following Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, Hobbs said: \u8220\'20\'1CBring it on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the long-term impact of the decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Arizona is not yet clear, a number of providers said Tuesday that they will stay open as long as they can. Planned Parenthood Arizona, which operates multiple locations in the state, intends to continue providing abortions as long as the procedure is legal. Thanks to a court order in a separate case, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  appears to be able to legally provide abortions beyond the 14-day window and potentially as late as into May.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRegardless of today\u8217\'20\'19s decision, what I can tell you is that our doors will remain open,\u8221\'20\'1D Angela Florez, president and CEO of Planned Parenthood Arizona, told reporters on a call after the supreme court decision. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to provide what essential healthcare we can within the limitations of the law, and we hope that supporters will continue to support and that patients will still continue to feel safe in our care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dr Gabrielle Goodrick, a longtime \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in Phoenix, also told the Guardian that her clinic would continue offering abortions, at least through the 14-day window.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not closing. Ever. That\u8217\'20\'19s not a question,\u8221\'20\'1D Goodrick said. \u8220\'20\'1CI have reassurances from the governor and the attorney general that they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to prosecute, but I need to investigate that further.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The ruling became a campaign issue almost as soon as it was issued. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  quickly laid the blame on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , whose three supreme court appointees voted to overturn Roe, paving the way for state-level \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. The revived ban is \u8220\'20\'1Ca reality because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who brags about being \u8216\'20\'18proudly the person responsible\u8217\'20\'19 for overturning Roe v Wade, and made it possible for states to enforce cruel bans\u8221\'20\'1D, the vice-president said in a statement. Harris also warned of nationwide restrictions to reproductive care that could come with a second Trump presidency.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president will visit Arizona on Friday for a trip that was planned before Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 , who is running against the Republican and stalwart Trump supporter Kari Lake to represent Arizona in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , condemned the law in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur fight against extremist bans like the one enacted today has never been more important \u8211\'20\'13 which is why I\u8217\'20\'19m committed to doing whatever it takes to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at the federal level,\u8221\'20\'1D Gallego said.\par \par \uc2 Arizona is one of roughly a dozen states where voters may get a chance to vote directly on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights come November. However, as a key battleground state in the presidential election, the stakes in Arizona are particularly high, since Democrats hope that outrage over Roe\u8217\'20\'19s overturning will also propel their candidates \u8211\'20\'13including Joe Biden \u8211\'20\'13 to victory.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s decision is likely to galvanize voters. Several states have held \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures since Roe fell, and in every state \u8211\'20\'13 including Republican strongholds such as Kansas and Kentucky \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters have triumphed.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Lake said that she opposed the Tuesday ruling. Lake has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/kari-lake-clarifies-stance-abortion-rcna141431"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously called \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe ultimate sin\u8221\'20\'1D, but like many other Republicans in the wake of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters\u8217\'20\'19 ballot box successes, has moved to moderate her position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am calling on \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  and the statelegislature to come up with an immediate commonsense solution that Arizonans can support,\u8221\'20\'1D Lake said. \u8220\'20\'1CUltimately, Arizona voters will make the decision on the ballot come November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Until the 1864 ban is enforced, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is accessible in Arizona up until 15 weeks of pregnancy. Under the 1864 ban, it is illegal to help \u8220\'20\'1Cprocure the miscarriage\u8221\'20\'1D of a pregnant woman. The law only permits abortions to save a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life and does not have exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 The impact of the ruling will reverberate beyond Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s borders. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/12/arizona-abortion-ban-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Goodrick}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/12/arizona-abortion-ban-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  last year that many of her patients come from Texas, which has banned almost all abortions since even before Roe fell. Because Texas is home to one in 10 women of reproductive age in the US, Arizona has been a critical release valve for Texans fleeing the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Lauren Gambino contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240409ek49002ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
