\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US defense secretary rejects Israel genocide accusations; Blinken and Cameron urge US House to pass Ukraine aid - as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong \par \uc2 8,935 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2024\par 20:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our latest Israel-Gaza and Ukraine coverage below:Read all our Israel-Gaza war coverageRead all our Ukraine coverage\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruled to let a law banning almost all abortions in the state go into effect. The justices said Arizona could enforce a 1864 near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that went unenforced for decades after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide in the 1973 decision Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arizona governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , a Democrat, said Tuesday was a \u8220\'20\'1Cdark day\u8221\'20\'1D for the state and implored \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters to make their voices heard in November.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  criticized the Arizona supreme court ruling, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?page=with:block-6615800b8f08a7be969b286f#block-6615800b8f08a7be969b286f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blaming }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe extreme agenda of Republican elected officials who are committed to ripping away women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom\u8221\'20\'1D and calling the ban \u8220\'20\'1Ccruel\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , in response to the ruling by the Arizona supreme court, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?page=with:block-661590898f081c30cb1764bd#block-661590898f081c30cb1764bd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  the state had \u8220\'20\'1Crolled back the clock to a time before women could vote\u8221\'20\'1D, and said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was resopnsible for the ruling. Harris will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?page=with:block-66159c7d8f081c30cb176541#block-66159c7d8f081c30cb176541"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travel }}}\uc2  to Arizona on Friday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  and his UK counterpart, foreign secretary \uc2 David Cameron\uc2 , urged Congress to approve new military aid for Ukraine after talks in Washington during a joint press conference following talks in Washington on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Blinken said the supplemental budget request that the president has made of Congress is \u8220\'20\'1Curgent\u8221\'20\'1D and should be taken to a vote \u8220\'20\'1Cas quickly as possible\u8221\'20\'1D. Victory for Ukraine is \u8220\'20\'1Cvital for American and European security\u8221\'20\'1D, Cameron said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cameron {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-661550bb8f0829dd35c0b2ef#block-661550bb8f0829dd35c0b2ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also met}}}\uc2  with Trump over dinner on Monday at his Mar-a-Lago estate. During the briefing with Blinken, Cameron defended the meeting as a standard encounter with an opposition figure and said it covered a number of pressing global issues but did not elaborate. \u8220\'20\'1CThese things are entirely proper,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-661566d88f08b431e5f5882f#block-661566d88f08b431e5f5882f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8217\'20\'19s campaign said the former president and Cameron discussed the Ukraine war and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe need for Nato countries to meet their defense spending requirements\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Defense secretary Lloyd Austin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-661570188f08b431e5f588df#block-661570188f08b431e5f588df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the US has seen \u8220\'20\'1Cno evidence\u8221\'20\'1D that Israel was committing genocide in Gaza. Austin addressed a Senate armed services committee during a budget hearing and was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?page=with:block-661598f58f08b431e5f58a91#block-661598f58f08b431e5f58a91"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interrupted }}}\uc2  several times by protesters calling for the US to stop funding Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A New York appeals court judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66156e4c8f08b431e5f588b9#block-66156e4c8f08b431e5f588b9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2  the latest bid by Trump to delay his 15 April trial on criminal charges stemming from hush money paid to an adult film star.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican far-right Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  escalated her threat to oust Mike Johnson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?page=with:block-661541bb8f08cbf8b1ee9c5c#block-661541bb8f08cbf8b1ee9c5c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issuing}}}\uc2  a searing indictment of the House speaker in a letter explaining her decision to file a motion to oust him.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will travel to Arizona on Friday just days after the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court upheld a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The vice president\u8217\'20\'19s trip to Arizona, her second this year, was already in the works prior to Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s court decision and will likely take on a heightened focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and access, Politico reported.\par \par \uc2 The White House said Harris will use her visit \u8220\'20\'1Cto continue her leadership in the fight for reproductive freedoms\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fifteen prominent historians filed an amicus brief with the supreme court, rejecting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s claim in his federal election subversion case that he is immune to criminal prosecution for acts committed as president.\par \par \uc2 Authorities cited in the document include the founders Alexander Hamilton, James Madison and John Adams, in addition to the historians\u8217\'20\'19 own work.\par \par \uc2 Trump, the historians {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/sites/default/files/2024-04/23-939%20Brief.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Casserts that a doctrine of permanent immunity from criminal liability for a president\u8217\'20\'19s official acts, while not expressly provided by the constitution, must be inferred.\par \par \uc2 To justify this radical assertion, he contends that the original meaning of the constitution demands it. But no plausible historical case supports his claim.\par \par \uc2 Despite widespread legal and historical opinion that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s immunity claim is groundless, the supreme court, to which Trump appointed three justices, will consider the claim.\par \par \uc2 Oral arguments are scheduled for 25 April. The court recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/05/us-supreme-court-trump-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed attempts}}}\uc2 , supported by leading historians, to remove Trump from ballots under the 14th amendment, passed after the civil war to bar insurrectionists from office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-661570188f08b431e5f588df#block-661570188f08b431e5f588df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  earlier, }}}\uc2  defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  told the Senate earlier today that the \uc2 US government\uc2  has seen \u8220\'20\'1Cno evidence\u8221\'20\'1D that Israel was committing genocide in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Austin addressed a Senate armed services committee during a budget hearing and was interrupted several times by protesters calling for the US to stop funding Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The UK also confirmed in meetings with US counterparts that there would be no changes to arms exports to Israel, although it would be kept under review.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the clip:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Louisiana \u8217\'20\'19s Republican-controlled senate advanced a bill on Monday that would empower state and local law enforcement to arrest and jail people in the state who entered the US illegally, similar to embattled legislation in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Amid national fights between Republican states and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over how and who should enforce the US-Mexico border, Louisiana joins a growing list of legislatures seeking to expand states\u8217\'20\'19 authority over border enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Proponents of the bill, such as the legislation\u8217\'20\'19s author, GOP state senator Valarie Hodges, say Louisiana has the \u8220\'20\'1Cright to defend our nation\u8221\'20\'1D. Hodges has accused the federal government of neglecting responsibilities to enforce immigration law, an argument heard from GOP leaders across the country.\par \par \uc2 Opponents argue the bill is unconstitutional, will not do anything to make the state safer, and will only fuel negative and false rhetoric directed toward migrants.\par \par \uc2 Across the nation, reliably red legislatures have advanced tougher immigration enforcement measures.\par \par \uc2 The Oklahoma house passed a bill that would prohibit state revenue from being used to provide benefits to those living in the state illegally. A bill in Tennessee, which is awaiting the governor\u8217\'20\'19s signature, would require law enforcement agencies in the state to communicate with federal immigration authorities if they discover people who are in the country illegally. Measures that mirror parts of the Texas law are awaiting the governor\u8217\'20\'19s signature in Iowa, while another is pending in Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s statehouse.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/louisiana-immigration-law-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana advances bill to allow local authorities to enforce immigration laws }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers and climate advocates called on utilities to \u8220\'20\'1Cditch the \uc2 American Gas Association\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D at a press conference at the US Capitol on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmericans are already paying the price of climate change,\u8221\'20\'1D said Senator \uc2 Ed Markey\uc2  of Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 They shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to pay the salaries of those who are fueling it.\par \par \uc2 A trade association representing more than 200 US utilities, the \uc2 AGA\uc2  has a well-documented history of lobbying against climate regulations and policies \u8211\'20\'13 activity funded in part by members\u8217\'20\'19 ratepayers\u8217\'20\'19 utility bills. It\u8217\'20\'19s a \u8220\'20\'1Cdirty game,\u8221\'20\'1D said Xavier Boatwright of \uc2 the Sierra Club\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Both the event and a protest outside the \uc2 AGA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s headquarters earlier Tuesday were led by the anti-gas nonprofit organization the Gas Leaks Project.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s nothing natural about natural gas,\u8221\'20\'1D said the group\u8217\'20\'19s senior communications director Maria Luisa Cesar.\par \par \uc2 The extraction and use of gas, called natural gas by industry interests, emits planet-heating and toxic pollution. Reports show the \uc2 AGA\uc2  has been aware of these {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.euronews.com/green/2023/03/07/gas-industry-knew-about-indoor-pollution-from-stoves-50-years-ago-investigation-reveals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dangers}}}\uc2  for 50 years, but has continued to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/us-building-codes-climate_n_65bd6df7e4b05c8779f93a8e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 undercut}}}\uc2  climate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/22691755/gas-utilities-fight-electrification-preemption"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efforts}}}\uc2 . Rhode Island senator Sheldon Whitehouse said:\par \par \uc2 The fossil fuel industry depends in roughly equal parts on hydrocarbons and lies.\par \par \uc2 In August, the New England utility \uc2 Eversource\uc2  cut ties with the \uc2 American Gas Association\uc2 . Advocates are calling on other utilities to follow its lead. Four states have also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://energyandpolicy.org/tracking-states-getting-politics-out-of-utility-bills/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed legislation}}}\uc2  to prevent the use of ratepayer dollars to fund political activity.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Also in Arizona, Eva Burch, a Democratic state lawmaker who drew national attention {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/20/eva-burch-abortion-speech-arizona-senator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after announcing}}}\uc2  her decision to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month, said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 today\u8217\'20\'19s court decision}}}\uc2  to enforce a ban - using a law that was originally drafted in the 19th Century before women could vote and before Arizona was a state - would have devastating consequences for women such as her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA couple of weeks ago I had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a safe legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  here in Arizona for a pregnancy that I very much wanted,\u8221\'20\'1D Burch said.\par \par \uc2 Somebody gave me a procedure so that I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to experience another miscarriage \u8211\'20\'13 the pain, the mess, the discomfort. And now we\u8217\'20\'19re talking about whether or not we should put that doctor in jail. This is outrageous.\par \par \uc2 Burch predicted the ruling would backfire on conservatives who have fought to allow the ban to be enforced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe people of Arizona have had enough,\u8221\'20\'1D Burch said.\par \par \uc2 We are electing pro-choice candidates in November. Watch it happen.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says Arizona ruling 'rolls back clock to a time before women could vote'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has responded to a ruling by the Arizona supreme court to let a law banning almost all abortions in the state go into effect, saying the state had \u8220\'20\'1Crolled back the clock to a time before women could vote\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the vice president said there was \u8220\'20\'1Cone person responsible\u8221\'20\'1D for the ruling, which will allow a law first passed in 1864 to go into effect, \u8220\'20\'1Cby his own admission \u8230\'20\'26 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris said the \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme and dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D ban criminalizes almost all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in the state and \u8220\'20\'1Cputs women\u8217\'20\'19s lives at risk\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a reality because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who brags about being \u8216\'20\'18proudly the person responsible\u8217\'20\'19 for overturning Roe v. Wade, and made it possible for states to enforce cruel bans.\par \par \uc2 She added:\par \par \uc2 The alarm is sounding for every woman in America: if he has the opportunity, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would sign off on a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. He has called for punishing women and doctors. If he wins, he and his allies have plans to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and restrict access to birth control, with or without Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , a Democrat, called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 today\u8217\'20\'19s news}}}\uc2  from the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court on an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban a \u8220\'20\'1Cdark day\u8221\'20\'1D for the state and implored \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters to make their voices heard in November.\par \par \uc2 Hobbs vowed to do everything in her power to preserve access to reproductive care and contraception in the state, pointing to actions she has already taken. After winning the election in 2022, Hobbs last year issued a sweeping executive order banning county attorneys from prosecuting women who seek abortions and doctors who perform them.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the possibility that her directive could be challenged in court, Hobbs said: \u8220\'20\'1CBring it on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the news conference, held moments after the state supreme court released its decision, Hobbs called on the Republican-led state legislature to \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediately\u8221\'20\'1D repeal the ban. But the legislature is unlikely to do so. The leaders of both chambers joined anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists in favor of allowing the territorial-era ban to take effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe legislature has ignored the will of the voters on this issue for decades,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The ballot box is the way that voters can have their say and overrule the legislature on this issue that the vast majority of Arizonans support.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt is a dark day in Arizona. We are just fourteen days away from one of the most extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the country.\par \par \uc2 But my message to Arizona women is this: I won't rest, and I won't stop fighting until we have secured the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That is my promise to you.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  (@GovernorHobbs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovernorHobbs/status/1777756501974934007?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The national security adviser, Jake Sullivan, just said that \uc2 US government\uc2  agencies were still involved in an \u8220\'20\'1Cinformal review\u8221\'20\'1D of the \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/05/israeli-inquiry-blames-wck-aid-killings-on-grave-errors-by-military-personnel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 review}}}\uc2  of the killing by the Israeli military of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/03/very-best-of-humanity-the-seven-aid-workers-killed-in-israeli-airstrike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven aid workers}}}\uc2  with the group \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  in Gaza earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Sullivan said that the CIA director, \uc2 Bill Burns\uc2 , was involved in further talks in Cairo in Egypt at the weekend, where states such as the US and Qatar are trying to broker a ceasefire in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza and the return of the remaining hostages held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  since the massacre it perpetrated in southern Israel last 7 October.\par \par \uc2 Sullivan said the US \u8220\'20\'1Chas seen Israel take some steps forward\u8221\'20\'1D in the talks, while the latest statements from \uc2 Hamas\uc2  were regarded as \u8220\'20\'1Cless than encouraging\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said more humanitarian aid was reaching Gaza, which he said was \u8220\'20\'1Cgood, but not good enough\u8221\'20\'1D, amid Israel\u8217\'20\'19s blockade and siege of the Palestinian territory.\par \par \uc2 And amid Israel pulling troops out of Khan Younis in southern Gaza, in a pause in its offensive actions, Sullivan said the US has still not seen \u8220\'20\'1Ca credible and executable\u8221\'20\'1D plan from Israel about what it would do to move or protect Palestinians in the event that, as it has pledged to do, it invades Rafah.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just arrived back at the White House after a very short trip to Washington\u8217\'20\'19s main Union Station rail hub, to deliver remarks about healthcare.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  was originally due to brief the media at 1.30pm in the regular daily session in the west wing, but obviously everything is being pushed back because the president\u8217\'20\'19s schedule shifted later than originally expected, also. The US national security adviser, Jake Sullivan, will join the briefing. It\u8217\'20\'19s getting underway now.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you highlights from the briefing. There has been a lot of international-facing news today, especially with the latest on high-level talks in the Middle East about Israel\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/09/unwra-vital-to-avert-starvation-in-gaza-says-agency-official"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 war in Gaza}}}\uc2  and US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  and the UK foreign secretary, \uc2 David Cameron\uc2  meeting in Washington, DC, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?page=with:block-661563478f08a7be969b26af#block-661563478f08a7be969b26af"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and urging}}}\uc2  the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  to approve new military aid for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has criticized the Arizona supreme {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court ruling}}}\uc2  from earlier today to let an old law on the books banning almost all abortions in the state go into effect \u8211\'20\'13 albeit with a 14-day delay to allow further legal challenges before it does.\par \par \uc2 The US president blamed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe extreme agenda of Republican elected officials who are committed to ripping away women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom\u8221\'20\'1D and called the ban \u8220\'20\'1Ccruel\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a statement issued from the White House moments ago, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CMillions of Arizonans will soon live under an even more extreme and dangerous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which fails to protect women even when their health is at risk or in tragic cases of rape or incest. This cruel ban was first enacted in 1864 \u8211\'20\'13 more than 150 years ago, before Arizona was even a state and well before women had secured the right to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The statement ended with: \u8220\'20\'1C Vice-President Harris and I stand with the vast majority of Americans who support a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. We will continue to fight to protect reproductive rights and call on Congress to pass a law restoring the protections of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  for women in every state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  has taken a strong lead in recent months on efforts by the Biden administration and the Biden-Harris re-election campaign to win support for protecting reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 This follows, in particular, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark overturning}}}\uc2  of the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the conservative-dominated supreme court in 2022 and further attacks on rights ranging from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to contraception to IVF by the hard right.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona court upholds old law banning most abortions\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  supreme court ruled on Tuesday to let a law banning almost all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abortions}}}\uc2  in the state go into effect, a decision that could curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US south-west and could make Arizona one of the biggest battlefields in the 2024 electoral fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The justices said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  could enforce a 1864 near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, first passed before Arizona became a state, that went unenforced for decades after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide in the 1973 decision Roe v Wade. However, the justices also ruled to hold off on requiring the state to enforce the ban for 14 days, in order to allow advocates to ask a lower court to pause it again.\par \par \uc2 The ban can only be enforced \u8220\'20\'1Cprospectively\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the 4-2 ruling. Minutes after the ruling Kris Mayes, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic attorney general, vowed not to prosecute any doctors or women under the 1864 ban.\par \par \uc2 You can read the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 full story here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , and the UK foreign secretary, \uc2 David Cameron\uc2 , urged Congress to approve new military aid for Ukraine after talks in Washington.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Blinken and Cameron held a joint press conference where the US secretary of state said the stalled Ukraine funding is critical for US, European and world security. The supplemental budget request that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has made of Congress is \u8220\'20\'1Curgent\u8221\'20\'1D and should be taken to a vote \u8220\'20\'1Cas quickly as possible\u8221\'20\'1D, Blinken {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-661563478f08a7be969b26af#block-661563478f08a7be969b26af"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 . Victory for Ukraine is \u8220\'20\'1Cvital for American and European security\u8221\'20\'1D, Cameron said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cameron {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-661550bb8f0829dd35c0b2ef#block-661550bb8f0829dd35c0b2ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also met}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over dinner on Monday at his Mar-a-Lago estate. During the briefing with Blinken, Cameron defended the meeting as a standard encounter with an opposition figure and said it covered a number of pressing global issues but did not elaborate. \u8220\'20\'1CThese things are entirely proper,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-661566d88f08b431e5f5882f#block-661566d88f08b431e5f5882f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said the former president and Cameron discussed the Ukraine war and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe need for Nato countries to meet their defense spending requirements\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US defense secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-661570188f08b431e5f588df#block-661570188f08b431e5f588df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  a Senate armed services committee hearing that the US has seen no evidence that Israel is committing genocide in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A New York appeals court judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66156e4c8f08b431e5f588b9#block-66156e4c8f08b431e5f588b9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2  the latest bid by Trump to delay his 15 April trial on criminal charges stemming from hush money paid to an adult film star.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican far-right Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  escalated her threat to oust Mike Johnson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/09/trump-biden-election-campaign-updates-congress-ukraine?page=with:block-661541bb8f08cbf8b1ee9c5c#block-661541bb8f08cbf8b1ee9c5c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issuing}}}\uc2  a searing indictment of the House speaker in a letter explaining her decision to file a motion to oust him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a key \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race in Ohio this year, where the incumbent leftwing Democrat, \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 , is expected to face a tough challenge from Bernie Moreno, a car dealer turned Trump-backed populist firebrand.\par \par \uc2 Like many Trump-backed candidates, Moreno is making it his business to blame China for woes affecting blue-collar workers. Earlier this year, he went so far as to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iheart.com/podcast/71-mike-allen-29515262/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tell}}}\uc2  a conservative radio host: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Buick Envision was made in China, I told \uc2 General Motors\uc2  I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t sell one of them, don\u8217\'20\'19t even ship it to me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The problem about the claim, which Moreno has made elsewhere, is that as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2024/04/08/bernie-moreno-ohio-senate-general-motors-buick-china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Spectrum News reports}}}\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 \u8220\'20\'1CMoreno\u8217\'20\'19s dealership did sell the Chinese-made SUVs for several years, and even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BeachwoodBuick/status/493850602812616704"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promoted the vehicles}}}\uc2  on social media, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/CrestmontBuickGMC/posts/pfbid07ShHTuXho7jUG2MqEoCe5mAxTBoQn8zyjfWYqBi6YirRqseLUou1AgknNAzbJziQl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 numerous}}}\uc2  social media {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BeachwoodBuick/status/1143896451044524038"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posts}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After detailing such posts, Spectrum {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2024/04/08/bernie-moreno-ohio-senate-general-motors-buick-china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adds}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGM, the parent company of Buick, confirmed to Spectrum News the Envision was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.buick.com/media/us/en/buick/vehicles/envision/2016.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only manufactured in China}}}\uc2 . The SUV became the first Chinese-made vehicle to be imported by a major US automaker when it debuted in Michigan in 2016.\par \par \uc2 The imports were called a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.autoweek.com/news/future-cars/a1857086/no-you-probably-cant-blame-slow-buick-envision-rollout-presidential-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cslap in the face\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2 , which felt the vehicles should be made on US soil by American workers.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Moreno, Reagan McCarthy, told Spectrum: \u8220\'20\'1CIn response to the closure of the Lordstown Plant here in Ohio [in March 2019], Bernie made a decision to stop any new inventory of Envision\u8217\'20\'19s [sic] from being sold at his dealership. After he sold off the inventory he already had on the lot, he refused to take orders for more Envisions. There is zero contradiction here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There are contradictions elsewhere in Moreno\u8217\'20\'19s campaign statements, though, as the Guardian discussed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/28/republican-bernie-moreno-questionable-campaign-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/28/republican-bernie-moreno-questionable-campaign-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Moreno says he fled socialism in Colombia for the US in 1971. What does history say?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge denies Trump's request to delay hush-money trial while he appeals gag order\par \par \uc2 A New York appeals court judge has rejected the latest bid by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to delay his 15 April trial on criminal charges stemming from hush money paid to an adult film star.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers had requested the trial to be postponed indefinitely while he appeals a gag order that bars him from commenting about jurors, witnesses and others connected to the case.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys argue that Justice Juan Merchan \u8217\'20\'19s order restricting his public comments is an unconstitutional prior restraint on his free speech rights while he campaigns for president. Merchan imposed the order last month after finding Trump made statements in various legal cases that the judge called \u8220\'20\'1Cthreatening, inflammatory\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdenigrating\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During the hearing on Tuesday, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Emil Bove said:\par \par \uc2 The First amendment harms arising from this gag order right now are irreparable.\par \par \uc2 Justice Cynthia Kern issued the order following a Tuesday morning hearing, but a full panel of appeals judges will later consider the former president\u8217\'20\'19s underlying challenge to the gag order.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Austin, asked what the consequences of a deadly mass famine in Gaza would be, said:\par \par \uc2 It will accelerate violence, and it will have the effect of ensuring that there\u8217\'20\'19s a long-term conflict.\par \par \uc2 Addressing the Senate armed services committee, the defense secretary added:\par \par \uc2 It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to happen... We should continue to do everything we can, and we are doing this, to encourage the Israelis to provide humanitarian assistance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 The defense secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , speaking during a Senate armed services committee hearing, said pressure on Israel to improve humanitarian aid to Gaza appears to be working, but that more must be done. Austin said:\par \par \uc2 It clearly had an effect. We have seen changes in behavior, and we have seen more humanitarian assistance being pushed into Gaza. Hopefully that trend will continue.\par \par \uc2 During the meeting, a number of senators decried the civilian casualties in Gaza and called on the administration to press Israel to protect the population in the Palestinian territory.\par \par \uc2 Austin said he spoke with his Israeli counterpart, the defense minister, Yoav Gallant, on Monday and that he repeated US insistence that Israel must move civilians out of the battle space in Gaza and properly care for them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  rejects accusations Israel has committed genocide in Gaza\par \par \uc2 The US has seen no evidence that Israel is committing genocide in Gaza, the defense secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , has said.\par \par \uc2 Austin, addressing a Senate armed services committee during a budget hearing today, said:\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t have any evidence of genocide being created.\par \par \uc2 He also avoided referring to the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks on southern Israel on 7 October as a genocide, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Chorrific terrorist attack\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ccertainly \u8230\'20\'26 a war crime\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Austin\u8217\'20\'19s testimony was interrupted several times by protesters calling for the US to stop funding the war.\par \par \uc2 enltrA protester interrupted Defense Sec. \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  during a Senate hearing on the Defense Dept.'s budget, calling for a cease-fire in Gaza as they were removed from the room by police. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JRdzFBTwL0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JRdzFBTwL0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NBC Politics (@NBCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCPolitics/status/1777732127032762382?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cameron was asked if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  gave any assurance that the US would remain a Nato member if he is re-elected to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The UK foreign secretary says he won\u8217\'20\'19t go into what he said during his dinner with Trump, but that he has argued consistently for getting \uc2 Nato\uc2  in its strongest possible shape and getting all of its members to meet the alliance\u8217\'20\'19s target of spending 2% of GDP on defense this year.\par \par \uc2 He says the best things Nato can do is to keep the Ukrainians in this fight, and that he will \u8220\'20\'1Cmake that argument to anyone who will listen\u8221\'20\'1D. He says supporting Ukraine is \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely good value for money\u8221\'20\'1D for the US and its allies.\par \par \uc2 For like 5 or 10% of your defense budget, almost half of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s prewar military equipment has been destroyed, without the loss of a single American life. This is an investment in United States\u8217\'20\'19 security.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cameron says that the UK\u8217\'20\'19s position on arms sales to Israel remains \u8220\'20\'1Cunchanged\u8221\'20\'1D after the latest assessment of the government\u8217\'20\'19s legal advice.\par \par \uc2 He says Israel remains a \u8220\'20\'1Cvital\u8221\'20\'1D defensive security partner to the UK.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cameron is asked why he is not meeting with the US House speaker, Mike Johnson, during his visit to Washington.\par \par \uc2 The UK foreign secretary says he has a range of meetings with senators and members of Congress from both sides of the aisle, and that he does \u8220\'20\'1Cwith great trepidation\u8221\'20\'1D. Cameron says:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not for foreign politicians to tell legislators in another countries what to do. It\u8217\'20\'19s just that I am passionate about the importance of defending Ukraine against this aggression, that I think it is up to the interests of US security that Putin fails in his illegal invasion.\par \par \uc2 Cameron says there will be people in Tehran, Pyongyang and Beijing looking at how the US and UK stand by its allies.\par \par \uc2 So I\u8217\'20\'19m here to offer my opinion and to meet with anyone who wants to talk to me about it to make those arguments.\par \par \uc2 He says he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdelighted\u8221\'20\'1D to have these meetings this afternoon and tomorrow, and that he will make time for anyone in Congress who would welcome a conversation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Blinken: 'the ball is in \uc2 Hamas\uc2 's court' after 'very serious' offer made\par \par \uc2 Blinken says the US is working \u8220\'20\'1C24/7\u8221\'20\'1D with Qatar, Egypt and Israel on reaching a ceasefire and hostage-release agreement.\par \par \uc2 He says there is a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery serious\u8221\'20\'1D offer for \uc2 Hamas\uc2  on the table that \u8220\'20\'1Cshould be accepted\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that he believes that the fact that \uc2 Hamas\uc2  has not said yes \u8220\'20\'1Cis a reflection of what it really thinks about the people of Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 which is not much at all\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The ball is in \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s court. The world is watching to see what it does.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cameron calls meeting with Trump 'entirely proper'\par \par \uc2 Cameron, asked about his meeting with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Monday, says it was an \u8220\'20\'1Centirely proper\u8221\'20\'1D meeting that was in line with precedent of UK ministers speaking with opposition politicians in the run-up to elections.\par \par \uc2 The UK foreign secretary says it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cprivate\u8221\'20\'1D meeting and that he and Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscussed a range of important geopolitical subjects\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Blinken, responding to a reporter\u8217\'20\'19s question, says the US does not have a day for a potential Israeli operation in Rafah in southern Gaza.\par \par \uc2 He says \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been very clear with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , about the US\u8217\'20\'19s deep concerns about Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ability to conduct a major military operation that would do real harm to civilians.\par \par \uc2 Blinken says he expects that he will see Israeli colleagues again next week for further talks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cameron, reiterating Blinken\u8217\'20\'19s comments, says the UK and US want to see 500 trucks carrying humanitarian assistance getting into Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The UK foreign secretary calls on the water in Gaza to be switched back on, the Ashdod port and a northern crossing point to be opened, and for aid to reach across Gaza.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cameron emphasizes need for Ukraine aid and says US House must 'release this money and let it through'\par \par \uc2 David Cameron\uc2  starts his remarks off by saying that there is no closer alliance for the UK than its partnership with the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn a time of danger like this international affairs, close alliances really matter,\u8221\'20\'1D the UK foreign secretary says.\par \par \uc2 In terms of support for Ukraine, Cameron says:\par \par \uc2 We know what they need, and we know what is right for us. We know that if we give the Ukrainians the support they deserve, they can win this war.\par \par \uc2 Citing the Ukrainian foreign minister, Cameron says Ukraine needs air defenses, ammunition and money. He says it is important to send a clear message to all those around the world, including China, that the US and UK stands by its allies. Cameron says:\par \par \uc2 Nothing is more important than the supplemental request the Congress is looking at the moment. I come here with no intention to lecture anybody or tell anybody what to do or get in the way of the process of politics. I just come here as a great friend and believer in this country and a believer that it\u8217\'20\'19s profoundly in your interest, and your security, and your future, and the future for all your partners to release this money and let it through.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Blinken speaks about the Middle East \u8211\'20\'13 he says Israel has made \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant commitments\u8221\'20\'1D to significantly increase the supply of humanitarian assistance throughout Gaza, and that it is taking some \u8220\'20\'1Cinitial actions to move on those commitments\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut what matters is results and sustained results,\u8221\'20\'1D the secretary of state says, noting that the US \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be looking very carefully in the days ahead\u8221\'20\'1D that assistance is distributed effectively in Gaza, including that it gets to the north of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The US continues to work closely with Israel, Egypt and Qatar to reach an agreement for an immediate ceasefire and the release of hostages, Blinken says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Imperative' for US House to pass Ukraine aid, says Blinken\par \par \uc2 Blinken says it is \u8220\'20\'1Cimperative\u8221\'20\'1D now that the House is back in session to get a vote on Ukraine aid \u8220\'20\'1Cas quickly as possible\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The supplemental budget request that President Biden has made to Congress is \u8220\'20\'1Curgent\u8221\'20\'1D, he says.\par \par \uc2 Blinken says there has been genuine burden-sharing among the US and European and international allies in terms of support for Ukraine. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to continue to do our part,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Blinken: US and UK committed to supporting Ukraine's efforts against Russia\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  begins the news conference by saying he and Britain\u8217\'20\'19s foreign secretary, \uc2 David Cameron\uc2 , reaffirmed the imperative of continuing to support and help Ukraine defend itself against the ongoing Russian aggression.\par \par \uc2 The secretary of state says the UK has been an \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary leader\u8221\'20\'1D in the effort to support Ukraine from day one, including by imposing sanctions and export controls on Russia.\par \par \uc2 Blinken says he and Cameron discussed ways to strengthen efforts to prevent the transfer of weapons and materials to Russia for use in Ukraine. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an ongoing challenge,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 We see weapons and technologies to support the defense industrial base in Russia coming from North Korea from Iran from China. This is an area of particular concern for not only the United States and the United Kingdom, but many of our allies and partners throughout Europe.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 David Cameron\uc2  discussed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe need for Nato countries to meet their defense spending requirements\u8221\'20\'1D during a dinner at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate on Monday, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The pair discussed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe upcoming US and UK elections, policy matters specific to Brexit, the need for Nato countries to meet their defense spending requirements, and ending the killing in Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D the presumptive Republican nominee\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Blinken and Cameron to hold joint press conference\par \par \uc2 The UK foreign secretary, \uc2 David Cameron\uc2 , and the US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , are due to hold a joint press conference at 11:15am ET following talks in Washington about support for Ukraine and bringing stability to the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 Cameron {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/apr/09/david-cameron-donald-trump-meeting-washington-ukraine-support-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also met with}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ahead of his meeting with Blinken in an attempt to persuade the presumptive Republican presidential candidate to drop his opposition to a new package of aid for Ukraine that is being held up in Congress partly on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s instruction.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Though it is called \u8220\'20\'1Cnatural gas\u8221\'20\'1D by industry interests, gas is primarily made of methane, a greenhouse gas 80 times more planet-warming in the short term that has also been linked to asthma and other health risks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no such thing as clean methane gas,\u8221\'20\'1D Caleb Heeringa of the Gas Leaks Project shouted at a protest in Washington DC to demand that gas utilities stop using ratepayer dollars to fund their political agendas.\par \par \uc2 Attendees included actors from the Gas Leak Project\u8217\'20\'19s recently launched {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hotandtoxic.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hot & Toxic}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/ad-campaign-uses-humor-urge-americans-ditch-natural-gas-2024-03-23/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign}}}\uc2 , a faux reality show which parodies the marketing of gas stoves. Dressed in brightly colored outfits, they cheered when protesters mentioned pollutants such as carbon monoxide and benzene and pretended to try and snatch the banner away.\par \par \uc2 enltr"we won't pay for the \uc2 AGA\uc2 " {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BytYlJRaqU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BytYlJRaqU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ???????????? ???????? (@dharnanoor) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dharnanoor/status/1777696887245558010?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Authorities quickly asked the protesters to vacate the \uc2 American Gas Association\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s premises, so they relocated in front of the Capitol building.\par \par \uc2 The Gas Leaks project on Tuesday also launched DitchTheAGA.com, a website allowing viewers to determine if their utility is a member of the \uc2 American Gas Association\uc2 . If the answer is \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D, users can also easily email their local officials to demand that the utility cut ties.\par \par \uc2 At noon, the group will hold a press conference with Senator \uc2 Ed Markey\uc2  of Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Protesters gathered in Washington DC on Tuesday to demand that gas utilities stop using ratepayer dollars to fund their political agendas.\par \par \uc2 The demonstration took place outside the headquarters of the lobbying organization the \uc2 American Gas Association\uc2 , which represents nearly every gas utility in the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t pay for the \uc2 AGA\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D protesters cried.\par \par \uc2 enltrhappening now: protestors gather outside the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aga_naturalgas?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @aga_naturalgas}}}\uc2  headquarters in DC calling out the use of ratepayer dollars to fund pro-fossil fuel policies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GasLeaksProject?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GasLeaksProject}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JTQC7tk4TA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JTQC7tk4TA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ???????????? ???????? (@dharnanoor) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dharnanoor/status/1777696462450589842?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The trade group, funded in part by utility bills paid to its members, has come under fire for successfully working to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/us-building-codes-climate_n_65bd6df7e4b05c8779f93a8e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strip decarbonization}}}\uc2  measures from building codes and lobbying against an array of climate-friendly policies.\par \par \uc2 The protesters, convened by the anti-gas nonprofit The Gas Leaks Project, held a banner that said Ditch the \uc2 AGA\uc2  and signs that said \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican Gaslighting Association\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 David Cameron\uc2  is scheduled to hold talks with the secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , in Washington on Tuesday. Although they have much to discuss covering the future of Nato, China and a possible ceasefire in Gaza, the foreign secretary\u8217\'20\'19s key goal is to shift Republican thinking in Congress on the relevance of the threat posed by Russia to American interests.\par \par \uc2 A steady stream of European politicians have travelled to Washington on similar missions, only to return frustrated at the growing US indifference to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s fate.\par \par \uc2 The Republican House speaker, Mike Johnson, has so far declined to allow the Ukraine aid issue onto the floor of the Congress, but has indicated he might do so next week when Congress returns from recess. In February, the speaker refused to consider a Senate-passed foreign aid package that would have included $60bn for Ukraine because it lacked measures relating to security on the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 A key test for Cameron\u8217\'20\'19s trip is whether he gains meetings with the swing Republican congressmen including Johnson. At present no meeting with Johnson is slated for Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Talks will also focus on the Middle East, with the foreign secretary expected to set out the UK\u8217\'20\'19s reasoning for not suspending arms sales to Israel.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The risk is that past bad blood between \uc2 David Cameron\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over issues such as Brexit have poisoned the well, and Cameron, for all his persuasive skills, is not the British political leader most likely to make Trump change his mind and drop his opposition to a new Ukraine aid package.\par \par \uc2 Trump has said he can negotiate a peace deal on Ukraine in 24 hours. His allies say the deal will involve ceding Crimea and the Donbas region to Russia, formalizing the land grab that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  started in 2014 and continued with the full-scale invasion in 2022.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , said on Sunday that Ukraine would lose the war if US aid was withheld and Ukrainian air cover not improved.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSuccess for Ukraine and failure for [Vladimir] Putin are vital for American and European security,\u8221\'20\'1D Cameron said before his trip.\par \par \uc2 This will show that borders matter, that aggression doesn\u8217\'20\'19t pay and that countries like Ukraine are free to choose their own future. The alternative would only encourage Putin in further attempts to redraw European borders by force, and would be heard clearly in Beijing, Tehran and North Korea.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, he warned Congress not to show \u8220\'20\'1Cthe weakness displayed against Hitler\u8221\'20\'1D in the 1930s.\par \par \uc2 Cameron is also arguing that Ukraine has shown time and again that if it is given the resources it can succeed and would be ready to \u8220\'20\'1Cgo on the offensive\u8221\'20\'1D in 2025.\par \par \uc2 Aware that Trump believes Europe does not pull its weight in defending itself, Cameron is armed with statistics to show more than $184bn (\u163\'00\'A3145bn) has already been committed to Ukraine by European nations including more than $15bn (nearly \u163\'00\'A312bn) from the UK.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 David Cameron\uc2  meets Trump amid push to shore up Ukraine support\par \par \uc2 The UK foreign secretary, \uc2 David Cameron\uc2 , has taken the unusual and potentially risky step of travelling to see \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at his Mar-a-Lago residence in Florida before a visit to Washington DC on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Cameron was hoping to persuade the presumptive Republican presidential candidate to drop his opposition to a new package of aid for Ukraine that is being held up in Congress partly on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s instruction.\par \par \uc2 It is Cameron\u8217\'20\'19s second visit to the US to try to convince Republicans that it is in America\u8217\'20\'19s national interest for the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , not to make any further military advances in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Monday, a UK Foreign Office spokesperson played down the rarity of a Conservative foreign secretary trying to persuade a Republican not to make concessions to Russia over the future of Europe. The Foreign Office said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cstandard practice for ministers to meet opposition candidates as part of their routine international engagement\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Although Conservative politicians have met Trump, as has his great ally Nigel Farage, Monday\u8217\'20\'19s meeting was the first between a senior UK minister and Trump since he left office insisting that the presidential election had been stolen from him.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2  was one of eight Republicans who voted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/04/mcarthy-democracy-congress-politics-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eject}}}\uc2  the previous speaker, Kevin McCarthy, last October. But Buck quit Congress in protest of his party\u8217\'20\'19s domination by Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to CNN on Monday, Buck dismissed McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4581253-mccarthy-calls-greene-serious-legislator-amid-johnson-ouster-threat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contention}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Ca very serious legislator that deals with policy\u8221\'20\'1D, saying:\par \par \uc2 So many of the statements that Marjorie has made over the years are completely irresponsible. The idea that somehow the speaker [Johnson] is corrupt because he believes that we should be supporting an ally that has been invaded by a war criminal, [Russian leader] \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , and the idea that somehow anybody who is in agreement with Ukraine and our Nato allies is corrupt, it\u8217\'20\'19s just another distraction that she uses to take away from the core arguments that are so important.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  is ungovernable and should be known as \u8220\'20\'1CMoscow Marjorie\u8221\'20\'1D, said a former House Republican colleague, accusing the far-right Georgia congresswoman of \u8220\'20\'1Cgetting her talking points from the Kremlin\u8221\'20\'1D when opposing new federal aid for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2 , a Colorado rightwinger who left Congress last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OutFrontCNN/status/1777515804902277533"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 My experience with Marjorie is people have talked to her about not filing articles of impeachment on President Biden before he was sworn into office, not filing articles of impeachment that were groundless based on other individuals in the Biden administration. She was never moved by that. She was always focused on her social media account. And \u8216\'20\'18Moscow Marjorie\u8217\'20\'19 is focused now on this Ukraine issue and getting her talking points from the Kremlin and making sure she is popular and she is getting a lot of coverage.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CMoscow Marjorie.\u8221\'20\'1D Former Rep. \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2  tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ErinBurnett?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ErinBurnett}}}\uc2  how he really feels about Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zoFkWiMAu2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zoFkWiMAu2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Erin Burnett OutFront (@OutFrontCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OutFrontCNN/status/1777515804902277533?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the letter sent to colleagues this morning, Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  laid into Mike Johnson with a point-by-point takedown of his record as speaker.\par \par \uc2 She ticked through the instances that Johnson has negotiated with Democrats on major legislation, including a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/22/government-shutdown-averted-spending-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.2tn spending bill}}}\uc2  last month that averted a government shutdown and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/22/marjorie-taylor-greene-motion-mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prompted Greene}}}\uc2  to file a motion to move the speaker. At the time, she said the move was meant as \u8220\'20\'1Cmore of a warning than a pink slip\u8221\'20\'1D because she did not want to \u8220\'20\'1Cthrow the House into chaos\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But in her memo, Greene wrote that Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s actions have been \u8220\'20\'1Ca complete and total surrender to, if not complete and total lockstep with, the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 agenda that has angered our Republican base\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 If we win the House this fall, it will only be because President Trump is on the ballot, not because we have earned it.\par \par \uc2 enltrRead my full letter to my colleagues detailing why I filed a motion to vacate Speaker Johnson.\par \par \uc2 (1/2) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CByvpRo8My"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/CByvpRo8My}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DWQck3WpoZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DWQck3WpoZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 ???? (@RepMTG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1777687606416859496?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 undltr(2/2) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ieWIeihzUw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ieWIeihzUw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 ???? (@RepMTG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1777687619549217230?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 For his part, Johnson has tried to downplay Majorie Taylor Greene \u8217\'20\'19s threat and attempted to ease tensions.\par \par \uc2 Johnson and Greene exchanged text messages over the two-week Easter recess, and the pair was supposed to speak on Friday but the plan fell through, the Hill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4581611-johnson-gauntlet-greene-ouster-threat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 , citing a source.\par \par \uc2 In a statement last week, the House speaker said:\par \par \uc2 I respect Marjorie. She will always have an open door to the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s office. We do have honest differences on strategy sometimes but share the same conservative beliefs.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew \u8212\'20\'14 Speaker Mike Johnson is now responding to MTG, telling us in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CI respect Marjorie. She will always have an open door to the Speaker\u8217\'20\'19s office. We do have honest differences on strategy sometimes but share the same conservative beliefs.\u176\'00\'B0\u176\'00\'B0\u8220\'20\'1CIn spite of our\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hOXGnK9TyD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/hOXGnK9TyD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1775945298516279779?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  escalates pressure on Johnson in scathing memo\par \par \uc2 Republican Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  escalated her threat to oust Mike Johnson, issuing a searing indictment of the House speaker in a letter explaining her decision to file a motion to oust him.\par \par \uc2 In the five-page memo sent to her Republican colleagues on Tuesday morning, Greene laid out a detailed case against the speaker, accusing Johnson of failing to deliver on promises he ran on and breaking legislative procedural rules. Johnson is \u8220\'20\'1Cthrowing our own razor-thin majority into chaos by not serving his own GOP conference that elected him\u8221\'20\'1D, Greene wrote.\par \par \uc2 With so much at stake for our future and the future of our children, I will not tolerate this type of Republican \u8216\'20\'18leadership\u8217\'20\'19. This has been a complete and total surrender to, if not complete and total lockstep with, the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 agenda that has angered our Republican base so much and given them very little reason to vote for a Republican House majority.\par \par \uc2 Greene quoted the seven \u8220\'20\'1Ckey priorities\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson laid out when running for the speakership in October, and said he had \u8220\'20\'1Cnot lived up to a single one of his self-imposed tenets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Greene has not said if or when she plans to force a floor vote on Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s removal, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cwarning\u8221\'20\'1D and noting it would be a \u8220\'20\'1Crolling issue\u8221\'20\'1D, but the letter marks her first direct pitch to her GOP colleagues to join her push to oust the speaker.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some centrist Democrats have already indicated they will not allow Greene to let the chamber descend into chaos, especially if she forces the motion to vacate vote over the issue of Ukraine funding. Congressman \uc2 Jared Moskowitz\uc2 , a Democrat of Florida, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JaredEMoskowitz/status/1771209697091047484?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2  to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X last month:\par \par \uc2 I do not support Speaker Johnson but I will never stand by and let [Greene] \u8230\'20\'26 take over the people\u8217\'20\'19s House.\par \par \uc2 The House Democratic leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/02/28/us/politics/hakeem-jeffries-mike-johnson.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New York Times}}}\uc2  that he expected \u8220\'20\'1Ca reasonable number\u8221\'20\'1D of his caucus members would come to Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s assistance if his speakership was imperiled because of a vote on Ukraine aid.\par \par \uc2 But one of the leading House progressives, congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  of New York, has argued that Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 support for Johnson should come with some legislative strings attached. Ocasio-Cortez recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNNSOTU/status/1771892842736046111"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 My vote would most likely be for a Speaker Jeffries, which becomes an increasingly likely reality day after day as Republicans pursue further midterm resignation. But I think, for those of us and for any Democrat inclined, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think we do that for free.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 While Johnson weighs his legislative options to approve more money for Ukraine, the specter of the motion to vacate looms in the background.\par \par \uc2 If congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  of Georgia follows through on her threat to force a vote on Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s removal, the House must take up the matter within two legislative days. Johnson will then need the support of a majority of members to keep his job, and because of a recent string of Republican resignations, he can only afford to lose two votes within his conference.\par \par \uc2 As of now, few Republicans appear eager to revisit the spectacle of last fall, when the conference\u8217\'20\'19s repeated failures to elect a new speaker ground the House to a complete halt for weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Even as Johnson faces a challenge from the hard-right flank of his conference, other House Republicans insist the chamber must take action to assist Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 They warn that further inaction, after months of ignoring the White House\u8217\'20\'19s demands to approve more funding, will only embolden the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Mike Turner\uc2 , the Republican chair of the House intelligence committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/face-the-nation-full-transcript-03-31-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CBS News}}}\uc2  last Sunday:\par \par \uc2 We are at a critical juncture on the ground that is beginning to be able to impact not only morale of the Ukrainians that are fighting, but also their ability to fight. Putin knows this. This is obviously an area where we cannot allow Putin to win.\par \par \uc2 Johnson already has two legislative options to approve more money for Ukraine, the Senate-approved package and a smaller $66bn bill introduced by a bipartisan group of House members.\par \par \uc2 The second proposal would provide military-only funding for Ukraine, Israel and Taiwan, omitting the $10bn for humanitarian aid included in the Senate bill.\par \par \uc2 The House legislation also outlines a number of border security provisions, a bid to sway some Republican members who are otherwise wary of sending more money to Kyiv. Congressman Mike Lawler, a Republican of New York and one of the House bill\u8217\'20\'19s co-sponsors, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/03/31/politics/mike-lawler-ukraine-mike-johnson-cnntv/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  last Sunday:\par \par \uc2 I am hopeful that the speaker will put the bill on the floor or an amended version of the bill on the floor so that we can once and for all ensure that our allies have the aid and support that they need.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the House adjourned last month, the House speaker, Mike Johnson, vowed that the chamber would soon \u8220\'20\'1Ctake the necessary steps to address the supplemental funding request\u8221\'20\'1D, which includes money for Ukraine, Israel and Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 The Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/feb/13/us-senate-approves-95bn-aid-for-ukraine-israel-and-taiwan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  a $95bn foreign aid package in February, but Johnson indicated that the House would consider an amended proposal when members return to Washington. Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/01/mike-johnson-ukraine-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Fox News}}}\uc2  last Sunday:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve been talking to all the members, especially now over the district work period. When we return after this work period, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be moving a product, but it\u8217\'20\'19s going to, I think, have some important innovations.\par \par \uc2 Those innovations might include sending money to Kyiv as a loan or redirecting Russian assets seized under the Rebuilding Economic Prosperity and Opportunity (Repo) for Ukrainians Act.\par \par \uc2 But even those changes are unlikely to sway the most vocal Ukraine skeptics in the House Republican conference, such as the congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pressure mounts on Johnson over Ukraine aid as ouster threat looms\par \par \uc2 Good morning US politics readers.\par \par \uc2 The House returns today after a two-week Easter recess as the speaker, Mike Johnson, faces mounting pressure to advance a Ukraine aid package and the threat of an intra-party revolt if he does so.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has indicated the House will take up the issue of Ukraine funding this week, but many hard-right members of his conference remain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/14/republican-house-ukraine-support-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staunchly opposed}}}\uc2  to additional Ukraine aid and the Georgia congresswoman, \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , has already introduced a motion-to-vacate resolution, all but daring Johnson to move forward with a Ukraine aid bill so she can force a vote on the matter. Speaking to CNN last week, Greene said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m not saying I have a red line or a trigger, and I\u8217\'20\'19m not saying I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a red line or trigger. But I\u8217\'20\'19m going to tell you right now: funding Ukraine is probably one of the most egregious things that he can do.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the UK foreign secretary, \uc2 David Cameron\uc2 , is scheduled to meet with secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  and congressional lawmakers in Washington over the next two days. Ahead of his meeting with Blinken, Cameron took the unusual and potentially risky step of traveling to see \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at his Mar-a-Lago residence in Florida, in the hopes of persuading the presumptive Republican presidential candidate to drop his opposition to Ukraine aid deal that is being held up in Congress partly on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s instruction.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am ET. The secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , will meet with the British foreign secretary, \uc2 David Cameron\uc2 , at the state department.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 11:15am. Blinken and Biden will give a news conference.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 12.30pm. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will speak at Washington\u8217\'20\'19s Union Station about the \u8220\'20\'1Ccare economy\u8221\'20\'1D, a reference to care workers and family caregivers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1.30pm. The White House daily press briefing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 4pm. The House rules committee will meet to take up several bills, including a bill extending Section 702 in the FISA reauthorization and a resolution denouncing the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s immigration policies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 6pm. Biden and the first lady, Jill Biden, will welcome the Japanese prime minister, \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2  and his wife, Yuko Kishida, to the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will meet privately this afternoon in with relatives of Americans taken hostage in Gaza during the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terror attacks on southern Israel on 7 October.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240409ek49001s2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
