\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Biden campaign says Trump \u8216\'20\'18directly to blame\u8217\'20\'19 for Florida  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,105 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2024\par 20:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. You can read about Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c06b68f08601d5e73ab6c#block-660c06b68f08601d5e73ab6c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have condemned}}}\uc2  a Florida supreme court ruling that will allow a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to go into effect, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c0b8f8f08601d5e73ab9c#block-660c0b8f8f08601d5e73ab9c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seizing on}}}\uc2  a separate decision green lighting an initiative protecting access to the procedure to go before voters in November. The party has seen success in recent elections by campaigning against efforts to cut off access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and will try to replicate that in Florida, a state where Democratic candidates have struggled in recent years. To hammer the point home, top House lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c18a88f08bf76da23e425#block-660c18a88f08bf76da23e425"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convened a hearing}}}\uc2  in the state, which Democratic minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c1d098f08bf76da23e466#block-660c1d098f08bf76da23e466"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cground zero\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in the fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c3b698f08bf76da23e650#block-660c3b698f08bf76da23e650"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 Donald Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cdirectly to blame\u8221\'20\'1D for the Florida court ruling upholding the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator Sheldon Whitehouse{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c5c958f08df599c28afe0#block-660c5c958f08df599c28afe0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaled}}}\uc2  he was open to at least some of what Republican House speaker Mike Johnson is considering to approve military aid to Israel and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tina Smith, a Democratic senator from Minnesota, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c21ea8f08bf76da23e4a0#block-660c21ea8f08bf76da23e4a0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wants to repeal}}}\uc2  a moribund 19th-century law that some fear could be used to stop abortions nationwide.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Opponents of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c264f8f08df599c28ad62#block-660c264f8f08df599c28ad62"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are encouraging}}}\uc2  voters to choose \u8220\'20\'1Cuninstructed\u8221\'20\'1D in Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s primary today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the top Republican in the Senate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c33298f08bf76da23e5cd#block-660c33298f08bf76da23e5cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he wants to fight \u8220\'20\'1Cthe isolationist movement\u8221\'20\'1D in his party.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to today hold a small meeting with Muslims at the White House, rather than the larger gathering it traditionally hosts during Ramadan, in the latest sign of his administration\u8217\'20\'19s tensions with the community over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/04/01/1241988655/biden-iftar-ramadan-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Public Radio reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has repeatedly approved weapons transfers to Israel as it presses on with its invasion of Gaza, sparking protests from Muslims who have organized efforts to withhold their votes for Biden during the primaries. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the White House meeting tonight, from NPR:\par \par \uc2 The gathering is in lieu of the traditional Ramadan iftar dinner or Eid celebrations the White House usually hosts with Muslim leaders, and it comes amid ongoing political tensions given the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The goal, according to people familiar with the plans, is to allow guests to have a \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantive\u8221\'20\'1D conversation with the president about the situation in Gaza. Vice President Harris and national security adviser Jake Sullivan will also attend, the sources said. Biden last met with Muslim and Arab-American leaders at the White House in late October.\par \par \uc2 The sources said the White House had initially planned to host a small, solemn Ramadan dinner Tuesday evening, but plans changed after a number of Muslim invitees said they did not feel comfortable dining at the White House while scores of Palestinians are on the brink of starvation.\par \par \uc2 The White House still intends to host a small iftar dinner later Tuesday evening for a dozen or so Muslim staffers \u8212\'20\'14 a scaled-down version of the traditional celebration.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats fear the rift between Biden and Arab and Muslim communities could cost him support crucial to winning the November election, particularly in swing state Michigan. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/03/muslim-arab-american-reject-biden-outreach-michigan-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It could cost him the election\u8217\'20\'19: Muslim and Arab Americans reject Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18inept\u8217\'20\'19 outreach}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another tentative and potential sign of movement has emerged on the long-stalled military aid package for Ukraine and Israel.\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator Sheldon Whitehouse weighed in on Republican House speaker Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s comments yesterday, where he floated some potential demands he may make to move the package through his chamber. Whitehouse seems alright with two of the three changes Johnson requested, but takes issue with the third:\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m glad it looks like Ukraine aid will move. I\u8217\'20\'19m glad my REPO bill is part of the package. I don\u8217\'20\'19t mind a loan if the president can waive it. But it\u8217\'20\'19s just plain gross that Republicans need extraneous tribute for their fossil fuel donors. Yuck. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UV4iSCCNP4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/UV4iSCCNP4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sheldon Whitehouse (@SenWhitehouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1775238469956100340?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrOn the \u8220\'20\'1Cpause,\u8221\'20\'1D there\u8217\'20\'19s been no close look at LNG climate effects.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sheldon Whitehouse (@SenWhitehouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1775238471155642853?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFossil gas polluters just want us to look at the burner tip, not at massive methane leakage, nor emissions from transport, pressurizing, shipping, depressurizing and more transport \u8212\'20\'14 could be way worse than local coal. So they don\u8217\'20\'19t want it measured.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sheldon Whitehouse (@SenWhitehouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1775238472195838226?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Republicans and Democrats have been tussling over the aid proposal for months, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s mulled concessions will be palatable to Democrats, or enough for his fellow Republicans, many of whom are demanding new, strict border security policies to support the bill. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on where the House speaker says he now stands on the bill:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/01/mike-johnson-ukraine-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Johnson hints vote on Ukraine aid is up next despite threat to speakership}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is making a swing through Michigan and Wisconsin today, two states he will almost certainly need to win if he is to return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 His stop in Michigan took him to Grand Rapids, an area where Democrats have lately made inroads in what was traditionally Republican territory. It\u8217\'20\'19s also the site of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mlive.com/news/grand-rapids/2024/03/michigan-republicans-blast-immigration-policies-after-man-in-us-illegally-accused-of-murder.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a murder allegedly committed}}}\uc2  by an undocumented immigrant, and during his appearance in the city, Trump reiterated his vows to crack down on people in the country illegally:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CUnder Crooked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , every state is now a border state. Every town is now a border town.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 President Trump in Grand Rapids, Michigan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Y7Mu8nbfpf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Y7Mu8nbfpf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 RSBN ???? (@RSBNetwork) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RSBNetwork/status/1775235333279412494?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Attacks on migrants have been a mainstay for Trump since his first run for the White House, and thus far, this campaign has been no different:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/05/donald-trump-migrants-hannibal-lecter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump takes bizarre turn as he ratchets up racist rhetoric against migrants}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The first criminal trial \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  faces begins 15 April in New York City, on charges related to making hush money payments ahead of the 2016 election. The former president has taken to insulting various people involved in the case, and as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports, now faces a gag order:\par \par \uc2 The judge overseeing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  forthcoming criminal trial in New York expanded an existing gag order on Monday, preventing the former president from making inflammatory comments about the judge\u8217\'20\'19s family members, after they became the target of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s personal attacks.\par \par \uc2 The new protective order continues to allow Trump to rail against the judge and the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , who charged Trump last year with falsifying records to cover up a sex scandal before the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 But Trump is now expressly prohibited from assailing the family members of any lawyers or court staff involved in the case, as well as family members of the judge and the district attorney, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  supreme court justice Juan Merchan wrote in the revised order.\par \par \uc2 The order cited the recent attacks Trump had leveled at the judge\u8217\'20\'19s daughter and rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s contention that he should be free to criticize what he perceived to be conflicts of interest and other complaints because they amounted to \u8220\'20\'1Ccore political speech\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis pattern of attacking family members of presiding jurists and attorneys assigned to his cases serves no legitimate purpose,\u8221\'20\'1D Merchan wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CIt merely injects fear in those assigned or called to participate in the proceedings, that not only they, but their family members as well, are \u8216\'20\'18fair game\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/01/trump-gag-order-expanded-after-attacks-on-new-york-judges-daughter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump gag order expanded after he attacks judge\u8217\'20\'19s daughter on social media}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in Florida, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell reports that the federal judge handling \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trial on charges related to hiding classified documents has yet to schedule a start date, despite the best efforts of prosecutors:\par \par \uc2 The prospects of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  going to trial in July on charges of retaining national security documents, as suggested by special counsel prosecutors, are rapidly diminishing, with the judge overseeing the case yet to issue a schedule weeks after she was presented with the potential options.\par \par \uc2 The US district judge Aileen Cannon received proposed trial start dates from Trump and the special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  more than a month ago in advance of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/01/trump-mar-a-lago-documents-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing ostensibly to settle the matter}}}\uc2  in Fort Pierce, Florida, but she has still not decided when the proceeding will begin.\par \par \uc2 As a result, Trump has been able to avoid filing certain pre-trial motions that have to be completed before the case can proceed to trial, playing into his strategy of trying to delay the case as much as possible before the 2024 election in November.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal strategy for all of his criminal cases has been to delay, under the calculus that winning re-election would enable him to appoint a loyalist as attorney general who could direct prosecutors to drop the case, or pardon himself if he was convicted.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/02/judge-delay-schedule-trump-classified-documents-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge\u8217\'20\'19s inaction in Trump classified documents case dashes July trial hopes}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 There are more than 13.4 million people registered to vote in Florida, according to its division of elections, and one of them very well may be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Long associated with New York\u8217\'20\'19s real estate scene, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/oct/31/trump-florida-mar-a-lago-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he changed his residence}}}\uc2  from the Empire State to the Sunshine State during his time in the White House. That means he can vote on Florida\u8217\'20\'19s ballot initiative that will decide whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are enshrined in the state constitution \u8211\'20\'13 and you can expect that reporters will try their darnedest over the coming months to get him to reveal which way he leans on the issue.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Floridians will have an opportunity to weigh in on the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access this November, when they vote on an initiative that would enshrine reproductive rights in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on the Biden campaign press call, Fentrice Driskell, the Democratic leader of the Florida house, argued that the state supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to uphold an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban underscored the urgency of the November elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are seeing what Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda looks like here in Florida: extremist politicians inserting themselves into women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare, threatening doctors with prison time and endangering women\u8217\'20\'19s health and lives,\u8221\'20\'1D Driskell said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only thing that can stop governmental interference into our lives and exam rooms is to stay in the fight and by exercising our right to vote. This November, Florida will draw a line in the sand and say enough.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats hope that the presence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  initiative on the ballot might tip the scales in their party\u8217\'20\'19s favor in Florida, but they acknowledge that the task will be difficult, given Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 recent dominance in the purple state. Trump carried the state by 3 points in 2020, increasing his advantage from 2016 even as he lost the national election to Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re clear-eyed about how hard it will be to win Florida, but we also know that Trump does not have it in the bag,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julie Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager. \u8220\'20\'1CWe definitely see Florida in play.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign says Trump 'directly to blame' for Florida \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign team said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cdirectly to blame\u8221\'20\'1D for the ruling upholding an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Florida, given that the former president nominated three of the supreme court justices who helped overturn Roe v Wade in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Maga [\u8217\'20\'19Make America Great Again\u8217\'20\'19] Republicans across this country are ripping away access to reproductive health care and inserting themselves into the most personal decisions women can make, from contraception to IVF,\u8221\'20\'1D Julie Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager, told reporters on a press call.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd make no mistake: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will do everything in his power to try and enact a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if he\u8217\'20\'19s reelected.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, the Biden campaign released a new ad, titled \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GgtPkQtEb_k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trust}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, that highlights Trump\u8217\'20\'19s past comments bragging about the reversal of Roe and also warns of the possibility of a federal ban. The ad will air across battleground states as part of the Biden campaign\u8217\'20\'19s broader media blitz this spring.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are the stakes in November, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue to make sure that every single voter knows them,\u8221\'20\'1D Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez said. \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s the bottom line: Trump and Maga Republicans are working to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, while President Biden and Vice-President Harris will never stop fighting to protect reproductive freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c06b68f08601d5e73ab6c#block-660c06b68f08601d5e73ab6c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have condemned}}}\uc2  a Florida supreme court ruling that will allow a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to go into effect, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c0b8f8f08601d5e73ab9c#block-660c0b8f8f08601d5e73ab9c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seizing on}}}\uc2  a separate decision to allow an initiative protecting access to the procedure to go before voters in November. The party has seen success in recent elections by campaigning against efforts to cut off access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and will try to replicate that in Florida, a state where Democratic candidates have struggled in recent years. To hammer the point home, top House lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c18a88f08bf76da23e425#block-660c18a88f08bf76da23e425"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convened a hearing}}}\uc2  in the state, which Democratic minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c1d098f08bf76da23e466#block-660c1d098f08bf76da23e466"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cground zero\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in the fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tina Smith, a Democratic senator from Minnesota, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c21ea8f08bf76da23e4a0#block-660c21ea8f08bf76da23e4a0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wants to repeal}}}\uc2  a moribund 19th-century law that some fear could be used to stop abortions nationwide.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Opponents of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c264f8f08df599c28ad62#block-660c264f8f08df599c28ad62"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are encouraging}}}\uc2  voters to choose \u8220\'20\'1Cuninstructed\u8221\'20\'1D in Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s primary today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the top Republican in the Senate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/02/election-updates-trump-rally-biden-campaign-latest?page=with:block-660c33298f08bf76da23e5cd#block-660c33298f08bf76da23e5cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he wants to fight \u8220\'20\'1Cthe isolationist movement\u8221\'20\'1D in his party.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress has some unfinished business to deal with when it returns to Washington DC next week, in the form of a military aid package for Israel, Ukraine and other US allies. It\u8217\'20\'19s been held up by Republicans in the House, some of whom are opposed to further aid to Kyiv, and the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports that the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican has signaled he will make overcoming these holdouts a priority:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mitch-mcconnell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitch McConnell}}}\uc2  will spend the rest of his time in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cfighting\u8221\'20\'1D isolationists in his own Republican party, the longtime GOP leader said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m particularly involved in actually fighting back against the isolationist movement in my own party,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whas11.com/video/news/politics/senate-minority-leader-mitch-mcconnell-discusses-ukraine-new-uofl-head-coach/417-0ce37b02-4061-4098-b351-437766bd36c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told WHAS}}}\uc2 , a radio station in his state, Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd some in the other as well. And the symbol of that lately is: are we going to help Ukraine or not? I\u8217\'20\'19ve got this sort of on my mind for the next couple years as something I\u8217\'20\'19m going to focus on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McConnell, 82, has led {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  in the Senate for 17 years. In March, he said he would step down at the end of this year, after an election in which Republicans have a good chance of retaking the chamber.\par \par \uc2 McConnell assured his decision to step down was not related to recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/06/rand-paul-comments-mitch-mcconnell-freeze-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 health scares}}}\uc2  and said he would stay to the end of his term in 2027.\par \par \uc2 Isolationism has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/13/republicans-ukraine-aid-analysis-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surged}}}\uc2  in the Republican party under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , president between 2017 and 2021 and the presumptive nominee again for November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/02/mitch-mcconnell-republican-isolationists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitch McConnell: I will fight isolationist Republicans for rest of Senate term}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s allies, including the United States and Britain, are demanding it investigate the killing of seven aid workers in Gaza that were with the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  charity.\par \par \uc2 Follow our live blog for more on this developing story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/apr/02/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-israel-gaza-war-today-gaza-foreign-aid-workers-killed-idf-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Middle East crisis live: Netanyahu admits Israeli forces killed Gaza aid workers in \u8216\'20\'18tragic\u8217\'20\'19 strike}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The youth climate group Sunrise Movement is continuing its efforts to support a permanent ceasefire in Gaza by calling on Wisconsin progressives to vote \u8220\'20\'1Cuninstructed delegation\u8221\'20\'1D in today\u8217\'20\'19s primary, which will serve as a test of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s standing in the crucial swing state.\par \par \uc2 Progressive organizers in Wisconsin have launched a campaign, based on similar initiatives in states like Michigan and Minnesota, in support of the \u8220\'20\'1Cuninstructed\u8221\'20\'1D option to protest Biden\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBiden\u8217\'20\'19s best chance to succeed in November is by supporting an immediate and permanent ceasefire and ending unconditional military aid to the Israeli government,\u8221\'20\'1D Michele Wiendling, political director of Sunrise Movement, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president is hemorrhaging the support of young voters by aiding in the destruction of people\u8217\'20\'19s lives and homes in Gaza. If President Biden wants to defeat Trump, he must listen to young people, people of color, and the working class who put him in office in 2020 and immediately change course.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Polls close in Wisconsin at 9pm ET, so Biden will soon learn how much support he is at risk of losing in the battleground state.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 A slew of states are holding presidential primaries today \u8211\'20\'13 including Wisconsin, where the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman}}}\uc2  reports opponents of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel hope to send a shot across his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s bow in a swing state crucial to his re-election hopes:\par \par \uc2 Voters in Wisconsin cast their ballots today in an election that will test voter enthusiasm for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and potentially enshrine two amendments in the state constitution impacting election administration across the state.\par \par \uc2 The president and former president are already the presumptive nominees and will almost certainly face off in the general election in November, and it seems that the threat of prosecution, general unpopularity and advanced age can\u8217\'20\'19t stop them.\par \par \uc2 But while the primary will not offer alternative candidates, a group of activists in Wisconsin see it as an opportunity to push Biden on his policy toward Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Gaza. The organizers, inspired by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/28/michigan-uncommitted-vote-biden-israel-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cuncommitted\u8221\'20\'1D campaign}}}\uc2 , which garnered more than 100,000 votes there, are calling on voters to choose \u8220\'20\'1Cuninstructed\u8221\'20\'1D instead of Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe margins of our elections are so incredibly close \u8211\'20\'13 less than 1% in the last two presidential election cycles \u8211\'20\'13 so I think it would behoove the administration to pay attention,\u8221\'20\'1D said Reema Ahmad, the lead organizer of the Listen to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2  campaign.\par \par \uc2 Organizers with the campaign aim to turn out as many voters for \u8220\'20\'1Cuninstructed\u8221\'20\'1D as Biden\u8217\'20\'19s margin of victory in 2020 to demonstrate their critical role in November, Ahmad said. The campaign has relied on the support of a broad network of progressive organizations, including the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest network of Latino voters, Voces de la Frontera Action and Black Leaders Organizing Communities (Bloc), groups that helped propel Biden to his narrow 2020 victory.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/02/wisconsin-primary-biden-trump-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden faces test in Wisconsin as Gaza supporters call for \u8216\'20\'18uninstructed\u8217\'20\'19 vote}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator announces plan to repeal 19th century law that could stop \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator Tina Smith announced she is leading an effort to repeal the Comstock Act, a federal anti-obscenity law passed in 1873 that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters fear could be used to ban the procedure nationwide.\par \par \uc2 While the Biden administration considers the act irrelevant, it remains in force and includes language that could criminalize the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication such as mifepristone, or drugs used in surgical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The concern is that a future president who opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , could decide to enforce the statute to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even in states that allowed the procedure to continue after Roe v Wade was overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLegislation to repeal Comstock could take many forms, and we need to do it the right way. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19ve begun reaching out to my colleagues in the House of Representatives and the Senate to build support and see what legislation to repeal the Comstock Act might look like,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Smith, who represents Minnesota, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/02/opinion/comstock-act-abortion-repeal.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists will continue to exploit any avenue they can find to get the national ban they champion, and I want to make sure my bill shuts down every one of those avenues. Once the Supreme Court has had its say (and many legal analysts speculate that the mifepristone case heard last week should be thrown out on procedural grounds, and may well be), I\u8217\'20\'19ll be ready to have mine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Comstock Act came up last week before the supreme court as a conservative group argued to remove mifepristone from pharmacy shelves. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/27/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court hearing not a success for anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  doctors, experts say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top House Democrat \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  calls Florida 'ground zero' in fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\par \par \uc2 Democratic House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  said Florida is \u8220\'20\'1Cground zero\u8221\'20\'1D in the fight for reproductive rights, after the state supreme court allowed a ban on abortions after six weeks of pregnancy to go into effect, while also green-lighting a ballot initiative to protect access to the procedure:\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Minority Leader Jeffries (D-NY) on Florida Supreme Court \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida is now ground zero in the fight to protect a woman's freedom to make her own reproductive health care decisions. As House Democrats... we stand with you to protect reproductive freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uI8oU1EDK0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uI8oU1EDK0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1775171742916284829?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Congress is on recess right now, with lawmakers spread across the country, but Jeffries and other lawmakers are holding a special hearing in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Broward county to focus public attention on how the court ruling will affect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Democrats are hoping that the ballot initiative will help them win congressional seats in the state in November \u8211\'20\'13 and perhaps even help \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  carry Florida, which would greatly increase his chances of winning another term in the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top House Democrats have convened in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Broward county for a committee hearing intended to focus attention on how the state\u8217\'20\'19s impending six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban will affect women and families.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s congresswoman \uc2 Debbie Wasserman Schultz\uc2 , who represents the area:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. \uc2 Debbie Wasserman Schultz\uc2  (D-FL) opens a field hearing in Florida after the state Supreme Court allowed a 6-week ban to take effect in May:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will impact not only millions of women in the Sunshine State, but millions more across the South who... look to Florida.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/atT66fA9nJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/atT66fA9nJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1775170087193919754?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other legal news yesterday, a federal judge rejected an attempt by the president\u8217\'20\'19s son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  to have tax charges against him dismissed. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what that means, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer promised to continue \u8220\'20\'1Cvigorously\u8221\'20\'1D contesting federal tax charges against the president\u8217\'20\'19s son after a California judge rejected an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/27/hunter-biden-tax-evasion-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempt}}}\uc2  to dismiss them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe strongly disagree with the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision and will continue to vigorously pursue Mr Biden\u8217\'20\'19s challenges to the abnormal way the special counsel handled this investigation and charged this case,\u8221\'20\'1D Abbe Lowell said, after the judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 After a plea agreement to avoid charges {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/26/why-hunter-biden-plea-deal-fell-apart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell apart}}}\uc2  last year, the special counsel, David Weiss, charged Biden nine times, accusing him of evading $1.4m in taxes. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/11/hunter-biden-arraignment-federal-tax-charges-los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded}}}\uc2  not guilty. He also pleaded not guilty to criminal charges for allegedly lying about addiction issues when purchasing a gun.\par \par \uc2 Weiss was appointed US attorney for Delaware by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/sco-weiss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made}}}\uc2  a special counsel by \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , the US attorney general appointed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  has long been the subject of Republican attempts to establish corruption involving his father, culminating in an impeachment effort which after a series of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/21/response-biden-impeachment-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chaotic hearings}}}\uc2  appears unlikely to succeed.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s son argues that the charges against him are politically motivated, arising from Republican pressure on Weiss. The special counsel rejects such claims.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/02/hunter-biden-federal-tax-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hunter Biden lawyer promises to \u8216\'20\'18vigorously\u8217\'20\'19 contest federal tax charges}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  on just what exactly the Florida supreme court decided yesterday, and how it will upend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state:\par \par \uc2 Florida residents will get the chance to vote on a ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  state supreme court ruled on Monday, teeing up a dramatic electoral showdown over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in a state that has become a haven for women fleeing southern \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 The decision is a victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists \u8211\'20\'13 but one that was significantly tempered by a second decision also issued on Monday, in which the state supreme court ruled to uphold Florida\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. That decision paves the way for a separate six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 passed in 2023 but on hold pending the outcome of the case over the 15-week ban \u8211\'20\'13 to take effect.\par \par \uc2 The six-week ban will take effect in 30 days.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/01/florida-abortion-right-constitution-vote-november-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida supreme court clears way for both \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ballot measure and six-week ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign manager sees opportunity in Florida after \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling\par \par \uc2 Florida voters haven\u8217\'20\'19t given the state\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes to a Democrat since \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election victory in 2012. But after the state supreme court ruling yesterday allowing a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban passed by its Republican lawmakers to go into effect, Julie Chavez Rodriguez, the Biden-Harris campaign manager, said the president has a shot at winning the Sunshine state in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are entering the general election with multiple pathways to 270 electoral votes \u8211\'20\'13 something Team Trump is not afforded. That includes investing in Florida as a pathway to victory: a state where President Biden has a compelling story of results, Trump and [Republican US senator] \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s extreme agenda is making Floridians\u8217\'20\'19 lives worse, and the Democratic coalition is growing and energized,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote in a memo.\par \par \uc2 Beyond outrage over the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Chavez Rodriguez noted Florida\u8217\'20\'19s top court also allowed a ballot initiative to protect access to the procedure to appear on the November ballot, potentially giving Democrats an opportunity to fire up their voters:\par \par \uc2 With an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  amendment officially on the ballot this November in Florida, President Biden and Vice President Harris and their commitment to fighting back against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attacks on reproductive freedom will help mobilize and expand the electorate in the state, given the overwhelming majority of Floridians support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. And Florida Republicans will be forced to defend their cruel, indefensible support of this \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden condemns Florida court's 'extreme decision' that will allow six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to take effect\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  decried yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s Florida court ruling that sets the stage for the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to take effect, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Coutrageous\u8221\'20\'1D and warning women\u8217\'20\'19s health will suffer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYesterday\u8217\'20\'19s extreme decision puts desperately needed medical care even further out of reach for millions of women in Florida and across the South,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Court not only upheld Florida\u8217\'20\'19s current ban on women being able to make their own reproductive choices, it will likely trigger Governor DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 even more extreme law that would prevent women from accessing care before many even know they are pregnant. It is outrageous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s bans \u8211\'20\'13 like those put forward by Republican elected officials across the country \u8211\'20\'13 are putting the health and lives of millions of women at risk. These extreme laws take away women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom to make their own health care decisions and threaten physicians with jail time simply for providing the medical care that they were trained to provide.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats look to turn up heat on GOP after Florida court authorizes six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Democrats have not had much luck in Florida lately, where its status as a swing state has been eroded by years of Republican victories. And the GOP once again got their way yesterday when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/01/florida-abortion-right-constitution-vote-november-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a court allowed}}}\uc2  a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban signed by governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  to take effect in 30 days. But voters in many states, even those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 otherwise}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hostile}}}\uc2  to Democrats, have signaled that they are not on board with efforts to tighten access to the procedure, and today, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign and its allies are seizing on the Florida ruling to argue it is a sign of what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would do if returned to the White House and perhaps regain some momentum in Florida. At 10am ET, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , the Democratic House minority leader, \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , the health and human services secretary, and other lawmakers will hold a hearing in Broward county on threats to productive freedom, while the Biden-Harris campaign is convening a call between reporters and North Carolina governor Roy Cooper to elaborate on the message.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will hold two rallies today in swing states Michigan and Wisconsin, where he\u8217\'20\'19s expected to hammer Biden over immigration policy \u8211\'20\'13 reliably fertile ground for Republicans. The former president has voiced support for banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/20/trump-abortion-ban-zurawski-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at 15 weeks of pregnancy}}}\uc2 , and we\u8217\'20\'19ll see if he weighs in on the decision in Florida.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel has expressed \u8220\'20\'1Csincere sorrow\u8221\'20\'1D over the deaths of seven aid workers in Gaza, which killed nationals of the UK, US, Australia, Poland and Palestine. Follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/apr/02/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-israel-gaza-war-today-gaza-foreign-aid-workers-killed-idf-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our live blog}}}\uc2  for the latest on this story.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A slew of states are holding primaries today, including Wisconsin, Connecticut, Rhode Island and New York, while Arkansas and Mississippi will hold primary run offs. Trump and Biden both already have the delegates they need to win their parties\u8217\'20\'19 nominations.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House press briefing takes place at 1.30pm.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240402ek42001xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
