\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Senate Democrats demand end to rightwing \u8216\'20\'18judge shopping\u8217\'20\'19 but move draws immediate attack from Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 5,176 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 March 2024\par 21:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read all our politics news here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats feuded with their Republican counterparts over the practice of \u8220\'20\'1Cjudge shopping\u8221\'20\'1D, which critics say a conservative group used to get their challenge to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone before the supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 though the justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606f3b58f082a6ebed935ac#block-6606f3b58f082a6ebed935ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sounded skeptical}}}\uc2 . In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606ed478f08cfe8870d322d#block-6606ed478f08cfe8870d322d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter sent today}}}\uc2  to the body overseeing federal courts, Democratic majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and eight colleagues urged them to stand firm against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606f6dc8f082a6ebed935ed#block-6606f6dc8f082a6ebed935ed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican attacks}}}\uc2  on a new policy to cut down on the practice. But there is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606cc208f08cfe8870d3009#block-6606cc208f08cfe8870d3009"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one thing}}}\uc2  the top lawmakers in Congress agree on: Russia\u8217\'20\'19s imperative to free jailed Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , who was arrested one year ago today. \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606d2388f08cfe8870d3061#block-6606d2388f08cfe8870d3061"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined}}}\uc2  the calls for his release, while the Journal made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606cff68f082a6ebed9333d#block-6606cff68f082a6ebed9333d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a renewed push}}}\uc2  to raise public awareness of his plight.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606b1798f082a6ebed93136#block-6606b1798f082a6ebed93136"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised big bucks}}}\uc2  at a fundraiser in New York City last night, but faced familiar disruptions from pro-Palestine protesters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606ea0b8f08cfe8870d3208#block-6606ea0b8f08cfe8870d3208"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also has plans}}}\uc2  to rake in money, with an event scheduled for next week in Florida.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-66070c658f082a6ebed93753#block-66070c658f082a6ebed93753"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly approved}}}\uc2  another shipment of weapons to Israel despite growing protests over the death toll in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A proposal to free jailed Americans, Gershkovich included, and \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2  fell apart after the Russian dissident\u8217\'20\'19s death last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606d63e8f0831dce2219d22#block-6606d63e8f0831dce2219d22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Journal reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump and eight co-defendants {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-660716528f08cfe8870d3452#block-660716528f08cfe8870d3452"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly appealed}}}\uc2  a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling allowing \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  to continue prosecuting the Georgia election subversion case.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election is set to be like no other, because one of the two major candidates is facing criminal charges in two states and at the federal level.\par \par \uc2 But whether any of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s cases will be resolved before election day remains a major unanswered question. One of the indictments got its trial date set this week, but the rest are mired in pre-trial motions. Have a look at our explainer for an idea of where things stand:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Donald Trump case tracker: where does each investigation stand?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump, co-defendants appeal ruling allowing \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  to prosecute Georgia election subversion case \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and eight of his co-defendants in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/13/trump-georgia-case-charges-dismissed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia election subversion case}}}\uc2  have appealed a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling allowing Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  to continue prosecuting the case, the Atlanta Journal-Constitution reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrBreaking: Trump and eight other defendants in the Fulton election interference case appeal ruling that allowed DA \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  to stay on case.\par \par \uc2 They argue, among other things, that Judge McAfee erred when he determined Willis didn't have a personal stake in the case\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tamar Hallerman (@TamarHallerman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TamarHallerman/status/1773793542575472734?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe appeal isn't a surprise -- defendants had asked McAfee for permission to appeal, which he granted earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 It's not up to the Georgia Court of Appeals to decide whether to take up the appeal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NIn7yUGXmk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/NIn7yUGXmk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tamar Hallerman (@TamarHallerman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TamarHallerman/status/1773794151173173645?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the group argued that Willis should be removed from the case because she had a conflict of interest in hiring as a special counsel Nathan Wade, who she had had a romantic relationship with.\par \par \uc2 Judge Scott McAfee ruled that Willis could stay as prosecutor, but only if Wade quit, which he did. However, McAfee also allowed Trump and the others to appeal his ruling, which they have now done.\par \par \uc2 Needless to say, the appeal could further delay the trial of one of the four criminal indictments Trump is facing, potentially leaving it to be settled after the November presidential election. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/20/trump-fani-willis-georgia-appeal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Defendants can appeal decision to keep Fani Willis on Trump case, judge rules}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s decision to supply Israel with more weapons comes as the state department said famine conditions \u8220\'20\'1Cquite possibly\u8221\'20\'1D are present in parts of northern Gaza. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about that, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/peterbeaumont"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Beaumont}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Famine is already probably present in at least some areas of northern Gaza, while other areas are in danger of falling into conditions of starvation, the US state department said on Friday a day after the world\u8217\'20\'19s top court ordered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  to admit food aid into the territory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we can say with confidence that famine is a significant risk in the south and centre but not present, in the north, it is both a risk and quite possibly is present in at least some areas,\u8221\'20\'1D a state department official told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The US comments add to a growing and powerful consensus that Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military offensive in the Palestinian coastal territory has triggered a famine.\par \par \uc2 The number of trucks distributing aid in south and central {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  had nearly reached 200 a day, an increase on a month ago, but more were needed, the state department official said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou need to address the full nutrition needs of the population of Gaza of all ages. That means more than just that minimal survival level feeding,\u8221\'20\'1D the official said, adding that malnutrition, and infant and young-child mortality was a significant, growing problem.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has to be addressed by additional assistance coming and the right kind of assistance coming in,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/29/famine-gaza-us-state-department-israel-food-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Famine is now probably present in Gaza, US says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden administration approves another shipment of bombs, military jets to Israel despite concerns over death toll \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signed off on another transfer to Israel of military jets and bombs, including 2,000-pound munitions linked to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/01/jabalia-camp-airstrike-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 devastating strikes}}}\uc2  in Gaza, despite growing concerns among Democrats of the civilian toll in the country\u8217\'20\'19s campaign against \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2024/03/29/us-weapons-israel-gaza-war/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has repeatedly sent arms to Israel following \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 7 October attack, and continues to press Congress to approve legislation authorizing $14bn in military aid. The support has sparked a backlash towards the president from protesters concerned over the death toll in Gaza, where 32,000 people have died following Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the weapons transfer, from the Post:\par \par \uc2 The new arms packages include more than 1,800 MK84 2,000-pound bombs and 500 MK82 500-pound bombs, according to Pentagon and State Department officials familiar with the matter. The 2,000 pound bombs have been linked to previous mass-casualty events throughout Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military campaign in Gaza. These officials, like some others, spoke to \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  on the condition of anonymity because recent authorizations have not been disclosed publicly.\par \par \uc2 The development underscores that while rifts have emerged between the United States and Israel over the war\u8217\'20\'19s conduct, the Biden administration views weapons transfers as off-limits when considering how to influence the actions of Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have continued to support Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself,\u8221\'20\'1D said a White House official. \u8220\'20\'1CConditioning aid has not been our policy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats, including allies of President Biden, say the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  has a responsibility to withhold weapons in the absence of an Israeli commitment to limit civilian casualties during a planned operation in Rafah, a final \uc2 Hamas\uc2  stronghold, and ease restrictions on humanitarian aid into the enclave, which is on the brink of famine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden administration needs to use their leverage effectively and, in my view, they should receive these basic commitments before greenlighting more bombs for Gaza,\u8221\'20\'1D Sen. \uc2 Chris Van Hollen\uc2  (D-Md.) said in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to back up what we say with what we do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Israeli government declined to comment on the authorizations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia state legislators have changed laws that will make it easier to challenge a voter\u8217\'20\'19s registration.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s George Chidi reports:\par \par \uc2 Georgia legislators changed state election laws in the midnight hours of Friday, widening the criteria to challenge a voter\u8217\'20\'19s registration, removing bar codes from printed ballots and increasing the documentation local elections officials must produce to certify elections.\par \par \uc2 The proposals will take effect 1 July, assuming the Georgia governor, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , signs the legislation into law.\par \par \uc2 Voting rights groups expressed their highest concern about how Senate Bill 189 potentially expands challenges to voter registrations. Conservative advocates have been issuing large-scale systematic challenges to voters \u8211\'20\'13 dozens or hundreds at a time in some districts, like Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s Fulton and DeKalb counties.\par \par \uc2 Each challenge under existing law has to be considered on its individual merits under current law, which can exhaust the resources of local election officials, voting rights advocates argue.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/29/georgia-state-election-law-changes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia lawmakers make it easier to challenge a voter\u8217\'20\'19s registration}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to visit Baltimore following bridge collapse\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said on Friday that he will visit Baltimore next week, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s expected visit follows the collapse of the Francis Scott Key Bridge earlier this week after the Singaporean-flagged cargo ship Dali crashed into it.\par \par \uc2 Six men, who were filling potholes on the bridge, are presumed dead. The bodies of two of the men who were trapped in their vehicle were recovered from the Patapsco River on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The authorities identified the men as Alejandro Hern\u225\'00\'E1ndez Fuentes, a 35-year-old originally from Mexico who was living in Baltimore, and Dorlian Ronial Castillo Cabrera, 26, who was from Guatemala and was living in Dundalk, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/maryland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maryland}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  rapid response director Alex Floyd issued the following statement on Friday in response to Michael Whatley\u8217\'20\'19s appointment as the new chair of the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hand picked Michael Whatley to take over the \uc2 RNC\uc2  because he parroted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless lies about the 2020 election, and Whatley is returning the favor by making election denialism a key litmus test to join the GOP.\par \par \uc2 Putting an election denying extremist like Whatley in charge of the \uc2 RNC\uc2  makes it clear that the future of our democracy is on the ballot in this election \u8211\'20\'13 and the American people will once again reject Trump and his MAGA allies this November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats are feuding with their Republican counterparts over the practice of \u8220\'20\'1Cjudge shopping\u8221\'20\'1D, which critics say a conservative group used to get their challenge to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone before the supreme court, which nonetheless {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606f3b58f082a6ebed935ac#block-6606f3b58f082a6ebed935ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sounded skeptical}}}\uc2 . In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606ed478f08cfe8870d322d#block-6606ed478f08cfe8870d322d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter sent today}}}\uc2  to the body overseeing federal courts, Democratic majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and eight colleagues urged them to stand firm against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606f6dc8f082a6ebed935ed#block-6606f6dc8f082a6ebed935ed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican attacks}}}\uc2  on a new policy to cut down on the practice. But there is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606cc208f08cfe8870d3009#block-6606cc208f08cfe8870d3009"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one thing}}}\uc2  the top lawmakers in Congress agree on: Russia\u8217\'20\'19s imperative to free jailed Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , who was arrested one year ago today. \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606d2388f08cfe8870d3061#block-6606d2388f08cfe8870d3061"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined}}}\uc2  the call for his release, while the Journal made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606cff68f082a6ebed9333d#block-6606cff68f082a6ebed9333d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a renewed push}}}\uc2  to raise public awareness of his plight.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606b1798f082a6ebed93136#block-6606b1798f082a6ebed93136"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised big bucks}}}\uc2  at a fundraiser in New York City last night, but faced familiar disruptions from pro-Palestine protesters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606ea0b8f08cfe8870d3208#block-6606ea0b8f08cfe8870d3208"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also has plans}}}\uc2  to rake in money with an event scheduled for next week in Florida.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A proposal to free jailed Americans, Gershkovich included, and \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2  fell apart after the Russian dissident\u8217\'20\'19s death last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/29/us-politics-biden-trump-updates?page=with:block-6606d63e8f0831dce2219d22#block-6606d63e8f0831dce2219d22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Journal reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  squabbles with Democrats over 'restoring trust' in federal judges\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , is not happy with Democrats or the Judicial Conference for the attempt to limit \u8220\'20\'1Cjudge shopping\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 McConnell has been transformative when it comes to the federal courts. As Senate leader in 2016, he famously blocked \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  from filling a supreme court vacancy, giving \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  the opportunity to appoint three justices \u8211\'20\'13 all of whom have generally signed on to conservative decisions, including the overturning of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The Judicial Conference\u8217\'20\'19s new rule does not specifically deal with the supreme court, but rather the path that lawsuits take to get there. But in a floor speech earlier this month, before the Senate departed for its ongoing recess, McConnell criticized Democratic majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  for supporting the new policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats are salivating at the possibility of shutting down access to justice in the venues favored by conservatives,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. McConnell went on:\par \par \uc2 If Republicans see a federal judiciary that is using its procedural independence to wade into political disputes, any incentive we may have to defend that procedural independence will vanish, as well.\par \par \uc2 This was an unforced error by the Judicial Conference. I hope they will reconsider. And I hope district courts throughout the country will instead weigh what is best for their jurisdictions, not half-baked \u8220\'20\'1Cguidance\u8221\'20\'1D that just does Washington Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 bidding.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While Democrats are upset over how a conservative group used \u8220\'20\'1Cjudge shopping\u8221\'20\'1D to pursue a lawsuit against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reports that most supreme court justices did not appear ready to decide the case in their favor during arguments earlier this week:\par \par \uc2 The supreme court on Tuesday seemed skeptical of arguments made by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors asking it to roll back the availability of mifepristone, a drug typically used in US medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The arguments were part of the first major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case to reach the justices since a 6-3 majority ruled in 2022 to overturn Roe v Wade and end the national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rightwing groups that brought the case argued that the justices should roll back measures taken since 2016 by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) to expand the drug\u8217\'20\'19s availability. A decision in the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors\u8217\'20\'19 favor would apply nationwide, including in states that protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, and would probably make the drug more difficult to acquire.\par \par \uc2 Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  now accounts for almost two-thirds of abortions performed in the US.\par \par \uc2 Much of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s arguments focused on whether the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors who sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , a coalition known as the Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine, have standing, or the right to bring the case in the first place. The doctors claim they will suffer harm if they have to treat women who experience complications from mifepristone, an argument the Biden administration, which appealed the case to the court, has rejected as too speculative.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court seems skeptical of arguments against \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  drug mifepristone}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats demand end to rightwing 'judge shopping'\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats including majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  have today called for the federal courts\u8217\'20\'19 policymaking body to stand firm against conservative attacks on its new rule intended to curb the practice of \u8220\'20\'1Cjudge shopping\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The term is a reference to the practice of litigants suing over government policies in certain jurisdictions where federal judges may be sympathetic to their cause. An example of this may be seen in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/25/abortion-pill-case-fda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the lawsuit by a conservative group attempting to remove}}}\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone from pharmacies, which was first filed before a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -appointed federal judge in Texas who previously worked for a rightwing Christian law firm.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the Judicial Conference of the United States {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscourts.gov/news/2024/03/12/conference-acts-promote-random-case-assignment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a new policy that \u8220\'20\'1Caddresses all civil actions that seek to bar or mandate state or federal actions, \u8216\'20\'18whether by declaratory judgment and/or any form of injunctive relief.\u8217\'20\'19 In such cases, judges would be assigned through a district-wide random selection process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The policy drew attacks from Republicans including Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , who described it as \u8220\'20\'1Chalf-baked\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a letter sent today to the Judicial Conference\u8217\'20\'19s secretary, Schumer and eight other Democratic senators specifically singled out the mifepristone case, and wrote:\par \par \uc2 This judge-shopping tactic is more pernicious than it might appear. Even though there are only a few courts subject to this issue, single district judges can issue rulings that thwart congressional statutes and stymie agency actions on a nationwide basis. That means certain plaintiffs are motivated to file their cases in divisions where they know the judge hearing the case is aligned with their goals.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The anti-democratic practice of judge shopping erodes the rule of law and the public\u8217\'20\'19s trust in the judiciary. Your new policy rebalances our court system and will help to restore Americans\u8217\'20\'19 confidence in judicial rulings. We encourage you to defend it as courts across the country implement it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  may have had a big night of fundraising in New York yesterday, but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is looking to outdo him next week, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joannawalters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joanna Walters}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  report:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are in a new phase of a heavyweight fundraising smackdown as the US president raised a record $25m at a glitzy event with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bill Clinton}}}\uc2  on Thursday night, while Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Republican campaign claimed it would outdo Biden next week with a $33m event in Florida, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 Biden and his Democratic predecessor headlined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/28/biden-fundraiser-new-york-obama-clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a star-studded fundraiser}}}\uc2  with Clinton at the Radio City Music Hall event, hosted by Mindy Kaling and featuring Lizzo, Queen Latifah and Stephen Colbert.\par \par \uc2 Obama and Biden flew to the city on Air Force One together in a show of unity and Democratic campaign heft as the 2024 election enters an important phase between the main primary season and the summer nominating conventions, which are expected to anoint Biden and Trump as their parties\u8217\'20\'19 candidates.\par \par \uc2 The glittering Democratic fundraiser was punctuated by protests not just outside but also inside the auditorium, as attendees rose at several different moments to shout over the discussion, referencing Biden\u8217\'20\'19s backing of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel-hamas-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShame on you, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D one yelled, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/29/biden-trump-election-fundraising"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden and Trump shift to new phase of urgent fundraising in 2024 US election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Why did Russia arrest Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , and what might they want in return for his release? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2  looks into the question, one year into the American journalist\u8217\'20\'19s detention:\par \par \uc2 Friday marks the grim first anniversary of the day when masked Russian officers grabbed \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , an American journalist, at a steakhouse in Yekaterinburg where he was waiting to eat on a reporting trip.\par \par \uc2 Gershkovich, a 32-year-old reporter for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/wallstreetjournal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2 , has not seen a day of freedom since. He has been held in the infamous Lefortovo prison on the outskirts of Moscow, where the Soviet author Alexander Solzhenitsyn was once detained.\par \par \uc2 A half century later, Gershkovich is there on the grounds of spying charges that are entirely unsupported by evidence. Despite that glaring absence, a Moscow court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/russian-detention-of-wsj-reporter-evan-gershkovich-extended-by-three-months"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held a closed hearing this week}}}\uc2  to grant the \uc2 Federal Security Service (FSB)\uc2  approval to hold the journalist another three months.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/29/evan-gershkovich-russia-prison-wsj-reporter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s not broken\u8217\'20\'19: a year later, Evan Gershkovich is still in Russian prison}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more of what we know about Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s detention in Russia, one year on:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on Friday said the US was working every day to secure the release of \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/29/evan-gershkovich-russia-prison-wsj-reporter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first anniversary}}}\uc2  of the 32-year-old Wall Street journalist\u8217\'20\'19s detention in Russia on charges of spying that he and the \uc2 US government\uc2  vehemently reject.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJournalism is not a crime, and Evan went to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  to do his job as a reporter \u8211\'20\'13 risking his safety to shine the light of truth on Russia\u8217\'20\'19s brutal aggression against Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Gershkovich was arrested while on a reporting trip to the Ural Mountains city of Yekaterinburg and he became the first American reporter to be detained in Russia accused of espionage since the cold war.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal, the New York-based, Murdoch-owned daily financial and news publication, published a dramatic front page on Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WSJ/status/1773644279711207464"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posting an image}}}\uc2  on X, formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , featuring a large blank space under the headline \u8220\'20\'1CHis story should be here\u8221\'20\'1D. Next to the stark space are articles about what the reporter has lost in the last year and a piece titled \u8220\'20\'1CAuthoritarians Threaten Journalists Around \uc2 Globe\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Federal Security Service\uc2 , or FSB, alleges Gershkovich was acting on US orders to collect state secrets \u8211\'20\'13 but provided no evidence to support the accusation, which he, the Journal and the \uc2 US government\uc2  deny. Washington has designated him as wrongfully detained and US officials are engaged on several fronts in efforts to free the reporter.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/29/evan-gershkovich-biden-anniversary-wall-street-journal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Evan Gershkovich: Biden \u8216\'20\'18working every day\u8217\'20\'19 to free WSJ reporter held in Russia}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The last major prisoner swap the United States agreed to with Russia won the release of \uc2 WNBA\uc2  star Brittney Griner in December 2022.\par \par \uc2 The US, in turn, sent to Russia jailed arms dealer Viktor Bout, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/12/freed-russian-arms-dealer-viktor-bout-joins-ultranationalist-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has since joined}}}\uc2  an ultranationalist party. Griner, meanwhile, is back on the court, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/jun/28/she-brings-light-brittney-griners-triumphant-return-to-the-wnba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 playing for the Phoenix Mercury}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For more on how Griner\u8217\'20\'19s release came about, and what we could expect from any exchange that frees Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , here\u8217\'20\'19s our coverage:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/dec/09/brittney-griner-arrives-in-us-after-prisoner-exchange-with-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brittney Griner arrives in US after prisoner exchange with Russia}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 During an Oval Office meeting with \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2  last month, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  proposed to the German chancellor that he authorize the release of a Russian hitman serving life in prison for murder, in hopes of coaxing \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  to release three high-profile prisoners.\par \par \uc2 These included Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , ex-Marine Paul Whelan and prominent Russian dissident \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/russia/russia-u-s-prisoner-swaps-gershkovich-whelan-be4576f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as the Journal reports}}}\uc2 , the proposal went nowhere because Navalny died in an Arctic penal colony a week later. Now, it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear what Putin wants in order to secure the release of the detained Americans.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the story, from the Journal:\par \par \uc2 It was the most shocking of a series of setbacks in secret prisoner talks between Washington and Moscow that have now bedeviled two U.S. presidencies.\par \par \uc2 America once had only one prisoner it considered wrongfully jailed in Russia, the 54-year-old Whelan. But through nearly six years of intense and combative negotiations, Putin has run up the score, stockpiling his prisons with Americans to swap for the very few Russians abroad he cares to bring back.\par \par \uc2 Both Presidents Biden and Trump found themselves facing the crude asymmetry between the U.S. and Russia, whose leader of a quarter-century can order foreigners plucked from their hotel rooms and sentenced to decades on spurious charges.\par \par \uc2 Putin, whom Biden called \u8220\'20\'1Ca butcher,\u8221\'20\'1D hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been a normal negotiating partner. After news of Navalny\u8217\'20\'19s sudden death interrupted an annual lunch among chiefs of the leading Western security agencies, several attendees immediately wondered if the Russian ruler had ordered a hit. Weeks later, the U.S. hasn\u8217\'20\'19t offered a public assessment of how he died, while Russia has cited only \u8220\'20\'1Cnatural causes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the same time, America has been an easy mark, polarized by its culture wars and susceptible to the power of celebrity-driven campaigns that leveled a degree of pressure on the White House never felt by the Kremlin.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden condemns \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 's 'wrongful detention' in Russia on anniversary of arrest\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has joined in on calling for Russia to release Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , who was arrested one year ago today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday we mark a painful anniversary: one year of American journalist \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wrongful detention in Russia,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Journalism is not a crime, and Evan went to Russia to do his job as a reporter \u8212\'20\'14 risking his safety to shine the light of truth on Russia\u8217\'20\'19s brutal aggression against Ukraine. Shortly after his wholly unjust and illegal detention, he drafted a letter to his family from prison, writing: \u8220\'20\'1CI am not losing hope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As I have told Evan\u8217\'20\'19s parents, I will never give up hope either. We will continue working every day to secure his release. We will continue to denounce and impose costs for Russia\u8217\'20\'19s appalling attempts to use Americans as bargaining chips. And we will continue to stand strong against all those who seek to attack the press or target journalists \u8212\'20\'14 the pillars of free society.\par \par \uc2 To Evan, to Paul Whelan, and to all Americans held hostage or wrongfully detained abroad: We are with you. And we will never stop working to bring you home.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 To remind readers of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s continued detention of their reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , the Wall Street Journal has left their front page today largely blank:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CHis Story Should Be Here\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s front page of The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 One year stolen. We will not rest until \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  is free. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/IStandWithEvan?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #IStandWithEvan}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SVsezqwzS7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SVsezqwzS7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 WSJ Communications (@WSJPR) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WSJPR/status/1773673962980934045?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And sent users of their mobile app a push alert to where his journalism should be:\par \par \uc2 qmeltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/IStandWithEvan?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #IStandWithEvan}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QoE8jBRIKD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QoE8jBRIKD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Pershing (@benpershing) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benpershing/status/1773718313144664243?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congressional leaders demand Russia release Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\par \par \uc2 In a rare joint statement, the Democratic and Republican leaders of the Senate and House of Representatives have condemned Russia\u8217\'20\'19s detention of Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , and called for his release.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , an American citizen and reporter for The Wall Street Journal, has now spent a year wrongfully detained by Putin\u8217\'20\'19s government. We continue to condemn his baseless arrest, fabricated charges, and unjust imprisonment,\u8221\'20\'1D reads the statement from Democratic Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , Republican House speaker Mike Johnson, Republican Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  and Democratic House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They continue:\par \par \uc2 Forty-five years ago, Evan\u8217\'20\'19s parents, Ella and Mikhail Gershkovich, found refuge in the United States after fleeing the Soviet Union. Today, Putin is restoring Soviet-style control through repression at home and aggression abroad.\par \par \uc2 On the anniversary of \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s captivity, we reaffirm the importance of his work. Journalism is not a crime, and reporters are not bargaining chips. The Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to silence Evan and intimidate other Western reporters will not impede the pursuit of truth.\par \par \uc2 We repeat our call for the Russian government to release Evan, Paul Whelan, and others it has wrongfully detained without further delay.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  goes, pro-Palestine protesters follow.\par \par \uc2 This has been increasingly the case after the Biden administration gave its ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/un-gaza-ceasefire-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 perhaps waning}}}\uc2  ) support to Israel following its invasion of Gaza. During his fundraiser at New York\u8217\'20\'19s Radio City Music Hall last night, Biden was interrupted five times by protesters, while more gathered outside:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden claimed many Republican lawmakers aren't with Trump, argued old age brings 'wisdom'\par \par \uc2 Sitting next to his former boss \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and Democratic predecessor \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  talked about lots last night in a conversation moderated by comedian Stephen Colbert.\par \par \uc2 That included politically perilous topics such as his advanced age. At 81, he is the oldest president to have ever served, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/03/poll-biden-too-old"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls indicate}}}\uc2  that voters are concerned about his fitness for the job.\par \par \uc2 Reverting to the carefree tone he took {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/08/joe-biden-came-out-swinging-at-his-state-of-the-union-address-will-it-be-enough#:~:text=Joe%20Biden%2C%2081%2C%20had%20brought,address%20concerns%20over%20his%20age."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when discussing the subject at his State of the Union address}}}\uc2  earlier this month, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1Cone thing age does bring is a little bit of wisdom. And I know I don\u8217\'20\'19t look much over forty, I know that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also floated the theory that many Republicans don\u8217\'20\'19t actually want to support the policies that his rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  plans to put before them. \u8220\'20\'1CThe thing that disturbs me most is I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what it is that my predecessor has on these guys. Why they\u8217\'20\'19re not stepping up more like \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  and others because, I know, I know that they don\u8217\'20\'19t like a lot of what\u8217\'20\'19s going on,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, accusing Trump of wanting to cut Social Security and tighten \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis last guy that I ran against, and am running against again this time \u8230\'20\'26 his ideas are from the 18th, 19th century,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden needles Trump, faces protesters at New York fundraiser that netted campaign more than $26m\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog reader. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  went to New York City yesterday on a mission: raise a massive amount of money for his presidential campaign in a city that\u8217\'20\'19s long been fertile territory for Democrats. The president accomplished his mission last night at Radio City Music Hall, bringing in what his campaign said was more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/28/biden-fundraiser-new-york-obama-clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  $26m in a moderated conversation alongside }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/28/biden-fundraiser-new-york-obama-clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barack Obama }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/28/biden-fundraiser-new-york-obama-clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/28/biden-fundraiser-new-york-obama-clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bill Clinton}}}\uc2  , where Biden said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s ideas \u8220\'20\'1Care from the 18th, 19th century\u8221\'20\'1D. The president aims to continue raking it in today, spending the morning holding another fundraiser in the city, before flying back to Washington DC. But as has happened {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/31/biden-pro-palestine-protest-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly}}}\uc2  in recent months, Biden was interrupted during the event by protesters opposed to his support for Israel. Despite the fact that the Biden administration allowed passage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/un-gaza-ceasefire-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this week}}}\uc2  of a \uc2 UN\uc2  security council resolution calling for a ceasefire in Gaza and one of his top allies in Congress has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/14/chuck-schumer-israel-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broken with its government}}}\uc2 , the disruptions were a sign that he may have a ways to go in winning back voters disaffected over his policy towards what America considers its top Middle East ally.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we are watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Today marks the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/29/evan-gershkovich-russia-prison-wsj-reporter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one-year anniversary of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s detention of Wall Street Journal reporter }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/29/evan-gershkovich-russia-prison-wsj-reporter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Evan Gershkovich}}}\uc2 . In a statement, Biden decried his \u8220\'20\'1Cwholly unjust and illegal detention\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump announced he would make a speech about \u8220\'20\'1CBiden\u8217\'20\'19s Border Bloodbath\u8221\'20\'1D next Tuesday in Grand Rapids, Michigan, where a man in the US illegally has been accused of murder, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mlive.com/news/grand-rapids/2024/03/michigan-republicans-blast-immigration-policies-after-man-in-us-illegally-accused-of-murder.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MLive reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Congress is out, meaning no progress is expected on thorny issues such as border security legislation, or aid to Israel and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240329ek3t001p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
