\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Women who used  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills on \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  mifepristone case: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s maddening\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Clea Skopeliti \par \uc2 1,167 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2024\par 20:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Three women share their stories of getting medication abortions, and their thoughts on that access being curtailed\par \par \uc2 Mercy\u8217\'20\'19s periods had always been very regular, so when she missed one in 2016, she immediately took a pregnancy test. It was positive, and she managed to get an appointment at an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic the next day.\par \par \uc2 Despite being able to act quickly, she was in her seventh week of pregnancy by the time she could take \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in Ohio \u8211\'20\'13 a state that was, at the time, debating banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the moment embryonic cardiac activity is detected (usually around six weeks). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2016/12/07/politics/ohio-abortion-bill/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio has since enshrined \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  in its state constitution following a referendum.\par \par \uc2 After the supreme court heard oral arguments this week in its first \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case since it overturned Roe v Wade almost two years ago, Mercy reflected on her experience of accessing a medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There have been fears that the case \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2  v Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine \u8211\'20\'13 could curtail access to medication abortions, though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/27/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal experts say}}}\uc2  it does not appear to be going well for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors.\par \par \uc2 When she arrived at the clinic, Mercy, 22 at the time, faced harassment. \u8220\'20\'1CThere were protesters outside the building. They had signs and a billboard with a chopped-up baby on it. They screamed at me as I entered the building. It felt very threatening and judgmental \u8211\'20\'13 I would bundle myself up in hoodies to obscure my identity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During a follow-up appointment, she arrived just before the clinic had opened, and hid behind nearby bushes to dodge the protesters. \u8220\'20\'1CI was terrified,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI felt like a sitting duck.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite facing intimidation from protesters, Mercy, now 29, knew she was not ready to be a parent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wanted it, but it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t planned,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI wasn\u8217\'20\'19t able to have a kid at the time \u8211\'20\'13 I was a student and had trouble affording things. There\u8217\'20\'19s no way I could have supported a baby.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amid debates about \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D bills, Mercy had been aware there were unavoidable delays. At her first appointment, the providers at the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic were unable to find the embryo with ultrasound and the appointment was rescheduled for a week later. Mercy was then required to wait 24 hours between seeing the ultrasound and obtaining the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but due to her class schedule and clinic opening times, she had to wait another week.\par \par \uc2 The staff at the clinic were compassionate and non-judgmental, she remembers, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThey were fantastic to me. It was one of the most empowering experiences I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever had. They reassured me it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t my fault, I\u8217\'20\'19d taken precautions and things happened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her experience taking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in her seventh week went smoothly. She took the mifepristone in the clinic, and misoprostol later, along with a single dose of an antibiotic, which the doctor told her might make her drowsy. She said: \u8220\'20\'1CI just curled up on my bed and went straight to sleep. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how bad the cramping might have been, but by the time I woke up the next morning it was like I was having a heavy period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She described her experience as being \u8220\'20\'1Creally straightforward and non-traumatic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was glad to be in a place that I considered safe, without others\u8217\'20\'19 judgment and to be able to process it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Caitlin, 35, underwent a medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a hospital in California the day after the news leaked that the supreme court would be overturning Roe v Wade in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a very somber experience, and the doctor prescribing me the medication was clearly incredibly upset,\u8221\'20\'1D she remembers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy nervousness about the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was overshadowed by the leak. In some ways it helped with nervousness \u8211\'20\'13 like we were all in this experience together \u8211\'20\'13 but it was emotionally painful. I realised that in California, it was going to affect me much less than people in other parts of the country \u8211\'20\'13 but depending on who\u8217\'20\'19s in power in the US, it could turn into a country-wide thing. I wondered: is this the last time I have this operation? I may never want or need it again, but I want to have the option,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Following an ultrasound, which she declined to see, Caitlin took the mifepristone pill in the hospital, and the misoprostol at home. She was nine weeks pregnant. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was pretty painful,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a lot for your body to go through. I thought, no one\u8217\'20\'19s doing this because they want to.\u8221\'20\'1D But she was glad to be at home with support from her partner and roommate.\par \par \uc2 She said she had been \u8220\'20\'1Cmanically refreshing\u8221\'20\'1D the news for updates on the supreme court mifepristone case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m really nervous about the outcome. I really appreciate the ingenuity of the providers who send medication to the states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal. We\u8217\'20\'19ve been forced to get creative. I\u8217\'20\'19m not surprised conservatives are trying to reverse the work\u8217\'20\'19s that been done,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI see the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement here to be another way to subjugate people in poverty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kelly, 46, has had three medication abortions over the years. Her first was in early 2001, shortly after mifepristone had been authorized for use by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in 2000. After unsuccessfully trying to access the morning-after pill in Salem, Oregon, she went to a Planned Parenthood clinic in Portland, where staff confirmed she was pregnant. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was an accidental pregnancy at 23, I didn\u8217\'20\'19t have a permanent job \u8211\'20\'13 and I knew from a young age I didn\u8217\'20\'19t want children,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Her experience in 2001 \u8211\'20\'13 and 2016 and 2017 \u8211\'20\'13 of accessing mifepristone at \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  in Portland was straightforward, with \u8220\'20\'1Cvery clear instructions\u8221\'20\'1D from the clinic. She was prescribed a painkiller to help with the heavy cramping that accompanies the second pill, misoprostol.\par \par \uc2 Kelly felt that being able to take \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills at home made the process easier. \u8220\'20\'1CMedical settings give me a lot of anxiety \u8211\'20\'13 to do it at home felt more comfortable. My partner made me food, I got to sit on the couch and be in my own bathroom,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn my later two abortions, I was very settled in my career, but again didn\u8217\'20\'19t want kids. I\u8217\'20\'19ve never had any regrets, never any mental health issues as a result. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been set on not having children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reflecting on the supreme court case, Kelly said: \u8220\'20\'1CAs a lifelong feminist, I am shocked that were in this level in the US. We\u8217\'20\'19re just at a point where access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been turned on its head in the US. Mifepristone is completely safe. Thankfully, it looks like they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to rule in favour [of restricting access] \u8211\'20\'13 but the fact it could be [restricted] is maddening.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240327ek3r00361\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
