\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Alabama Democrat Marilyn Lands says voters ready for \u8216\'20\'18change\u8217\'20\'19 after surprise win \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,316 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2024\par 20:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For more on this story, read our full report:Democrat wins in Alabama after focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and IVF\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-660420078f088c06d312753d#block-660420078f088c06d312753d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are cheering}}}\uc2  Marilyn Lands, who managed to seize a state house seat from Republicans in deep-red Alabama, fuelled by her promises to protect IVF access and repeal the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. To be clear: the party {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-66046cb18f08210af248ebc1#block-66046cb18f08210af248ebc1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 does not have}}}\uc2  the numbers to make either of those promises happen in a state thoroughly dominated by the GOP, but it\u8217\'20\'19s nonetheless {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-660431c28f080353e883d457#block-660431c28f080353e883d457"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the latest instance}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies using concerns about reproductive rights to win elections in hostile territory. Meanwhile, in Texas, a federal appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-6604368c8f080353e883d4a2#block-6604368c8f080353e883d4a2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maintained the block}}}\uc2  on a Republican-backed law that would allow state police to arrest suspected illegal border crossers. The legislation will probably remain on hold until either appeals judges or the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  rules on its merits.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-6604546a8f08fad6611626cd#block-6604546a8f08fad6611626cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wants to reschedule}}}\uc2  a meeting with US officials that it called off after Washington allowed a \uc2 UN\uc2  security council resolution calling for a ceasefire in Gaza to pass.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Disney{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-660442098f08921ff91c2556#block-660442098f08921ff91c2556"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended its feud}}}\uc2  with allies of Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , which erupted after the entertainment giant criticized the state\u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kansas Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-66042e338f080353e883d433#block-66042e338f080353e883d433"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moved to}}}\uc2  force \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to ask patients the reason why they are seeking the procedure, and probably have the votes to get around an expected veto by the Democratic governor, Laura Kelly.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-660447818f08921ff91c2583#block-660447818f08921ff91c2583"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is under a new gag order}}}\uc2  in his hush-money case. But it does not apply to the presiding judge Juan Merchan, so the former president attacked him on his social media network this morning.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jeffrey Clark, a former justice department official indicted alongside Trump in Georgia for allegedly trying to overturn the 2020 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-660472d88f089666f5a94ad3#block-660472d88f089666f5a94ad3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded the fifth}}}\uc2  at a hearing that could lead to him losing his law license in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  says a settlement reached between \uc2 Disney\uc2  and his allies over who controls Walt Disney World\u8217\'20\'19s governing district \u8220\'20\'1Cvindicated\u8221\'20\'1D his administration\u8217\'20\'19s policies:\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (R-FL) on reaching settlement with \uc2 Disney\uc2  over the state's control of the special tax district that includes the theme park:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere's going to be ways where we can do things that are in the best interest of...Florida. And I think \uc2 Disney\uc2  can be a part of that.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4hyJqPUdwX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4hyJqPUdwX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1773055696663150964?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the end of the long-running squabble:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/27/ron-desantis-disney-settlement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis allies reach settlement over who controls Disney\u8217\'20\'19s governing district}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jeffrey Clark, the former justice department official who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/29/trump-official-move-trial-federal-court-election-2020-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicted in Georgia}}}\uc2  alongside \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for allegedly trying to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election victory in the state, repeatedly declined to answer questions today at a hearing that could see him lose his law license in Washington DC, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/03/27/d-c-bar-investigators-rest-case-against-jeffrey-clark-00149368"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Clark repeatedly invoked the fifth amendment\u8217\'20\'19s protecting against self incrimination in response to questions from DC Bar panel investigators, who rested their case after today\u8217\'20\'19s hearing.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that, from Politico:\par \par \uc2 Clark\u8217\'20\'19s decision to invoke his constitutional right against self-incrimination underscores the criminal jeopardy he faces in other ongoing legal proceedings. In Atlanta, he\u8217\'20\'19s charged alongside Trump in an alleged racketeering conspiracy to corrupt the 2020 election, and in Washington DC, federal prosecutors identified him \u8211\'20\'13 but have not charged him \u8211\'20\'13 as one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alleged co-conspirators in a scheme to seize power.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will invoke the Fifth,\u8221\'20\'1D Clark said in response to a question about when he first met Trump. Clark also said the question was covered by attorney-client, law enforcement and executive privileges. \u8220\'20\'1CA veritable phalanx of privileges,\u8221\'20\'1D Clark added wryly as the exercise wore on.\par \par \uc2 The Fifth Amendment to the Constitution protects Americans from being forced to provide testimony that may incriminate themselves in legal proceedings. For Clark, that\u8217\'20\'19s particularly important as he faces a potential criminal trial in Georgia. His attorneys worried that forcing Clark to take the stand simply to invoke his Fifth Amendment right would drive headlines or embarrass Clark, but the DC Bar panel presiding over the hearing permitted investigators to pose several dozen questions to Clark.\par \par \uc2 Clark himself grew combative as the questioning wore on, accusing the lead investigator, Hamilton Fox, of seeking to humiliate him on the stand by forcing him to repeatedly invoke the Fifth Amendment. His bristling prompted Merrill Hirsh, the chair of the panel presiding over the hearing, to admonish Clark not to argue with Fox or risk potentially waiving the privileges he invoked.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats nationwide are taking heart from Marilyn Lands\u8217\'20\'19s victory in Alabama, seeing it as a validation of their strategy to make concerns over reproductive care access a centerpiece of their pitch to voters.\par \par \uc2 But Lands\u8217\'20\'19s election does not change the fundamental balance of power in Alabama, where the Republican party firmly controls the levers of power. All elected officials are members of the GOP, which has supermajorities in the state house and senate.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers in Alabama have lately spent their time passing laws {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/29/alabama-house-senate-ivf-protection-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restricting diversity and inclusion}}}\uc2  programs from being established at public schools and state agencies, and barring trans people from using public bathrooms that align with their gender identity at colleges and universities.\par \par \uc2 They also moved quickly to pass legislation allowing in vitro fertilization care to continue after the state supreme court issued a ruling that forced fertility clinics to cancel appointments. Democrats supported that effort:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/29/alabama-house-senate-ivf-protection-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama legislature passes bill aiming to protect IVF after embryo ruling}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Marilyn Lands\u8217\'20\'19s victory yesterday in the special election for Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s state house is probably the most exciting thing to happen for Democrats in the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/dec/12/roy-moore-loses-alabama-senate-race-doug-jones-wins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since Doug Jones won }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/dec/12/roy-moore-loses-alabama-senate-race-doug-jones-wins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Senate seat in 2018}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His victory came after multiple women alleged sexual assault or other inappropriate behavior by the Republican candidate, \uc2 Roy Moore\uc2 . In an interview last night with CNN, Jones, who was ousted from the Senate by the Republican Tommy Tuberville in the 2020 elections, described Lands\u8217\'20\'19s win as \u8220\'20\'1Ca huge deal\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThis is a huge win for Alabama, not just for Democrats. It\u8217\'20\'19s a huge win for women,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DougJones?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DougJones}}}\uc2  says after Marilyn Lands, who made reproductive rights her campaign focus, won in Alabama's special election last night. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ii2NjzSHWA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ii2NjzSHWA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1772960945813266919?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After shock win in Alabama, the Democrat Marilyn Lands says voters are ready for 'change'\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Huntsville, Alabama broadcaster WHNT, the Democrat Marilyn Lands predicted better days ahead for the beleaguered party:\par \par \uc2 enltrMarilyn Lands on winning a special election Tuesday for a state House seat as a Democrat in deep-red Alabama:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt's a victory tonight for women, for families, for Alabama in general.... It feels like it's the start of a change here. And I think we'll see more change in 2026.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QSF5j1z8e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QSF5j1z8e0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1773023053196218650?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Lands yesterday was elected to Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s state house in a special election to fill a vacant seat previously held by the GOP, in a rare instance of Democrats making inroads in one of the most thoroughly Republican states in the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The recovery operation in Baltimore continues amid reports that a truck has been found amid the wreckage of the Francis Scott Key bridge.\par \par \uc2 For more on the disaster, and the effort to get the economically vital port of Baltimore back up and running, follow our live blog:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/baltimore-bridge-collapse-latest-missing-people-search-ship-black-box"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Baltimore bridge collapse live news: truck reportedly recovered from water as shifting debris makes recovery efforts treacherous }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House media briefing is under way in the west wing now, with the press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , just introducing the transportation secretary, \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , who\u8217\'20\'19s appearing as the guest today to talk about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/27/baltimore-bridge-workers-names"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bridge disaster}}}\uc2  in Baltimore.\par \par \uc2 Buttigieg paid tribute to the six workers who are missing and presumed dead after the bridge collapse, and the two workers who survived, one badly injured, who were all repairing the bridge\u8217\'20\'19s road surface \u8220\'20\'1Cwhile we all slept\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 Buttigieg said that the port will be reopened as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 The National Transportation Safety Board\uc2  is investigating the bridge\u8217\'20\'19s collapse, with Buttigieg saying that the bridge, which was completed in the 1970s, was not build to withstand an impact from the size of container ship that operates these days and which hit the bridge strut in the early hours of Tuesday morning, leading to the entire bridge\u8217\'20\'19s collapse, closing the port for all traffic.\par \par \uc2 Guardian US has a dedicated live blog covering all the developments in the Baltimore bridge disaster and you can follow that news {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/baltimore-bridge-collapse-latest-missing-people-search-ship-black-box"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Israel has asked to reschedule a meeting with US officials to discuss its military plans in Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s southern city of Rafah, a US official said on Wednesday, days after the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , abruptly scrapped the planned talks, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu called off a planned visit to Washington by a senior Israeli delegation after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/un-gaza-ceasefire-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US allowed passage}}}\uc2  of a Gaza ceasefire resolution at the United Nations on Monday, in a move that appeared to reflect growing US frustration with the Israeli premier.\par \par \uc2 US officials said the Biden administration was perplexed by the Israeli cancellation and considered it an overreaction to the security council resolution, insisting there had been no change in policy.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, a US official said Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s office \u8220\'20\'1Chas said they\u8217\'20\'19d like to reschedule the meeting dedicated to Rafah. We are now working with them to set a convenient date.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu is considering sending a delegation for a White House meeting on Rafah as early as next week but the scheduling is still being worked out, an Israeli official in Washington told Reuters on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 There was no immediate comment from the Israeli prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s office. The planned talks are expected to focus on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s threatened offensive in Rafah, the last relatively safe haven for Palestinian civilians in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The White House said last week it intended to share with Israeli officials alternatives for eliminating the Palestinian militant group \uc2 Hamas\uc2  without a ground offensive in Rafah that Washington says would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisaster\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , will travel to France and Belgium next week, a state department spokesperson, \uc2 Matthew Miller\uc2 , told reporters on Wednesday, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Blinken will meet with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/nato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nato}}}\uc2  secretary general, \uc2 Jens Stoltenberg\uc2 , and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukrainian}}}\uc2  foreign minister, Dmytro Kuleba, while in Brussels for a Nato meeting, Miller said at a regular news briefing.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the state department does not think hostage talks with Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  are over, Miller said, adding that Washington thinks there is an ability to continue to pursue the release of hostages.\par \par \uc2 He also said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe do\u8221\'20\'1D when asked if the department believed a limited military campaign in Rafah, in the south of Gaza, can take out remaining commanders of the Palestinian militant group \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hamas\uc2  controls the territory and led the attack on southern Israel on 7 October last year in which more than 1,200 people were massacred and more than 240 people were taken hostage into Gaza, with more than 100 remaining captive at this time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-660420078f088c06d312753d#block-660420078f088c06d312753d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are cheering}}}\uc2  Marilyn Lands, who managed to seize a state house seat from Republicans in deep-red Alabama, fueled by her promises to protect IVF access and repeal the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. To be clear: the party does not have the numbers to make either of those promises happen in a state thoroughly dominated by the GOP, but it\u8217\'20\'19s nonetheless {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-660431c28f080353e883d457#block-660431c28f080353e883d457"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the latest instance}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies using concerns about reproductive rights to win elections in hostile territory. Meanwhile, in Texas, a federal appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-6604368c8f080353e883d4a2#block-6604368c8f080353e883d4a2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maintained the block}}}\uc2  on a Republican-backed law that would allow state police to arrest suspected illegal border crossers. The legislation will probably remain on hold until either appeals judges or the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  rules on its merits.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Disney{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-660442098f08921ff91c2556#block-660442098f08921ff91c2556"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended its feud}}}\uc2  with allies of Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , which erupted after the entertainment giant criticized the state\u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kansas Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-66042e338f080353e883d433#block-66042e338f080353e883d433"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moved to}}}\uc2  force \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to ask patients the reason they are seeking the procedure, and probably have the votes to get around an expected veto by the Democratic governor, Laura Kelly.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/27/trump-biden-latest-republican-democrat-win-alabama-ronna-mcdaniel?page=with:block-660447818f08921ff91c2583#block-660447818f08921ff91c2583"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is under a new gag order}}}\uc2  in his hush-money case. But it does not apply to the presiding judge Juan Merchan, so the former president attacked him on his social media network this morning.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Apparently in some kind of foul mood, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also insulted his one-time ally \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  following her hiring from NBC yesterday, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112164618833623869"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mocked}}}\uc2  the former \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) chair \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 , for her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/26/ronna-mcdaniel-nbc-rnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firing by NBC}}}\uc2  days after being hired as a political analyst.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWow!\u8221\'20\'1D the former president and presumptive Republican nominee, who ejected McDaniel from the \uc2 RNC\uc2  in favour of his daughter-in-law \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112164618833623869"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on his Truth Social platform.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  got fired by Fake News NBC. She only lasted two days, and this after McDaniel went out of her way to say what they wanted to hear. It leaves her in a very strange place, it\u8217\'20\'19s called NEVER NEVERLAND, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not a place you want to be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McDaniel\u8217\'20\'19s hiring was announced by NBC last Friday. Interviewed on Meet the Press on Sunday, she disavowed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lie that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  stole the 2020 election but also claimed there were electoral \u8220\'20\'1Cproblems\u8221\'20\'1D in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 Protests from on-air talent and an NBC union group also concerned McDaniel\u8217\'20\'19s combative relations with the press in seven years as \uc2 RNC\uc2  chair, a period coinciding with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s takeover of the Republican party. On Tuesday evening McDaniel was gone \u8211\'20\'13 giving her a four-day NBC career, not the two claimed by Trump.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/27/trump-ronna-mcdaniel-nbc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump mocks ex-RNC chair Ronna McDaniel for being fired by NBC }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , he has once again been gagged under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/26/trump-gag-order-hush-money-case#:~:text=A%20New%20York%20judge%20on,upcoming%20hush%2Dmoney%20criminal%20trial."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an order issued yesterday}}}\uc2  by the judge handling his criminal case in New York on charges related to making hush -money payments.\par \par \uc2 But judge Juan Merchan \u8217\'20\'19s ruling does not prevent the former president from attacking him, and so that\u8217\'20\'19s what Trump did this morning, on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112168132432855508"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his Truth Social network}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 This Judge, by issuing a vicious \u8220\'20\'1CGag Order,\u8221\'20\'1D is wrongfully attempting to deprive me of my First Amendment Right to speak out against the Weaponization of Law Enforcement, including the fact that Crooked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , and their Hacks and Thugs are tracking and following me all across the Country, obsessively trying to persecute me, while everyone knows I have done nothing wrong!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2  and DeSantis allies end squabble sparked by Florida's 'don't say gay' law\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2  and allies of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , have reached an agreement to end a nearly two-year-long court battle that began after the entertainment giant spoke out against the state\u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis put his conservative policies at the center of his quixotic attempt to win the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination, but ended up dropping out after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/16/ron-desantis-second-place-iowa-caucus-whats-next-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 getting pummeled}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s January caucuses.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the AP on what the settlement of the case will entail:\par \par \uc2 Allies of the Florida governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , and \uc2 Disney\uc2  reached a settlement agreement on Wednesday in a lawsuit over who controls Walt Disney World\u8217\'20\'19s governing district.\par \par \uc2 In a meeting, the members of the board of the Central Florida Tourism Oversight District approved the settlement agreement, ending almost two years of litigation that was sparked by DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/20/disney-world-desantis-lgbtq-housing-taxes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 takeover of the district}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Disney\uc2  supporters following the company\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to Florida\u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law.\par \par \uc2 The 2022 law bans classroom lessons on sexual orientation and gender identity in early grades and was championed by DeSantis, who used \uc2 Disney\uc2  as a punching bag in speeches until he suspended his presidential campaign this year.\par \par \uc2 As punishment for \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s opposition, DeSantis took over the governing district through legislation passed by the Republican-controlled Florida legislature and appointed a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/03/desantis-disney-tourism-dei-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 board of supervisors}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Disney\uc2  sued DeSantis and his appointees, claiming the company\u8217\'20\'19s free speech rights were violated for speaking out against the legislation. A federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/31/walt-disney-ron-desantis-lawsuit-dismissed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed}}}\uc2  that lawsuit in January.\par \par \uc2 Before control of the district changed hands from \uc2 Disney\uc2  allies to DeSantis appointees early last year, the \uc2 Disney\uc2  supporters on its board signed agreements with \uc2 Disney\uc2  shifting control over design and construction at Disney World to the company.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/27/ron-desantis-disney-settlement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis allies reach settlement over who controls Disney\u8217\'20\'19s governing district}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Christian D Menefee, the attorney for Texas\u8217\'20\'19s populous Harris county, said the federal appeals court decision putting the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/20/texas-immigration-law-appeals-court-freezes-order-allowing-prosecution-of-migrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contentious immigration law}}}\uc2  on hold \u8220\'20\'1Cshows that Republicans in Texas are overstepping their authority once again and disregarding the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s jurisdiction over immigration laws \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Menefee, a Democrat whose county includes the city of Houston, continued:\par \par \uc2 Our communities should not have to live in a state of fear and confusion, which is exactly what SB4 was designed to do. Unfortunately, Republican leaders in Austin are more interested in fueling anti-immigrant rhetoric than actually creating real, workable solutions to address our immigration laws.\par \par \uc2 While this back-and-forth can create a sense of uncertainty for the people who live here, this ruling makes me hopeful that the Fifth Circuit will follow clear Supreme Court precedent and rule against the law when it considers the merits.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Appeals court keeps Texas law allowing police to arrest suspected illegal border crossers on hold\par \par \uc2 A ruling late on Tuesday from a federal appeals court will for now block a Texas law allowing police to arrest people suspected of entering the country illegally, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/texas-migrant-arrest-law-court-blocked-f4b568e0e940b906f5c06943ac797f97"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The law passed by Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Republican government has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/20/texas-border-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawn criticism}}}\uc2  from the Biden administration, which warned it will undermine border security by involving state police in the enforcement of federal immigration law. Texas\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Greg Abbott, argues it\u8217\'20\'19s necessary to deter migrants entering from Mexico, after such arrivals surged following Biden taking office.\par \par \uc2 This isn\u8217\'20\'19t the final word on the law \u8211\'20\'13 its legality will likely be decided by a federal appeals court, or the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the ongoing saga, from the AP:\par \par \uc2 The 2-1 ruling late Tuesday from a three-judge panel of the 5th U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals will likely prevent enforcement of the law until a final decision on its merits, either by the 5th Circuit or the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ruling followed a March 20 hearing by a three-judge panel of the court. It\u8217\'20\'19s just the latest move in a seesaw legal case over Republican Gov. Greg Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s strict new immigration law that is not yet ended.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department has argued that Texas\u8217\'20\'19 law is a clear violation of federal authority and would create chaos at the border. Texas has argued that President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration isn\u8217\'20\'19t doing enough to control the border and that the state has a right to take action.\par \par \uc2 Chief Judge Priscilla Richman, an appointee of Republican President \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2 , cited a 2010 Arizona law that was largely stricken by the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  to say immigration enforcement is exclusively a federal responsibility.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor nearly 150 years, the Supreme Court has held that the power to control immigration \u8212\'20\'14 the entry, admission, and removal of noncitizens \u8212\'20\'14 is exclusively a federal power,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Richman, an appointee of Republican President \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Texas law, Richman wrote, \u8220\'20\'1Ccreates separate, distinct state criminal offenses and related procedures regarding unauthorized entry of noncitizens into Texas from outside the country and their removal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She was joined in the opinion by Judge Irma Carrillo Ramirez, a Biden appointee.\par \par \uc2 Judge Andrew Oldham, an appointee of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and a former aide to Abbott, dissented with the majority decision.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more of what the surprise Democratic victory in an Alabama special election might mean for the presidential campaign in November, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/oliver-milman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Milman}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama}}}\uc2  Democrat who campaigned against the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has won a special election to the state legislature, a stark signal that reproductive rights is a potent issue for Democratic candidates, even in the deep south.\par \par \uc2 Marilyn Lands won the state house seat on Tuesday, defeating Teddy Powell, a Republican, by 63% to 37%. Lands, a licensed professional counselor, previously ran for the seat in 2022 and lost by 7% to David Cole, a Republican who resigned last year after pleading guilty to voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 Lands made Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and access to contraception and in vitro fertilization central to her campaign, speaking openly about her own previous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  experience in a TV ad that featured her saying that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cshameful that today women have fewer freedoms than I had two decades ago\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lands said that her win sent a clear message in the wake of Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which came into effect after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  struck down Roe v Wade in 2022. In February, there was also a highly controversial state supreme court decision that threatened the use of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 IVF}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/27/alabama-democrat-win-marilyn-lands"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat wins election in conservative Alabama after focus on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  and IVF}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 One of the earliest indications that the overturning of Roe v Wade would represent an earthquake in American politics was seen in Kansas, another reliably Republican state.\par \par \uc2 Just weeks after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in 2022, Kansas voters rejected a referendum that would have allowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be banned in the state. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-kansas-reporting-patients-data-0bfd8740d247ce5c5d41a0f59252a242"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2  that Republicans who dominate the Kansas legislature haven\u8217\'20\'19t given up, and yesterday approved a law that will require doctors to ask women the reasons why they are seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Democratic governor, Laura Kelly, is likely to veto it, but the GOP appears to have the votes to override it.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that, from the AP:\par \par \uc2 At least eight states require similar reporting, but none of them has had a statewide vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights as Kansas did in August 2022. In the first state ballot question on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs decision, voters decisively protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights under the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are frustrated because Republicans and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups have pursued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-medication-reversal-kansas-01304fcbe7b014ec46f818633faf28a7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new rules for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers}}}\uc2  despite the 2022 vote. But supporters of the reporting bill say it would give the state better data that would help legislators make policy decisions.\par \par \uc2 The bill would require providers to ask patients 11 questions about their reasons for terminating a pregnancy, including that they can\u8217\'20\'19t afford another child, raising a child would hinder their education or careers, or a spouse or partner wanted her to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A woman would not be required to answer, however.\par \par \uc2 The bill also would require providers to report each patient\u8217\'20\'19s age, marital status, race and education level, while using a \u8220\'20\'1Cconfidential code\u8221\'20\'1D for each patient so that they wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be identified to the state. The state would be barred for at least five years from identifying the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the data it publishes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights were also on the minds of the supreme court justices yesterday, when they considered a challenge by a conservative group to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone. But while many of the justices who heard the case voted to overturn Roe v Wade, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jessica-glenza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jessica Glenza}}}\uc2  report they don\u8217\'20\'19t appear inclined to take similar action against medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  hearing that held the potential to reshape \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authority did not go well for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors behind the case, legal experts said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The consensus is a positive sign for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates, who feared the case would curtail access to medication abortions, which now account for the majority of all abortions nationally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very possible that they will just toss the lawsuit out because the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors didn\u8217\'20\'19t have legal standing to sue,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lawrence Gostin, a professor at Georgetown Law School and an expert in global public health law, said about the justices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn my view, the lawsuit was absurd on its face and deserves to be thrown out because these anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors had very little injury,\u8221\'20\'1D Gostin added.\par \par \uc2 The case deals with \uc2 FDA\uc2  regulation of the drug mifepristone, one-half of a two-drug regimen used to terminate an early pregnancy. A group representing the doctors, called the Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine, has sought to roll back \uc2 FDA\uc2  decisions that expanded mifepristone access, such as allowing doctors to prescribe it via telehealth.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/27/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court hearing not a success for anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  doctors, experts say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The politics sages at Sabato\u8217\'20\'19s Crystal Ball have a breakdown of Democrat Marilyn Lands\u8217\'20\'19s triumph in Alabama.\par \par \uc2 Lands lost by about seven percentage points in 2022, but the seat became open again after Republican David Cole resigned when it turned out he did not actually live in the district, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/alabama-ivf-abortion-legislature-378c3fa32dcfc2d0401f3893828482af"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the AP}}}\uc2 . That paved the way for Lands to crush the Republican challenger for the open seat, Teddy Powell :\par \par \uc2 enltrIn the Huntsville AL area, Democrats have flipped state House District 10 tonight. In 2022, Marilyn Lands (D) lost by about 7 points. This time, she won by almost 25%, sweeping nearly everything.\par \par \uc2 This was a stronger margin here than \uc2 Doug Jones\uc2 's 23-point spread from 2017. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NUlH8cZEeF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NUlH8cZEeF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 J. Miles Coleman (@JMilesColeman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JMilesColeman/status/1772807746749927711?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 But Democrats may not want to get too excited about the victory, since the seat has been trending away from the GOP over the last few presidential elections:\par \par \uc2 enltrAlso, going with this, per DRA, it was roughly 60%-39% for McCain and gave Romney 62%. Trump won it by 14 in 2016, but was down to carrying by 1 in 2020--so def. one area of AL moving the wrong way for Rs longer term.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 J. Miles Coleman (@JMilesColeman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JMilesColeman/status/1772846028280021326?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats and Biden campaign cheer surprise special election victory in Alabama\par \par \uc2 Just how did Marilyn Lands end up ousting Republicans from a suburban state house seat in northern Alabama? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/alabama-ivf-abortion-legislature-378c3fa32dcfc2d0401f3893828482af"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Associated Press reports}}}\uc2  that the licensed counselor\u8217\'20\'19s pitch to voters included the following demands: \u8220\'20\'1COur legislature must repeal Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s no-exceptions \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, fully restore access to IVF, and protect the right to contraception.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Voters liked what they heard, and so did the Democratic party at large. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what chair \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  had to say about Lands\u8217\'20\'19s victory:\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s election \u8211\'20\'13 one of the first since the devastating decision by the Alabama supreme court that stopped IVF care \u8211\'20\'13 was a referendum on Maga Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 out-of-touch extremism on reproductive rights. Marilyn Lands\u8217\'20\'19 victory demonstrates that voters aren\u8217\'20\'19t going to sit idly by while Maga Republicans lay the groundwork for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 And Julie Chavez Rodriguez, manager of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign:\par \par \uc2 Last month, Alabamans lost access to fertility treatments because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Tonight, the voters in Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s 10th house district elected a pro-choice champion in Marilyn Lands, sending Trump and extreme Maga Republicans a clear message: they know exactly who\u8217\'20\'19s to blame for restricting their ability to decide how and when to build their families and they\u8217\'20\'19re ready to fight back. Trump overturned Roe vWade, paving the way for attacks on women\u8217\'20\'19s freedoms like we saw in Alabama \u8211\'20\'13 now he\u8217\'20\'19s running to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gut access to IVF nationwide. Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s results should serve as a major warning sign for Trump: voters will not stand for his attacks on reproductive healthcare. This November will be no different.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In surprise victory, Democrat wins state House seat in deep red Alabama after campaign focused on reproductive rights\par \par \uc2 Last night, Democrats in Alabama did something they do not often do in the deeply conservative state: win a seat in the state house of representatives back from the GOP. And how they did it may be a sign of what we can expect to work with voters nationwide as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  stumps for a second term while trying to gain complete control of Congress in November. In the case of Alabama, the Democrat Marilyn Lands campaigned on repealing Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and fully restoring access to in vitro fertilization, the fertility treatment that the Alabama supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/alabama-ivf-protection-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 briefly outlawed}}}\uc2  last month. Lands lost the race for the seat in the swing district just two years ago, but in last night\u8217\'20\'19s special election triumphed with a more than 25% margin over the Republican candidate.\par \par \uc2 Why does this all matter? For Democrats, it\u8217\'20\'19s the latest sign that voters remain uncomfortable with the implications of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 2022 decision overturning Roe v Wade, and those objections can be harnessed to make inroads even in the most inhospitable terrain, like Alabama. Whether Biden and his allies can repeat the act just over seven months from now is an open question.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we are watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Six construction workers working on Baltimore\u8217\'20\'19s Francis Scott Key bridge when it was struck by a container ship and collapsed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/27/baltimore-bridge-workers-names"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are presumed dead}}}\uc2 , after rescuers spent most of yesterday attempting to locate them.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 , the former Republican party chair known for spreading \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election lies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/26/ronna-mcdaniel-nbc-rnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was axed}}}\uc2  by NBC after an outcry.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Americans once narrowly supported Israel\u8217\'20\'19s campaign in Gaza, but are now generally opposed to it, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/642695/majority-disapprove-israeli-action-gaza.aspx?utm_source=alert&utm_medium=email&utm_content=morelink&utm_campaign=syndication"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new polling}}}\uc2  from Gallup shows.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240327ek3r001xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
