\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrat wins election in conservative Alabama after focus on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  and IVF\b0\par\par\uc2 Oliver Milman \par \uc2 575 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2024\par 18:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Marilyn Lands elected to state legislature in deep red state by significant margin after centering reproductive rights in campaignAlabama surprise Democratic victory \u8211\'20\'13 live updates\par \par \uc2 An Alabama Democrat who campaigned against the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has won a special election to the state legislature, a stark signal that reproductive rights is a potent issue for Democratic candidates, even in the deep south.\par \par \uc2 Marilyn Lands won the state house seat on Tuesday, defeating Teddy Powell, a Republican, by 63% to 37%. Lands, a licensed professional counselor, previously ran for the seat in 2022 and lost by 7% to David Cole, a Republican who resigned last year after pleading guilty to voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 Lands made Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and access to contraception and in vitro fertilization central to her campaign, speaking openly about her own previous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  experience in a TV ad that featured her saying that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cshameful that today women have fewer freedoms than I had two decades ago\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lands said that her win sent a clear message in the wake of Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which came into effect after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  struck down Roe v Wade in 2022. In February, there was also a highly controversial state supreme court decision that threatened the use of IVF.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a giant step forward for Alabama, this is a victory tonight for women, for families, for Alabama in general,\u8221\'20\'1D Lands told WHNT News 19 in the wake of her win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels like it\u8217\'20\'19s the start of a change here,\u8221\'20\'1D she added of the state\u8217\'20\'19s politics. \u8220\'20\'1CI think we are ready for something different, we are tired of Alabama being 49th and 50th in all the key metrics. We can do better, we are better and I want to make that happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lands said she would work to overturn Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, one of the most stringent in the US, which outlaws \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any stage of pregnancy with no exceptions for rape or incest. It is only permitted in situations where the life of the pregnant person is in danger.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, Alabama women and families sent a clear message that will be heard in Montgomery and across the nation,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1COur legislature must repeal Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s no-exceptions \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, fully restore access to IVF, and protect the right to contraception.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The special election does little to tip the balance of power in conservative Alabama, with Republicans holding a commanding 75 to 27 advantage over Democrats in the state house.\par \par \uc2 However, Democrats have hailed the victory as a further sign that restricting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has proved electorally damaging to Republicans, particularly in the sort of seat contested by Lands. The Democrat won in the state\u8217\'20\'19s 10th district, which comprises parts of Huntsville and Madison, a relatively affluent and educated area of northern Alabama only narrowly carried by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis special election is a harbinger of things to come \u8211\'20\'13 Republicans across the country have been put on notice that there are consequences to attacks on IVF \u8211\'20\'13 from the bluest blue state to the reddest red, voters are choosing to fight for their fundamental freedoms by electing Democrats across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Heather Williams, president of the Democratic Legislative Campaign Committee, in a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/03/26/abortion-winning-strategy-alabama-democrat-00149205"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent to Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240327ek3r00231\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
