\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 Clashing convictions mark protests as \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  weighs  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 1,018 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2024\par 21:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Key takeaways: supreme court \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill hearingHearing on mifepristone most consequential \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related case since overturning of Roe v Wade nearly two years ago\par \par \uc2 Supporters and opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights gathered on the steps of the supreme court on Tuesday, where, just beyond the marbled columns, the justices were hearing oral arguments in the most consequential \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related case since it overturned Roe v Wade nearly two years ago.\par \par \uc2 At stake is the accessibility of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mifepristone-supreme-court-abortion-d451e14148ffbe6ce4811b1a37651480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mifepristone}}}\uc2 , the first pill in a two-drug regimen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2024/03/medication-abortion-accounted-63-all-us-abortions-2023-increase-53-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 used in nearly two-thirds of all abortions in the country}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In clashing speeches, advocates shared their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stories, with one speaker describing how the experience drove her to shun the procedure and another sharing how the decision to terminate her pregnancy allowed her to leave an abusive relationship and pursue a career in medicine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is something I shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to reveal to strangers or to politicians for my choice to be respected,\u8221\'20\'1D Brittany House, a patient advocate with \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , told the hundreds of pro-choice supporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D House continued, \u8220\'20\'1Cis supposed to be between a patient and their provider.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yards away, a group of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents lay on the ground with red balloons that said \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  kills\u8221\'20\'1D. A pregnant woman had scrawled \u8220\'20\'1Cfully human\u8221\'20\'1D on her bare belly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19d like to see the \uc2 FDA\uc2  really step up and bring back some of those commonsense protections for women,\u8221\'20\'1D said Felipe Avila of the National Association of Pro-Life Nurses, repeating the disputed claim at the heart of the case that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved pill is dangerous.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/self-managed-abortions-avoid-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Self-managed abortions have soared}}}\uc2  since the supreme court eliminated federal protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June 2022, paving the way for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly two dozen states to restrict or ban access to the procedure}}}\uc2 . Decades of research have concluded that a combination of mifepristone and misoprostol is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/01/health/abortion-pill-safety.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safe and effective method}}}\uc2  for terminating a pregnancy in the first trimester.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt allows them to access medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the comfort and privacy of their own home,\u8221\'20\'1D said Divya Shenoy, a family medicine physician and the director of primary care at the Planned Parenthood of Metropolitan Washington. \u8220\'20\'1CNot being able to have this option would be really, really challenging for a lot of patients who are trying to seek \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Inside the courtroom, a majority of the justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared skeptical of the arguments }}}\uc2  in favor of restricting access to mifepristone put forth by a group of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors.\par \par \uc2 Outside, pop music blared as activists squared off in testy exchanges that did little to win converts on one of the most deeply held convictions in American life.\par \par \uc2 One young anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist carried a bound version of \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Project 2025, an 887-page conservative-policy blueprint for a Trump second term that instructs the next president to work with Congress \u8220\'20\'1Cto enact the most robust protections for the unborn that Congress will support\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A pro-choice activist came dressed as Anthony Comstock, the 19th-century anti-vice crusader behind the eponymous Comstock Act. Some conservatives and Trump allies see enforcement of the 1873 law, which barred the mailing of \u8220\'20\'1Clewd\u8221\'20\'1D materials including drugs that could be used to terminate a pregnancy, as a possible path to banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide without Congress.\par \par \uc2 The activist, wearing mutton chops and a top hat and speaking as Comstock, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI am back as a representative of the century they want to bring us back to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mr. Comstock of the eponymous Comstock Act came back to \u8220\'20\'1Csupport my fellow brethren.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lY2CwwLjKa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lY2CwwLjKa}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1772635399057186940?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 A group of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights protesters was part of a planned act of civil disobedience intended to highlight the gravity of the case that could once again dramatically reshape the legal landscape, including in states that protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . About 14 people were arrested, according to the groups involved.\par \par \uc2 The case, which could be decided in June, may also have profound implications in the race for the White House. Even as conservative lawmakers roll back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, voters have repeatedly chosen to protect it at the ballot box, even in deep red states.\par \par \uc2 Julie von Haefen, a Democratic state lawmaker from battleground North Carolina who attended the rally at the supreme court, said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a defining issue of the 2024 election, especially in suburban areas like the one she represents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter Trump, suburban women rose up and said: \u8216\'20\'18We don\u8217\'20\'19t want this, we don\u8217\'20\'19t want any more bans, we want to be able to control her healthcare decisions,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Von Haefen said in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s definitely something that people talk a lot about in areas like mine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a nod to how important advocates believe the issue will be this election, activists carried mock-campaign signs that said \u8220\'20\'1CMife & Miso 2024\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Moments before oral arguments began, Mira Michels of Aid Access, an organization that mails \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to people across the US, swallowed a mifepristone pill dispensed to her by a roving \u8220\'20\'1CRoe-bot\u8221\'20\'1D. After a swig of water, she declared: \u8220\'20\'1CTastes like freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The robots are operated remotely from states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jul/23/shield-laws-provide-abortion-care-aid-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with so-called shield laws}}}\uc2 , which protect clinicians who serve patients in states where providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal. In practice, a patient would have a telehealth appointment with a provider, and the machine would then dispense the pill.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone dispensing robots {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FfMXj2d5Xe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FfMXj2d5Xe}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1772615258252726450?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Rebecca Gomperts, the Dutch physician who founded Aid Access, said the machines were intended \u8220\'20\'1Cto show that we\u8217\'20\'19re not living in the Middle Ages. We live in the 21st century and we\u8217\'20\'19re not going back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 No matter how the justices rules, Gomperts said her group would continue to find ways to help American women access medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis case is not about taking this off the market yet,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo it will continue to be available and our providers are going to continue to ship it to women in all 50 states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240326ek3q002xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
