\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 How the  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill case at the supreme court could undo the \uc2 FDA\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza in New York \par \uc2 1,267 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2024\par 16:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The medical industry watches with trepidation as mifepristone case could have huge consequences for drug regulationExplainer: the mifepristone caseTell us: have you used an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill in the US?\par \par \uc2 A supreme court case about one little pill \u8211\'20\'13 mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 has the medical and pharmaceutical world on edge. The pill, at the heart of a case that will be argued on Tuesday, is part of a two-drug regimen used to treat miscarriage and end early pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Despite a more than 20-year track record of safe real-world use, backed up by more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/01/health/abortion-pill-safety.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 100 peer-reviewed studies}}}\uc2 , a group of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors is seeking to roll back \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration (FDA)\uc2  decisions that changed and relaxed some prescribing rules.\par \par \uc2 If the doctors succeed, despite contested and in some cases {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://retractionwatch.com/2024/02/06/papers-used-by-judge-to-justify-abortion-pill-suspension-retracted/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now-retracted evidence of harm}}}\uc2 , the case could reshape \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US and have enormous and unpredictable consequences for how drugs are prescribed, regulated and developed.\par \par \uc2 A ruling in favor of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors could threaten everything from trust in medicine to specific drugs to the US\u8217\'20\'19s position as the world\u8217\'20\'19s foremost drug innovator.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am terrified,\u8221\'20\'1D said Juan Hincapie-Castillo, a drug policy researcher, licensed pharmacist and assistant professor of epidemiology at the University of North Carolina. \u8220\'20\'1CThis case is shifting the whole paradigm of how things could go moving forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone was approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in 2000 with stringent requirements for how it should be prescribed: only up to seven weeks\u8217\'20\'19 gestation, dispensed in person with mandatory follow-up appointments, and with enhanced risk-reporting requirements for doctors. Along with misoprostol, the second drug in the regimen, it is, in effect, designed to induce the equivalent of a miscarriage at home.\par \par \uc2 After more than 20 years and scientific articles spanning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/01/health/abortion-pill-safety.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 countries}}}\uc2 , the scientific consensus is that the \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill\u8221\'20\'1D has a remarkable track record of safety and effectiveness that, in the media, is often compared to that of Tylenol or Viagra.\par \par \uc2 But following the fall of Roe v Wade in 2022, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors initiated a lawsuit against the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in Amarillo, Texas, arguing that the drug\u8217\'20\'19s approval should be withdrawn. The Trump-appointed judge Matthew Kacsmaryk ruled in favor of the doctors. Were his decision not appealed, it would have resulted in a de facto nationwide ban on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The threat to our industry is real, the threat to patients is real, and it extends far beyond this medicine\par \par \uc2 Dr Amanda Banks\par \par \uc2 The government appealed to the fifth circuit appeals court in New Orleans, with a long history of law that deferred to expert federal agencies and the \uc2 FDA\uc2 . Although the fifth circuit struck down part of Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision, which would have in effect banned the drug nationally, the appeals court ruled in favor of the doctors\u8217\'20\'19 arguments against two \uc2 FDA\uc2  decisions in 2016 and 2021.\par \par \uc2 At both of those times, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  relaxed prescribing rules. The agency allowed doctors to see patients for one visit, approved the drug for up to 10 weeks\u8217\'20\'19 gestation, reduced risk reporting, allowed dispensing through the mail and retail pharmacies, and even reduced the dose of mifepristone from 600 to 200mg.\par \par \uc2 It may sound like a wonky distinction \u8211\'20\'13 but the case is viewed with fear and trepidation by nearly the entire medical industry. And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.drugtopics.com/view/hundreds-of-pharma-executives-sign-open-letter-condemning-mifepristone-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hundreds of pharmaceutical executives}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/23/23-235/284910/20231012165311306_Amicus%20Brief%20of%20American%20College%20of%20Obstetricians%20and%20Gynecologists%20et%20al..pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doctors associations}}}\uc2  and even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/23/23-235/284867/20231012145300905_2023-10-12%20Pharma%20Industry%20Cert-Stage%20Amicus%20Br%20FINAL.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 companies regulated by the FDA}}}\uc2  have lined up in the agency\u8217\'20\'19s defense.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s for two reasons. First, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors don\u8217\'20\'19t show a typical case of harm. They argue in briefs that a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/23/23-235/279230/20230908165000535_USFDA%20et%20al.%20v.%20Alliance%20for%20Hippocratic%20Medicine%20et%20al.%20Petition.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fraction of doctors}}}\uc2  might have been forced to treat women who needed follow-up care from medication abortions, even though no specific party is named.\par \par \uc2 Second, their arguments undermine the deference courts have long had for expert federal agencies, and in particular for the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , which is both the global gold standard for rigorous scientific review, and is directly involved in high-stakes decisions about the trade-offs of particular medicines in ways that have immediate impact on American health.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe threat to our industry is real, the threat to patients is real, and it extends far beyond this medicine,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Amanda Banks, an entrepreneur and former biotechnology executive, said in a press call. And the risk to the future of medical innovations is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot just in the US, but globally at fundamental risk\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Most immediately, a decision that rolls back the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s changes would reimpose all the prescribing restrictions once placed on mifepristone, even though they are not medically necessary. That would once again reshape \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US, including in Democratic-led states who may have thought themselves immune from such restrictions. More than half of abortions in the US are now performed with medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It could also dramatically alter the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authority. If the agency\u8217\'20\'19s decisions can be undone by a judge or it can be sued by any group who outlines theoretical harm, it opens the doors for judges to make medical decisions and for nearly anyone opposed to a drug to sue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat you don\u8217\'20\'19t want is for patients to have science unwound, so they end up faced \u8211\'20\'13 not only with fewer drugs or less innovation \u8211\'20\'13 but with outdated regimens and unnecessary burdens,\u8221\'20\'1D said Eva Temkin, an attorney who worked at the \uc2 FDA\uc2  for nearly a decade, and now advises pharmaceutical companies, medical device manufacturers and biotechnology companies at the law firm Paul Hastings.\par \par \uc2 Contraception, hormone blockers to treat gender dysphoria, vaccines and even some chemotherapy drugs all have detractors who could target the drugs in court, experts said. Commercial rivals may also have a new avenue to limit a drug\u8217\'20\'19s availability.\par \par \uc2 A decision in favor of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs would also dramatically alter the drug development landscape, which relies heavily on a stable body of law for investment. Bringing a new drug to market can cost anywhere from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/publication/57126"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less than $1bn to more than $2bn}}}\uc2 , and may take {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://phrma.org/policy-issues/Research-and-Development-Policy-Framework?__hstc=45788219.4d79b65e8497a30240ab4aa3e5db183c.1643647800477.1643647800477.1643647800477.1&__hssc=45788219.1.1643647800478&__hsfp=2234910243"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10 to 15 years}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the most vibrant venture capital and investment community in the globe here, by several billions dollars \u8211\'20\'13 orders of magnitude as compared to any other region on the globe,\u8221\'20\'1D said Banks. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been incredibly successful, and the reason why it\u8217\'20\'19s incredibly successful is because we have a very, very data-driven \uc2 FDA\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 That\u8217\'20\'19s not the kind of judgment that can be replaced in a couple of weeks in a hearing by someone who isn\u8217\'20\'19t trained.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s experts are not the sort of scientists who \u8220\'20\'1Cchange between administrations\u8221\'20\'1D, said Hincapie-Castillo.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps most alarming for the medical and pharmaceutical industries is that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 whose expert, independent reviews are the envy of many countries \u8211\'20\'13 might be undone by what many prominent researchers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://brennancenter.org/our-work/analysis-opinion/invent-your-own-facts-approach-many-abortion-laws-use-medically-incorrect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consider pseudoscience}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese decisions need to be shaped by the consensus science that we have, and not judicial decisions that are influenced by junk science,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ushma Upadhyay, a public health social scientist trained in demography and a professor in the department of obstetrics and gynecology at the \uc2 University of California, San Francisco\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.contraceptionjournal.org/article/S0010-7824(24)00070-2/fulltext"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Her work}}}\uc2  with a pharmacist helped lead to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://retractionwatch.com/2024/02/06/papers-used-by-judge-to-justify-abortion-pill-suspension-retracted/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retraction of two papers}}}\uc2  cited by the district court in Texas.\par \par \uc2 If the case goes against the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , said Hincapie-Castillo, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very concerned with medications \u8211\'20\'13 what it\u8217\'20\'19s going to look like going forward. These special interest groups have shown us their true colors, and they want to diminish the authority of government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240325ek3p001jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
