\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 The next \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 ?  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  pill case spotlights rightwing judge and his wife\u8217\'20\'19s shadowy connections\b0\par\par\uc2 Melissa Segura \par \uc2 1,359 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2024\par 15:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judge James Ho ruled to restrict mifepristone. His wife Allyson is linked to the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group that brought the caseExplainer: the mifepristone caseHow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill case court could undo the FDA\par \par \uc2 When the former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointed the Texas attorney James Ho to the fifth circuit court of appeals in 2017, lawyers at the prominent law firm Gibson Dunn \u8211\'20\'13 where Ho worked before his appointment \u8211\'20\'13 had a problem: how to replace the politically connected Ho. Turns out, they didn\u8217\'20\'19t even need to change the home address for his replacement. Ho\u8217\'20\'19s wife, Allyson, moved into her husband\u8217\'20\'19s position and his old office.\par \par \uc2 Meet the Hos.\par \par \uc2 Few people outside of legal circles have heard of the Hos, yet the couple is tied to the case before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  that will determine women\u8217\'20\'19s access to mifepristone, a drug commonly used in medication abortions. The court hears arguments in the case on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Ho served on the three-judge panel last summer that ruled to restrict access to mifepristone. The legal group behind the mifepristone case, \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , made at least six payments from 2018 through 2022 to his wife, Allyson, a powerhouse federal appellate lawyer who has argued in front of the supreme court and has deep connections to the conservative legal movement that has led the attack on the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.levernews.com/trump-judges-anti-abortion-ruling-followed-payments-from-group-leading-case/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 payments}}}\uc2  don\u8217\'20\'19t violate the court\u8217\'20\'19s code of conduct, according to Stephen Gillers, a \uc2 New York University\uc2  emeritus professor of law and author of Regulation of Lawyers: Problems of Law and Ethics. But some court watchers argue that Ho\u8217\'20\'19s failure to recuse himself from the case illustrates why public trust in the judiciary is eroding. One recent survey found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanbar.org/groups/judicial/publications/appellate_issues/2023/winter/public-confidence-and-the-courts/#:~:text=Falling%20Confidence%20in%20Federal%20and%20State%20Courts&text=A%20National%20Judicial%20College%20survey,judges%20is%20on%20the%20decline."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 63% of judges}}}\uc2  noted a dip in the public\u8217\'20\'19s positive perception of them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Americans see a case like this \u8211\'20\'13 so clearly concocted and motivated by special interests, and with evident connections between those interests and the judges on the case, it does tremendous damage to the reputation of the courts, and to the public trust in their ability to give all litigants an even shake,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alex Aronson, the executive director of the non-partisan group Court Accountability and a former chief counsel to the Democratic senator Sheldon Whitehouse.\par \par \uc2 In an email to the Guardian, James Ho wrote that he \u8220\'20\'1Cconsulted our court\u8217\'20\'19s ethics advisor prior to sitting in that case, and was advised that there was no basis for recusal. In any event, my wife\u8217\'20\'19s practice is to donate honoraria to charity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Hos are just one of the increasing number of power couples in the conservative movement in which the wife of a prominent official works in the background, laying the groundwork for Republican policies that their spouses will rule upon or legislate. In the mifepristone case, the wife of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dm1l19z832j5m.cloudfront.net/2024-02/FDA-v-Alliance-for-Hippocratic-Medicine-2024-02-22-SCOTUS-Opening-Brief_0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri senator Josh Hawley}}}\uc2 , Erin, is the attorney of record for \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  and argued the case before Ho. The supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  rankled the legal world when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/justice-thomas-recuse-14th-amendment-case-wifes-jan/story?id=106803474"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he refused to recuse}}}\uc2  himself from a case involving questions about the January 6 insurrection and the \u8220\'20\'1CStop the Steal\u8221\'20\'1D campaign to which his wife, Ginni Thomas, was closely tied.\par \par \uc2 For Aronson, these are examples of \u8220\'20\'1Cserious concerns about what is becoming an apparent pattern of coordinated activity by some of these couples in this extremist movement, including the Thomases, Hawleys and Hos\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ho\u8217\'20\'19s rulings have included zealous language, referencing what he called in one decision \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ca5.uscourts.gov/opinions/pub/18/18-50484-CV0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the moral tragedy of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. He has suggested that protection orders in domestic violence cases \u8220\'20\'1Care too often misused as a tactical device in divorce proceedings \u8211\'20\'13 and issued without any actual threat of danger\u8221\'20\'1D. Orin Kerr, a \uc2 University of California, Berkeley\uc2 , law professor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OrinKerr/status/987016941461098496?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E987016941461098496%7Ctwgr%5Ebb525b20fe480cad931174851b537a86532d9d6d%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nhpr.org%2F2018-07-26%2Flegal-opinions-or-political-commentary-a-new-judge-exemplifies-the-trump-era"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  that one of Ho\u8217\'20\'19s opinions \u8220\'20\'1Creads like a politician\u8217\'20\'19s op-ed, not a legal opinion; judges should stick to law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the mifepristone case, in which Ho supported rolling back decisions made by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  to loosen restrictions on the drug, he wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CUnborn babies are a source of profound joy for those who view them. Expectant parents eagerly share ultrasound photos with loved ones. Friends and family cheer at the sight of an unborn child. Doctors delight in working with their unborn patients \u8211\'20\'13 and experience an aesthetic injury when they are aborted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He has chafed legal traditionalists from the moment of his swearing-in, when he opted for the ceremony to be held in the private library of Harlan Crow \u8211\'20\'13 the conservative mega-donor who, \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  revealed, has lavished \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  with trips on his yacht and paid the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-harlan-crow-private-school-tuition-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  $6,000-a-month private school tuition}}}\uc2  for the justice\u8217\'20\'19s great-nephew. Ho worked as a clerk for Thomas in 2005.\par \par \uc2 Ho vowed to boycott hiring Yale Law School graduates as clerks after students interrupted conservative speakers on campus, noting \u8220\'20\'1Ccancellations and disruptions seem to occur with special frequency\u8221\'20\'1D at the Ivy League school.\par \par \uc2 His caustic writings have drawn the spotlight while his wife, Allyson, has been working more inconspicuously, helping lay the legal foundation for conservative policies in her own work.\par \par \uc2 She appears frequently as a speaker for the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2 , the group that has led the conservative effort to reshape the judiciary. She has also worked pro bono for the Christian right organization {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://firstliberty.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 First Liberty Institute}}}\uc2 , a group that describes its mission \u8220\'20\'1Cto defend and restore religious liberty in our schools, for our churches and houses of worship, inside the military, and throughout the public arena\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  paid Allyson Ho to do, yet ending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is central among the organization\u8217\'20\'19s goals. The group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adflegal.org/press-release/roe-v-wade-reversed-us-supreme-court-upholds-ms-law-protects-mothers-unborn-babies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helped write }}}\uc2  the Mississippi law that led to the Dobbs decision that overturned Roe v Wade and ended the 50-year-old constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Her husband\u8217\'20\'19s financial disclosures list descriptions of \u8220\'20\'1CAcademy\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom Summit\u8221\'20\'1D, next to some of the payments. The \uc2 ADF\uc2  hosts various legal trainings as part of its ADF Legal Academy that \u8220\'20\'1Cseamlessly combines outstanding legal training with an unwavering commitment to Christian principles\u8221\'20\'1D and a Young Lawyers Academy.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 ADF\uc2  often invites lawyers of various backgrounds and experiences to speak at events. \uc2 ADF\uc2  offers honorariums for speaker participation. Allyson Ho is an exceptional lawyer with vast and diverse legal experience.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A request to speak with Allyson Ho sent to Gibson Dunn has not been answered.\par \par \uc2 The Texas senators Ted Cruz and \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2 , both Republicans, appointed Allyson to the state\u8217\'20\'19s committee responsible for recommending and vetting its recommendations to fill judicial vacancies. Neither Cruz nor Cornyn\u8217\'20\'19s offices responded to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s request for the names or dates of service for the judicial vetting committee nor did they respond to questions about what role, if any, Allyson had in her husband\u8217\'20\'19s nomination to the bench.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, the Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , hired Allyson and Gibson Dunn, at a rate of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dallasnews.com/news/2023/09/25/plaintiffs-in-foster-care-suit-eye-more-fines-for-texas-abbott-to-pay-millions-in-fight/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1,313 per hour}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 with a $7m cap \u8211\'20\'13 to represent the state in a decade-long legal battle in which a federal judge determined Texas had failed to protect foster children. The state had previously been represented by attorneys on its own payroll. The move to hire Allyson and her firm signaled that Texas could be looking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dallasnews.com/news/politics/2023/05/11/texas-hires-well-connected-private-lawyers-may-stiffen-defense-in-foster-care-lawsuit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fight back }}}\uc2  against court orders mandating Texas comply with federal monitors appointed to ensure the safety of vulnerable children in its care by appealing district court rulings to the fifth circuit court of appeals \u8211\'20\'13 the court on which James Ho serves.\par \par \uc2 The mifepristone case might just be the beginning of the Hos\u8217\'20\'19 influence, Gillers, the \uc2 NYU\uc2  professor, said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Trump wins the election, you\u8217\'20\'19ll see Ho on the short list of nominees to the supreme court,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is obviously behaving in a way that makes him a very prominent candidate in a Republican administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That appointment could once again leave an empty office \u8211\'20\'13 one that some might want Allyson to fill.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240325ek3p0012z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
