\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Cruel\u8217\'20\'19: the supreme court could send one-time  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  deserts like Hawaii back in time\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,787 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2024\par 15:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 States in which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal but was long inaccessible have benefited from the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s expansion of a key \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugExplainer: the mifepristone caseTell us: have you used an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill in the US?\par \par \uc2 They treated a patient who had wanted to get pregnant, but decided to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than have a child with her abusive partner. They treated patients who had lost their houses in the 2023 Maui fires, found themselves homeless and pregnant, and wanted abortions. They treated patients who got pregnant after someone tampered with their birth control and patients who could not afford to take time off work to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Colleen Bass and Sharon Offley, two certified nurse midwives from Hawaii, were able to do all of that because the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) decided, over the last decade, to expand the availability of a common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 Bass and Offley run a full-spectrum women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare clinic on the small Hawaiian island of Kauai. Adding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services in 2021, as the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rules around the pill evolved, was \u8220\'20\'1Ckind of a no-brainer\u8221\'20\'1D, Offley said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt felt like a moral obligation,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs our community became aware of our services, we became aware that there was a much greater demand and a need for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services than we had even known previously.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But now, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , nearly 5,000 miles away from Bass and Offley\u8217\'20\'19s idyllic practice a block from the Pacific Ocean, could jeopardize the future of their work.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the court will hear arguments in a case about mifepristone, one of two drugs commonly used in a US medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is the first major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case to make it back to the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court since its 6-3 conservative majority ruled in 2022 to overturn Roe v Wade, and its outcome could severely restrict the availability of medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a regimen that now accounts for 63% of all US abortions, according to data released this week by the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rightwing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups who filed the case have argued that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  overstepped its authority when it first approved mifepristone for use in abortions in 2000, but the supreme court will focus on later measures, taken by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in 2016 and 2021, that significantly expanded access to the drug.\par \par \uc2 Those measures permitted healthcare providers other than doctors to prescribe mifepristone. They also eased restrictions that had forced patients to pick mifepristone up in person from facilities that had to meet arduous certification requirements. Today, patients can receive mifepristone through telemedicine as well as pick it up at their everyday pharmacies.\par \par \uc2 If the supreme court rewinds these measures, many people will probably have to go to much greater lengths to end their pregnancies. The availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US would plummet, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and their supporters told the Guardian \u8211\'20\'13 even in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal, such as Hawaii.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the supreme court overrides the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and reinstates the in-person dispensing requirements, there is no doubt that some prescribers who are currently offering this essential medication to their patients will no longer be able to do so,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julia Kaye, senior staff attorney at the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Freedom Project, who co-authored an amicus brief in the case. \u8220\'20\'1CFor some patients \u8211\'20\'13 particularly low-income patients, people of color, folks living in rural areas and women with abusive partners \u8211\'20\'13 losing a telehealth option for mifepristone would mean losing access altogether.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Providers in Hawaii already know the consequences of these restrictions, because they have lived through them.\par \par \uc2 Hawaii is a reliably Democratic state whose lawmakers have built strong state-level protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But just because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal does not mean it is accessible \u8211\'20\'13 and in reality, much of watery Hawaii was an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cdesert\u8221\'20\'1D even before Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise. Out of the eight major islands that make up the Hawaiian archipelago, five did not have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers as of 2021. Patients often had little choice but to take an often pricey flight or boat ride to the islands of Oahu, Hawaii Island or Maui for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Dr Graham Chelius, a family medicine doctor on Kauai, sued the \uc2 US government\uc2  in 2017, arguing that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  should loosen its rules around mifepristone, which at the time required an onerous certification process to be able to dispense the drug. Those rules meant that Chelius\u8217\'20\'19s patients could not obtain medication abortions on Kauai \u8211\'20\'13 despite the fact that the drug has been found to be safer than Viagra.\par \par \uc2 In court documents, Chelius detailed his patients\u8217\'20\'19 struggle to travel from Kauai and from its surrounding smaller islands \u8211\'20\'13 including an island that does not have paved roads or cellphone service, much less healthcare providers \u8211\'20\'13 to Oahu, which is roughly 100 miles away from Kauai. One woman, who already had one child and was struggling with addiction, arrived at Chelius\u8217\'20\'19s office seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Because Chelius was blocked from giving her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, she had to travel to Oahu. The difficulty of getting there delayed the woman\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Medication abortions are usually performed within the first trimester of pregnancy. Instead of taking a few pills, the delay meant the woman had to undergo a surgical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt also required her to bear the costs of staying on Oahu \u8211\'20\'13 in a hotel, away from her home and her family \u8211\'20\'13 overnight,\u8221\'20\'1D Chelius wrote in court documents. \u8220\'20\'1CThis was utterly unaffordable for her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other patients could not swing the trip.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had cases where women carried pregnancies to term against their will, despite extraordinary measures that we went through at the time to try to get people to travel to Oahu to access women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D Chelius said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 The time between knowing you want an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 that can be torture for people\par \par \uc2 Dr Jamie Phifer\par \par \uc2 Because of the complex nature of the case, there are a dizzying array of possible outcomes. The court could reverse the rules that allowed telehealth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It could narrow the range of providers permitted to prescribe mifepristone. Retail pharmacies, like CVS and \uc2 Walgreens\uc2 , which just recently began dispensing the pill, could lose their ability to stock it.\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists who brought the lawsuit against the \uc2 FDA\uc2  have argued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/23/23-235/301142/20240222125412317_23-235%20%2023-236%20Brief%20for%20the%20Respondents.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in court papers}}}\uc2  that in-person visits are necessary to properly assess the age of a pregnancy and to diagnose ectopic pregnancies, or doomed pregnancies that cannot be treated through an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Over the last decade, they say, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has erased important safeguards without the data to back up their decisions.\par \par \uc2 But more than 100 studies of mifepristone, conducted across multiple countries, have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/01/health/abortion-pill-safety.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all concluded}}}\uc2  that the drug can be safely used to terminate a pregnancy. The \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iris.who.int/bitstream/handle/10665/362984/WHO-SRH-22.1-eng.pdf?sequence=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laid out a protocol}}}\uc2  for people to use the drug to \u8220\'20\'1Cself-manage\u8221\'20\'1D their own abortions, without any doctor supervision. And out of more than 6,000 telemedicine abortions conducted in the United States between 2021 and 2022, fewer than 1% reported serious adverse reactions, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-024-02834-w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study released last month}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will have a really profound impact everywhere and probably a disproportionate impact on our island, because of the necessity moving forward for basically everyone seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have to get on an airplane and fly,\u8221\'20\'1D Offley said. \u8220\'20\'1CSeeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for any reason \u8211\'20\'13 undesired pregnancy, rape, incest, fetal anomaly. There\u8217\'20\'19d be no distinction. That service would disappear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  decided in 2021, amid the coronavirus pandemic, to allow providers to offer telemedicine abortions. That change became permanent in 2023. The decision gave rise to a new kind of provider: the entirely virtual \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. Such clinics service women all over the country, helping offset the impact of the state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that effectively shuttered all of the brick-and-mortar clinics in more than a dozen red states.\par \par \uc2 In September 2023, providers performed almost 14,000 abortions via telehealth \u8211\'20\'13 16% of all abortions in the country. Some of these abortions were legally provided even to people who live in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 16 states}}}\uc2  with near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, under \u8220\'20\'1Cshield laws\u8221\'20\'1D. On the books in a handful of states, these statutes essentially commit states to protecting providers who prescribe and ship pills to people in states with restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Virtual clinics can be a critical release valve for brick-and-mortar clinics, which are often booked out for weeks in advance by patients fleeing states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. \u8220\'20\'1CThe biggest thing was time,\u8221\'20\'1D one 32-year-old telehealth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patient from Oregon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ajph.aphapublications.org/doi/10.2105/AJPH.2023.307437"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told researchers in a 2023 study}}}\uc2  of telemedicine abortions. \u8220\'20\'1C[Clinics were] booked out for weeks, and I didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to wait weeks.\u8221\'20\'1D Another patient, a 21-year-old also from Oregon, added: \u8220\'20\'1CI couldn\u8217\'20\'19t afford a surgical or medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the clinic. [Telehealth care] is half the price of abortions where I live.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMore than half of our patients are getting their medications delivered to their doorstep within 48 hours of engaging with our website,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Jamie Phifer, a family medicine doctor and medical director for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Demand, a virtual clinic that ships \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to more than a dozen states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal. \u8220\'20\'1CThe time between knowing you want an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 that can be torture for people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Phifer, like many representatives from other virtual clinics interviewed by the Guardian, did not know exactly what they would do if the supreme court moves to curtail access to mifepristone. One virtual clinic \u8211\'20\'13 Lilith Care, which serves Hawaii, Rhode Island and Massachusetts \u8211\'20\'13 would probably shut down altogether, the nurse-midwife behind the service said.\par \par \uc2 Typically, US medication abortions include doses of both mifepristone and a second drug, misoprostol. Depending on the justices\u8217\'20\'19 eventual ruling, \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Demand might switch to offering misoprostol-only abortions. Those abortions are safe and effective, but less effective than abortions performed using a combination of mifepristone and misoprostol. They can also be more painful.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s frankly cruel to women when you know that a safe, effective method with mifepristone and misoprostol has been around for more than 23 years,\u8221\'20\'1D Phifer said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd now you\u8217\'20\'19re forcing them into a misoprostol-only regimen, which is three doses of a medication that makes you feel like absolute shit and results in a much more prolonged process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bass and Offley have also debated moving to offering misoprostol-only abortions, a pivot that they called, in unison: \u8220\'20\'1Cludicrous\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt just seems so crazy that we\u8217\'20\'19re even faced with this,\u8221\'20\'1D Bass said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240324ek3o0015p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
