\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump says he would testify in hush money trial; court lowers bond in fraud case to $175m for now \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,462 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 March 2024\par 20:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s looming trials, read our latest stories:Trump told to pay $175m bond in 10 days in civil fraud caseTrump hush-money trial start date set for 15 April\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-6601a2758f08049f814f57eb#block-6601a2758f08049f814f57eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will go to trial on 15 April}}}\uc2  in New York City on charges related to making hush-money payments, after a judge rejected his attorney\u8217\'20\'19s arguments that prosecutors had committed misconduct and the trial should be delayed, or canceled outright. The decision raises the possibility that the former president could be convicted or exonerated of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-6601a55b8f0836b1893af298#block-6601a55b8f0836b1893af298"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the four sets}}}\uc2  of criminal charges he faces before the November presidential election \u8211\'20\'13 which could upend the campaign. However, things could still change. Trump says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-6601a68f8f08049f814f5830#block-6601a68f8f08049f814f5830"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he\u8217\'20\'19ll appeal}}}\uc2  the ruling, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-6601973b8f0836b1893af191#block-6601973b8f0836b1893af191"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scored a win}}}\uc2  at an appeals court in a separate matter earlier today, when his attorneys managed to get the bond he must produce in his civil fraud judgment reduced, and his payment date delayed.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-6601cc028f08d320eb5f296e#block-6601cc028f08d320eb5f296e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hear a case}}}\uc2  brought by a conservative group against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies warn is a preview of a second Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s aspirations.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Before the appeals court ruling, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-66017d6e8f08049f814f55c5#block-66017d6e8f08049f814f55c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump came close}}}\uc2  to blowing his deadline to produce at $454m bond, which he said he was struggling to find backers for.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  security council{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-66018dd88f0836b1893af101#block-66018dd88f0836b1893af101"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a resolution}}}\uc2  calling for a ceasefire in Gaza after the United States abstained.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-6601d5388f08e7385d08632a#block-6601d5388f08e7385d08632a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 encouraged}}}\uc2  Israel to wrap up its invasion of Gaza, warning that it was risking its international reputation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-660180778f08049f814f55ea#block-660180778f08049f814f55ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mocked}}}\uc2  Trump after he gave himself an award for golfing at his own club.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump tells Israel to 'get it done' in Gaza, warns of damage to international reputation\par \par \uc2 In an interview with a conservative publication, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  encouraged Israel \u8220\'20\'1Cto finish up your war\u8221\'20\'1D in Gaza and warned \u8220\'20\'1Cyou\u8217\'20\'19re losing a lot of the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments came {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/un-gaza-ceasefire-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the same day}}}\uc2  as the United States allowed the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council to pass a resolution calling for a ceasefire in Gaza, reversing months of obstruction. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has seen some Democratic supporters defect recently over his support for Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , and earlier this month, the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/14/chuck-schumer-israel-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  him of inhibiting peace and called for Israel to hold new elections.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.israelhayom.com/2024/03/25/trump-to-israel-hayom-only-a-fool-would-have-not-acted-like-israel-on-oct-7/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with Israel Hayom}}}\uc2 , which is owned by the family of \uc2 Sheldon Adelson\uc2 , a conservative mogul and supporter of both Trump and Netanyahu who died in 2021, Trump expressed support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s response to the 7 October attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would act very much the same way as you did. You would have to be crazy not to,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 But he also criticized Israel for harming its reputation, as images of destroyed infrastructure and dead civilians poured out of Gaza:\par \par \uc2 You have to finish up your war. To finish it up. You gotta get it done. And, I am sure you will do that. And we gotta get to peace, we can\u8217\'20\'19t have this going on. And I will say, Israel has to be very careful, because you\u8217\'20\'19re losing a lot of the world, you\u8217\'20\'19re losing a lot of support, you have to finish up, you have to get the job done.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 With the supreme court set to weigh a conservative challenge against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reports on a study showing more and amore Americans are relying on the medication to end their pregnancies:\par \par \uc2 In the six months after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, roughly 26,000 more Americans used pills to induce their own at-home abortions than would have done so if Roe had not fallen, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jama/fullarticle/2816817?resultClick=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new study}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Published on Monday in Jama, one of the leading peer-reviewed medical journals in the United States, the study comes ahead of a key Tuesday hearing at the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  at which the justices will hear oral arguments in a case that could determine the future of a major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 Pills are used in 63% of all abortions within the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/healthcare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US healthcare}}}\uc2  system, and the study suggests they are being used by even more people than previously known in order to evade \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions that now blanket much of the US.\par \par \uc2 Analyzing data from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill suppliers who operate outside of the US healthcare system, the study provides a rare window into the growing practice known as \u8220\'20\'1Cself-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. Although definitions of self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can vary, the practice generally refers to abortions that take place outside the formal healthcare system, without the aid of a US-based clinician.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/self-managed-abortions-avoid-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Tip of the iceberg\u8217\'20\'19: US self-managed abortions soar post-Roe, study shows}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s hearing on Tuesday on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/24/hawaii-mifepristone-abortion-pill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the availability of a widely used \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill}}}\uc2 , Democratic senator Elizabeth Warren warned that a future Trump administration would seek to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Warren said the case brought by a conservative group, which centers on the drug mifepristone, highlighted the stakes of the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans have gone to the courts acting as if they know better than the scientific experts at the \uc2 FDA\uc2  about the safety of medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said today on a press call organized by the Biden campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat does that tell us? \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Maga Republicans are prepared to use every tool in their toolbox to control women\u8217\'20\'19s bodies: banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, ending access to IVF and even attacking contraception access.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Julie Chavez Rodriguez, manager of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign, said they planned to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a central theme, noting that Democrats had performed strongly in elections where the issue was on the ballot. The campaign, she said, would keep reminding voters that it was Trump who laid the groundwork to overturn Roe v Wade with his appointment of three conservative supreme court justices.\par \par \uc2 Mini Timmaraju\uc2 , the CEO of \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2 , said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support of a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban at 15 or 16 weeks of pregnancy would backfire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is still an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D she said on the call. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd as we showed in Virginia, Americans hate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, they will not fall for it, they will not stand for it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign hammers Trump as 'weak and desperate'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign has released a statement attacking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after a weekend the former president spend {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/25/trump-golf-biden-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 awarding himself}}}\uc2  while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/25/trump-fraud-bond-deadline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggling to secure a bond}}}\uc2  for his civil fraud conviction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is weak and desperate \u8211\'20\'13 both as a man and a candidate for president,\u8221\'20\'1D said James Singer, a spokesman for the Biden-Harris campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis campaign can\u8217\'20\'19t raise money, he is uninterested in campaigning outside his country club, and every time he opens his mouth, he pushes moderate and suburban voters away with his dangerous agenda. America deserves better than a feeble, confused, and tired \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 National security spokesman John Kirby has just wrapped up his part of the press briefing at the White House and left the room, leaving press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  handing questions about congressional matters now involving the stuck legislation over aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Kirby said of Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/un-gaza-ceasefire-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 canceling of the high level delegation}}}\uc2  visit to the White House tomorrow for talks on Gaza:\u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s disappointing, we would have preferred to have had that meeting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kirby said that Israeli defense minister Yoav Gallant is currently at the White House for a long-scheduled visit, meeting with national security adviser Jake Sullivan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHumanitarian assistance will be on the agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirby emphasized.\par \par \uc2 He said that the US abstained in the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council resolution vote this morning calling for an immediate ceasefire and the release of the remaining hostages by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , which controls Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe chose to abstain [rather than veto] because it did not include language condemning \uc2 Hamas\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirby said. And it did link a ceasefire to a hostage deal. The US put forward a ceasefire resolution last Friday but it was more conditional than the one it abstained on today. The US resolution last week was vetoed by Russia and China.\par \par \uc2 Kirby added: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Hamas\uc2  could solve all these problems right now by putting down their arms and releasing the hostages.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Israeli defense minister Yoav Gallant is in Washington, meeting with national security adviser Jake Sullivan today and will meet with US defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Julian Borger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/un-gaza-ceasefire-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote earlier}}}\uc2  that after the vote at the \uc2 UN\uc2  [this morning], the office of \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  cancelled a planned visit to Washington by two of his ministers, intended to discuss a planned Israeli offensive on the southernmost Gazan city of Rafah, which the US opposes. The White House said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery disappointed\u8221\'20\'1D by the decision. However, a previously arranged visit by the Israeli defence minister, Yoav Gallant, went ahead.\par \par \uc2 US national security spokesperson John Kirby said just now at the White House press briefing underway that Israel was still \u8220\'20\'1Ca friend and ally\u8221\'20\'1D and that the US was still supplying Israel with aid and weapons.\par \par \uc2 But the US is adamant that Israel should not only agree to a ceasefire tied to a hostage deal but should not invade Rafah, the city closest to Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s southern border with Egypt, which is packed with more than 1.5 million desperate Palestinians who fled the military operation that has decimated a lot of Gaza further north.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the same concerns about a ground offensive in Rafah that we had yesterday and the day before,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirby said.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military bombed parts of Rafah overnight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 National security spokesperson John Kirby just spoke to the press about the US abstaining on the vote at the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council in New York earlier today calling for an immediate ceasefire in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur vote does not represent, repeat, does not represent, a shift in our policy,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Kirby added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe wanted to get to a place where we could support this resolution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US did not support it because it did not contain language condemning \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , he said.\par \par \uc2 He was just asked about Israel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/25/israel-gaza-live-unrwa-aid-north-gaza-un-security-council-vote-ceasefire-middle-east-latest?page=with:block-660193598f0836b1893af14d#block-660193598f0836b1893af14d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 then cancelling}}}\uc2  the high-level diplomatic delegation visit to the White House tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are kind of perplexed by this,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. He said it was a non-binding resolution at the \uc2 UN\uc2  so does not hamper \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael\u8217\'20\'19s ability to go after \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He emphasized that the US has not changed its policy, no matter what the Israeli government is implying.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House press briefing is running later than originally scheduled today.\par \par \uc2 Press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is due to be joined in the west wing briefing room by national security spokesperson John Kirby.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre usually deals with most of the domestic issues while Kirby deals with foreign policy issues.\par \par \uc2 The situation in Russia after the probable-Islamic State attack last Friday night at a concert hall and the latest on Israel-Gaza will be prominent on the agenda.\par \par \uc2 The US abstained on a \uc2 UN\uc2  security council vote on an immediate ceasefire and hostage release earlier today, following which Israel cancelled its diplomatic government visit to Washington to discuss Rafah.\par \par \uc2 The briefing is getting underway now.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-6601a2758f08049f814f57eb#block-6601a2758f08049f814f57eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will go to trial on 15 April}}}\uc2  in New York City on charges related to making hush-money payments, after a judge rejected his attorney\u8217\'20\'19s arguments that prosecutors had committed misconduct and the trial should be delayed, or canceled outright. The decision raises the possibility that the former president could be convicted or exonerated of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-6601a55b8f0836b1893af298#block-6601a55b8f0836b1893af298"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one the four sets}}}\uc2  of criminal charges he faces before the November presidential election \u8211\'20\'13 which could upend the campaign. However, things could still change. Trump says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-6601a68f8f08049f814f5830#block-6601a68f8f08049f814f5830"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he\u8217\'20\'19ll appeal}}}\uc2  the ruling, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-6601973b8f0836b1893af191#block-6601973b8f0836b1893af191"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scored a win}}}\uc2  at an appeals court in a separate matter earlier today, when his attorneys managed to get the bond he must produce in his civil fraud judgment reduced, and his payment date delayed.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Before the appeals court ruling, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-66017d6e8f08049f814f55c5#block-66017d6e8f08049f814f55c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump came close}}}\uc2  to blowing his deadline to produce at $454m bond, which he said he was struggling to find backers for.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  security council{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-66018dd88f0836b1893af101#block-66018dd88f0836b1893af101"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a resolution}}}\uc2  calling for a ceasefire in Gaza after the United States abstained.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump gave himself an award at his own golf club, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/25/trump-hush-money-trial-fraud-bond-deadline-latest-updates?page=with:block-660180778f08049f814f55ea#block-660180778f08049f814f55ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawing mockery}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he would testify at hush-money trial\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would testify in his defense at the hush-money trial, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said yes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would have no problem testifying. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t do anything wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 He was then asked if he was worried that a conviction would hurt his presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 It could \u8220\'20\'1Cmake me more popular because the people know it\u8217\'20\'19s a scam\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump replied. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a Biden trial.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The former president has inhabited the witness stand before, including in author E Jean Carroll \u8217\'20\'19s second defamation trial earlier this year:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/25/e-jean-carroll-defamation-trial-trump-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump takes stand and gives brief testimony in E Jean Carroll trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Todd Blanche, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney, then took over to more concisely outline his objections with the former president going to trial on 15 April.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe very much believe that starting this trial in April, or even starting this trial at any point before the election, is completely unfair to President Trump. It\u8217\'20\'19s completely unfair to the American people who are evaluating who they want to be the next president,\u8221\'20\'1D Blanche said.\par \par \uc2 He referred to 15 April as \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a day we should go to trial, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue to fight\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has kicked off his press conference with familiar allegations that the criminal prosecutions against him amount to \u8220\'20\'1Celection interference\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re dying to get this thing started. The judge cannot go faster. He wants to get it started so badly,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, after New York judge Juan Merchan ruled not long ago that his hush-money trial could begin on 15 April.\par \par \uc2 Trump then appears to mix his words, and implies that elections should not be held because {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of all his legal troubles}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s illegal, what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing. It\u8217\'20\'19s criminal what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing, and it\u8217\'20\'19s never been done before in this country. You can\u8217\'20\'19t have an election in the middle of a political season,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. Perhaps he meant to say \u8220\'20\'1Ctrial\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump to hold press conference after New York judge allows hush-money case to proceed\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he will hold a press conference at 1pm, following New York judge Juan Merchan \u8217\'20\'19s ruling allowing his trial on charges related to making hush-money payments to begin on 15 April.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will appeal judge's ruling beginning hush-money trial on 15 April\par \par \uc2 As he departed the Manhattan courthouse where Judge Juan Merchan ruled that his trial on charges related to making hush-money payments can begin on 15 April, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced that he would appeal the decision.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The ruling setting 15 April as the start of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trial on charges related to paying hush money raises the prospect that the former president will receive a verdict on one of his four criminal matters before the November election.\par \par \uc2 The other three cases \u8211\'20\'13 two of which concern his attempts to block \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win in 2020, and the third regarding his possession of classified documents after leaving the White House \u8211\'20\'13 remain tied up in pre-trial motions and appeals. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of all the cases\u8217\'20\'19 status:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Donald Trump case tracker: where does each investigation stand?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York judge rules Trump hush money case can start on 15 April\par \par \uc2 Judge Juan Merchan has ruled that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s trial on charges related to making hush-money payments will begin on 15 April.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys had alleged misconduct by Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s office in sharing evidence, and asked for the charges to be dismissed, or the proceedings to be delayed at least 90 days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe district attorney of NY County is not at fault for the late production of documents from the US attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office,\u8221\'20\'1D Merchan said.\par \par \uc2 He added that \u8220\'20\'1Cdefendant has been given a reasonable amount of time to prepare,\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CJury selection in this matter will commence in 21 days, on April 15.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will 'abide' by ruling to put up reduced bond\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112157116408288187"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a post on Truth Social}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he would put up the $175m bond required to satisfy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/trump-penalties-new-york-fraud-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the judgment in his New York civil fraud case}}}\uc2 , while attacking \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , the judge who presided over the trial, and the state attorney general Letitia James.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will abide by the decision of the Appellate Division, and post either a bond, equivalent securities, or cash. This also shows how ridiculous and outrageous Engoron\u8217\'20\'19s original decision was at $450 Million,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote.\par \par \uc2 He also let fly at Engoron, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CHis credibility, and that of Letitia James, has been shattered.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general's office says Trump 'still facing accountability' despite reduced bond\par \par \uc2 In a statement, a spokesperson for New York attorney general Letitia James said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is still liable for paying the full amount of his judgment, even though an appeals court reduced how much he must put up as a bond:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is still facing accountability for his staggering fraud. The court has already found that he engaged in years of fraud to falsely inflate his net worth and unjustly enrich himself, his family, and his organization. The $464 million judgment \u8211\'20\'13 plus interest \u8211\'20\'13 against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the other defendants still stands.\par \par \uc2 The former president is responsible for $454m of the total judgment in the case, with the rest to be paid by his co-defendants.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has narrowly avoided defaulting on his obligation to put up a bond after being found liable for civil fraud in New York. But even if he had blown his deadline, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  reports that it may have taken a long time for New York authorities to seize his assets to satisfy the judgment:\par \par \uc2 The face-off between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/letitia-james"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Letitia James}}}\uc2 , the New York attorney general, could reach a denouement as soon as Tuesday when James assumes the legal right to begin seizing the former US president\u8217\'20\'19s assets in lieu of a $454m fine Trump says he can\u8217\'20\'19t meet.\par \par \uc2 But anyone expecting Anthony Miranda, sheriff of the city of New York, to show up at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s premiere property and home on 5th Avenue to cart off the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.idesignarch.com/inside-donald-and-melania-trumps-manhattan-apartment-mansion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faux-Louis XIV furniture, the golden cherubs, crystal chandeliers }}}\uc2  or chisel the 24-karat gold from the architraves and cornices, may be disappointed.\par \par \uc2 Collecting a financial judgment is a slow and arduous process, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  real estate attorneys, especially when the assets that could be seized to satisfy that judgement are properties withheld in a complex web of ownership and titles, subject to mortgages and co-ownership claims.\par \par \uc2 The same problem that Trump says he faces raising a bond against his properties is the same problem that James could find in liquefying his assets to satisfy the punishment brought in after she won a fraud trial against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s real estate empire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBonds people do not like to use property as collateral because it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to liquify the asset if there\u8217\'20\'19s a default,\u8221\'20\'1D said Adam Leitman Bailey, a real estate attorney, \u8220\'20\'1Cand for the attorney general this isn\u8217\'20\'19t so easy either. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be very difficult to seize his properties. It takes a lot of work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/24/letitia-james-seize-trump-assets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Seizing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s New York properties will not be easy for Letitia James}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Appeals court reduces Trump bond to $175m, extends deadline\par \par \uc2 A state appeals court has reduced the bond \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  must put up in response to his civil fraud judgment in New York to $175m, and given him 10 more days to get the money together, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Previously, the former president had until today to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/trump-penalties-new-york-fraud-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 produce a $454m bond}}}\uc2  in response to a judge\u8217\'20\'19s finding that he fraudulently manipulated the value of his assets, an amount {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/22/trump-money-claims-fundraising-fraud-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump said}}}\uc2  he was not able to secure.\par \par \uc2 Due to an error by Reuters, this post was corrected to note the decision was made by a New York appeals court, not a federal court.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A key plank of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pitch to presidential election voters has been a return to what he characterizes as the good old days of his first term in the White House. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  reports that the former president appears to mean what he says, as he gets together his old team of problematic campaign advisors:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s getting the band back together. But this time they come with political baggage, conspiracy theories and, in some instances, criminal convictions.\par \par \uc2 The former US president\u8217\'20\'19s old acolytes are returning to the fold, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/03/20/trump-far-righters-return"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eager to exert influence}}}\uc2  on his bid for the White House and have their say in a potential second administration. That poses a headache for his election campaign team, whose efforts to run a disciplined operation can be upended at any moment by the mercurial Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump always wants to feel comfortable about the people who surround him and what better way to do that than to get the band back together?\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/people/william-a-galston/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bill Galston}}}\uc2 , a senior fellow at the \uc2 Brookings Institution\uc2  thinktank in Washington DC. \u8220\'20\'1CWe could look forward to the greatest hits ad nauseam.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If a man is judged by the company he keeps, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speaks volumes. There was uproar in 2022 when when the rapper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uk.news.yahoo.com/white-nationalist-2024-rival-happened-182947203.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kanye West brought the white supremacist Nick Fuentes to dinner}}}\uc2  at his Mar-a-Lago estate in Palm Beach, Florida.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inner circle includes the far-right representatives \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  of Florida and \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  of Georgia; \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , a former Democrat turned rightwing media personality and outspoken critic of aid to Ukraine; and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , a biotech entrepreneur who has pushed the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat replacement\u8221\'20\'1D theory and claimed that the 6 January 2021 insurrection was an inside job.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/25/trump-inner-circle-manafort-gaetz-mtg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Headache for campaign team as Trump gets the band back together}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US abstains as \uc2 UN\uc2  security council passes resolution calling for ceasefire in Gaza\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in Manhattan, the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council just passed a resolution calling for a ceasefire in Gaza, after failing to do so for months due to the vetos of major powers.\par \par \uc2 The United States objected to previous resolutions but abstained from this vote, allowing it to pass and potentially signaling a new approach to its relationship with Israel, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  faces {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/08/why-joe-biden-support-israel-relationship-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mounting criticism}}}\uc2  from allies in the Democratic party over his support for its invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Follow our live blog for the latest on this developing story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/25/israel-gaza-live-unrwa-aid-north-gaza-un-security-council-vote-ceasefire-middle-east-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Gaza live: UN security council passes resolution calling for immediate ceasefire, as US abstains}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Merchan asked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team why they waited so long to bring the document receipt issues to him, noting that they had met on 15 February.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney Todd Blanche responded: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we met with the court on the 15th, the process was ongoing. There wasn\u8217\'20\'19t any resolution at that point \u8230\'20\'26 we didn\u8217\'20\'19t know if [the request] would be granted. We didn\u8217\'20\'19t believe, even as I sit here today, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what kind of intervention we could have sought from your honor at that point. We had certainly been trying to get these materials.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Merchan also asked both sides: \u8220\'20\'1CHow many of those documents were actually relevant to this case?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The prosecution said: \u8220\'20\'1COur assessment is that the number of relevant usable new documents is quite small. Our analysis is ongoing but I think we have in the neighborhood of 300 or fewer are related to the subject matter of this case. The people believe that those materials are almost exclusively cumulative in our view [and] largely inculpatory.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As the hearing kicked off, Judge Juan Merchan started by recapping \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s arguments.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys claim that Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  did not share evidence in a timely manner, and have asked Merchan to either delay the case by at least 90 days, or throw it out altogether.\par \par \uc2 Merchan noted Trump attorney Todd Blanche filed a motion that accused \u8220\'20\'1Cthe people of engaging in serious discovery violations\u8221\'20\'1D, which were \u8220\'20\'1Cspecifically to interfere in the 2024 presidential election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The hearing is about to begin.\par \par \uc2 Judge Juan Merchan just arrived on the bench. Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  came into the room shortly before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump arrives in Manhattan courtroom for hearing where judge could further delay hush-money trial\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just walked into the Manhattan courtroom for what could be a pivotal hearing in his hush-money case, as judge Juan Merchan weighs whether to set a new trial date, or delay proceedings further.\par \par \uc2 Wearing a navy suit, red tie and white shirt, the former president entered just before 10am, without much of an expression on his face.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a witch-hunt and a hoax,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, before going into the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Among the readers of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Truth Social account is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 or at least whoever manages his X account.\par \par \uc2 They saw fit to mock the former president for announcing he had received an award from \u8230\'20\'26 well, himself:\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations, Donald. Quite the accomplishment. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nyDivqPwoI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nyDivqPwoI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1772084227200164325?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search for a $454m bond, and what happens if he does not secure one in the coming hours, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dominic-rushe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominic Rushe}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Time was running out for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  to secure a bond covering the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/trump-penalties-new-york-fraud-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $454m loss}}}\uc2  for his recent fraud case loss on Monday, opening the way for New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general to begin the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/24/letitia-james-seize-trump-assets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long, slow process}}}\uc2  of seizing his assets.\par \par \uc2 The former president has until Monday to secure a bond covering the half-billion-dollar judgment against him while he appeals the decision. Trump must post collateral covering 120% of the judgment, according to court filings, a sum of more than $557m. Last week his lawyers said it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cpractical impossibility\u8221\'20\'1D for him to secure a bond of this size.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA bond of this size is rarely if ever seen. In the unusual circumstance that a bond of this size is issued, it is provided to the largest public companies in the world, not to individuals or privately held businesses,\u8221\'20\'1D his lawyers argued.\par \par \uc2 The attorney general, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/letitia-james"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Letitia James}}}\uc2 , had made clear that she will seize Trump assets if the bond is not secured. On Friday her office filed judgments in Westchester county, north of New York City, home to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sprawling Seven Springs estate and golf course.\par \par \uc2 A judgment has already been entered in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  City, home to some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most famous assets, including Trump Tower and 40 Wall Street.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/25/trump-fraud-bond-deadline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Deadline arrives for Trump to secure $454m bond or risk seizure of assets}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As deadline to post $454m bond looms, Trump asks 'Why should I be forced to sell my "babies"'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is this morning doing what he does: raging on Truth Social about the latest developments in his rollercoaster of a career as a businessman and politician, the latest subject being the massive $454m bond he is on the hook for.\par \par \uc2 The former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/22/trump-money-claims-fundraising-fraud-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has not found someone willing to back his guarantee}}}\uc2 , raising the possibility that Letitia James may start freezing his bank accounts and seizing his property. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112156189891475737"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 On Truth}}}\uc2 , Trump was apoplectic about the prospect that he\u8217\'20\'19d have to part with some of his real estate, or his \u8220\'20\'1Cbabies\u8221\'20\'1D, in order to satisfy his financial obligations:\par \par \uc2 Crooked Pols!!! There should be no FINE. Did nothing wrong! Why should I be forced to sell my \u8220\'20\'1Cbabies\u8221\'20\'1D because a CORRUPT NEW YORK JUDGE & A.G. SET A FAKE AND RIDICULOUS NUMBER. \u8220\'20\'1CTAKE HIS CASH SO THAT HE CAN\u8217\'20\'19T USE IT TO DEFEAT HIS POLITICAL OPPONENT, CROOKED \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D ELECTION INTERFERENCE, ALL HEADED UP BY THE WHITE HOUSE - THIS INCLUDES FANI AND THE CORRUPT MANHATTAN D.A. BRAGG ADMITTED THERE WAS NO CRIME, WAS MORTIFIED BY WHAT MARK POMERANCE DID - AND HE SHOULD BE. WITCH HUNT!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York judge may set new trial date in Trump hush money case as ex-president faces deadline for bond\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Today is another big one for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his lawyers, who are expected in a New York City courtroom for a hearing that may decide when his case on charges related to hush money payments goes to trial anytime soon. Jury selection was originally supposed to begin today, but Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  requested a delay after receiving new documents from federal prosecutors. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/24/trump-hush-money-stormy-daniels-hearing-delay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now says no further postponements}}}\uc2  are necessary, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll see if judge Juan Merchan agrees. Trump has been indicted four times, but all of his cases have been tied up in pre-trial motions and appeals, raising the possibility that none are resolved prior to his expected face off in the November presidential election against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . The Manhattan case appears to be the one closest to starting trial, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll see if Merchan gets the ball rolling, or gives the former president another delay.\par \par \uc2 Today is also the deadline for Trump to put up a $454m bond required by the judgement in his fraudulent property valuation case, or face that prospect that New York attorney general Letitia James starts seizing his bank accounts and, potentially, his commercial property. The former president has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/24/eric-trump-donald-trump-new-york-bond"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had trouble}}}\uc2  finding a backer willing to do that, but there\u8217\'20\'19s still time for someone to step up.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/02/joe-biden-disapproval-rating-new-low"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has not been popular with voters}}}\uc2  for most of his presidency, overtook Trump in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.economist.com/interactive/us-2024-election/trump-biden-polls/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Economist\u8217\'20\'19s polling average}}}\uc2 , perhaps a sign of better days to come.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Congress left Washington DC after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/23/us-senate-passes-spending-package-avoid-government-shutdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 narrowly averting}}}\uc2  a partial government shutdown, but leaving behind all kinds of unfinished business, including whether or not to approve military aid to Israel and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  spars with reporters at 1pm ET.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240325ek3p00236\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
