\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge confirms monitor to oversee Trump business empire\u8217\'20\'19s finances \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 5,853 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 March 2024\par 20:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Retired federal judge who monitors finances of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business empire has been confirmed to stay in that role for three more years, judge rulesThis blog has now closed. You can read the latest on the Trump trials here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Congress appears on course to avert a partial government shutdown that would have begun over the weekend, after Republican and Democratic leaders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc23158f0874ddc2053fd4#block-65fc23158f0874ddc2053fd4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed}}}\uc2  to a compromise funding the departments where spending has not yet been authorized. Both parties touted wins in the deal, with Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc36ef8f08f1bd6ae974fd#block-65fc36ef8f08f1bd6ae974fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointing to}}}\uc2  its cuts to \uc2 Unrwa\uc2 , the \uc2 United Nations agency for Palestinian refugees\uc2 , and the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc627d8f082c10cb6f37b5#block-65fc627d8f082c10cb6f37b5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cheering}}}\uc2  its funding for the homeland security department, while warning more was needed. But as with all things in Congress, nothing is sure until it passes, and the House and Senate have until Friday if they want to prevent several federal departments from closing.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  said no further delays in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s hush-money trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc80cf8f08e3ded8d7ed82#block-65fc80cf8f08e3ded8d7ed82"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were necessary}}}\uc2 . We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if a judge agrees.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barbara Jones, a retired federal judge, had her term monitoring Trump\u8217\'20\'19s finances {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc77bf8f08e3ded8d7ed08#block-65fc77bf8f08e3ded8d7ed08"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extended for another three years}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican Study Committee released its conservative budget proposal, which is meant to signal GOP priorities. Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc5bbb8f085b228adf9a33#block-65fc5bbb8f085b228adf9a33"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seized on it}}}\uc2  to argue Republicans want to cut social security and ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Top House Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc54108f08f1bd6ae97650#block-65fc54108f08f1bd6ae97650"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on Hamas}}}\uc2  to release hostages taken on 7 October, and Qatar and Egypt to pressure the group.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Are you better off now than you were four years ago? Trump asked. The Biden campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc673a8f085b228adf9b3d#block-65fc673a8f085b228adf9b3d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 answered}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Air force intelligence analyst accused of sharing classified information with anti-government group - report\par \par \uc2 An air force intelligence analyst is alleged to have shared classified information with supporters of a group that predicts a second civil war in the United States, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2024/03/21/discord-classified-documents-boogaloo-alaska/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 , citing a newly unsealed \uc2 FBI\uc2  affidavit.\par \par \uc2 The incident is similar to that of Jack Teixeira, a Massachusetts air national guard member who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/04/jack-teixeira-prison-sentence-pentagon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has pleaded guilty}}}\uc2  to charges related to sharing troves of classified information with gamers on the platform Discord. In the newly revealed case, air force intelligence analyst Jason Gray used \uc2 Discord\uc2  to share a smaller amount of classified material, and is currently jailed after being found with child pornography.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that, from the Post:\par \par \uc2 Investigators said that Jason Gray shared information that he \u8220\'20\'1Clikely obtained\u8221\'20\'1D from his access to \uc2 National Security Agency\uc2  intelligence while he served at a base in Alaska, according to the affidavit, which was dated November 2022 and accompanied a search warrant for a Discord account that Gray said he operated.\par \par \uc2 At the time the \uc2 FBI\uc2  sought the warrant, Gray had already admitted to Air Force investigators that he had created a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  group for supporters of the loosely-organized, anti-government Boogaloo movement, whose followers anticipate a second U.S. civil war. Gray, whom investigators described as unhappy with his military career, participated in several pro-Boogaloo Discord channels and shared the classified NSA intelligence with seven other individuals possibly \u8220\'20\'1Cin furtherance of the Boogaloo ideology,\u8221\'20\'1D the affidavit stated.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t immediately clear if investigators initially suspected Gray of sharing classified information on \uc2 Discord\uc2  when he consented to let them examine his account. But given that he had been discovered months before Teixeira was arrested, the incident raises questions about what the Defense Department knew about personnel who were able to share highly guarded government secrets on a chat platform.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Progressive lawmakers, led by independent senator Bernie Sanders and Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , today unveiled another proposal for a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreen New Deal\u8221\'20\'1D for public housing.\par \par \uc2 In a speech at the Capitol, Ocasio-Cortez cast the policy as a way both to lower housing costs and to fight the climate crisis, while providing well-paid union jobs:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AOC}}}\uc2  (D-NY) announces congressional progressives are relaunching the \u8220\'20\'1CGreen New Deal for Public Housing\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA different world is not only possible, a different world is arriving today.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9ZKFtUcKNu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9ZKFtUcKNu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1770887883420819833?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the progressive push, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dharna-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dharna Noor}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/21/aoc-bernie-sanders-housing-new-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AOC and Sanders aim to place public housing at center of Green New Deal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may have been indicted four times, but each of his criminal trials is facing delays of various sorts that could leave them unresolved before the 5 November presidential election. In his prosecution in Florida for allegedly hiding classified documents, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that the judge overseeing the case appears sympathetic to some of his most far-fetched arguments, which have slowed the proceedings:\par \par \uc2 The federal judge overseeing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  prosecution on charges of retaining classified documents appears to be entertaining his most brazen defenses that could ultimately result in ensuring the acquittal of the former president.\par \par \uc2 The issue revolves around an order from the US district judge Aileen Cannon on Monday asking Trump and prosecutors in the office of the special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  to draft jury instructions for two scenarios that gave extraordinary credit to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense theories.\par \par \uc2 The two jury instruction scenarios, as conceived by Cannon, were so beneficial to Trump and so potentially incorrect on the law of the Espionage Act that it would bring into serious doubt whether it made sense for prosecutors to take the case to trial.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.648652/gov.uscourts.flsd.648652.407.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her two-page order}}}\uc2 , Cannon asked for both parties to draft jury instructions supposing it was true that Trump had the power under the Presidential Records Act to turn any White House document \u8211\'20\'13 classified or not \u8211\'20\'13 into personal records: records he was authorized to retain.\par \par \uc2 The authorization issue is key to the case because Trump was indicted for unlawfully retaining national security materials under the Espionage Act. If Trump could show that he was somehow authorized to keep the documents at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2 , it would preclude his prosecution.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/21/implications-trump-classified-documents-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Mar-a-Lago judge is entertaining Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most brazen defenses}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Manhattan DA Bragg says no more delays necessary in Trump hush-money case\par \par \uc2 Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  told a judge today that after reviewing recently obtained documents, he does not believe any further delays are necessary in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s case over alleged hush-money payments.\par \par \uc2 Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s case was to be the first of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s four criminal indictments to go to trial, with jury selections set to begin Monday. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/15/trump-hush-money-trial-delayed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bragg last week asked}}}\uc2  for a delay of 30 days so lawyers could reviews documents received from federal prosecutors, who had previously investigated whether Trump paid an adult film star not to speak out about a sexual encounter.\par \par \uc2 A judge agreed with that request, but in a filing today, Bragg said there was no need to delay the case further, arguing there has been \u8220\'20\'1Cmore than enough time for the parties to review what the people now have good reason to believe is the limited number of relevant records in the [federal prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19] recent productions. This court should accordingly deny defendant\u8217\'20\'19s request for more extreme sanctions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s finances, the former president may get a lifeline on Friday if shareholders allow him to float his media company. But a clause in the deal means it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely to resolve his issues paying a massive civil fraud judgment. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/danmilmo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dan Milmo}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wealth is set to increase by about $3.4bn (\u163\'00\'A32.7bn) if a shareholder vote on Friday paves the way for the float of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/14/trump-truth-social-financial-losses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump Media business}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former US president is preparing to list Trump Media & Technology Group, which operates the Truth Social tech platform, via a merger with a special purpose acquisition company, or Spac.\par \par \uc2 The Spac, called \uc2 Digital World Acquisition\uc2 , has scheduled a vote on the merger with Trump Media for Friday. However, there are complications around the planned vote after Digital World sued sponsor ARC Global Investments, which is trying to delay the deal, to back the merger.\par \par \uc2 If the merger goes ahead and Trump Media goes public as soon as next week, the presumptive Republican presidential nominee would not be able to cash in any of his potential paper wealth immediately. The merger document contains a provision that blocks major shareholders from selling stock for six months.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s finances are under pressure as he prepares to contest the US presidency with the incumbent, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , for a second time. Last month Trump was formally ordered by a New York judge to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/trump-penalties-new-york-fraud-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pay $454m}}}\uc2  following a civil fraud case, in which the former president was found to have manipulated the value of his properties to obtain advantageous loan and insurance rates.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/21/donald-trump-wealth-to-rise-by-more-than-3bn-if-shareholders-back-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump to make $3.4bn if shareholders back plan to float Trump Media}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge confirms monitor to oversee Trump business empire's finances\par \par \uc2 Retired federal judge Barbara Jones, who has been monitoring the finances of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s business empire, the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , for over a year, has been confirmed to stay in that role for three more years, a judge decided today.\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , in New York, who presided in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial in recent months, made the announcement on Thursday. The former US president has so far been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/18/trump-cant-post-bond-fraud-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unable to raise}}}\uc2  a massive bond of $454m to cover the fine imposed by Engoron for the fraudulent conduct, ABC news {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/judge-trumps-civil-fraud-trial-imposes-monitor-oversee/story?id=108352797"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As part of his judgment, he also announced that a monitor would oversee the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  and Jones will now have the power to crawl all over the family business empire\u8217\'20\'19s books and also suggest changes to how it operates.\par \par \uc2 Engoron issued his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/16/trump-verdict-judge-new-york-fraud-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 financial punishment}}}\uc2  to Trump and co-defendants, including his two adult sons, Don Jr and Eric, last month. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  attorney general, Letitia James, sued Trump for inflating the value of his assets on government financial statements.\par \par \uc2 enltrNews\par \par \uc2 In the civil fraud case, Justice Engoron issues an order detailing retired Judge Barbara Jones' tasks monitoring the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , including by issuing quarterly reports and advising him of any violations.\par \par \uc2 The order {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HnlcRHo9s5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/HnlcRHo9s5}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4uOE0NGLUN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4uOE0NGLUN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1770860450420236351?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/world/2024/mar/21/us-calls-for-immediate-ceasefire-in-gaza-with-draft-un-resolution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft US security council resolution on Gaza marks a shift in the American position}}}\uc2 , but it is a nuanced shift, retaining the linkage between a ceasefire and hostage release while loosening that linkage and emphasising that an immediate end to hostilities is the priority.\par \par \uc2 The primary focus for now is the hostage negotiations underway in Qatar which are moving into high gear again, with CIA and \uc2 Mossad\uc2  chiefs, William Burns and David Barnea expected to fly into Doha on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The US draft resolution is designed to provide a sense of urgency to those talks. It also represents an attempt by the Biden administration to keep pressure on \uc2 Hamas\uc2  while seeking to regain some international credibility and mend ties with allies after three vetoes of \uc2 UN\uc2  ceasefire resolutions.\par \par \uc2 The latest veto was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/world/2024/feb/20/us-vetoes-un-resolution-ceasefire-israel-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cast on 20 February,}}}\uc2  on an Algerian ceasefire resolution. At the time the US envoy to the \uc2 UN\uc2 , \uc2 Linda Thomas-Greenfield\uc2 , insisted that an unconditional ceasefire could derail the talks on a hostage deal, which Washington portrayed as the best way to a sustainable truce. The US mission at the \uc2 UN\uc2  circulated an alternative text which the security council \u8220\'20\'1Cunderscores its support for a temporary ceasefire in Gaza as soon as practicable, based on the formula of all hostages being released.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A month has passed since then, however. There has been no hostage deal and Gaza has slipped much further towards absolute catastrophe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/world/2024/mar/20/world-bank-report-finds-imminent-risk-of-catastrophic-famine-in-gaza-strip"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with a UN panel of experts warning that a famine is imminent}}}\uc2 . The US is struggling to avoid the accusation of complicity in that disaster, and February\u8217\'20\'19s version of the text now looks all the more complacent.\par \par \uc2 The new version of the draft resolution circulated on Thursday morning represents stronger language.\par \par \uc2 The full article of which the above is an extract will be launched online by the Guardian very soon. All eyes are on the United Nations headquarters in New York to see what happens next.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Congress appears on course to avert a partial government shutdown that will begin over the weekend, after Republican and Democratic leaders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc23158f0874ddc2053fd4#block-65fc23158f0874ddc2053fd4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed}}}\uc2  to a compromise funding the departments where spending has not yet been authorized. Both parties touted wins in the deal, with Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc36ef8f08f1bd6ae974fd#block-65fc36ef8f08f1bd6ae974fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointing to}}}\uc2  its cuts to \uc2 UNRWA\uc2 , the \uc2 United Nations agency for Palestinian refugees\uc2 , and the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc627d8f082c10cb6f37b5#block-65fc627d8f082c10cb6f37b5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cheering}}}\uc2  its funding for the homeland security department, while warning more was needed. But as with all things in Congress, nothing is sure until it passes, and the House and Senate have until Friday to do that if they want to prevent several federal departments from closing.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican Study Committee released its conservative budget proposal, which is meant to signal GOP priorities. Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc5bbb8f085b228adf9a33#block-65fc5bbb8f085b228adf9a33"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seized on it}}}\uc2  to argue Republicans want to cut Social Security and ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Top House Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc54108f08f1bd6ae97650#block-65fc54108f08f1bd6ae97650"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on Hamas}}}\uc2  to release hostages taken on 7 October, and Qatar and Egypt to pressure the group.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Are you better off now than you were four years ago, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  asked. The Biden campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/21/government-shutdown-trump-biden-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-65fc673a8f085b228adf9b3d#block-65fc673a8f085b228adf9b3d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 answered}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, at the conclusion of their latest hearing in their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/15/biden-impeachment-mike-johnson-white-house-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 troubled}}}\uc2  impeachment investigation into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , oversight committee chair James Comer proposed having the president himself testify. The White House\u8217\'20\'19s reaction? \u8220\'20\'1CLOL\u8221\'20\'1D. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 A White House spokesperson poured cold water on Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 stated intention to invite \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to testify in public in his own impeachment hearings, lamenting \u8220\'20\'1Ca sad stunt\u8221\'20\'1D and telling the rightwing congressman steering the effort: \u8220\'20\'1CCall it a day, pal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 James Comer of Kentucky, the Republican chair of the House oversight committee, has led attempts to impeach the president over alleged corruption involving the business dealings of his son {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hunter-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hunter Biden}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the end of a long hearing on Wednesday, Comer said: \u8220\'20\'1CIn the coming days I will invite President Biden to the oversight committee to provide his testimony and explain why his family received tens of millions of dollars \u8230\'20\'26 We need to hear from the president himself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ian Sams, the White House spokesperson for oversight and investigations, responded swiftly and brutally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLOL,\u8221\'20\'1D Sams {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IanSams46/status/1770577655798091802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 , adding a face-palm emoji.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CComer knows 20-plus witnesses have testified that [\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ] did nothing wrong. He knows that the hundreds of thousands of pages of records he\u8217\'20\'19s received have refuted his false allegations. This is a sad stunt at the end of a dead impeachment. Call it a day, pal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/21/response-biden-impeachment-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House on Republican plan for Biden to testify on impeachment: \u8216\'20\'18LOL\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 On his Truth Social network, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  recently asked a question presidential candidates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hks.harvard.edu/publications/are-you-better-you-were-4-years-ago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have posed to voters for more than 40 years}}}\uc2  : are you better off now than you were four years ago?\par \par \uc2 On X, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign seized on the post to remind Americans that the last ten months of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency were catastrophic, as Covid-19 devastated the economy upended daily life, and killed hundreds of thousands of people:\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald, I\u8217\'20\'19m glad you asked. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/janV4f4L3p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/janV4f4L3p}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1770846934917378264?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House said it \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly supports\u8221\'20\'1D passage of the bill to fund the remaining federal departments that have not yet had spending authorized for the 2024 fiscal year, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Ca compromise between Republicans and Democrats\u8221\'20\'1D that would invest \u8220\'20\'1Cin key priorities for the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But in their statement, the Office of Management and Budget has one quibble. It notes that the Biden administration \u8220\'20\'1Cfought for and secured additional resources in H.R. 2882 so that the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  (DHS) can maintain its current capacity to manage the border\u8221\'20\'1D, which is seeing a surge in migrant arrivals, but that funding won\u8217\'20\'19t be sufficient:\par \par \uc2 However, DHS funding levels are still inadequate and the Administration reiterates its call to the Congress to take up and pass the bipartisan border security agreement, which would provide DHS with policy changes and resources it needs to better secure our border and protect the homeland.\par \par \uc2 The bipartisan border security agreement they are referring to appears to be dead, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/07/us-senate-vote-bipartisan-border-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed by Republicans}}}\uc2  who felt it did not go far enough \u8211\'20\'13 even though their lawmakers were involved in negotiating it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden hits out at conservative budget proposal, warning of cuts to social security, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Congress is in the midst of passing a consensus budget that will avert a government shutdown set to begin over the weekend. But, as it does every year, the conservative Republican Study Committee (RSC) yesterday released a budget proposal that would enact a number of rightwing policies on everything from immigration to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to taxation.\par \par \uc2 The RSC is the largest caucus among House Republicans, and its budget is meant to show where lawmakers stand on various issues. It\u8217\'20\'19s also fodder for Democrats, as they seek to convince voters that Republican intend to enact extreme policies. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has to say about it, in a statement:\par \par \uc2 My dad had an expression, \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t tell me what you value. Show me your budget, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you what you value.\u8221\'20\'1D The Republican Study Committee budget shows what Republicans value. This extreme budget will cut Medicare, Social Security, and the Affordable Care Act. It endorses a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. The Republican budget will raise housing costs and prescription drugs costs for families. And it will shower giveaways on the wealthy and biggest corporations. Let me be clear: I will stop them.\par \par \uc2 A summary of the RSC\u8217\'20\'19s budget can be found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hern.house.gov/uploadedfiles/section_by_section_-_rsc_fy_2025_budget.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s plans to at the United Nations call for a ceasefire in Gaza may mark a significant shift in its policy towards Israel, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/peterbeaumont"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Beaumont}}}\uc2  report:\par \par \uc2 The US has drafted a new \uc2 UN\uc2  security council resolution calling for an \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediate ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D and hostage deal in Gaza, amid mounting pressure on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  to halt its military campaign and allow the delivery of substantial amounts of humanitarian aid into the Palestinian territory.\par \par \uc2 The secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , presented the resolution as calling for \u8220\'20\'1Can immediate ceasefire tied to the release of hostages\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US has consistently argued that the route to a ceasefire has to be through a hostage deal, but the new draft resolution presented on Thursday, seen by the Guardian, is more ambiguous about the linkage.\par \par \uc2 The draft says the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermines the imperative of an immediate and sustained ceasefire to protect civilians on all sides, allow for the delivery of essential humanitarian assistance, and alleviate humanitarian suffering, and towards that end unequivocally supports ongoing international diplomatic efforts to secure such a ceasefire in connection with the release of all remaining hostages\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A European diplomat at the \uc2 UN\uc2  said the stress on an \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediate\u8221\'20\'1D ceasefire and the phrase \u8220\'20\'1Ctowards that end\u8221\'20\'1D showed significant movement in the US position. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it is a shift in saying that a ceasefire is not contingent on a specific deal,\u8221\'20\'1D the diplomat said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/21/us-calls-for-immediate-ceasefire-in-gaza-with-draft-un-resolution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US calls for immediate Gaza ceasefire and hostage deal in draft UN resolution}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Top House Republicans call on \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to release remaining hostages taken on 7 October\par \par \uc2 Three top-ranking Republicans in the House, speaker Mike Johnson, majority leader Steve Scalise and foreign affairs committee chair Michael McCaul, have called on \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to release the remaining hostages taken in the 7 October attack, and on Qatar and Egypt to use their leverage to get the group to accept a deal:\par \par \uc2 It is despicable that \uc2 Hamas\uc2  continues to hold over 130 innocent civilians hostage, including American citizens, nearly half a year later. As negotiations to secure their release resume, we urge Qatar and Egypt to use all of their leverage to immediately secure the release of the hostages on reasonable terms. There must be tangible, severe consequences for delaying or impeding negotiations, and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  should understand that delays or further harm to these civilians will come at a cost. Lives are at stake and time is of the essence. Continued negotiations should carry a vital sense of urgency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign and his Save America Pac reported raising a combined $15.9m in February and ended the month with more than $37m on hand, according to filings with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2  last night.\par \par \uc2 That is up from January, when the committees raised only $13.8m, but it is still lagging behind \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, which said he and the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  raised $53m last month and ended February with $155 on hand.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign communications director, Steven Cheung, said:\par \par \uc2 Americans know that they were better off with President Trump four years ago than with Crooked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his disastrous policies. We need a return to America First policies that successfully kept our country safe and supercharged the economy for all Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  put up these kinds of numbers on The Apprentice, he\u8217\'20\'19d fire himself,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign communications director, Michael Tyler, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US government\uc2  on Thursday filed a sprawling antitrust case against \uc2 Apple\uc2 , alleging that the tech giant has illegally prevented competition by restricting access to its software and hardware.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/mar/21/us-antitrust-lawsuit-apple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The case }}}\uc2  is a direct challenge to the company\u8217\'20\'19s core products and practices, including its iMessage service and how devices such as the iPhone and \uc2 Apple\uc2  Watch connect with one another.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, filed in federal court in New Jersey, alleges that \uc2 Apple\uc2  has monopoly power in the smartphone market and uses its control over the iPhone to \u8220\'20\'1Cengage in a broad, sustained, and illegal course of conduct\u8221\'20\'1D, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s suit against \uc2 Apple\uc2  is a landmark case targeting the most valuable publicly traded company in the world and follows a raft of antitrust suits aimed at big tech. \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Apple\uc2 , \uc2 Meta\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  have all faced investigations from regulators in recent years, both in the United States and Europe, over allegations that they have consolidated power while illegally stifling competition. All have market capitalizations above a trillion dollars.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US calls for immediate ceasefire in Gaza with draft \uc2 UN\uc2  resolution\par \par \uc2 The US has drafted a new \uc2 UN\uc2  security council resolution calling for an \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediate ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D in Gaza, amid mounting pressure on Israel to halt its military campaign and allow the delivery of substantial amounts of humanitarian aid into the Palestinian territory.\par \par \uc2 Details of the resolution, which calls for \u8220\'20\'1Can immediate ceasefire tied to the release of hostages\u8221\'20\'1D in Gaza, were disclosed by the US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , as he toured the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The US has vetoed previous \uc2 UN\uc2  security council votes on the nearly six-month-long war, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/feb/20/us-vetoes-un-resolution-ceasefire-israel-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 objecting as recently as in February}}}\uc2  to the use of the term \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediate\u8221\'20\'1D in a draft submitted by Algeria, and the new draft marks a significant step in its approach to the conflict.\par \par \uc2 Details of the new draft resolution were revealed as the \uc2 UN{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unosat.org/products/3804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released an analysis of satellite imagery}}}\uc2  showing that 35% of buildings in Gaza had been damaged or destroyed during Israel\u8217\'20\'19s offensive, which has claimed almost 32,000 Palestinian lives.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/mar/21/middle-east-crisis-live-israel-gaza-benjamin-netanyahu-ceasefire-proposal-antony-blinken-latest-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Middle East crisis live: Hamas says people killed at al-Shifa hospital were patients as IDF claims \u8216\'20\'18terrorists\u8217\'20\'19 were hiding there}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House has announced it is waiving about $5.8bn in federal student loans for nearly 78,000 public sector workers.\par \par \uc2 Another 380,000 borrowers working in public service will also receive emails signed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to say that they are on track to have their debt cancelled within two years.\par \par \uc2 Under the public service loan forgiveness program, qualifying borrowers \u8211\'20\'13 including teachers, nurses, social workers, firefighters and other public servants \u8211\'20\'13 are eligible for student debt cancellation because they reached 10 years of payments while working in public service.\par \par \uc2 A statement from the president said:\par \par \uc2 These public service workers have dedicated their careers to serving their communities, but because of past administrative failures, never got the relief they were entitled to under the law.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The Biden-Harris Administration is announcing $5.8 billion in additional student loan debt relief for 77,700 borrowers - the result of fixes to the Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Bcg6EWoDEn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Bcg6EWoDEn}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vMsv4pZg9t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vMsv4pZg9t}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Department of Education\uc2  (@usedgov) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/usedgov/status/1770822029559697470?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/11/hunter-biden-arraignment-federal-tax-charges-los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded not guilty}}}\uc2  to federal tax and gun charges, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/18/hunter-biden-house-republicans-private-deposition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testified}}}\uc2  in private. So has James Biden, the president\u8217\'20\'19s brother.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing featured two Republican witnesses, both former associates of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . Tony Bobulinski appeared in person. Jason Galanis appeared by video link {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?c5110955/hunter-biden-business-associate-jason-galanis-testifies-prison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from prison}}}\uc2  in Alabama, where he is serving a near-16-year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/jason-galanis-sentenced-manhattan-federal-court-multiple-securities-fraud-schemes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sentence}}}\uc2  for fraud.\par \par \uc2 Another key source for Republicans, Alexander Smirnov, was recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/hunter-biden-alexander-smirnov-detention-fbi-informant-0069256e9606617f890d0cf6771983ab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 imprisoned}}}\uc2  in Nevada after being charged with lying to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  about supposed corruption involving the Biden family. Smirnov has also been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/alexander-smirnov-fbi-informant-bidens-fraudster-in-prior-case/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 linked}}}\uc2  to Russian intelligence.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Bobulinski and Galanis claimed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was involved in family business activities, though a meeting described by Bobulinski took place in 2017, after Biden left office as vice-president and years before he beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to become president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A White House spokesperson poured cold water on Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 stated intention to invite \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to testify in public in his own impeachment hearings, lamenting \u8220\'20\'1Ca sad stunt\u8221\'20\'1D and telling the rightwing congressman steering the effort: \u8220\'20\'1CCall it a day, pal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 James Comer of Kentucky, the Republican chair of the House oversight committee, has led attempts to impeach the president over alleged corruption involving the business dealings of his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . At the end of a long hearing on Wednesday, Comer said:\par \par \uc2 In the coming days I will invite President Biden to the oversight committee to provide his testimony and explain why his family received tens of millions of dollars \u8230\'20\'26 We need to hear from the president himself.\par \par \uc2 Ian Sams, the White House spokesperson for oversight and investigations, responded swiftly and brutally. \u8220\'20\'1CLOL,\u8221\'20\'1D Sams {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IanSams46/status/1770577655798091802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 , adding a face-palm emoji.\par \par \uc2 enltrLOL ?????\par \par \uc2 Comer knows 20+ witnesses have testified that POTUS did nothing wrong. He knows that the hundreds of thousands of pages of records he\u8217\'20\'19s received have refuted his false allegations.\par \par \uc2 This is a sad stunt at the end of a dead impeachment.\par \par \uc2 Call it a day, pal. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XZpGEo8NOj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XZpGEo8NOj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ian Sams (@IanSams46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IanSams46/status/1770577655798091802?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Johnson says he will invite Netanyahu to address Congress\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, Mike Johnson, has said he plans to invite Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , to address Congress, amid rising tensions between Democrats and the Israeli leader over the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will certainly extend that invitation,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/video/2024/03/21/house-speaker-mike-johnson-have-to-get-spending-deal-done-by-the-weekend-stakes-are-too-high.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  on CNBC this morning.\par \par \uc2 The speaker told reporters on Wednesday that he held a \u8220\'20\'1Clengthy\u8221\'20\'1D conversation with Netanyahu, and that he was considering inviting the Israeli leader to speak with lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 It comes after the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the highest-ranking Jewish politician in the US and a longtime advocate for Israel, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/14/chuck-schumer-israel-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blasted}}}\uc2  Netanyahu in a floor speech and called for Israel to hold new elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Spending deal bars US funds to \uc2 UN agency for Palestinians\par \par \uc2 Congressional leaders have rolled out a $1.2tn spending package that would fund large swaths of the government for the rest of the fiscal year 2024, the product of a deal between President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , House speaker Mike Johnson and Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The package combines funding for half of the 12 annual government spending bills, including for the departments of defense, labor, homeland security, health and human services, education and state; the internal revenue service; and general government foreign operations.\par \par \uc2 The package includes over $490m in funding to hire 22,000 border patrol agents, which Republicans are touting as the \u8220\'20\'1Chighest level ever funded\u8221\'20\'1D, the Hill reports.\par \par \uc2 Negotiators have been highlighting funding boosts for border security technology, increases to Border Patrol overtime pay that had been green-lit in the annual defense authorization bill last year, and funding for 41,500 detention beds. Democrats have also seized on a lack of border wall funding after a partisan fight over DHS spending.\par \par \uc2 The package includes more than $10.5bn for the \uc2 Transportation Security Administration\uc2  (\uc2 TSA\uc2 ), which is $1.2bn above fiscal year 2023 levels.\par \par \uc2 Republicans secured a 12-month prohibition on federal funding for the \uc2 UNRWA\uc2 , the \uc2 United Nations agency for Palestinian refugees\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The package also includes $6bn for the President\u8217\'20\'19s Emergency Plan for Aids Relief, as well as $1.65bn for the Global Fund.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s wealth is set to increase by more than $3bn (\u163\'00\'A32.35bn) if a shareholder vote on Friday paves the way for the float of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/14/trump-truth-social-financial-losses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump Media business}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president is preparing to list Trump Media & Technology Group, which operates the Truth Social tech platform, via a merger with a special purpose acquisition company, or Spac.\par \par \uc2 The Spac, called \uc2 Digital World Acquisition\uc2 , has scheduled a vote on the merger with Trump Media for Friday. However, there are complications around the planned vote after Digital World sued sponsor ARC Global Investments, which is trying to delay the deal, to back the merger.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/21/donald-trump-wealth-to-rise-by-more-than-3bn-if-shareholders-back-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If the merger goes ahead}}}\uc2  and Trump Media goes public as soon as next week, the presumptive Republican presidential nominee would not be able to cash in immediately, however. Trump would need a waiver to circumvent a provision that blocks major shareholders from selling stock for six months.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s finances are under pressure as he prepares to contest the presidency with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for a second time. Last month Trump was formally ordered by a New York judge to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/trump-penalties-new-york-fraud-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pay $454m}}}\uc2  following a civil fraud case, in which the former president was found to have manipulated the value of his properties to obtain advantageous loan and insurance rates.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.house.gov/billsthisweek/20240318/WDI39597.PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 full text}}}\uc2  of the 1,012-page, six-bill spending package unveiled by congressional leaders early this morning.\par \par \uc2 If passed by Friday night, the package would take the threat of a government shutdown off the table until the beginning of the next fiscal year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the House speaker, touted what he called a series of wins for Republicans in the spending package, from higher spending for defense and border security to a cutoff of US funding for the \uc2 UN agency for Palestinian refugees (UNRWA)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a statement released along with the text of the legislation, Johnson said:\par \par \uc2 This FY24 appropriations legislation is a serious commitment to strengthening our national defense by moving the Pentagon toward a focus on its core mission.\par \par \uc2 In a closed-door meeting with GOP lawmakers on Wednesday, Johnson noted the bill funds 8,000 additional detention beds for noncitizens awaiting their immigration proceedings or removal from the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe homeland [security] piece was the most difficult to negotiate because the two parties have a wide chasm between them,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at the GOP leadership\u8217\'20\'19s weekly press conference yesterday.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 I think the final product is something that we were able to achieve a lot of key provisions in, and wins, and it moved in a direction that we want even with our tiny, historically small majority.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congress unveils $1.2tn spending package ahead of shutdown\par \par \uc2 Good morning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics }}}\uc2  readers. Congressional leaders on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/21/us-congress-releases-11tn-spending-package-to-avert-shutdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formally announced }}}\uc2  a $1.2tn spending deal to fund the federal government, giving lawmakers less than two days to avert a partial government shutdown. The package is the most substantial bipartisan legislation that Mike Johnson has negotiated since he ascended to the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s chair, and comes after disputes among House Republicans, Senate Democrats and the White House over border security funding.\par \par \uc2 The Republican-controlled House will vote on the sprawling package on Friday, leaving the Democratic-majority Senate only hours to pass the package of six bills that covers about two-thirds of the $1.66tn in discretionary government spending for the fiscal year that began on 1 October.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , the secretary of state, is in Cairo to discuss the situation in Gaza. He will meet Egypt\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Abdel Fattah El-Sisi\uc2 , and foreign minister \uc2 Sameh Shoukry\uc2  as well the representatives from Egypt, Jordan, Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, Qatar and the \uc2 Palestinian Authority\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9am ET. \uc2 Kevin Hern\uc2 , chair of the Republican study committee and other members of the RSC will unveil the FY2025 budget proposal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am. The House appropriations committee will hear from \uc2 Shalanda Young\uc2 , the director of the Office of Management and Budget.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 11am. Mike Johnson, the House speaker, will host the Congressional Gold Medal ceremony honoring the Ghost Army of the second world war.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 12.45pm. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will headline a fundraiser in Houston, Texas.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 3.45pm. Doug Emhoff, the second gentleman, will speak in Denver\u8217\'20\'19s Argo Park about rebuilding communities divided by developments decades ago. He\u8217\'20\'19ll be accompanied by \uc2 Tom Perez\uc2 , White House intergovernmental affairs director and a Biden senior adviser.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240321ek3l001xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
