\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas woman denied  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  decries \u8216\'20\'18cruelty\u8217\'20\'19 of Trump 15-week ban proposal\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in Washington \par \uc2 539 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 March 2024\par 18:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Amanda Zurawski, who nearly died waiting for procedure, says Trump will inflict \u8216\'20\'18chaos\u8217\'20\'19 in remarks released by Biden camp\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wabcradio.com/2024/03/19/332694/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voiced}}}\uc2  support for a 15-week national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign released an angry response from a Texas woman who nearly died due to that state\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures, enduring a \u8220\'20\'1Cnightmare\u8221\'20\'1D she said Trump created.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy family has been forever altered by the nightmare that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  created by overturning Roe,\u8221\'20\'1D Amanda Zurawski said.\par \par \uc2 In June 2022, five rightwing \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices \u8211\'20\'13 three appointed by Trump \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the ruling that had guaranteed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at the federal level since 1973.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs v Jackson ruling returned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to individual US states, allowing Republican-run states like Texas to impose severe restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Zurawski, from Austin, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/zurawski-v-texas-plaintiffs-stories-remarks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued}}}\uc2  the state of Texas after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/woman-suing-texas-abortion-ban-vomits-on-stand-rcna95162"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly dying}}}\uc2  during pregnancy, having at first been denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI nearly died because my doctor could not give me the care I needed,\u8221\'20\'1D she said on Wednesday, \u8220\'20\'1Cand my ability to have children in the future has been forever compromised by the damage that was caused.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In post-Dobbs elections, Republican threats to reproductive rights have proved an effective campaign issue for Democrats. The Biden campaign has duly made protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a central part of its platform.\par \par \uc2 As Trump campaigns to return to the White House, he must consider how loudly he can boast of his role in bringing down Roe while courting women, moderates and independents.\par \par \uc2 His campaign previously denied reports that he had expressed support for a national ban at 16 weeks, which it called \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But on Tuesday, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wabcradio.com/2024/03/19/332694/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told WABC radio}}}\uc2 , from New York: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to come up with a time \u8211\'20\'13 and maybe we could bring the country together on that issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe number of weeks now, people are agreeing on 15. And I\u8217\'20\'19m thinking in terms of that. And it\u8217\'20\'19ll come out to something that\u8217\'20\'19s very reasonable. But people are really, even hardliners are agreeing \u8230\'20\'26 15 weeks seems to be a number that people are agreeing at.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Polling shows most Americans believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal through the initial stages of pregnancy. According to an Associated Press-NORC poll last June, about half of US adults say abortions should be permitted at 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Trump told WABC: \u8220\'20\'1CAll the legal scholars on both sides agree: it\u8217\'20\'19s a state issue. It shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be a federal issue, it\u8217\'20\'19s a state issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also said he supported exceptions for cases of rape, incest or threats to the life of the mother, because: \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s the problem, you have to win elections. And otherwise, you\u8217\'20\'19d be right back where you started.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In her statement, Zurawski criticised press coverage of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump isn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8216\'20\'18signaling\u8217\'20\'19, he isn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8216\'20\'18suggesting\u8217\'20\'19, he isn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8216\'20\'18leaning toward\u8217\'20\'19 anything \u8211\'20\'13 he is actively planning to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide if he\u8217\'20\'19s elected, inflicting the same cruelty and chaos I\u8217\'20\'19ve experienced on the entire country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot allow that to happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240320ek3k002jw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
