\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Abortions sharply increase in US despite bans in Republican-led states\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 446 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 March 2024\par 15:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 1m abortions performed in 2023, a 10% increase from 2020, according to \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\par \par \uc2 Abortions in the US have sharply increased despite bans implemented in Republican-led states after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More than 1m abortions were performed in the US in 2023, a 10% increase from 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2024/03/medication-abortion-accounted-63-all-us-abortions-2023-increase-53-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to research}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , an American policy organization which advocates for sexual and reproductive health.\par \par \uc2 The latest data provides a more comprehensive picture of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the first full year after the supreme court issued the Dobbs decision that rolled back federalized rights and protections to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 A rise in medication abortions largely drove the increase, the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  said. Also known as medical abortions, medication abortions are performed by taking a dose of two pills: mifepristone and misoprostol .\par \par \uc2 Medication abortions made up 63% of all abortions in the US in 2023, with 642,700 medication abortions taking place in formal healthcare settings. Only 492,210 medication abortions occurred in 2020, making up 53% of US abortions, the study concluded.\par \par \uc2 But the number of medication abortions in 2023 may be higher than the study suggests. Current figures do not include self-managed abortions or those who received \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication in states where there are total bans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions proliferate post-Dobbs, medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be the most viable option \u8211\'20\'13 or the only option \u8211\'20\'13 for some people, even if they would have preferred in-person procedural care,\u8221\'20\'1D Guttmacher\u8217\'20\'19s principal research scientist, \uc2 Rachel Jones\uc2 , said in a news release.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  in 2000 first approved mifepristone to terminate pregnancies of up to 10 weeks when used with misoprostol.\par \par \uc2 Despite mifepristone and misoprostol being determined safe, Republicans have continually attempted to curtail access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication. And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/republicans-abortion-pill-mail-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last July}}}\uc2 , a Republican-backed spending bill included several provisions to prevent access to the pill via the mail nationwide and broadly curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court on 26 March is scheduled to start hearing a case to decide the future of mifepristone. The decision could drastically restrict access to the medication, with a ruling expected in summer 2024.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReinstating outdated and medically unnecessary restrictions on the provision of mifepristone would negatively impact people\u8217\'20\'19s lives and decrease \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Guttmacher\u8217\'20\'19s director of federal policy, Amy Friedrich-Karnik, said.\par \par \uc2 The latest figures on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  come as at least 20 states have enacted near-total or complete bans on the procedure after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative supermajority eliminated the federal right once provided by the 1973 Roe decision.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240319ek3j0028q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
