\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A campaign for vengeance\u8217\'20\'19: critics warn of a radical second Trump term\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,999 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 March 2024\par 12:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 28\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 After a chaotic first term, experienced advisers are ready to usher in a second presidency \u8216\'20\'18driven by imaginary grievances\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The US election primary season is in effect over. Conventional wisdom holds that the two major candidates will now pivot towards the centre ground in search of moderate voters. But \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has never been one for conventional wisdom.\par \par \uc2 Detention camps, mass deportations, capital punishment for drug smugglers, tariffs on imported goods, a purge of the justice department and potential withdrawal from \uc2 Nato\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/11/donald-trump-president-2024-biden-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump policy agenda}}}\uc2  is radical by any standard including his own, pushing the boundaries set during his first presidential run eight years ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2016 he was still, in his own mind at least, positioning himself to be beloved by everybody,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kurtbardella?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Eauthor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kurt Bardella}}}\uc2 , a Democratic strategist. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why \u8216\'20\'18Drain the swamp\u8217\'20\'19 was a more populist, appealing message to all sides of the aisle because everyone on some level felt like Washington\u8217\'20\'19s broken, Washington\u8217\'20\'19s left us behind.\par \par \uc2 In a lot of ways Trump is Ahab and Moby Dick is the United States of America\par \par \uc2 Democratic strategist Kurt Bardella\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow you flash-forward to 2024 and we\u8217\'20\'19re getting a much darker version of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , one who seems to be driven by imaginary grievances from the 2020 election. There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing unifying about that message in any way; it\u8217\'20\'19s incredibly self-centred. This is a campaign for vengeance. In a lot of ways he is Ahab and Moby Dick is the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Eight years ago Trump, seeking to become the first US president with no prior political or military experience, was running with a clean slate. If anything, there was a suspicion that his background as a thrice-married New York celebrity implied some ideological fluidity and latent liberal instincts.\par \par \uc2 But he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/jun/16/donald-trump-announces-run-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced his candidacy}}}\uc2  in June 2015 by promising to build a wall on the southern border, using xenophobic language to portray Mexicans as \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminals\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Crapists\u8221\'20\'1D and promising to \u8220\'20\'1Cmake America great again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During the campaign he described international trade deals as \u8220\'20\'1Ca disaster\u8221\'20\'1D and called for increased tariffs on imports. He promised sweeping tax cuts and vowed to repeal \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Affordable Care Act and environmental regulations, describing the climate crisis as \u8220\'20\'1Ca total hoax\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump pledged to nominate supreme court justices opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and, in one TV interview, suggested that women who have abortions should be punished. With backing from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nra"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Rifle Association}}}\uc2 , he opposed gun safety reforms.\par \par \uc2 Overseas, the Republican candidate deployed the slogan \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica first\u8221\'20\'1D, questioning the Nato alliance while calling for improved relations with Russia. He vowed to destroy the \uc2 Islamic State\uc2  and called for \u8220\'20\'1Ca total and complete shutdown of Muslims entering the United States until our country\u8217\'20\'19s representatives can figure out what is going on\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump did implement his first attempt at a Muslim ban almost immediately after taking the Oval Office in January 2017, prompting protests, airport chaos and a long legal battle in the courts. The supreme court ruled in June 2018 that the third iteration of the law could go into full effect, meaning considerable restrictions on Muslim travellers entering the country.\par \par \uc2 Trump failed to overturn the Affordable Care Act, but his presidency was hugely consequential in other ways. His $1.5tn tax cut added to the national debt and, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2019/oct/09/trump-tax-cuts-helped-billionaires-pay-less"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research has shown}}}\uc2 , helped billionaires more than the working class. The US pulled out of the Paris climate agreement. Trump reshaped the federal judiciary and appointed three supreme court justices who would be instrumental in ending the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/donald-trump-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 botched the response to a coronavirus pandemic}}}\uc2  that has now left more than a million Americans dead, initially underplaying the threat and later suggesting that patients might inject bleach as a cure. In the summer of 2020, Trump is said to have wanted the US military to shoot peaceful protesters in Washington during the Black Lives Matter demonstrations.\par \par \uc2 In the aftermath of his 2020 election defeat, and dozens of criminal charges against him, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s extremism has broadened and deepened as he heads into an electoral rematch with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . He won the Republican primaries with ease, prompting commentators to warn of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/03/05/us/politics/trump-presidency-election-voters.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collective amnesia}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/35106042-2e96-4dde-8cf6-734c6e89fd9e?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiossneakpeek&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the banality of chaos}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D as many voters seemingly become numb to his demagoguery.\par \par \uc2 However, an AP VoteCast poll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-biden-2024-election-nominee-polling-f80f8d7193e7901768b1bf67378c442a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found six in 10 moderate Republicans}}}\uc2  in New Hampshire and South Carolina were concerned that Trump was too extreme to win a general election.\par \par \uc2 For example, he now argues that presidents should have total immunity and openly threatens the guardrails of American democracy. \u8220\'20\'1CI only want to be a dictator for one day,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/21/donald-trump-new-hampshire-rally-dictator-biden-manchester"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he told supporters in Manchester}}}\uc2 , New Hampshire, earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 He has said he would try to strip tens of thousands of career employees of their civil service protections as he seeks to \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally obliterate the deep state\u8221\'20\'1D. Given his rage at the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and federal prosecutors pursuing criminal cases against him, Trump may target people linked to those prosecutions for retribution.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s even uglier in his language now. He\u8217\'20\'19s even more cruel in his approach. He\u8217\'20\'19s gotten much more extreme\par \par \uc2 Former Republican congressman Joe Walsh\par \par \uc2 His signature issue, border security, is once again taking centre stage with record levels of migrants caught crossing into the US. In response, he has pledged to launch the biggest deportation effort in American history. This would involve far-reaching roundups and detention camps to hold people while they await removal, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/11/us/politics/trump-2025-immigration-agenda.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reported}}}\uc2 . He has also refused to rule out reinstating a Muslim travel ban and a hugely controversial family separation policy.\par \par \uc2 Trump further wants to build more of the border wall \u8211\'20\'13 his first administration built 450 miles (724km) of barriers across the 1,954-mile (3,144km) border, but much of that replaced existing structures. He also wants to end automatic citizenship for children born in the US to immigrants living in the country illegally, an idea he flirted with as president.\par \par \uc2 The former Republican congressman Joe Walsh said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s even uglier in his language now. He\u8217\'20\'19s even more cruel in his approach. He\u8217\'20\'19s gotten much more extreme, which you would think means, oh my God, how stupid politically, because he needs people in the middle. But it is big issue and Democrats have never understood how important immigration and the border are and so Trump feels as if he can demagogue it in even more of an extreme fashion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has called for the death penalty for drug smugglers and those who traffic women and children. In a broader anti-crime push, he says he will require local law enforcement agencies to use divisive policing measures including stop-and-frisk. Last year, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/sanfrancisco/news/anaheim-trump-advocates-shooting-people-who-rob-stores/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told a rally in Anaheim, California}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CVery simply, if you rob a store, you can fully expect to be shot as you are leaving that store.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under the mantra \u8220\'20\'1CDrill, baby, drill\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump says that he would increase oil drilling on public lands and offer tax breaks to oil, gas and coal producers. He would again exit the Paris climate accords, end wind subsidies and eliminate environmental regulations.\par \par \uc2 Trump has suggested that he is open to making cuts to the social security and Medicare welfare programmes. But one area in which he has hinted at moderation is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , publicly acknowledging that the national ban favoured by some Republicans would be electoral kryptonite, although it was reported last month that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/02/16/us/politics/trump-abortion-ban.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 privately expressed support}}}\uc2  for a 16-week limit with exceptions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://watson.brown.edu/people/faculty-fellows/schiller"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wendy Schiller}}}\uc2 , a political science professor at Brown University in Providence, Rhode Island, said: \u8220\'20\'1CHis campaign has been smart to float the 16-week ban because I think most Americans fall somewhere between 16 and 20 weeks as something they can live with. If he basically says the federal government will not try to do a six-week ban, we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to come after a foetal heartbeat bill \u8211\'20\'13 so if you live in a swing state like Michigan that has codified \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I\u8217\'20\'19m not coming after you \u8211\'20\'13 that is strategically a smart position. But it would be considered a modification to the centre on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He is an empty vessel for these other people around him who do have very specific policy ideas, most of them rooted in straight authoritarianism\par \par \uc2 Reed Galen of the Lincoln Project\par \par \uc2 On foreign policy, Trump claims that even before he is inaugurated, he will have settled the war between Russia and Ukraine. Last week, after visiting the former president at his Mar-a-Lago estate in Florida, Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s autocratic prime minister, \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.axios.com/click/34676070.23927/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY25uLmNvbS8yMDI0LzAzLzExL2V1cm9wZS9vcmJhbi10cnVtcC11a3JhaW5lLWludGwvaW5kZXguaHRtbD91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc3NuZWFrcGVlayZzdHJlYW09dG9w/58c6e533a79328702e8b4bbfB53f8ffc9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump promised him}}}\uc2  that he would end Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war with Ukraine by not giving \u8220\'20\'1Ca single penny\u8221\'20\'1D in aid.\par \par \uc2 The Republican nominee also says he will continue to \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamentally re-evaluate\u8221\'20\'1D Nato\u8217\'20\'19s purpose and mission. At one recent rally, he said he would \u8220\'20\'1Cencourage\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Russia to attack Nato allies who do not pay their bills. And he says he will institute a system of tariffs of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxbusiness.com/video/6334380407112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 perhaps 10%}}}\uc2  on most foreign goods.\par \par \uc2 Sometimes it can all seem like campaign bluster unlikely to survive the scrutiny of advisers, Congress or the courts. But whereas Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 win took everyone by surprise, perhaps including him, resulting in a first term marred by infighting and hastily written executive orders, this time there are allies who consider a second term is possible, or even probable, and are ready to hit the ground running.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/election-2024-conservatives-trump-heritage-857eb794e505f1c6710eb03fd5b58981#:~:text=WASHINGTON%20(AP)%20%E2%80%94%20With%20more,and%20replace%20it%20with%20a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign and groups}}}\uc2  such as the Heritage Foundation and America First Policy Institute thinktanks are assembling Project 2025 policy books with detailed plans. Groups of conservative lawyers are sizing up what orders Trump might issue on a second presidency\u8217\'20\'19s first day. With lessons learned, his administration could be even more ruthless and efficient.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hoover.org/profiles/lanhee-j-chen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lanhee Chen}}}\uc2 , a fellow in American public policy studies at the \uc2 Hoover Institution\uc2  thinktank in Stanford, California, said: \u8220\'20\'1CSome of the general framing and themes around what it is he wants to do are relatively consistent. What is different this time around is that there\u8217\'20\'19s more of an architecture and infrastructure supporting a lot of these policy proposals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you look at the ecosystem of organisations that\u8217\'20\'19s involved in helping him think through what a second term agenda would look like, it\u8217\'20\'19s much more robust in 2024 than it was in 2016. So I don\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily subscribe to the view that the substance is all that different or somehow more extreme. It\u8217\'20\'19s just there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot more people who are thinking about it. Some of them are authorised; some of them are probably not authorised .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Critics of Trump warn that, while Trump himself has few core beliefs, he would effectively become a vehicle for extremists to push a far-right agenda wildly out of step with the majority of Americans. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lincolnproject.us/bios/reed-galen/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reed Galen}}}\uc2 , a co-founder of the anti-Trump Lincoln Project, said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe is an empty vessel for these other people around him who do have very specific policy ideas, most of them rooted in straight authoritarianism or some noxious mix of authoritarianism and Christian dominionism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care. For all of it, it\u8217\'20\'19s a means to an end. If I win do these people help me or do they hurt me? Do they give me more control? Do they give me less control? Do they give me more access to making sure I\u8217\'20\'19m never going to go to jail, that I can persecute and prosecute my political enemies, that I can make life harder for the media?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Galen added: \u8220\'20\'1CIn many ways, he is the leader of the torchlight parade but he\u8217\'20\'19s being taken arm in arm and pushed from behind by a bunch of very noxious individuals with what I would call fundamentally anti-democratic and un-American ideology.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240317ek3h000m9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
