\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Why the rift between anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  activists and Republican lawmakers is growing\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani \par \uc2 1,094 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 March 2024\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Alabama supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision causing a temporary halt in IVF care shines spotlight on problem between two groups\par \par \uc2 There is a growing rift in the decades-old marriage between anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists and Republican lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 The problem came into view last month, after a bombshell decision from the Alabama supreme court temporarily halted in vitro fertilization (IVF). The ruling, which described frozen embryos as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/alabama-governor-ivf-provider-protection-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extrauterine children}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, unraveled when the Republican-controlled legislature passed short-term protections for IVF providers.\par \par \uc2 Under a new law signed last week by Republican governor \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2 , IVF providers are temporarily protected from civil litigation and criminal prosecution in the event of \u8220\'20\'1Cdamage or death of an embryo\u8221\'20\'1D during treatment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn our state, we work to foster a culture of life,\u8221\'20\'1D the governor said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/toddcstacy/status/1761071789751366038"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a statement}}}\uc2  about the court ruling. \u8220\'20\'1CThis certainly includes some couples hoping and praying to be parents who utilize IVF.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The move offered a helpful, if limited lifeline, to IVF patients in the state. The new law does not refute the Alabama supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s controversial position that an embryo, stored for the purpose of IVF, is a person. Nor does it permanently shield IVF providers from legal penalties.\par \par \uc2 Despite its limited scope, the Republican-backed law took a step to align the GOP with US public consensus, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scribd.com/document/710089283/cbsnews-20240303-1-SUN#fullscreen&from_embed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which overwhelmingly supports IVF}}}\uc2 . It also invoked the wrath of rightwing Christian activists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTragically, the Governor of Alabama has given the IVF industry a license to kill,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.liveaction.org/al-governor-signs-horrific-bill-that-gives-ivf-docs-license-to-kill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said Lila Rose}}}\uc2 , president of Live Action, a non-profit that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CStripping embryonic human beings of legal protections is also unconstitutional.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are even running ads against Alabama Republicans using the same provocative imagery \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cblood, babies and scalpels\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that is typically leveraged against Democrats, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/03/12/anti-abortion-advocates-gop-ivf-00146369"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The backlash from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, many of which are hostile to IVF, represents a persistent problem for Republicans in the post-Roe era. The party, once united under the simple goal of repealing Roe v Wade, cannot figure out how to advance the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s most hardline policy goals without alienating large swaths of US voters.\par \par \uc2 In their rush to announce a restrained, politically-safe stance in support of IVF, Alabama Republicans inadvertently angered their own Christian conservative base.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have a lot of Christian Right and pro-life groups that think that Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court decision was good, and \u8211\'20\'13 if anything didn\u8217\'20\'19t go far enough,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a law professor at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CFor state lawmakers in solidly red districts, where there\u8217\'20\'19s no chance that a Democrat could win, the Christian right could launch a primary challenge against Alabama Republicans who supported the IVF bill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not the first time that the rightwing Christian movement has demanded that Republican lawmakers split from public opinion on reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  repealed the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  guaranteed by Roe v Wade, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists rejoiced: the Right to Life lobby had finally won. Uninhibited by Roe, state Republican leaders were free to set their own laws on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access \u8211\'20\'13 and yet wholly unprepared to answer the thorny legal questions that followed: should \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans offer an exception for cases where the life of the mother is jeopardized? What about cases where a rape or incest victim is impregnated by their abuser?\par \par \uc2 Like IVF, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban exceptions are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maristpoll.marist.edu/polls/abortion-rights-in-the-united-states/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported by the majority of US voters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The GOP\u8217\'20\'19s conservative Christian base, however, argued that exceptions should not exist, or at least be extremely narrow in scope. Rightwing activists believe that a fetus is a \u8220\'20\'1Cpreborn person\u8221\'20\'1D entitled to the same rights and protections as any other American citizen.\par \par \uc2 The concept of fetal personhood, once a fringe ideology that could be mostly ignored by mainstream Republican lawmakers, now underscores much of the modern anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s work.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in states like Georgia and Alabama, for example, contain language that define a fetus as a person. In 2022, Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s department of revenue announced that \u8220\'20\'1Cany unborn child with a detectable human heartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D can be counted as a dependent on tax forms.\par \par \uc2 The Alabama supreme court ruling itself hinges on the belief that a fetus is a legally-protected person.\par \par \uc2 Even before Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise, fetal personhood seeped into the criminal justice system, enabling the prosecution and criminalization of pregnancy complications. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/19/steep-rise-criminalizing-pregnant-people-during-roe-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020}}}\uc2 , Oklahoma police arrested a 19-year-old woman who had a miscarriage in her second trimester of pregnancy. Alleging that she had used meth, police charged her with first-degree manslaughter of the fetus (a medical examiner identified five other potential factors that may have led to the miscarriage).\par \par \uc2 As fetal personhood continues to transform American politics and law, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobbyists have been more willing to turn on Republican allies for failing to champion the ideology.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPoliticians cannot call themselves pro-life, affirm the truth that human life begins at the moment of fertilization, and then enact laws that allow the callous killing of these preborn children simply because they were created through IVF,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rose in her statement condemning the Alabama governor\u8217\'20\'19s support of IVF.\par \par \uc2 Prompted by Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s IVF wars, leading far-right think tanks are also pressuring congressional Republicans to back fetal personhood on the national stage. In a memorandum released late last month, \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  urged conservatives to view the Alabama supreme court decision on embryos as a means of protecting children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis ruling merely ensures that parents using the service can rest assured that their children will receive the same legal protections as everyone else\u8217\'20\'19s,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/life/commentary/alabama-embryo-ruling-brings-much-needed-regulation-fertility-industry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the memo said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is unclear if the GOP will ultimately back fetal personhood, or decide that the ideology is too extreme.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, 124 Republicans co-sponsored the federal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/431#:~:text=This%20bill%20declares%20that%20the,an%20individual%20comes%20into%20being."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Life at Conception Act}}}\uc2 , which would give embryos the rights of people \u8220\'20\'1Cat the moment of fertilization, cloning, or other moment when the individual comes into being\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A recent attempt by Senate Democrats to advance a bill protecting the procedure failed after a single Republican blocked it.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, House Republicans have repeatedly sidestepped questions about federal protections for IVF, leaving Alabama lawmakers to answer fundamental questions about fetal personhood on their own.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not my belief that Congress needs to play a role here,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Republican House speaker, Mike Johnson, at a West Virginia press conference on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CI think this is being handled by the states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240317ek3h000p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
