\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  puts  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  front and center with visit to Minnesota clinic\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 518 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 March 2024\par 23:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice-president toured \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  facility signaling issue will be key in election\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  visited a \uc2 Planned Parenthood\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic on Thursday, becoming what is believed to be the first vice-president ever to do so.\par \par \uc2 Harris stopped by a clinic in Minnesota, a state where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal following the overturning of Roe v Wade, as part of her nationwide tour to highlight the impact of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s downfall. Harris also toured the clinic, which remained open to patients as the nation\u8217\'20\'19s first female vice-president made her historic visit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWalking through this clinic, that\u8217\'20\'19s what I saw, \u8230\'20\'26 people who have dedicated their lives to the profession of providing healthcare in a safe place that gives people dignity,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told reporters after her tour. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I think we should all want that for each other.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Protesters had already assembled outside the clinic by the time of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s arrival. They carried signs with messages such as \u8220\'20\'1CPlanned Parenthood = \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris and Joe Biden are banking on outrage over Roe to help propel them to a second term in the White House come November. Anger over the landmark decision\u8217\'20\'19s demise was credited with helping stop a much-promised \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D of Republican victories in the 2022 midterms, as well as leading \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to triumph in multiple ballot initiatives, including in red states such as Kentucky, Kansas and Ohio.\par \par \uc2 One in eight voters now say that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is their top issue in the 2024 elections, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/press-release/1-in-8-voters-say-abortion-is-most-important-to-their-vote-they-lean-democratic-support-biden-and-want-abortion-to-be-legal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a KFF poll released last week}}}\uc2 . Harris and Biden have said that they would like to codify Roe\u8217\'20\'19s protections into law \u8211\'20\'13 legislation that is unlikely to move anytime soon, given the degree of inaction and polarization in the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s record on and ability to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights dims in comparison to his running mate\u8217\'20\'19s. Biden, a devout Catholic, has said that he is personally \u8220\'20\'1Cnot big\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And while Biden highlighted the threat to \u8220\'20\'1Creproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D in his State of the Union address to Congress last week, he did not say the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, Harris has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/09/kamala-harris-reaching-voters-abortion-gaza-election-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoken far more openly about the issue}}}\uc2 . On Thursday, she mentioned \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care\u8221\'20\'1D and said that the overturning of Roe has led to a \u8220\'20\'1Chealthcare crisis\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CElections matter,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen it comes to national elections and who sits in the \uc2 United States Congress\uc2 , there\u8217\'20\'19s a fundamental point on this issue that I think most people agree with, which is that one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government should not be telling women what to do with her body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked about her role in this issue, Harris said: \u8220\'20\'1CMy role is to do what I just did, which is to articulate exactly these points and to continue to articulate them, and to organize folks around what I know is an issue that is impacting more people than you will ever really know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240314ek3e0038u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
