\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s Likud party says Israel \u8216\'20\'18not a banana republic\u8217\'20\'19 after \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  calls for new elections \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 5,700 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 March 2024\par 21:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our full report here:Full report: Netanyahu is obstacle to peace, says \uc2 Chuck Schumer\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of the latest developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s hush-money case said they were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f3544a8f081c54654f314e#block-65f3544a8f081c54654f314e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not opposed}}}\uc2  to a 30-day delay in the trial, currently set to begin on 25 March, due to a recent disclosure of thousands of pages of documents by federal prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  visited a \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  clinic in Minnesota, marking what her office said was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65f2e9328f08ba0296d13b82#block-65f2e9328f08ba0296d13b82"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  first time }}}\uc2  a president or vice-president has toured a facility that performs abortions, as the White House escalates its defense of reproductive rights in this year\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  called for Israel to hold new elections, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/14/chuck-schumer-israel-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying }}}\uc2  he believed the prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , had \u8220\'20\'1Clost his way\u8221\'20\'1D and risked turning the country into a pariah with its bombardment of Gaza and the worsening humanitarian crisis it caused. Schumer also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f348a08f081c54654f30ca#block-65f348a08f081c54654f30ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  for \uc2 Palestinian Authority\uc2  president \uc2 Mahmoud Abbas\uc2  to step down.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f325228f08fe8721ddfb3a#block-65f325228f08fe8721ddfb3a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit back}}}\uc2  at Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s comments calling for new Israeli leadership, describing them as \u8220\'20\'1Cgrotesque and hypocritical\u8221\'20\'1D. Republican House speaker Mike Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f32c008f08fe8721ddfbc2#block-65f32c008f08fe8721ddfbc2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s comments were \u8220\'20\'1Chighly inappropriate\u8221\'20\'1D. House Republican conference chair \uc2 Elise Stefanik{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f33adb8f08ba0296d1407b#block-65f33adb8f08ba0296d1407b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  Schumer \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not stand with Israel\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ruling Likud party responded to Schumer by defending Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s public support and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f343388f08ba0296d140fe#block-65f343388f08ba0296d140fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  saying }}}\uc2  Israel is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a banana republic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the United States, Michael Herzog,{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f320e98f08ba0296d13ee4#block-65f320e98f08ba0296d13ee4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s remarks were \u8220\'20\'1Cunhelpful\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ccounterproductive to our common goals\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Dozens of American Muslim and Palestinian-American organizations and leaders in Chicago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f34d448f08fe8721ddfd98#block-65f34d448f08fe8721ddfd98"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned down}}}\uc2  a White House meeting over the lack of policy change on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing killings in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f3058e8f08fe8721ddf949#block-65f3058e8f08fe8721ddf949"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attended}}}\uc2  a hearing in Fort Pierce, Florida, as a federal judge heard arguments from the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers to dismiss the classified documents prosecution.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jim Jordan, the chair of the House judiciary committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f3321f8f081c54654f2f73#block-65f3321f8f081c54654f2f73"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened}}}\uc2  Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  with contempt of Congress if she does not comply with his committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into her office.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f30c698f08ba0296d13da8#block-65f30c698f08ba0296d13da8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 came out }}}\uc2  in opposition to the planned sale of Pittsburgh\u8217\'20\'19s US Steel to Japan\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York district attorney agrees to 30-day delay in Trump hush money trial\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office said they will not oppose \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s request to delay his hush money trial by 30 days, citing newly disclosed evidence from the US attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 Jury selection was scheduled to begin on 25 March, marking the former president\u8217\'20\'19s first criminal trial. But in a court filing on Thursday, Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  wrote:\par \par \uc2 Although the People are prepared to proceed to trial on March 25, we do not oppose an adjournment in an abundance of caution and to ensure that defendant has sufficient time to review the new materials.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration imposed sanctions on three extremist Israeli settlers in the occupied West Bank who are accused of harassing and attacking Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 Two Israeli outposts were also targeted in the latest sanctions, which the US state department said had been bases for violence against Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 Washington has repeatedly asked Israel to hold violent settlers accountable and complained that its actions allowing settlement expansion diminish hopes for a two-state solution.\par \par \uc2 In response, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s far-right national security minister \uc2 Itamar Ben-Gvir\uc2  said the sanctions were \u8220\'20\'1Cfurther proof that the US administration does not understand who is an enemy and who is its supporter\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 The settlers are the best of our sons who build, settle and bring security to the country, they deserve a salute not a knife in the back.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Chicago Muslim and Palestinian groups refuse White House meeting over Israel's killings in Gaza\par \par \uc2 Dozens of American Muslim and Palestinian-American organizations and leaders in Chicago have turned down a White House meeting over the lack of policy change on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing killings in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cair.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/LettertoWhiteHouse.pdf?emci=3f540276-28e2-ee11-aaf0-002248223197&emdi=6ff47653-2de2-ee11-aaf0-002248223197&ceid=235075"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  sent to White House officials, the organizations said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFirst, there is no point in more meetings \u8230\'20\'26 With a genocide that has flattened Gaza \u8230\'20\'26 the White House has not only refused to call for a ceasefire, but also enabled this blatant campaign of ethnic cleansing to take place by providing financial and military means, as well as diplomatic support at the United Nations. A meeting of the minds is nowhere in sight.\par \par \uc2 Second, there is no confusion as to our consistent demand for an immediate and permanent ceasefire to end the mass murder of civilians and stave off the worst humanitarian crisis in modern times. We believe another meeting would only act to whitewash months of White House inaction followed by meek handouts \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 we demand, at minimum, an immediate and permanent ceasefire, complete Israeli withdrawal from Gaza, ultimately ending the siege and blockade of Gaza, allowing the natural flow of humanitarian aid, reinstating funding to \uc2 UNRWA\uc2 , a cessation of weapons sales or transfers to Israel, and accountability measures for all war crimes, crimes against humanity, the crime of genocide, and justice and liberation for the Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 That is what history will judge us by, not more token meetings when every day is of the essence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Schumer also calls for \uc2 Mahmoud Abbas\uc2  to step down as \uc2 Palestinian Authority\uc2  president\par \par \uc2 In addition to his calls for new Israeli elections, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is also calling for \uc2 Palestinian Authority\uc2  president \uc2 Mahmoud Abbas\uc2  to step down.\par \par \uc2 According to Schumer, Abbas must step down for a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew generation of Palestinian leaders who\u8217\'20\'19ll work towards attaining peace with a Jewish state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe PA under new leadership must reform to viably serve as the basis for a Palestinian state with the trust of the people,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Schumer has already sparked backlash among Republican leaders and the Israeli government over his calls from earlier today for new elections in Israel.\par \par \uc2 enltrPalestinian Authority President Abbas must step down for a new generation of Palestinian leaders who'll work towards attaining peace with a Jewish State.\par \par \uc2 The PA under new leadership must reform to viably serve as the basis for a Palestinian State with the trust of the people.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1768346627943592137?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 : 'Israel can't survive if it becomes a pariah'\par \par \uc2 In a series of tweets on Thursday, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is maintaining his calls for new Israeli elections, saying Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  has \u8220\'20\'1Clost his way by allowing his political survival to take precedence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Schumer went on to accuse Netanyahu of pushing support for Israel \u8220\'20\'1Cto new lows\u8221\'20\'1D and said that Israel \u8220\'20\'1Ccan\u8217\'20\'19t survive if it becomes a pariah\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrNetanyahu lost his way by allowing his political survival to take precedence\par \par \uc2 He's in coalition with far-right extremists Smotrich & Ben-Gvir\par \par \uc2 He's too willing to tolerate the Gaza civilian toll\u8212\'20\'14pushing support for Israel to new lows\par \par \uc2 Israel can't survive if it becomes a pariah\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1768340612611219504?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Israel's Likud party responds to Schumer's election calls: Israel is 'not a banana republic'\par \par \uc2 Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Likud party has responded to \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s calls for new elections, saying that Israel is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a banana republic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It went on to say, \u8220\'20\'1CContrary to Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s words, the Israeli public supports a total victory over \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , rejects any international dictates to establish a Palestinian terrorist state, and opposes the return of the \uc2 Palestinian Authority\uc2  to Gaza.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenator Schumer is expected to respect Israel\u8217\'20\'19s elected government and not undermine it. This is always true, and even more so in wartime,\u8221\'20\'1D it added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is continuing to defend his calls for new Israeli elections, writing in another post on X:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople on all sides are turning away from a two-state solution\u8212\'20\'14including Israel\u8217\'20\'19s PM Netanyahu who has been rejecting Palestinian statehood and sovereignty.\par \par \uc2 As the highest-ranking Jewish elected official in America and a staunch defender of Israel, I say:\par \par \uc2 This is a grave mistake.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrPeople on all sides are turning away from a two-state solution\u8212\'20\'14including Israel\u8217\'20\'19s PM Netanyahu who has been rejecting Palestinian statehood and sovereignty\par \par \uc2 As the highest-ranking Jewish elected official in America and a staunch defender of Israel, I say:\par \par \uc2 This is a grave mistake\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1768338412124119049?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Key event\par \par \uc2 House Republican conference chair \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  has joined a handful of Republican leaders who have criticized \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  over his calls for new Israeli elections.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Thursday, Stefanik said: \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of meddling in elections of a sovereign nation, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  should follow House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 lead in supporting our ally in their darkest hour. The obstacle to peace is \u8230\'20\'26 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  does not stand with Israel. House Republicans do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CChuck Schumer does not stand with Israel. House Republicans do.\u8221\'20\'1D - Chair {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepStefanik?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepStefanik}}}\uc2  on Schumer calling for new Israeli elections. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PlBCw10Db3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PlBCw10Db3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Republicans (@HouseGOP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseGOP/status/1768315558720631223?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Since 7 October, Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  and his war cabinet have faced increasing opposition and condemnation over their handling of the hostage crisis and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s subsequent war on Gaza where its forces have killed more than 30,000 Palestinians while forcibly displacing about 2 million survivors.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Despite fierce criticisms from Republican leaders, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is sticking to his word over his calls for new Israeli elections.\par \par \uc2 In a post on X, Schumer wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt this critical juncture, I believe a new election in Israel is the only way to allow for a healthy and open decision-making process about the future of Israel, at a time when so many Israelis have lost their confidence in the vision and direction of their government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrAt this critical juncture, I believe a new election in Israel is the only way to allow for a healthy and open decision-making process about the future of Israel, at a time when so many Israelis have lost their confidence in the vision and direction of their government.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1768331043298230542?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2 , the Republican senator of Texas, said Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Cout of line\u8221\'20\'1D in his comments calling for Israel to hold new elections.\par \par \uc2 Schumer was \u8220\'20\'1Cundermining\u8221\'20\'1D America\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cclosest ally and the only democracy in the Middle East,\u8221\'20\'1D Cornyn posted to X. He added:\par \par \uc2 This is a blatant attempt to appease extremists in his party to the detriment of our relationship with Israel.\par \par \uc2 enltrSenator Schumer is out of line.\par \par \uc2 He should NOT be undermining our closest ally & the only democracy in the Middle East in the wake of a brutal terror attack.\par \par \uc2 \u176\'00\'B0This is a blatant attempt to appease extremists in his party to the detriment of our relationship with Israel. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aVXYkIEEB6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/aVXYkIEEB6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  (@JohnCornyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnCornyn/status/1768326229835354183?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jim Jordan threatens Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  with contempt\par \par \uc2 Jim Jordan, the chair of the House judiciary committee, has threatened the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , with contempt of Congress if she does not comply with his committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into her office.\par \par \uc2 The House judiciary committee last month issued a subpoena to Willis \u8220\'20\'1Cfor documents related to the Committee\u8217\'20\'19s oversight of the Fulton county district attorney office\u8217\'20\'19s alleged misuse of federal grant funds\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to Willis, Jordan wrote:\par \par \uc2 While you have indicated that additional documents may be forthcoming in response to the Committee\u8217\'20\'19s subpoena, the Committee has yet to receive any additional responsive materials in the three weeks since your initial response. Accordingly, the Committee expects that you will produce all responsive documents to the subpoena in the categories prioritized by the Committee no later than 12:00 p.m. on March 28, 2024. If you fail to do so, the Committee will consider taking further action, such as the invocation of contempt of Congress proceedings.\par \par \uc2 enltrGeorgians deserve to know where their federal tax dollars are going.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  hasn\u8217\'20\'19t produced the documents we subpoenaed.\par \par \uc2 Contempt is on the table. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7CDxJhffOF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7CDxJhffOF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Jim Jordan (@Jim_Jordan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Jim_Jordan/status/1768321600510742644?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , the Democratic Pennsylvania senator, told HuffPost\u8217\'20\'19s Igor Bobic that he agreed with some of what \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said on the Senate floor this morning.\par \par \uc2 Fetterman said he does not support Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s call for new elections in Israel, however, adding:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe we should be intervening in any of that \u8230\'20\'26 I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t want any nation, even our closest allies, to have influence on our elections.\par \par \uc2 enltrFetterman says he agreed with some of what Schumer said but he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t support his call for new elections in Israel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe we should be intervening in any of that\u8230\'20\'26I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t want any nation, even our closest allies, to have influence on our elections,\u8221\'20\'1D he said\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Igor Bobic (@igorbobic) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/igorbobic/status/1768321469887508531?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The protest vote against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s stance on Gaza continued in Washington and Georgia this week, where thousands of voters chose no one, sending a message to the president that their votes depend on a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 Washington, a reliably blue state, saw support from local elected officials and major unions in its multi-faith push for \u8220\'20\'1Cuncommitted\u8221\'20\'1D delegates. They spent about $20,000 and began organizing on 24 February. More than 56,000 voters selected uncommitted delegates on the ballots counted so far, though more than 200,000 ballots remain uncounted there as of Thursday morning.\par \par \uc2 Georgia \u8217\'20\'19s ballot didn\u8217\'20\'19t have an uncommitted option, so organizers there put together a \u8220\'20\'1Cleave it blank\u8221\'20\'1D campaign, calling on voters to cast a ballot, but not fill it out, to send a message to Biden on Gaza. Nearly 6,500 voters there left it blank. And nearly 9,000 voters chose \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 , which some protest voters have selected because she supports a ceasefire. Combined, the votes exceed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s margin of victory in the state in 2020, which was about 12,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 The uncommitted movement started in Michigan \u8217\'20\'19s presidential primary, where more than 100,000 Democratic voters chose the protest vote in a state with a large proportion of Muslim and Arab Americans. Next, Super Tuesday saw several states push for uncommitted, with Minnesota seeing the highest percentage of such voters, at 19%. Then came Hawaii, where 29% of voters in a low-turnout primary voted for uncommitted. All three states got enough votes to earn delegates to the Democratic national convention in August.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Johnson says Schumer's Israel comments 'highly inappropriate'\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican House speaker, described \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s call for new leadership in Israel as \u8220\'20\'1Chighly inappropriate\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cplain wrong\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Johnson, at a last-minute press conference alongside House GOP leaders, said:\par \par \uc2 This is not only highly inappropriate, it\u8217\'20\'19s just plain wrong for an American leader to play such a divisive role in Israeli politics while our closest ally in the region is in an existential battle for its very survival.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters during House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 annual retreat at the Greenbrier Resort in West Virginia, Johnson added:\par \par \uc2 We need to be standing with Israel, and we need to give our friends and allies our full support we have to stand with and support them right now. But what you\u8217\'20\'19re seeing from the White House and clearly from the Senate Democrats is really exactly the opposite.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House did not comment on Senate majority leader Chuck Schume r\u8217\'20\'19s comments on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , or his calls for new elections in Israel.\par \par \uc2 The White House\u8217\'20\'19s national security spokesperson, John Kirby, in a call with reporters said:\par \par \uc2 We know that leader Schumer feels strongly about this. So, we\u8217\'20\'19ll certainly let him speak to it and to his comments.\par \par \uc2 He said the Biden administration would \u8220\'20\'1Cstay focused on making sure that Israel has what it needs to defend itself while doing everything that they can to avoid civilian casualties\u8221\'20\'1D, CNN reported.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is also \u8220\'20\'1Cstill focused laser-focused on trying to get a temporary ceasefire in place so that we can get the hostages out and get more aid\u8221\'20\'1D, Kirby added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 McConnell says Schumer's Israel comments 'grotesque and hypocritical'\par \par \uc2 Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has hit back at \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f314298f08ba0296d13e20#block-65f314298f08ba0296d13e20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speech}}}\uc2  on the Senate floor calling for new elections in Israel, describing the Senate majority leader\u8217\'20\'19s comments as \u8220\'20\'1Cgrotesque and hypocritical\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a statement following Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s speech, McConnell accused the Democratic party of having \u8220\'20\'1Can anti-Israel problem\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 It is grotesque and hypocritical for Americans who hyperventilate about foreign interference in our own democracy to call for the removal of the democratically elected leader of Israel.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 Israel is not a colony of America whose leaders serve at the pleasure of the party in power in Washington. Only Israel\u8217\'20\'19s citizens should have a say in who runs their government. This is the very definition of democracy and sovereignty. Either we respect their decisions, or we disrespect their democracy.\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. McConnell: "It is grotesque and hypocritical for Americans who hyperventilate about foreign interference in our own democracy to call for the removal of a democratically elected leader of Israel. This is unprecedented. We should not treat fellow democracies this way at all." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/K6xOd1a9Ey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/K6xOd1a9Ey}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1768299378760905204?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Israel's ambassador to US says Schumer's call for new elections 'unhelpful'\par \par \uc2 Michael Herzog, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the United States, has criticized {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/14/harris-abortion-biden-trump-us-elections-latest?page=with:block-65f314298f08ba0296d13e20#block-65f314298f08ba0296d13e20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statements by}}}\uc2  the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , calling for new elections in Israel.\par \par \uc2 Schumer, the first Jewish majority leader in the Senate and the highest-ranking Jewish official in the US, strongly criticized Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , in a lengthy speech this morning on the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu had put himself in a coalition of far-right extremists and \u8220\'20\'1Cas a result, he has been too willing to tolerate the civilian toll in Gaza, which is pushing support for Israel worldwide to historic lows\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Posting to X, Herzog wrote:\par \par \uc2 Israel is a sovereign democracy. It is unhelpful, all the more so as Israel is at war against the genocidal terror organization \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , to comment on the domestic political scene of a democratic ally. It is counterproductive to our common goals.\par \par \uc2 enltrIsrael is a sovereign democracy. It is unhelpful, all the more so as Israel is at war against the genocidal terror organization \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , to comment on the domestic political scene of a democratic ally. It is counterproductive to our common goals.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ambassador Michael Herzog (@AmbHerzog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AmbHerzog/status/1768299875756618079?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican New York congressman sponsoring bill to protect IVF access\par \par \uc2 Congressman Marc Molinaro of New York said he was co-sponsoring a bill to protect access to in vitro fertilization (IVF), becoming the first Republican to do so.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://molinaro.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=2012"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  on Wednesday, Molinaro said he would be cosponsoring the Access to Family Building Act with Democratic congresswoman Susan Wild of Pennsylvania as \u8220\'20\'1Ca parent who has personal experience with IVF\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Molinaro said he was \u8220\'20\'1Ctroubled\u8221\'20\'1D by the ruling by Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court that found frozen embryos are children, adding that he supports \u8220\'20\'1Call women and families who choose IVF to bring life in to the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProtecting it is just common sense,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Molinaro, a vulnerable Republican seeking re-election, becomes the first GOP member to back legislation to protect the right to IVF.\par \par \uc2 Another Republican, congresswoman Anna Paulina Luna of Florida, was previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/rep-marc-molinaro-becomes-first-republican-back-bill-protecting-ivf-rcna143301"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  to have supported the bill but later said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cadded to the bill without confirmation\u8221\'20\'1D and that there \u8220\'20\'1Care amendments that would need to take place\u8221\'20\'1D for her to support it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Katie Britt, the Alabama senator who delivered a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/08/katie-britt-sotu-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 much-mocked}}}\uc2  State of the Union response last week, rued the \u8220\'20\'1Cirony\u8221\'20\'1D of being told by the Republican speaker of the House, Mike Johnson, that \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19ll be fine\u8221\'20\'1D before giving her disastrous speech.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the hard-right Texas senator Ted Cruz, on his Verdict with Ted Cruz podcast, Britt said Johnson told her:\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People are going to tell you horror stories about all of these things that happen and people\u8217\'20\'19s career being blown up over it.\u8217\'20\'19 And he\u8217\'20\'19s like, \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19ll be fine. It\u8217\'20\'19ll be fine.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 It was not fine. Her speech focused on Republican talking points prominently including immigration and crime. But Britt\u8217\'20\'19s bizarrely dramatic delivery, in particular in a lurid section on sex trafficking and immigration subsequently picked apart by factcheckers and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/11/katie-britt-speech-victim-cnn-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the subject of the story herself}}}\uc2 , prompted widespread mockery.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  used a speech on the Senate floor to call for a temporary ceasefire in Gaza and say that Israel has lost its way in its war on Gaza, adding that \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  should call an election.\par \par \uc2 Schumer said it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave mistake\u8221\'20\'1D for Israel to reject a two-state solution to the Middle East crisis, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 enltr"I believe that holding a new election once the war starts to wind down would give Israelis an opportunity to express their vision for the post-war future."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D-NY) calls for new elections in Israel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yFXM6504oh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yFXM6504oh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1768289417947431297?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 His intervention comes five months after Israel launched its military assault on Gaza after the 7 October surprise attack inside southern Israel that killed about 1,140 people and during which about 240 people were abducted and seized as hostages by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Hamas\uc2 -led ministry of health in the territory says the Israeli military operation has claimed over 31,340 Palestinian lives, many of them women and children. Much of the population of Gaza is displaced, and \uc2 UN\uc2  agencies have warned there is a severe risk of famine as the distribution of humanitarian aid has been restricted.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Schumer calls for new elections in Israel, calls Netanyahu an obstacle to peace\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, has called for Israel to hold new elections, arguing that prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s government \u8220\'20\'1Cno longer fits the needs of Israel\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Schumer, long a strong supporter of Israel and the highest-ranking Jewish official in the US, strongly criticized the Israeli leader in a 40-minute speech on the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 Israel must make \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant course corrections\u8221\'20\'1D to achieve lasting peace with the Palestinians, he said, adding that it would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave mistake\u8221\'20\'1D for Israel to reject a two-state solution.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu had put himself in a coalition of far-right extremists and \u8220\'20\'1Cas a result, he has been too willing to tolerate the civilian toll in Gaza, which is pushing support for Israel worldwide to historic lows\u8221\'20\'1D, Schumer said. He added:\par \par \uc2 If prime minister Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s current coalition remains in power after the war begins to wind down, and continues to pursue dangerous and inflammatory policies that test existing US standards for assistance, then the United States will have no choice but to play a more active role in shaping Israeli policy by using our leverage to change the present course.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 As a democracy, Israel has the right to choose its own leaders, and we should let the chips fall where they may. But the important thing is that Israelis are given a choice.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThe Netanyahu coalition no longer fits the needs of Israel after October 7. \u8230\'20\'26 The Israeli people are being stifled right now by a governing vision that is stuck in the past.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D-NY) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vWhO7XukFF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vWhO7XukFF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1768289177110446177?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are arguing for why US district judge Aileen Cannon should order the case charging him with mishandling classified documents should be dismissed, claiming they were his to keep because he designated them personal records while he was president.\par \par \uc2 The decision to designate the documents as personal records under the Presidential Records Act meant it was an official act of his presidency for which he could not face prosecution, his lawyers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/donald-trump-presidential-immunity-argument-dismissal-push-classified-nuclear-documents-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in a 22-page filing last month.\par \par \uc2 Classified information is material owned by the United States and cannot, by definition, be personal.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request to toss the charges amounted to an extraordinary interpretation of presidential power that would allow presidents to use national security secrets as they liked when they left office, legal experts suggested.\par \par \uc2 Previously, during the criminal investigation, Trump suggested documents were automatically declassified when he took them to the White House residence or that he could declassify using his mind.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden voices concern over proposed Japanese takeover of \uc2 US Steel\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has come out in opposition to the planned sale of Pittsburgh\u8217\'20\'19s US Steel to Japan\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 , arguing that the US needs to \u8220\'20\'1Cmaintain strong American steel companies powered by American steel workers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  announced in December that it planned to buy \uc2 US Steel\uc2  for $14.1bn in cash, raising concerns about what the transaction could mean for unionized workers, supply chains and US national security.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 I told our steel workers I have their backs, and I meant it. \uc2 US Steel\uc2  has been an iconic American steel company for more than a century, and it is vital for it to remain an American steel company that is domestically owned and operated.\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes as Biden is campaigning in the midwest, and ahead of next month\u8217\'20\'19s White House visit by Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 . Biden has made restoring American manufacturing a cornerstone of his agenda as he seeks reelection.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are expected to argue that the federal criminal case charging him with retaining classified documents at his Mar-a-Lago club should be thrown out on grounds of presidential immunity.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Aileen Cannon will consider the motion to dismiss the case based on their claim that the documents were Trump\u8217\'20\'19s to keep because he designated them personal records while he was president under the Presidential Records Act. The filing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.648652/gov.uscourts.flsd.648652.324.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s decision to designate records as personal and cause them to be removed from the White House plainly constitutes an official act within the \u8216\'20\'18outer perimeter\u8217\'20\'19 of the president\u8217\'20\'19s official duties.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors in the case brought by the special counsel, \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2 , have said the documents Trump is charged with possessing related to issues including nuclear weapons capabilities and US vulnerability to military attack, and that the statute does not apply to classified and top-secret documents like those kept at his Mar-a-Lago estate in Florida.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump arrives at Florida courthouse for hearing seeking dismissal of classified documents case\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has arrived at a federal courthouse in Florida, where a judge will hear arguments on whether to dismiss the criminal case accusing the former president of hoarding classified documents at his Mar-a-Lago estate after he left the White House.\par \par \uc2 The motorcade carrying Trump arrived shortly before the hearing was set to begin before the US district judge Aileen Cannon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senior White House officials are planning to meet today with Arab, Muslim and Palestinian-American community leaders in Chicago, according to several reports.\par \par \uc2 The meeting, first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/03/13/politics/white-house-officials-meeting-arab-muslim-leaders-chicago/index.html?email=620bb4708d235157723d480a0d8d4c265e55ec14&emaila=0ec8b2addfecba6de47e145bbfa10867&emailb=fa17fe37520b9c9752208dccf233e286aef975565778b97fc6ff23ae2388d5a7&utm_source=Sailthru&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=3.14.24%20BN%20Morning%20Thursday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  by CNN, comes as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  faces increasing backlash from Arab Americans and progressives over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/08/why-joe-biden-support-israel-relationship-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  his stance}}}\uc2  in the Israel-Gaza war. It also comes ahead of the Illinois Democratic primary on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Among the White House officials expected to attend Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s meeting are its director of intergovernmental affairs, \uc2 Tom Perez\uc2 , director of public engagement Steve Benjamin, liaison to Muslim-American communities Mazen Basrawi and national security council chief of staff Curtis Ried, CNN reported.\par \par \uc2 But leaders in the Palestinian communities angry at how Biden has handled the war in Gaza have declined to join the meeting, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/illinois-playbook/2024/03/14/illinois-palestinians-snub-white-house-00146944"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  by Politico, which quoted Hatem Abudayyeh, a group organizer, as saying:\par \par \uc2 All the Palestinian leadership we work with in Chicago have rejected this overture, and USPCN [U.S. Palestinian Community Network] considers anyone \u8211\'20\'13 Palestinian, Muslim, Arab \u8211\'20\'13 who takes a meeting with the White House to be an absolute sell-out. There\u8217\'20\'19s no more time for meetings.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former Treasury secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  'planning to buy TikTok'\par \par \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2 , the former Treasury secretary, said he is assembly a group of investors to make a bid to buy TikTok, a day after the House passed a measure to force ByteDance to either sell the social media platform or face a total ban in the US.\par \par \uc2 Mnuchin, speaking on CNBC this morning, said:\par \par \uc2 I think the legislation should pass and I think it should be sold. It\u8217\'20\'19s a great business and I\u8217\'20\'19m going to put together a group to buy TikTok.\par \par \uc2 The bill is now headed to the Senate, where its future is uncertain, though \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has said he will sign the legislation if it passes.\par \par \uc2 Mnuchin said:\par \par \uc2 This should be owned by US businesses. There\u8217\'20\'19s no way that the Chinese would ever let a US company own something like this in China.\par \par \uc2 TikTok, which has 170 million users in the US, has stated that it is not clear if China would approve any sale.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This will be \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s third trip to Minnesota as vice-president, and the sixth stop on her nationwide \u8220\'20\'1CFight for Reproductive Freedoms\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/12/19/vice-president-kamala-harris-launches-reproductive-freedoms-tour/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tour.}}}\par \par \uc2 There are no restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any stage of pregnancy in Minnesota, and the state has become a refuge for patients from neighboring restrictive states to seek abortions since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently illegal in more than a dozen states, including Minnesota neighbors North Dakota and South Dakota, and is restricted in Iowa and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the state of Minnesota by 7 percentage points in the 2020 presidential election against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to visit a clinic in the Minneapolis-St Paul area during operating hours today.\par \par \uc2 Her office declined to identify the facility before she arrives there, citing security reasons. The center provides a range of services, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , birth control and preventive wellness care.\par \par \uc2 The vice president was scheduled to tour the facility, speak with staff and be briefed on how Minnesota has been affected by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in surrounding states. She will also talk about what the Biden administration has done to protect reproductive rights, her office said.\par \par \uc2 She also was scheduled to speak at a Biden-Harris campaign event tailored to women.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris to visit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Minnesota\par \par \uc2 Good morning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics }}}\uc2  readers. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  today will visit a \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  clinic in Minnesota that provides \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, marking the first time a president or vice president has been to a reproductive health clinic, according to her office.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s trip to the Twin Cities is part of a nationwide tour she began in January to draw attention to the fallout after the reversal of Roe v Wade, and comes as Democrats play up their opposition to the rollback of reproductive rights ahead of the November election. Harris, the first woman elected vice-president, has emerged as the administration\u8217\'20\'19s most vocal and prominent defender of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. She has pointedly attacked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for saying he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/donald-trump-abortion-election-republicans-iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cproud\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  of helping to limit abortions, and blasted Republicans as extremists while pledging to push for federal legislation to restore the federal right to abortions.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Florida will hear arguments on whether to dismiss the federal criminal case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  involving his handling of classified documents. In addition to Trump, his co-defendants in the case, Walt Nauta and Carlos de Oliveira, are expected to attend the hearing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am. The Senate will meet to take up Dennis Hankins\u8217\'20\'19 nomination as US ambassador to Haiti, with a vote at noon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 2pm. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will participate in a campaign event in Saginaw, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240314ek3e001xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
