\par\par \uc2 Music\par \b \uc2 Morning-after pill handed out at Olivia Rodrigo concert in Missouri \u8211\'20\'13 where  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  is banned\b0\par\par\uc2 Alaina Demopoulos \par \uc2 1,070 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 March 2024\par 15:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 29\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Fans got access to $50 pill and condoms via singer\u8217\'20\'19s Fund 4 Good campaign to protect reproductive rights\par \par \uc2 Madelyn Ritter expected to leave the St Louis date of Olivia Rodrigo\u8217\'20\'19s Guts tour with merch \u8211\'20\'13 she didn\u8217\'20\'19t expect to also go home with some free emergency contraception.\par \par \uc2 But that\u8217\'20\'19s just what she saw upon entering the stadium. There, right by the women\u8217\'20\'19s bathrooms, was a table where concertgoers could donate to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds and pick up free condoms and morning-after pills, sometimes referred to as Plan B.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe noticed it immediately,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ritter, who is 25 (and, as she jokes, \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo old\u8221\'20\'1D to love the 21-year-old pop star). \u8220\'20\'1CI was like: \u8216\'20\'18What\u8217\'20\'19s this about?\u8217\'20\'19 They told me it was free, so my sister, her friend and I all took some. I personally don\u8217\'20\'19t need it, but I\u8217\'20\'19m going to save it in case something bad happens.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last month, in conjunction with her world tour, Rodrigo launched the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eifoundation.org/partners/olivia-rodrigos-fund-4-good/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fund 4 Good}}}\uc2  campaign, which aims to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s and girls\u8217\'20\'19 reproductive rights. A portion of sales from the tour will go toward the fund. As part of the initiative, Rodrigo paired with the National Network of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Funds, which connected her with local chapters at various stops on the tour.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are plenty of singers making a stand about social issues, but I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen anything like this,\u8221\'20\'1D Ritter said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 illegal}}}\uc2  in Missouri. (It is only permitted in the case of an emergency that threatens the life of a pregnant person.) Missouri Republicans are also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://missouriindependent.com/2024/01/25/missouri-republicans-abortion-medicaid-planned-parenthood/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trying to defund}}}\uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , which provides reproductive healthcare like STI screenings and contraception in the state.\par \par \uc2 Activists who staffed the table Ritter stopped by came from Right by You, a youth-focused text line that connects Missouri teens to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care out of state, birth control and information about their rights, and the Missouri \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund, which helps people cover the cost of an out-of-state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stephanie Kraft Sheley, project director of Right by You, said that Rodrigo had not specifically asked for the organization to hand out emergency contraception, which prevents pregnancy. \u8220\'20\'1CShe invited us, but it was our decision to bring it and hand it out,\u8221\'20\'1D Sheley said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt fills my heart with so much joy and gratitude to Olivia, and it shows how well received it will be when other artists step up and do this. I hope they follow this example.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Like Ritter, many concertgoers did not initially believe they could get the pill, which retails for up to $50, for free. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are always some people who reach for the emergency contraception and then say: \u8216\'20\'18What do I have to do in order to get this?\u8217\'20\'19 or \u8216\'20\'18Is it really free?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Sheley said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou might have to repeat that it\u8217\'20\'19s free three times. The look on their face when they realize they\u8217\'20\'19re being cared for and someone wants to help, that\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re here for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Artists frequently use their tour stops to campaign for various social causes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.headcount.org/artists/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HeadCount}}}\uc2 , an organization that works with musicians to help fans register to vote, has gone on the road with Billie Eilish, Lizzo, Ariana Grande, Harry Styles and more \u8211\'20\'13 including Rodrigo. (Rodrigo herself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2022/jun/25/so-many-women-are-going-to-die-olivia-rodrigo-lambasts-roe-vs-wade-decision-at-glastonbury"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lambasted}}}\uc2  the overturning of Roe v Wade at a Glastonbury performance in 2022, telling the conservative supreme court justices: \u8220\'20\'1CWe hate you.\u8221\'20\'1D) Rarely do those initiatives go as far as doling out free emergency contraception.\par \par \uc2 But as the 2024 election cycle become increasingly tumultuous, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/mar/13/taylor-swift-us-election-politics-joe-biden-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 softcore activism}}}\uc2  can feel hollow and phoned-in. On Super Tuesday, Taylor Swift posted an \uc2 Instagram\uc2  story urging fans to \u8220\'20\'1Cvote for the people who most represent YOU into power\u8221\'20\'1D. The plea garnered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/mar/05/taylor-swift-voting-primary-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mixed reactions}}}\uc2  online, with some followers disappointed with the vague, cautious wording.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI care a lot about who I\u8217\'20\'19m supporting and what I\u8217\'20\'19m putting my money towards,\u8221\'20\'1D Ritter said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m glad to know that I\u8217\'20\'19m supporting someone who has the same values that I do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Though most emergency contraceptive pills are colloquially known as Plan B due to the ubiquity of that brand, the pills passed out at Rodrigo\u8217\'20\'19s concert came from the startup Julie. A representative for Julie said in a statement that the company aims to \u8220\'20\'1Crewrite the morning-after pill for a new generation\u8221\'20\'1D. That basically means a rebrand: the package is cute and colorful, unlike more clinical-looking options.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReplacing the stigma and shame often associated with emergency contraception with access, exploration, and education is core to who we are, and we\u8217\'20\'19re thankful for artists like Olivia Rodrigo and initiatives like the Missouri \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund who share our mission,\u8221\'20\'1D the rep said.\par \par \uc2 Lizz Winstead founded the \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Front, a non-profit that fights for reproductive rights nationwide. She praised Rodrigo for centering local organizations doing on-the-ground work in St Louis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis gives them the opportunity to provide information and tools like emergency contraception with their branding and contact information,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone at her shows can learn who to go to for care. Long after Olivia is gone, folks at her show know how and where to connect in their own communities, which creates sustained support. That is exactly what we need right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday night, Rodrigo plays in Nebraska, which has a 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban with limited exceptions.\par \par \uc2 Since Missouri outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , activists have tried and failed to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Missouri ballot to let voters decide. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kcur.org/politics-elections-and-government/2024-03-13/missouri-voters-support-abortion-rights-ballot-measure-by-a-small-margin-new-poll-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent poll}}}\uc2  found that Missouri voters favor reproductive rights by a small margin.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights are top-of-mind for Ritter, who works as an emergency women\u8217\'20\'19s health nurse at a hospital in St Louis. She\u8217\'20\'19s administered misoprostol, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/17/what-abortion-pill-supreme-court-case-access-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 medication commonly used in abortions}}}\uc2 , to women who miscarry. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/jan/24/us-miscarriage-laws-abortion-rights-options"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miscarriages are under increased scrutiny}}}\uc2  in states with near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, stoking fear of criminal consequences.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been there for women on the worst days of their life, and it\u8217\'20\'19s disgusting to think that we don\u8217\'20\'19t have the right to make a decision about the when and where and why of our own bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D Ritter said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs a nurse, and just as someone who cares about women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare, I will be going to another Olivia Rodrigo show.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240313ek3d003bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
