\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris is reaching Democrats where Biden isn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8211\'20\'13 on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  and Gaza\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman and Lauren Gambino \par \uc2 2,045 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 March 2024\par 15:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As 2024 campaign begins, US vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s gender and race are strengths in fight to retain young voters and voters of color\par \par \uc2 Standing on the arch of the Edmund Pettus Bridge in Selma, Alabama, to commemorate the 59th anniversary of Bloody Sunday, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said she felt compelled to begin her remarks by addressing the deteriorating humanitarian catastrophe in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in Gaza are starving. The conditions are inhumane. And our common humanity compels us to act,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said, then stated: \u8220\'20\'1CGiven the immense scale of suffering in Gaza, there must be an immediate ceasefire.\u8221\'20\'1D Loud, sustained applause followed, before she added, after a pause: \u8220\'20\'1CFor at least six weeks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The remarks, the White House was quick to note, echoed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/biden-says-hopes-see-cease-fire-monday-israel-hamas-war-rcna140597"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments to a reporter days earlier}}}\uc2  and they reflected the administration\u8217\'20\'19s current efforts to broker a temporary break in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s offensive, to allow for the release of hostages and for desperately needed humanitarian aid to enter the besieged territory. Yet many Americans furious with Biden for his alliance with Israel heard from Harris what they felt has been lacking from the president.\par \par \uc2 There was an urgency to her speech \u8211\'20\'13 delivered in the footsteps of civil rights marchers who were trampled, teargassed and beaten with whips and billy clubs as they attempted to cross the bridge \u8211\'20\'13 that resonated. The setting seemed to acknowledge the youth movement furious with the president that views Palestinian rights as an extension of the racial justice movement. She pointedly criticized Israel for restricting the flow of aid into Gaza and expressed compassion for the Palestinian civilians living amid the rubble on the brink of famine.\par \par \uc2 As the 2024 general election contest begins, Harris has emerged as an emissary to the Democratic voters who have soured on Biden since propelling him to the White House in 2020. Over the last several months, she has embarked on a full-scale national tour to highlight the threats to reproductive rights posed by a second \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  administration \u8211\'20\'13 an issue that Biden has been criticized for shying away from. Now, as Harris adopts a more forceful tone on Gaza, she is also becoming a leading voice on Middle East diplomacy.\par \par \uc2 Both issues are poised to play a significant, if not decisive, role in the November general election. Polling shows an erosion of support among core Democratic constituencies amid widespread disillusionment with the economy, concern over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age and fury on the left at the administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 For Democrats, reminding voters about the threat Republicans still pose to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights may be the best way to energize young people while winning over independents and suburban women. Outrage over Roe was credited with halting the promised \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D of Republican victories in the 2022 midterms; \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot referendums have also repeatedly triumphed even in traditionally red states like Kansas, Kentucky and Ohio.\par \par \uc2 But Harris has her work cut out for her. Like Biden, Harris has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/approval/kamala-harris/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 viewed unfavorably}}}\uc2  throughout much of her tenure.\par \par \uc2 Antonio Arellano, a spokesperson for \uc2 NextGen\uc2 , a national youth-focused non-partisan voter registration and education program, called the 59-year-old Harris a \u8220\'20\'1Cliaison\u8221\'20\'1D between the administration and the parts of the Democratic base that were critical to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 victory but hold reservations about him now. With her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cfCfWUaASLg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 college campus tour}}}\uc2  and her reproductive rights tour, he said, Harris has helped elevate issues that are top of mind for young progressives and multiracial voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe brings an energy of vigor and excitement to the election that I think young people can really gravitate to when perhaps enthusiasm lacks elsewhere,\u8221\'20\'1D Arellano said.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Harris leapt into the US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars within a day of the leak of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 At a May 2022 speech at a conference for Emilys List, which works to elect Democratic women who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, Harris gave a fiery speech where she repeatedly asked: \u8220\'20\'1CHow dare they?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow dare they tell a woman what she can and cannot do with her own body?\u8221\'20\'1D Harris asked. \u8220\'20\'1CHow dare they try to stop her from determining her own future? How dare they try to deny women their rights and their freedoms?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris had spent the first several months of her vice-presidency frustrated by headlines about her apparent lack of direction, staff departures and unforced errors. Allies and experts have long seen sexism and racism in the public scrutiny of Harris, who is the first woman and the first woman of color to hold nationally elected office. The criticism seemed particularly unfair, they said, given that vice-presidents are historically overlooked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not saying that there shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have been any attention paid to management, especially when you see high-profile kinds of departures and hires,\u8221\'20\'1D said Andra Gillespie, an associate professor of political science at Emory College. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I think that there\u8217\'20\'19s still also the question of whether or not people have paid more attention to her, and also whether or not the public has had a more visceral reaction to her because of her race and gender.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But when it came to the fight over reproductive rights, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s gender, race and age and experience as a prosecutor combined to give her the edge of authenticity that Biden lacks on an issue that is increasingly critical to voters. Many of the 16 states that have enacted near-total post-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans do not have exceptions for rape or incest, a state of affairs that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/02/22/us/politics/kamala-harris-abortion-rights-michigan.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris has called \u8220\'20\'1Cimmoral\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a woman on the ticket and the first woman VP and a woman of color, and then secondly, as an AG, she is strongest when her profile is fighting and prosecuting the case. People really like her in that mode,\u8221\'20\'1D said Celinda Lake, a Democratic party strategist and a lead pollster on the 2020 Biden campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s so comfortable saying the word \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19. She\u8217\'20\'19s so comfortable leaning in and speaking to the repercussions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Emilys List, which first endorsed Harris 20 years ago when she was elected as San Francisco\u8217\'20\'19s district attorney, has previously committed to spending more than $10m on bolstering Harris in the 2024 elections, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/06/11/kamala-harris-emilys-list-pac-00101400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to reporting from Politico}}}\uc2  ; Jessica Mackler, the new president of Emilys List, said that nothing about their plan to support Harris had changed. \u8220\'20\'1CSupporting the vice-president is a huge part of our electoral priorities,\u8221\'20\'1D Mackler said.\par \par \uc2 Compared to his running mate, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s recent record on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is far more spotty. A devout Catholic, Biden has said that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot big\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and, in Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address, spoke at length about the procedure without ever referring to it by name. Instead, he talked of the importance of \u8220\'20\'1Creproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D and promised to \u8220\'20\'1Crestore Roe v Wade as the law of the land\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 When it comes to the Israel-Gaza war, Harris has begun to take a more visible role, and it appears that here, too, she may be pushing just beyond Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comfort zone.\par \par \uc2 NBC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/kamala-harris-gaza-speech-watered-down-cease-fire-rcna141750"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that the national security council toned down parts of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s Selma speech that were \u8220\'20\'1Charsher\u8221\'20\'1D on Israel. The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s office denied that her speech had been watered down.\par \par \uc2 On the Monday after her remarks, Harris met with \uc2 Benny Gantz\uc2 , a member of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war cabinet who had traveled to Washington against the wishes of the prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 . As she walked into the meeting, Harris denied that there was any daylight between her and the president on the conflict.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president and I have been aligned and consistent from the very beginning,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Many anti-war activists said Harris\u8217\'20\'19s remarks on Gaza were too little, too late. Yet others saw it as a sign of progress \u8211\'20\'13 that their pressure campaign was having an impact. Nearly 100,000 Democrats in Michigan voted uncommitted in the primary, which was held just days before her remarks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re feeling the pressure, and we want them to feel that pressure,\u8221\'20\'1D said Khalid Omar, who organized on behalf of the \u8220\'20\'1Cuncommitted\u8221\'20\'1D campaign in Minnesota. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want them to know that this is unacceptable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris\u8217\'20\'19s first joint campaign event of 2024, a rally in Virginia, was meant to focus on reproductive rights \u8211\'20\'13 but it was instead derailed by anger over the conflict in Gaza. After Harris and a Texas woman who had been denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  spoke about the importance of defending the procedure, Biden took the stage. He was almost immediately interrupted by a protester who yelled: \u8220\'20\'1CGenocide Joe, how many kids have you killed in Gaza?... Palestine is a feminist issue!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That protester was removed from the auditorium. Another soon cried out: \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael kills two mothers every hour!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Observers of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidency say the recent attention is recognition of the work she has been doing for months \u8211\'20\'13 both on domestic and foreign policy issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo the extent that she has found her voice, it\u8217\'20\'19s because people are finally listening,\u8221\'20\'1D said Donna Brazile, a Harris ally and veteran Democratic strategist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gufaculty360.georgetown.edu/s/contact/00336000014RiI2AAK/donna-brazile"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who teaches women\u8217\'20\'19s and gender studies at Georgetown University}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last month, Biden dispatched Harris again, this time to the Munich Security Conference, where her mission was to reassure American allies rattled by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on Nato. There she met with the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , and with \uc2 Yulia Navalnaya\uc2 , the wife of the Russian opposition leader \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 , hours after news broke of her husband\u8217\'20\'19s death in an Arctic penal camp.\par \par \uc2 Less than a week later, she was in Grand Rapids, Michigan, for a stop on her reproductive rights tour. While there, she made a surprise stop at the city\u8217\'20\'19s first Black woman-owned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.threads.net/@vp/post/C3sQ44YOozy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vinyl record shop}}}\uc2  and purchased a Miles Davis album from the owner, who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.threads.net/@vp/post/C3sQ44YOozy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thrilled by the visit}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 When the Tennessee legislature expelled two Black lawmakers, the White House sent Harris to Nashville, where she joined them in delivering an impassioned plea for gun control. In December, she traveled to Dubai for a \uc2 UN\uc2  climate summit, where she juggled wartime diplomacy \u8211\'20\'13 delivering at the time the sharpest commentary of any administration official on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 with climate policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHer vice-presidency has been significant both in terms of her spokesperson role and in terms of a number of significant and highly visible diplomatic assignments that President Biden has given her,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.slu.edu/law/faculty/joel-goldstein.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joel Goldstein}}}\uc2 , a historian of the US vice-presidency.\par \par \uc2 There is, however, another reason why scrutiny of Harris may be intensifying: her running mate\u8217\'20\'19s age.\par \par \uc2 If he wins a second term, Biden would turn 86 before leaving office. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/03/03/us/elections/times-siena-poll-registered-voter-crosstabs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times and Siena College}}}\uc2  survey found that 73% of registered voters believe Biden is \u8220\'20\'1Cjust too old\u8221\'20\'1D to be an effective president. The poll was conducted more than two weeks after a special counsel described him as a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/02/09/us/politics/biden-memory-age-democrats.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 well-meaning, elderly man with a poor memory}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdiminished faculties in advancing age\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe age of both Biden and Trump will focus more attention on the vice-presidential candidates,\u8221\'20\'1D Goldstein said.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have sought to leverage concerns about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s mental and physical health against Harris, casting her as an unsteady lieutenant ill-prepared to assume the presidency. In the weeks before dropping out of the Republican presidential primary, \uc2 Nikki Haley{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8JDyV4lHR68"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  that if Trump were to win the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination, he would lose to Biden, who would be unable to finish a second term, leading to a Harris presidency. The prospect, Haley said, \u8220\'20\'1Cshould send a chill up everyone\u8217\'20\'19s spine\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But Harris is leaning in to her leading role. After the State of the Union, she headed west to Arizona, the next stop on her reproductive rights tour. On Saturday she was scheduled to campaign with Latino organizers in battleground state Nevada.\par \par \uc2 To those who doubt whether the vice-president could step into the presidency, she is blunt.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m ready, if necessary,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told NBC News on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to be necessary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rachel Leingang contributed to this report from Minneapolis\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240309ek39001bb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
