\par\par \uc2 Society\par \b \uc2 US health secretary on Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s IVF ruling: \u8216\'20\'18Pandora\u8217\'20\'19s box was opened\u8217\'20\'19 after fall of Roe\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 1,053 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 March 2024\par 19:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2  says US must provide federal protections for reproductive rights if it hopes to avoid further restrictions\par \par \uc2 The health and human services secretary, \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , said the US must provide federal protections for reproductive rights if Americans hope to avoid further restrictions on in vitro fertilization, contraception and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an exclusive interview with the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Becerra\u8217\'20\'19s comments come in the wake of an Alabama supreme court decision that gave embryos the rights of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf#:~:text=In%20a%20first%2Dof%2Dits,Mobile%20fertility%20clinic%20to%20proceed."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and forced three of the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest fertility clinics to stop services for fear of litigation and prosecution. The fallout from the decision prompted the Alabama legislature to hastily sign new legislation that will give IVF providers with immunity from civil and criminal suits, which the governor signed into law on Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 He said the events in Alabama were linked directly to the \u8220\'20\'1Ctakedown\u8221\'20\'1D of Roe v Wade, a decision that provided a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  grounded in privacy and was overturned by conservative \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt wasn\u8217\'20\'19t until this new court came in\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that is, that three new supreme court justices were confirmed by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cthat we saw the attacks on Roe v Wade take hold, and today without Roe v Wade there are women who are trying to have babies in Alabama who are facing the consequences,\u8221\'20\'1D said Becerra.\par \par \uc2 He continued: \u8220\'20\'1CNone of this would be happening in Alabama on IVF if Roe v Wade was still the law of the land, and no one should try to deny that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Becerra\u8217\'20\'19s comments come ahead of Joe Biden addressing the nation in the State of the Union on Thursday night. Although the White House has not released the speech, a large number of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/4509630-state-union-address-guest-list/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic guests}}}\uc2  suggest reproductive rights may feature heavily.\par \par \uc2 Among the guests of high-ranking Democrats are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wbur.org/cognoscenti/2024/02/26/alabama-supreme-court-ruling-first-ivf-baby-elizabeth-carr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elizabeth Carr}}}\uc2 , the first person in the US to be born via IVF; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/07/texas-abortion-women-lawsuit-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amanda Zurawski}}}\uc2 , a Texas woman who nearly died of septic shock when she was denied a medically necessary \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/12/kate-cox-texas-abortion-case-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kate Cox}}}\uc2 , who had to flee Texas for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after she learned her fetus had a fatal chromosomal condition.\par \par \uc2 Also, sitting alongside First Lady Jill Biden as a guest of the president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/alabama-ivf-protection-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will be Latorya Beasley}}}\uc2 , from Birmingham, Alabama.\par \par \uc2 She and her husband had their first child, via IVF, in 2022. They were trying to have another child through IVF but Beasley\u8217\'20\'19s embryo transfer was suddenly canceled because of the Alabama court decision.\par \par \uc2 Beasley\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Crecent experience is yet another example of how the overturning of Roe v Wade has disrupted access to reproductive health care for women and families across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 More guests include reproductive endocrinologists, an Indiana doctor who provided an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a 10-year-old rape victim, and leaders of reproductive rights groups.\par \par \uc2 Becerra\u8217\'20\'19s comments emphasizing the importance of reproductive rights, Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 guest list for the State of the Union and a recent administration officials\u8217\'20\'19 trips to states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions are the most recent evidence of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/28/democrats-statehouse-races-campaign-spending"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 election bet}}}\uc2  : that when Republicans married the motivated minority of voters who support the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, they also divorced themselves from the broader American public, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/4507514-overwhelming-majority-americans-support-keeping-ivf-legal-for-women-poll/#:~:text=An%20overwhelming%20majority%20of%20Americans,it%20should%20not%20be%20legal."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broad margins of whom}}}\uc2  support IVF, contraception and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a result of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fall of Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 or actually the takedown of Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 my daughters have fewer rights in America than their mom did,\u8221\'20\'1D said Becerra. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that happens only when you have a supreme court that acts to overturn a constitutional protection.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Becerra said his agency would continue to enforce federal laws in Alabama, including laws that provide medical patients a right to privacy and the right to stabilizing emergency care, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/02/texas-emergency-abortions-ban-despite-federal-guidance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including emergency abortions}}}\uc2 , it is ultimately the courts in and politicians of Alabama who need to fix the upheaval their policies caused.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court in Alabama is the one that has to undo its wrongful decision,\u8221\'20\'1D said Becerra. \u8220\'20\'1CThe state legislature in Alabama should move to provide protections to families that rely on IVF \u8211\'20\'13 and serious comprehensive protections, not short-term, piecemeal protections that threaten anyone going through the process or any provider who wishes to provide quality IVF services.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although Alabama politicians have passed a bill to give IVF providers immunity from civil and criminal suits, national associations of fertility doctors have said the law does not go far enough to address the core problem \u8211\'20\'13 the supreme court \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/alabama-ivf-frozen-embryos-legislation-immunity-68d773d6ee89107c9a2e569110e7e31f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conflating fertilized eggs with children}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClearly, this goes way beyond \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Becerra. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would not surprise me if we also begin to see actions which undermine the ability of women to get basic family planning services,\u8221\'20\'1D including contraception.\par \par \uc2 While doctors and patients have reacted with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/23/fertility-doctors-reaction-alabama-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 astonishment, anger and sorrow}}}\uc2  at the Alabama supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement has cheered the decision. \u8220\'20\'1CFetal personhood\u8221\'20\'1D has long been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/21/us/abortion-anti-fetus-person.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the ultimate aim}}}\uc2  of the movement.\par \par \uc2 For years, Republicans have abetted this aim. As recently as 2023, 124 Republicans co-sponsored the federal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/431#:~:text=This%20bill%20declares%20that%20the,an%20individual%20comes%20into%20being."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Life at Conception Act}}}\uc2 , which would give embryos the rights of people \u8220\'20\'1Cat the moment of fertilization, cloning, or other moment when the individual comes into being\u8221\'20\'1D. This week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/06/kentucky-senate-child-support-unborn-children"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky Republicans}}}\uc2  advanced a bill to allow people to claim fetuses as dependents on their taxes.\par \par \uc2 They have also blocked federal legislation to protect IVF \u8211\'20\'13 twice. In late February, Senator Tammy Duckworth of Illinois introduced an IVF protection bill. Most recently, its expedited passage was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/28/senate-democrats-ivf-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked by the Republican}}}\uc2  senator \uc2 Cindy Hyde-Smith\uc2  of Mississippi (a state which, like Alabama, has a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban).\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, the Alabama decision has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/28/republicans-alabama-ivf-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 palpably uncomfortable}}}\uc2  for many members of the party. Trump has said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/tommy-tuberville-alabama-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he supports IVF}}}\uc2 , and views anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies as a threat to his campaign. Republicans such as Tommy Tuberville of Alabama and \uc2 Joni Ernst\uc2  of Iowa have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/29/alabama-embryo-ivf-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued awkward, noncommittal statements}}}\uc2  about the decision. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/senate-candidate-endorses_n_5997126"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ernst supported}}}\uc2  federal fetal personhood statutes in the past.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Roe v Wade was struck down by the Dobbs decision the Pandora\u8217\'20\'19s box was opened,\u8221\'20\'1D said Becerra. \u8220\'20\'1CNow, we see the consequences and how far the loss the protections of Roe go beyond \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240307ek37001s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
