\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Reproductive rights take center stage during Biden\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 642 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 March 2024\par 15:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden sought to capitalize on the passions stirred by GOP threats to reproductive freedom, while avoiding the word \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive rights took center stage at the 2024 State of the Union, as President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  sought to overcome concerns about his re-election chances by emphasizing an issue that has energized voters again and again since the overturning of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy predecessor took office determined to see Roe v Wade overturned and he brags about it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden, referring to former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his presumptive rival for the presidency. \u8220\'20\'1CLook at the chaos that has resulted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden has in large part pinned his hopes for re-election on the passions stirred by threats to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and, in particular, on his vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who has embarked on a nationwide tour to trumpet the threat to reproductive freedom posed by another Trump presidency. The demise of Roe, which was overturned with the help of three justices appointed by Trump, has led more than a dozen states to enact near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Many do not have exceptions for rape or incest, and doctors across the country have said that exceptions for cases of medical emergencies are unworkable in practice, prompting a stream of high-profile cases of women needing to flee their home states for life-saving medical care.\par \par \uc2 A number of guests attending this year\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address have ties to post-Roe disputes over reproductive rights that are now roiling the US. The first lady, Jill Biden, invited Kate Cox, a Texas woman who had to leave the state for an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as well as LaTorya Beasley, an Alabama woman whose in vitro fertilization treatment was halted after the state supreme court ruled that frozen embryos are \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes who believe life begins at fertilization have long worked to enshrine protections for embryos and fetuses into law \u8211\'20\'13 even though such rights can conflict with the rights of people carrying them.\par \par \uc2 Outrage over the overturning of Roe is credited with preventing a widely expected \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D of Republican victories in the 2022 midterms. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have also repeatedly won when the issue is put directly to voters in ballot referendums, including in traditionally red states such as Kansas, Ohio and Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 But during the segment of his address about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Biden did not actually utter the word, instead referring to \u8220\'20\'1Creproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D. Biden, a devout Catholic who has previously said he is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot big\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been criticized by reproductive rights advocates for shying away from using the word.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany of you in this chamber and my predecessor are promising to pass a national ban on reproductive freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy God, what freedoms will you take away next?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden singled out Beasley in his speech, urging members of Congress: \u8220\'20\'1CGuarantee the right to IVF. Guarantee it nationwide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last week, the Republican Tennessee senator \uc2 Cindy Hyde-Smith{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/28/senate-democrats-ivf-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked the passage}}}\uc2  of a bill by the Illinois senator Tammy Duckworth, a Democrat, to establish federal protections for IVF. On Thursday night, no Republicans appeared to stand in support of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plea for IVF, despite the fact that an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/03/03/americans-overwhelmingly-support-ivf-legal-women-poll-00144588"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelming majority}}}\uc2  of Americans support access to the treatment.\par \par \uc2 In his speech, Biden also quoted the supreme court majority opinion that overturned Roe. In the opinion, the supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  ruled that, in demolishing Roe, the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court was returning the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to state legislatures and female voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are not without electoral or political power,\u8221\'20\'1D Alito wrote. And, on Thursday night, Biden agreed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith all due respect, justices, women are not without electoral or political power,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re about to realize just how much.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240308ek38000m9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
