\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18My predecessor\u8217\'20\'19, hecklers, and lots of fire: key takeaways from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s state of the union address\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 1,037 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 March 2024\par 13:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The US president covered everything from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , from Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza, as well as the size of a Snickers barJoe Biden delivers feisty State of the Union address with vision for his second term\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  made a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/joe-biden-state-of-the-union-address"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forceful State of the Union address}}}\uc2  on Thursday, criticising former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over the January 6 insurrection, vowing to stand up to \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , urging Israel to play its part in the delivery of aid to Gaza, backing reproductive freedom and taking on rightwing antagonist \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  on immigration.\par \par \uc2 Here are some key takeaways from the speech.\par \par \uc2 He who shall not be named\par \par \uc2 Biden opened the speech with fiery denunciations of the rioters who stormed the Capitol on 6 January 2021, then singled out Republicans in the chamber and Trump. But he refused to utter Trump\u8217\'20\'19s name, saying that \u8220\'20\'1Cmy predecessor and some of you here seek to bury the truth about Jan 6.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He wrapped that into a larger theme that democracy is threatened like no time since the civil war, signalling a clear line of attack he will use against Trump.\par \par \uc2 He also criticised \u8220\'20\'1Cmy predecessor\u8221\'20\'1D for his assertion that Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  could \u8220\'20\'1Cdo whatever the hell he wants\u8221\'20\'1D with respect to Nato allies. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous, it\u8217\'20\'19s dangerous and it\u8217\'20\'19s unacceptable,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy message to President Putin, who I\u8217\'20\'19ve known for a long time, is simple: we will not walk away. I will not bow down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking with a vigour that his supporters have said has been lacking, he set up a contrast between his internationalist view of the world and the more isolationist leanings of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden v \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\par \par \uc2 One of the most striking moments of the night took place when Biden addressed the topic of immigration \u8211\'20\'13 which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/29/trump-biden-border-visits-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls show}}}\uc2  is a major weakness for the president going into the election against Trump.\par \par \uc2 As he spoke, the president was heckled by far-right Republican congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 . She demanded he say the name of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/01/university-of-georgia-laken-riley-murder-rightwing-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laken Riley}}}\uc2 , who is suspected to have been killed by an undocumented migrant.\par \par \uc2 Biden, who usually wants nothing to do with Greene, took her up on the offer. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened:\par \par \uc2 In unscripted moment, Biden holds up Laken Riley button that Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  (R-GA) gave him, using it as an opportunity to again call for the bipartisan border bill:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow many thousands of people being killed by illegals? \u8230\'20\'26 Get this bill done. We need to act now.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lkOzRF1Gd8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lkOzRF1Gd8}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1765941008414413294?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The age old question\par \par \uc2 When asked about his age and how it affects his ability to be president, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s stock answer is: watch me.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday night, he delivered what a lot of his own supporters had found wanting. It was a high-energy, forceful speech, and at times he taunted Republicans with ad-libs. When they heckled his support for bipartisan border security legislation, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CLook at the facts, I know you know how to read\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden leaned into his age, mentioning he was born during the second world war, but defended his vision for the country as fresh. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t lead America with ancient ideas that only take us back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden stumbled over a few words, and in the Republican response, Senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/katie-britt-alabama-biden-rebuttal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Katie Britt}}}\uc2  of Alabama called him \u8220\'20\'1Cdithering and diminished\u8221\'20\'1D but it was a more vigorous performance than other speeches where his remarks can be meandering or hard to hear.\par \par \uc2 Israel \u8216\'20\'18must do its part\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Biden announced plans for the US military to help {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/07/gaza-floating-port-aid-palestinians-impact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 establish a temporary pier}}}\uc2  on the coast of Gaza, an effort that the administration claims should significantly boost the flow of aid into the besieged territory.\par \par \uc2 But at the same time he said Israel \u8220\'20\'1Cmust also do its part\u8221\'20\'1D to alleviate suffering even as the \uc2 IDF\uc2  seeks to eliminate \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CTo the leadership of Israel I say this,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, \u8220\'20\'1CHumanitarian assistance cannot be a secondary consideration or a bargaining chip. Protecting and saving innocent lives has to be a priority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The unveiling of the plan was perhaps the most substantive element of his address that touched on the war. It allowed Biden to demonstrate that he\u8217\'20\'19s taking action in the face of anger and defiance from some Democrats over his strong support for Israel, even as the Palestinian death toll mounts.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ballot\par \par \uc2 The president said efforts to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  were an \u8220\'20\'1Cassault on freedom\u8221\'20\'1D, and he derided the supreme court ruling that overturned Roe v Wade, with members of that court seated just feet away.\par \par \uc2 He also welcomed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/biden-sotu-ivf-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kate Cox}}}\uc2 , a Dallas mother whose foetus had a fatal condition that put her own health at risk. She had to leave the state in order to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CMy God, what freedoms will you take away next?\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Through much of his career, Biden has not emphasised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. In his speech, he showed how much he believes that issue could be key to a second term.\par \par \uc2 Middle class Joe\par \par \uc2 Biden outlined an economic vision that went big and small. He touted a post-pandemic economic recovery that didn\u8217\'20\'19t sacrifice job creation in order to tame inflation. With housing prices still high, he proposed a tax credit that would reduce mortgage costs.\par \par \uc2 He also hammered Republicans for tax policies that favour the wealthy. \u8220\'20\'1CCheck the numbers. Folks at home, does anybody really think the tax code is fair?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden said there should be a minimum tax rate of 25% on billionaires, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cno billionaire should pay a lower federal tax rate than a teacher, a sanitation worker or a nurse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president talked about cracking down on junk fees or hidden charges that can chip away at Americans\u8217\'20\'19 budgets. He also criticised snack companies for \u8220\'20\'1Cshrinkflation,\u8221\'20\'1D or getting less product for the same price.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou get charged the same amount and you got about 10% fewer Snickers in it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With Associated Press\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240308ek3800232\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
