\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 State of the Union address as it happened: Biden spars with Republicans and announces aid pier for Gaza\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,123 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 March 2024\par 05:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US president makes last State of the Union address of this presidential term, with much at stake as he heads into re-election fight against Trump\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 In his third, and potentially last, State of the Union address, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  eschewed tradition and delivered a barrage of attacks on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who he only referred to as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea84398f087d93d3c5f827#block-65ea84398f087d93d3c5f827"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cmy predecessor\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . It was a sign of how Biden believes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s potential return to the White House poses an existential risk to American democracy, and perhaps also his awareness that he has a lot of support to rebuild to win a second term in November. While Democrats leapt to their feet for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s promises to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea805e8f087d93d3c5f810#block-65ea805e8f087d93d3c5f810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protect social security}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea7fb98f087d93d3c5f80e#block-65ea7fb98f087d93d3c5f80e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut child poverty}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea7b978f087d93d3c5f7ea#block-65ea7b978f087d93d3c5f7ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overhaul the country\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure}}}\uc2 , some found the president\u8217\'20\'19s use of the word {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea81b08f088169d35941b7#block-65ea81b08f088169d35941b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  objectionable. Meanwhile, Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator Katie Britt delivered the party\u8217\'20\'19s rebuttal, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea8f8c8f088169d3594211#block-65ea8f8c8f088169d3594211"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asking}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CAre you better off now than you were three years ago?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here are the highlights:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The 81-year-old president{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea87258f087d93d3c5f840#block-65ea87258f087d93d3c5f840"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 directly addressed}}}\uc2  his age, saying \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been told I\u8217\'20\'19m too old\u8221\'20\'1D while arguing he is still up for the job.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , a rightwing nemesis, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea76288f088169d3594167#block-65ea76288f088169d3594167"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 got unusually close}}}\uc2  to Biden, then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea89598f088169d35941e0#block-65ea89598f088169d35941e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heckled him}}}\uc2  during the speech over the murder of Georgia nursing student Laken Riley.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Six supreme court justices were present at the speech, only for Biden to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea7d208f08480e4918b79f#block-65ea7d208f08480e4918b79f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticize them directly}}}\uc2  for overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Protesters upset over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea70178f087d93d3c5f79a#block-65ea70178f087d93d3c5f79a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked a road}}}\uc2  leading to the Capitol ahead of the speech.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 George Santos was in the House chamber for the speech, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/mar/07/biden-state-of-the-union-updates?page=with:block-65ea718b8f08480e4918b74b#block-65ea718b8f08480e4918b74b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  to hang out with the people who removed him from office.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 House Democrats rankled by Biden's use of 'illegal' to describe murder suspect\par \par \uc2 Several Democratic House lawmakers have criticized \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for describing the undocumented migrant suspected of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/01/university-of-georgia-laken-riley-murder-rightwing-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 murdering Georgia nursing student }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/01/university-of-georgia-laken-riley-murder-rightwing-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laken Riley}}}\uc2  as an \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden made the remark during his State of the Union address, while being heckled by rightwing lawmaker \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , who blamed the president\u8217\'20\'19s border security policies for Riley\u8217\'20\'19s murder. Biden held up a pin with Riley\u8217\'20\'19s name on it, and called her \u8220\'20\'1Can innocent young woman who was killed by an illegal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Democrats took issue with that terminology, including Illinois\u8217\'20\'19s Chuy Garcia :\par \par \uc2 enltrAs a proud immigrant, I'm extremely disappointed to hear President Biden use the word "illegal."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congressman Chuy Garc\u237\'00\'EDa (@RepChuyGarcia) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepChuyGarcia/status/1765950131159859281?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  of Minnesota:\par \par \uc2 enltrLet me be clear: No human being is illegal.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  (@IlhanMN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IlhanMN/status/1765953197653279023?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And Delia Ramirez of Illinois:\par \par \uc2 enltrNo human being is illegal.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congresswoman Delia Ramirez (@repdeliaramirez) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/repdeliaramirez/status/1765938180157546887?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust ask yourself, are you better off now than you were three years ago?\u8221\'20\'1D Katie Britt asks in the Republican rebuttal to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address.\par \par \uc2 Expect that to be a theme of GOP campaigns nationwide, including \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 More, from Britt:\par \par \uc2 Look, we all recall when presidents faced national security threats with strength and resolve. That seems like ancient history right now. Our commander-in-chief is not in command. The free world deserves better than a doddering and diminished leader. America deserves leaders who recognize that secure borders, stable prices, safe streets and a strong defense are actually the cornerstones of a great nation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Alabama senator Katie Britt is delivering the Republican rebuttal to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address, and responded to his comments on Laken Riley.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight, President Biden finally said her name, but he refused to take responsibility for his own actions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Britt.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr President, enough is enough. Innocent Americans are dying and you only have yourself to blame. Fulfill your oath of office, reverse your policies, end this crisis and stop the suffering.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 One of the most striking moments of the night happened when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  addressed the topic of immigration \u8211\'20\'13 which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/29/trump-biden-border-visits-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls show}}}\uc2  is a major weakness of his going into the November contest against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As he spoke, the president was heckled by \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , a rightwing antagonist. Greene demanded he say the name of Laken Riley, who is suspected to have been murdered by an undocumented migrant.\par \par \uc2 Biden, who usually wants nothing to do with Greene, took her up on the offer. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn unscripted moment, Biden holds up Laken Riley button that Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  (R-GA) gave him, using it as an opportunity to again call for the bipartisan border bill:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow many thousands of people being killed by illegals? \u8230\'20\'26 Get this bill done. We need to act now.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lkOzRF1Gd8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lkOzRF1Gd8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1765941008414413294?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 During \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech, there were several rowdy heckles from \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and others. Then came an unexpected yell from the public balcony, directly opposite from where I am sitting in the press gallery.\par \par \uc2 A man wearing dark suit, blue shirt and yellow tie cupped his hands and shouted: \u8220\'20\'1CRemember Abbey Gate! United States Marines.\u8221\'20\'1D Abbey Gate, outside Kabul\u8217\'20\'19s airport, is where 13 US service members were killed during the withdrawal from Afghanistan two years ago.\par \par \uc2 His point made, the man voluntarily left before security yanked him out. Biden did not seem thrown off by the interruption as he carried on speaking. But the episode was a reminder that his approval rating has never quite recovered from the chaos in Kabul.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden directly addresses advanced age as he concludes State of the Union\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  rarely discusses his age, but did so directly as he closed his State of the Union address.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been told I\u8217\'20\'19m too old,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, continuing:\par \par \uc2 Whether young or old \u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19ve always known what endures. I\u8217\'20\'19ve known our north star, the very idea of Americans, that we\u8217\'20\'19re all created equal, deserve to be treated equally throughout our lives. We\u8217\'20\'19ve never fully lived up to that idea. We\u8217\'20\'19ve never walked away from it either. And I won\u8217\'20\'19t walk away from it now.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know it may not look like it, but I\u8217\'20\'19ve been around a while,\u8221\'20\'1D said the 81-year-old president, the oldest to ever hold the job.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou get to be my age, certain things become clearer than ever,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden continued. \u8220\'20\'1CI know the American story. Again and again, I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen the contrast between competing forces in the battle for the soul of our nation, between those who want to pull America back to the past and those who want to move America into the future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden appears to be wrapping up, in high spirits.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet me close with this,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, to sardonic applause.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know you don\u8217\'20\'19t want to hear any more, Lindsey. But I gotta say a few more things,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. He was presumably talking to South Carolina Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  discussed the war in Gaza, two progressive House Democrats sitting in the audience staged a minor protest.\par \par \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  and \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  remained sitting and held up signs that read: \u8220\'20\'1CLasting ceasefire now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden announces 'temporary pier' off Gaza coast to deliver humanitarian aid\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just announced the US military would build a pier off Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s coast to facilitate aid deliveries, and said no American soldiers would set foot in the enclave besieged by Israel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight, I\u8217\'20\'19m directing the US military to lead an emergency mission to establish a temporary pier in the Mediterranean on the coast of Gaza that can receive large shipments carrying food, water, medicine and temporary shelter,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo US boots will be on the ground. A temporary pier will enable a massive increase in the amount of humanitarian assistance getting into the Gaza every day \u8230\'20\'26 Israel must allow more aid into Gaza and ensure humanitarian workers aren\u8217\'20\'19t caught in the crossfire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 The words \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D have not passed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lips since he began this speech, but he has repeatedly referenced \u8220\'20\'1Cmy predecessor\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The most recent moment came when he discussed gun control and mass shootings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy predecessor told the \uc2 NRA\uc2  he\u8217\'20\'19s proud he did nothing on guns when he was president. After another shooting in Iowa recently, he said, when asked what to do about it, he said, \u8216\'20\'18just get over it.\u8217\'20\'19 There\u8217\'20\'19s his quote: \u8216\'20\'18Just get over it,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI say stop it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 A protester was just removed from the House gallery.\par \par \uc2 The man started yelling at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as he was addressing murder rates. It was hard to hear what he was saying, but it sounded like something about the marine corps.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  then sparred with Republicans over immigration reform, after the party {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/07/us-senate-vote-bipartisan-border-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed}}}\uc2  a bipartisan compromise to tie tighter border policies to aid to Ukraine and Israel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m told my predecessor called members of Congress in the Senate to demand they block the bill,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 But he appeared to lose his train of thought, and picked up a pin, worn by rightwing lawmaker \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , with the name Laken Riley, a Georgia woman suspected to have been killed by an undocumented immigrant.\par \par \uc2 He called Riley \u8220\'20\'1Can innocent young woman who was killed by an illegal\u8221\'20\'1D but then flubbed his next few words.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden then appeared to lure Republicans into a trap.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have two ways to go: Republicans can cut social security and give more tax breaks to the wealthy,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. But before he could continue, the GOP erupted into jeers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, that\u8217\'20\'19s the proposal,\u8221\'20\'1D the president countered. \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys don\u8217\'20\'19t want another $2tn tax cut? I kind of thought that\u8217\'20\'19s what your plan was. Good to hear you\u8217\'20\'19re not gonna cut another $2tn for the super wealthy. That\u8217\'20\'19s good to hear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Would it be a Democratic president\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union without an accusation that Republicans want to cut social security and Medicare? Nope!\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany of my friends on the other side of the aisle want to put social security on the chopping block,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf anyone here tries to cut social security, Medicare or raise the retirement age, I will stop you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  threw his weight behind a long-running push to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/31/house-child-tax-credit-business-tax-break-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restore a tax credit}}}\uc2  that is seen as crucial to lowering child poverty.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe child tax credit I passed during the pandemic cut taxes for millions of working families and cut child poverty in half,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. He then boomed:\par \par \uc2 Restore the tax credit! No child should go hungry in this country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 While voters haven\u8217\'20\'19t responded well to \u8220\'20\'1CBidenomics\u8221\'20\'1D, there have been multiple polls to show they do support \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policies on capping prescription drug costs and changes to Medicare pricing in a country where health care burdens run many families into debt.\par \par \uc2 Biden seems to have recognized that he must go beyond saying the economy is strong and that inflation is down and took a significant amount of time to talk about his actions to limit health costs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Affordable Care Act, old Obamacare, is still a very big deal,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1COver 100 million of you can no longer be denied health insurance because of a pre-existing condition. But my predecessor and many in this chamber want to take that protection away by repealing the Affordable Care Act. I won\u8217\'20\'19t let that happen. We stopped you 50 times before, and we will stop you again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did not hold back on criticizing the overturning of Roe v Wade, addressing his remarks directly to the justices who were in the room.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith all due respect, justices, women are not without \u8230\'20\'26 electoral or political power,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hit out at Republicans who voted against legislation he championed to revitalize the nation\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure, but nonetheless accepted the money it authorized.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd by the way, I noticed some of you have strongly voted against it but they\u8217\'20\'19re cheering on that money coming in,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said to applause, presumably from Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you don\u8217\'20\'19t want that money in your district, just let me know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden took a moment to recognize the pandemic \u8211\'20\'13 the lives lost and the social isolation.\par \par \uc2 He accused \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of not caring - to which someone from the audience shouted \u8220\'20\'1CLies!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now hitting out at the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 2022 decision overturning Roe v Wade, and vowing to codify the former precedent into law, if re-elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the American people send me a Congress that supports the right to choose, I promise you I will restore Roe v Wade as the law of the land again,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet secretaries stood and applauded at that line. The six supreme court justices in the room \u8211\'20\'13 two of whom voted to overturn Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 sat stonefaced.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden accuses Trump, Republicans of trying 'to bury the truth about January 6'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wasn\u8217\'20\'19t done with his attacks on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies, bringing up the January 6 attack and accusing them of trying to cover it up:\par \par \uc2 History watched three years ago on January 6 when insurrectionists stormed this very capitol and placed a dagger to the throat of American democracy. Many of you were here on that darkest of days, we all saw with our own eyes. The insurrectionists were not patriots \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19d come to stop the peaceful transfer of power, to overturn the will of the people. January 6 lies about the 2020 election and the plots to steal the election posed a great gravest threat to US democracy since the cvil war. But they fail.\par \par \uc2 He concluded:\par \par \uc2 Our predecessor and some of you here seek to bury the truth about January 6. I will not do that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden attacks Trump for blocking Ukraine aid\par \par \uc2 Minutes into his speech, the first point the president landed on was this: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is to blame for Congress\u8217\'20\'19s failure to pass more aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUkraine is being blocked by those who want to walk away from our world leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a long ago when a Republican president named \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  thundered, \u8216\'20\'18Mr. Gorbachev, tear down this wall.\u8217\'20\'19 Now, my predecessor, a former Republican president, tells Putin: \u8216\'20\'18Do whatever the hell you want.\u8217\'20\'19 That\u8217\'20\'19s a quote. A former president actually said that, bowing down to a Russian leader. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous, is dangerous and it\u8217\'20\'19s unacceptable.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  began by comparing the moment to one faced by Democratic president \uc2 Franklin Roosevelt\uc2  in 1941, when Adolf Hitler was on the march in Europe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, it\u8217\'20\'19s we who face an unprecedented moment in history, the union and yes, my purpose tonight is to wake up the Congress, alert the American people, that this is no ordinary moment either,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden begins State of the Union address\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has climbed the House dais to begin his third State of the Union address, and the last of his first term \u8211\'20\'13 and potentially his presidency.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll cover it live.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 The education secretary, \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2 , is not attending tonight\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address because he is the designated survivor, a White House official confirmed.\par \par \uc2 That means he stays in a secure location in case something happens to the president and leaders of the legislative and judicial branches during tonight\u8217\'20\'19s speech.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  appeared to have a brief encounter with one of his biggest antagonists: \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Georgia Republican congresswoman was decked out in a red Maga hat, and appeared to tell Biden, \u8220\'20\'1CSay her name, Mr President,\u8221\'20\'1D in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1765890655631425548"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reference}}}\uc2  to the murder of Laken Riley, a 22-year-old nursing student in the state. After she said that, Biden turned away.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have seized on Riley\u8217\'20\'19s death to attack the president\u8217\'20\'19s handling of migrant arrivals on the southern border, because the suspect in her murder was in the country illegally. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/01/university-of-georgia-laken-riley-murder-rightwing-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A young woman\u8217\'20\'19s killing in Georgia stokes a familiar rightwing war}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden enters House chamber to deliver State of the Union address\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now walking into the House of Representatives chamber ahead of his State of the Union address.\par \par \uc2 This will be the third such speech he has given since taking office in 2021, and the last before the November elections, when voters will decide whether to give Biden another four years in the White House, or replace him with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The president is making his way down a line of guests and members of Congress, shaking hands and speaking to them. The Democratic Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , is right behind him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 The vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and the Republican House speaker, Mike Johnson, have been getting to know each other as they wait on the House dais for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s arrival.\par \par \uc2 As CSPAN points out, Johnson is the third House speaker Harris has had the chance to socialize with since taking office. The first was her Democratic buddy \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  back in 2022, when Biden\u8217\'20\'19s allies controlled the House. The following year, Republicans took the majority and it was Republican Kevin McCarthy \u8211\'20\'13 but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/03/kevin-mccarthy-oust-republican-house-speaker-vote-result-matt-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 we all know what happened to him}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now it\u8217\'20\'19s Johnson:\par \par \uc2 enltrVice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has been seated next to a different Speaker of the House for each State of the Union address. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SOTU?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SOTU}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SOTU2024?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SOTU2024}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0AN6DAkLAN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0AN6DAkLAN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jeremy Art\uc2  (@cspanJeremy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspanJeremy/status/1765915690593124760?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 For some reason, expelled former Republican congressman George Santos has returned to watch the State of the Union from the House floor:\par \par \uc2 Axios reports he wanted to hang out with the lawmakers who voted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/01/george-santos-expelled-congress-vote#:~:text=Robert%20Reich%2C%20a%20Berkeley%20professor,the%20entire%20House%20GOP%20leadership."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to remove him from office}}}\uc2  last year for being a big-time liar:\par \par \uc2 enltr???? Scooplet: George Santos is coming to the State of the Union and plans to sit on the House floor among former colleagues who voted to expel him\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kadia Goba (@kadiagoba) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kadiagoba/status/1765885833918259243?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s drive from the White House to the Capitol was complicated by demonstrators who blocked roads to protest his support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza:\par \par \uc2 Biden was able to make it to the Capitol via an alternate route.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Hours before his State of the Union address, it emerged \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will announce the creation of a temporary port on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  shoreline to be built by US forces.\par \par \uc2 Biden will say the port will be built in the next few weeks to allow delivery of humanitarian aid on a large scale, amid warnings of a widespread famine among the territory\u8217\'20\'19s 2.3 million Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not waiting on the Israelis. This is a moment for American leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D a senior US official said on Thursday, reflecting growing frustration of what is seen in Washington as Israeli obstruction of ground deliveries of aid on a substantial scale.\par \par \uc2 The port will be built by US military engineers operating from ships off the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  coast, who will not need to step ashore, US officials said. The aid deliveries will be shipped from the port of Larnaca in Cyprus, which will become the main relief hub.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 An Alabama mother who saw a second round of IVF canceled after the state supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled that embryos were children}}}\uc2  will attend \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address on Thursday, as guests of the first lady, Jill Biden.\par \par \uc2 La Torya Beasley of Birmingham, Alabama, is among the first lady\u8217\'20\'19s 20 invited guests who \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonify issues or themes to be addressed by the president in his speech\u8221\'20\'1D, the White House said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Also among the guests of high-ranking Democrats are Elizabeth Carr, the first person in the US to be born via IVF; Amanda Zurawski, a Texas woman who nearly died of septic shock when she was denied a medically necessary \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; and Kate Cox, who had to flee Texas for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after she learned her fetus had a fatal chromosomal condition.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic women wear white to State of the Union in show of support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 As lawmakers and officials file into the chamber of the House of Representatives, a notable fashion trend has emerged.\par \par \uc2 Many female lawmakers are wearing white, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not an accident. The Democratic Women\u8217\'20\'19s Caucus says its members have donned the color along with pins reading \u8220\'20\'1CFighting for Reproductive Freedom\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur message is clear: women must be able to access the health care they need to control their own lives and futures. That means women, not politicians, should be in charge of whether, when, and how to start or grow their families. That includes access to birth control, access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and access to IVF,\u8221\'20\'1D the caucus chair Lois Frankel said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 Who is Katie Britt? Alabama senator to deliver Republican State of the Union rebuttal\par \par \uc2 The GOP has chosen first-term Alabama senator Katie Britt, the youngest Republican woman ever to serve in the Senate, to deliver the rebuttal to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-the-union-address"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 State of the Union address}}}\uc2  tonight.\par \par \uc2 At 42, Britt is also the third-youngest senator currently serving, presenting a counterpoint to the oldest sitting president.\par \par \uc2 Her rebuttal will come on the heels of a high-stakes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/29/alabama-embryo-ivf-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political showdown}}}\uc2  over women\u8217\'20\'19s access to in vitro fertilization in her home state.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/george-chidi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Chidi}}}\uc2  has written more about Britt here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/katie-britt-alabama-biden-rebuttal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who is Katie Britt? Alabama senator to deliver rebuttal to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 What to watch for\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will likely portray this election as he did in 2020: a contest between democracy and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , whose authoritarian rhetoric has escalated since he lost the 2020 election to Biden.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear how Biden will position himself on foreign policy. His administration faces mounting pressure from the right to abandon its support for Ukraine, which for more than two years has been fighting a Russian ground invasion. And he faces calls from a progressive anti-war movement to push for a ceasefire in Gaza, where more than 30,000 Palestinians have been killed by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military campaign. During his speech, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/world/2024/mar/07/biden-us-port-gaza-aid-delivery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden is expected to announce}}}\uc2  the creation of a port on the coast of Gaza to deliver more aid to the besieged enclave.\par \par \uc2 A week ago, Biden and Trump made dueling visits to the US-Mexico border, underscoring the centrality of immigration policy to the 2024 race \u8211\'20\'13 and the shift to the right that Biden and other Democratic politicians have made on the issue. During his speech in Brownsville, Texas, Biden called on Trump to support the bipartisan bill to restrict immigration on the southern border, which is languishing in Congress. How, and if, Biden speaks about immigration will be a prelude to his approach during the months ahead on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 This speech will also offer Biden an opportunity to address \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, an issue that has mobilized Democratic voters since the supreme court decision protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, Roe v Wade, was overturned. An Alabama supreme court decision in February ruling that frozen embryos can be considered children under state law \u8211\'20\'13 which has led to threats to access to in vitro fertilization there \u8211\'20\'13 brought concerns about reproductive healthcare access back to the fore. Biden has expressed his personal misgivings about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on religious grounds, but has defended Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 How to watch the State of the Union address\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address is scheduled to begin at 9pm ET/6pm PT tonight, 7 March, and will be broadcast on the major news networks, including ABC, NBC, \uc2 CBS\uc2  and FOX.\par \par \uc2 It will also be carried {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/sotu2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by CSPAN}}}\uc2  and streamed live {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/state-of-the-union-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on the White House website}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 'I promise you: I will restore Roe v Wade as the law of the land': Biden to vow at State of the Union\par \par \uc2 Democrats have tried and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/11/senate-abortion-rights-bill-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed}}}\uc2  to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights federally ever since it became clear the supreme court would overturn Roe v Wade, as it did in 2022. The party never had the votes, but at this evening\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address, Biden will make clear it would be a priority, if re-elected:\par \par \uc2 In its decision to overturn Roe v Wade the Supreme Court majority wrote \u8216\'20\'18Women are not without electoral or political power.\u8217\'20\'19 No kidding. Clearly those bragging about overturning Roe v Wade have no clue about the power of women in America. But they found out when reproductive freedom was on the ballot and won in 2022, 2023, and they will find out again in 2024. If Americans send me a Congress that supports the right to choose I promise you: I will restore Roe v Wade as the law of the land again.\par \par \uc2 He will also attempt to persuade Americans that the economy is doing all right:\par \par \uc2 I came to office determined to get us through one of the toughest periods in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history. And we have. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make the news, but in thousands of cities and towns the American people are writing the greatest comeback story never told. So let\u8217\'20\'19s tell that story here and now. America\u8217\'20\'19s comeback is building a future of American possibilities, building an economy from the middle out and the bottom up \u8211\'20\'13 not the top down, investing in all of America \u8211\'20\'13 in all Americans \u8211\'20\'13 to make sure everyone has a fair shot and we leave no one behind.\par \par \uc2 Biden may at some point choose to call out Trump by name, but from what the White House has released, he\u8217\'20\'19s only referring to him obliquely \u8211\'20\'13 and pointing out that they are not far apart in age. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the line:\par \par \uc2 My lifetime has taught me to embrace freedom and democracy. A future based on the core values that have defined America: honesty, decency, dignity, equality. To respect everyone. To give everyone a fair shot. To give hate no safe harbor. Now some other people my age see a different story: an American story of resentment, revenge, and retribution. That\u8217\'20\'19s not me.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at center of last State of the Union address before November elections\par \par \uc2 Good evening, US politics blog readers. Tonight at 9pm ET, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver what could be the most important speech of his presidency: the last State of the Union address before he faces \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the November presidential elections. The annual speech is an important one for any president, but carries extra weight for Biden because it is a major opportunity to reengage with voters who have drifted away from him over the past three years but will be crucial in defeating Trump. Democrats are jittery over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/04/biden-new-yorker-interview-trump-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 persistently bad poll numbers}}}\uc2 , which for more than two and a half years have defied anything the president does to turn the situation around. His campaign believes the struggle for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is key to turning the situation around \u8211\'20\'13 among the promises the president will make tonight is a pledge to codify Roe v Wade if re-elected with Democratic majorities in Congress, the White House says.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we are watching for this evening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The president has not shied away from attacking Trump as a threat to democracy in speeches since the start of the year, but this evening he\u8217\'20\'19ll be in a room full of Republican lawmakers loyal to the former president. Will he bash him in front of them?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rightwing lawmakers like \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  have made names for themselves by heckling Biden at prior State of the Union addresses. Will they repeat the act tonight?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age has been a concern among voters and even some Democrats who worry the 81-year-old isn\u8217\'20\'19t up to another four years in office. Will he address the touchy issue?\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240308ek380008f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
