\par\par \uc2 Society\par \b \uc2 State of the Union guest list shows reproductive rights in spotlight after Alabama IVF bill signed into law \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now); Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 5,603 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 March 2024\par 21:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Guests at Biden address to include Alabama woman whose IVF was cancelled, and Texas women who went through \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordealsUS Fall of Roe \u8216\'20\'18opened Pandora\u8217\'20\'19s box\u8217\'20\'19 for IVF, says US health secretary\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 My colleague Chris Stein will be covering \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address this evening on our dedicated live blog. In the meantime, here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 LaTorya Beasley, an Alabama mother who saw a second round of IVF canceled after the state supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled that embryos were children}}}\uc2 , and Kate Cox, the Texas mother {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65e9df438f082c67eb9c00a3#block-65e9df438f082c67eb9c00a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forced to travel }}}\uc2  outside her state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are among those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/biden-sotu-ivf-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to attend}}}\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address tonight, as guests of the first lady, Jill Biden.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65e9f51e8f08480e4918b22f#block-65e9f51e8f08480e4918b22f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announce}}}\uc2  in the State of the Union speech that US forces will build a temporary port on the Gaza shoreline in the next few weeks to allow delivery of humanitarian aid on a large scale.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65e9fbd48f087d93d3c5f2f0#block-65e9fbd48f087d93d3c5f2f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 welcomed}}}\uc2 Sweden into Nato in a statement after the country {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/07/sweden-joins-nato-after-ratification-hungary-drops-opposition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 officially became}}}\uc2  the 32nd member of the western military alliance. The Swedish prime minister, \uc2 Ulf Kristersson\uc2 , will be attending the State of the Union address tonight.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Katie Boyd Britt, a first-term 42-year-old Republican senator from Alabama, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65ea217d8f088169d3593e86#block-65ea217d8f088169d3593e86"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will deliver}}}\uc2  the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s official response to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address tonight \u8211\'20\'13 a move likely designed to highlight the big age gap between the two.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Byron Donalds, a Republican Florida congressman being floated as a possible vice presidential pick for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65ea26e18f088169d3593ecd#block-65ea26e18f088169d3593ecd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested}}}\uc2  he would be willing to decline to certify the 2028 election results if he was vice president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 No Labels, the third-party presidential movement, will reportedly to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65ea19f28f087d93d3c5f4ba#block-65ea19f28f087d93d3c5f4ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announce}}}\uc2  on Friday that it will move forward with a presidential bid in the November election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign described a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65ea0fa98f087d93d3c5f427#block-65ea0fa98f087d93d3c5f427"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new ad}}}\uc2  from a pro-Trump Super Pac questioning whether Biden can \u8220\'20\'1Ceven survive til 2029\u8221\'20\'1D as \u8220\'20\'1Ca sick and deranged stunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , the Republican former governor of Maryland who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/09/larry-hogan-republican-maryland-launches-senate-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  is running}}}\uc2  for Senate, has said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65e9f73b8f088169d3593c36#block-65e9f73b8f088169d3593c36"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would not }}}\uc2  vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the November election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Daniel Rodimer, a former pro wrestler who won a prominent endorsement from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  while unsuccessfully running for Congress in Nevada, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/daniel-rodimer-arrest-murder"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surrendered}}}\uc2  to authorities on Wednesday on an arrest warrant for murder.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican Florida congressman Byron Donalds became the latest vice-presidential contender to refuse to commit to certifying election results.\par \par \uc2 Donalds, at an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/03/07/byron-donalds-certifying-election-results-trump-vp?utm_campaign=editorial&utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Axios}}}\uc2  event, suggested he would be willing to decline to certify the 2028 election results if he was vice president. He also did not clarify if he would have certified the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 Donalds is one of the names being floated as a possible vice presidential pick for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . When asked if he would certify the 2028 results as vice president, he replied:\par \par \uc2 If you have state officials who are violating the election law in their states... then no, I would not.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he agreed with former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s move to certify the results, Donalds said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou can only ask that question of \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans have chosen Katie Boyd Britt, a first-term senator from Alabama, to deliver the party\u8217\'20\'19s official response to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address tonight \u8211\'20\'13 a move likely designed to highlight the big age gap between the two.\par \par \uc2 Britt, 42, is one of nine women in the Senate Republican conference and the youngest female Republican elected to the Senate.\par \par \uc2 In a statement announcing her speech, she said it was time for the next generation of American politicians \u8220\'20\'1Cto step up\u8221\'20\'1D. She added:\par \par \uc2 The Republican Party is the party of hardworking parents and families, and I\u8217\'20\'19m looking forward to putting this critical perspective front and center.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Republican Party is the party of hardworking parents and families, and I\u8217\'20\'19m looking forward to bringing this critical perspective front and center on March 7.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s time for the next generation to step up and preserve the American Dream for our children and our grandchildren. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QwImnQn21P"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QwImnQn21P}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Katie Britt (@KatieBrittforAL) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KatieBrittforAL/status/1763295406409044346?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans say she will offer a split screen of sorts when she delivers the party\u8217\'20\'19s rebuttal to the State of the Union address by Biden, 81.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s young, female and full of energy \u8211\'20\'13 opposite of everything \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is,\u8221\'20\'1D senator \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2  told the Hill. \u8220\'20\'1CThe contrast between the two, it\u8217\'20\'19s so different.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 No Labels to move ahead with US presidential bid \u8211\'20\'13 reports\par \par \uc2 The third-party presidential movement No Labels is expected to announce it will move forward with a presidential bid in the November election, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 About 800 No Labels delegates are expected to meet virtually in a private meeting and vote on Friday in favor of launching a presidential campaign for this fall\u8217\'20\'19s election, sources told AP and Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The group will not name its presidential and vice presidential picks on Friday, but instead it is expected to roll out a formal selection process late next week for potential candidates who would be selected in the coming weeks, the people said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The House passed a bill that would require federal authorities to detain any migrant charged with theft or burglary, named after a Georgia nursing student police have said was killed by a man who entered the US illegally.\par \par \uc2 The measure, called the Laken Riley Act, requires immigrations and customs enforcement to detain undocumented immigrants accused by local authorities of theft, burglary, larceny or shoplifting.\par \par \uc2 The bill would also allow states and individuals to sue the federal government for crimes committed by immigrants who enter the country illegally.\par \par \uc2 The bill was named after 22-year-old Laken Riley, who was killed on the campus of the University of Georgia while on a morning run last month. Riley\u8217\'20\'19s death has become a rallying point for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , after authorities arrested a Venezuelan man who entered the US illegally and was allowed to stay to pursue his immigration case.\par \par \uc2 The House approved the legislation hours before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is set to deliver his State of the Union address. Republicans have seized on Riley\u8217\'20\'19s death to hammer the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s border policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans will not stand for the release of dangerous criminals into our communities, and that\u8217\'20\'19s exactly what the Biden administration has done,\u8221\'20\'1D Republican House Speaker Mike Johnson told Fox News.\par \par \uc2 Laken is just one of the tragic examples of innocent American citizens who have lost their lives, been brutally and violently attacked by illegal criminals who are roaming our streets.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign has responded to a new ad from a pro-Trump Super Pac questioning Biden\u8217\'20\'19s ability to serve a second term in a new TV ad and whether the president can \u8220\'20\'1Ceven survive til 2029.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The ad, by Make America Great Again Inc, shows a clip from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s press conference after the death of Russian opposition leader \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During the briefing, Biden spoke about comments by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  about letting Russia \u8220\'20\'1Cdo whatever the hell they want\u8221\'20\'1D to Nato allies. Pausing for dramatic effect, Biden then says he should clear his mind \u8220\'20\'1Cand not say what I\u8217\'20\'19m really thinking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the Maga Inc ad, a narrator says: \u8220\'20\'1CWe can all see \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s weakness. If Biden wins, can he even survive to 2029. The real question is, can we?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrIf Biden wins, can he even survive till 2029? The real question is, can we? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nFZGuC3l1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2nFZGuC3l1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MAGA War Room (@MAGAIncWarRoom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MAGAIncWarRoom/status/1765707955574366567?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign spokesperson Ammar Moussa told NBC News that the ad is \u8220\'20\'1Ca sick and deranged stunt from a broke and struggling campaign\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 Trump tried this strategy four years ago and got his ass kicked by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 he should tune in tonight alongside tens of millions of Americans to see why President Biden will beat him again this November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A former congressional candidate backed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been arrested for murder.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Ramon Antonio Vargas reports:\par \par \uc2 A former pro wrestler who won a prominent endorsement from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  while unsuccessfully running for Congress in Nevada surrendered to authorities on Wednesday on an arrest warrant for murder.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Rodimer, 45, was booked in connection with the slaying of 47-year-old Christopher Tapp, who was reportedly beaten to death in Resorts World Las Vegas on 29 October.\par \par \uc2 Rodimer met Tapp \u8211\'20\'13 who was once charged with murder himself \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cthrough the classic car and racing circuit\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the local television news station {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.8newsnow.com/investigators/ex-congressional-candidate-wanted-in-las-vegas-strip-murder/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 KLAS}}}\uc2 , which reviewed police documents.\par \par \uc2 Investigators allege that Rodimer fatally attacked Tapp after he offered Rodimer\u8217\'20\'19s stepdaughter cocaine during a hotel room party.\par \par \uc2 Initially, authorities believed Tapp\u8217\'20\'19s death stemmed from a drug overdose and a fall, after an autopsy found evidence of blunt trauma and cocaine use. But detectives later determined Tapp had been in a fight inside the hotel room where he was found injured. He died later at a hospital.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/daniel-rodimer-arrest-murder"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump-backed former congressional candidate arrested for murder}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is a video of Maryland\u8217\'20\'19s former Republican governor \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who we reported about earlier \u8211\'20\'13 saying that he will not vote for either \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer Maryland Gov. \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  (R), who\u8217\'20\'19s running in his state\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  race, says he won\u8217\'20\'19t vote for either leading candidate in the 2024 presidential election:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m like 70% of the rest of the people in America who do not want \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to be president.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BowMC1HnCJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BowMC1HnCJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1765792682314478063?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Hogan, who recently stepped down from his third-party movement No Labels, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19ll hopefully have some ability to vote for someone that these people actually want to vote for rather than just voting against.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In a tweet on Thursday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  urged Americans to tune into his State of the Union address in which he plans to address \u8220\'20\'1Chow far we\u8217\'20\'19ve come in building the economy from the middle out and the bottom up \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to add that he plans to address \u8220\'20\'1Cthe work we have left to lower costs and protect our freedoms against MAGA attacks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m headed to the Capitol tonight to deliver my State of the Union address.\par \par \uc2 Join us at 9pm ET to hear how far we\u8217\'20\'19ve come in building the economy from the middle out and the bottom up and the work we have left to lower costs and protect our freedoms against MAGA attacks. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cpflojaeCH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cpflojaeCH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1765799637665841484?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 State of the Union guests include Alabama mother whose IVF was canceled\par \par \uc2 An Alabama mother who saw a second round of IVF canceled after the state supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled that embryos were children}}}\uc2  will attend \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address on Thursday, as guests of the first lady, Jill Biden.\par \par \uc2 La Torya Beasley of Birmingham, Alabama, is among the first lady\u8217\'20\'19s 20 invited guests who \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonify issues or themes to be addressed by the president in his speech,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Beasley and her husband had their first child, via IVF, in 2022. They were trying to have another child through IVF but Beasley\u8217\'20\'19s embryo transfer was suddenly canceled because of the Alabama court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision.}}}\par \par \uc2 Also on the guest list is Kate Cox, the Texas mother {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65e9df438f082c67eb9c00a3#block-65e9df438f082c67eb9c00a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forced to travel }}}\uc2  outside her state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The White House said the cases of Beasley and Cox, showed \u8220\'20\'1Chow the overturning of Roe v Wade has disrupted access to reproductive healthcare for women and families across the country\u8221\'20\'1D. In a statement, the White House said:\par \par \uc2 Stories like Kate\u8217\'20\'19s and LaTorya\u8217\'20\'19s should never happen in America. But Republican elected officials want to impose this reality on women nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/biden-sotu-ivf-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union guests include mother whose IVF was canceled and Kate Cox}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has welcomed Sweden into Nato in a statement after the country {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/07/sweden-joins-nato-after-ratification-hungary-drops-opposition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 officially became}}}\uc2  the 32nd member of the western military alliance.\par \par \uc2 Stockholm\u8217\'20\'19s ratification process was finally completed in Washington on Thursday, as Sweden and Hungary \u8211\'20\'13 the last country to ratify Sweden\u8217\'20\'19s membership \u8211\'20\'13 submitted the necessary documents after a drawn-out process that has taken nearly two years.\par \par \uc2 The ratification marked the end of a 20-month-long wait that started in May 2022 when it submitted its application to join alongside Finland, prompted by Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine in February that year.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Biden said he was \u8220\'20\'1Chonored\u8221\'20\'1D to welcome Sweden as Nato\u8217\'20\'19s newest ally, and that the alliance was \u8220\'20\'1Cstronger than ever\u8221\'20\'1D with its addition. He added:\par \par \uc2 Today, we once more reaffirm that our shared democratic values \u8211\'20\'13 and our willingness to stand up for them \u8211\'20\'13 is what makes Nato the greatest military alliance in the history of the world. It is what draws nations to our cause. It is what underpins our unity. And together with our newest Ally Sweden \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 NATO\uc2  will continue to stand for freedom and democracy for generations to come.\par \par \uc2 The Swedish prime minister, \uc2 Ulf Kristersson\uc2 , will be attending \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address as a guest of the first lady, the White House has confirmed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , the Republican former governor of Maryland who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/09/larry-hogan-republican-maryland-launches-senate-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  is running}}}\uc2  for Senate, has said he would not vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the November election.\par \par \uc2 Hogan, at an Axios event, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/03/07/larry-hogan-trump-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  he will vote for neither Trump nor \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and would instead seek out a third-party candidate. He said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m like 70% of the rest of people in America who do not want \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to be president, and I\u8217\'20\'19m hoping that there potentially is another alternative.\par \par \uc2 He added that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t know yet who that candidate will be. Hogan, one of the most outspoken and only Trump critics in the Republican party, last year said he would support the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for president, but at the time said he did not think Trump would be that candidate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to announce US will build port on Gaza shore for large-scale aid delivery\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will announce in the State of the Union speech that US forces will build a temporary port on the Gaza shoreline in the next few weeks to allow delivery of humanitarian aid on a large scale.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not waiting on the Israelis. This is a moment for American leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D a senior US official said on Thursday, reflecting growing frustration of what is seen in Washington as Israeli obstruction of road deliveries on a substantial scale.\par \par \uc2 The port will be built by US military engineers operating from ships off the Gaza coast, who will not need to step ashore, US officials said. The aid deliveries will be shipped from the port of Larnaca in Cyprus, which will become the main relief hub. The official said:\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the president will announce in his State of the Union address that he has directed the US military to undertake an emergency mission to establish a port in Gaza, working in partnership with like minded countries and humanitarian partners. This port, the main feature of which is a temporary pier, will provide the capacity for hundreds of additional truckloads of assistance each day.\par \par \uc2 Biden will also announce the opening of a new land crossing into the occupied and devastated coastal strip. Biden has been fiercely criticised within his own party for the failure to open up Gaza to humanitarian aid, with a famine looming and 30,000 Palestinians dead already since the start of war on 7 October.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address tonight will highlight Democratic successes and show the chaos in the House Republican party in stark relief.\par \par \uc2 During his floor remarks reported by CNN, Schumer said Biden will make it clear that \u8220\'20\'1Cafter so much adversity, America\u8217\'20\'19s economy is growing, inflation is slowing, and Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 agenda is delivering.\u8221\'20\'1D He said:\par \par \uc2 The difference between the parties will be as clear as night and day. Democrats are focused on lowering costs, creating jobs, putting money in people\u8217\'20\'19s pockets. But the hard right, which too often runs the Republican party in the House and now increasingly in the Senate, is consumed by chaos, bullying, and attacking things like women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom of choice.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Republican front-runner for president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has \u8220\'20\'1Cmade it abundantly clear that he\u8217\'20\'19s not running to make people\u8217\'20\'19s lives better, but rather on airing his personal political grievances,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to use State of the Union address to urge protection of rights\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver the final State of the Union address of his presidential term this evening, giving him an opportunity to tout his accomplishments and pitch his re-election campaign as he prepares for a rematch against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in November.\par \par \uc2 Previewing Biden\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union speech, his press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , said his remarks would focus on the president\u8217\'20\'19s vision for the nation\u8217\'20\'19s future and his legislative accomplishments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re going to hear the president address how democracy is under attack, how freedoms are certainly under attack,\u8221\'20\'1D including women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights and voting rights, Jean-Pierre told MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech will also highlight his agenda for a potential second term, the White House chief of staff Jeff Zients told NPR. Those include \u8220\'20\'1Clowering costs, continuing to make people\u8217\'20\'19s lives better by investing in childcare, eldercare, paid family and medical leave, continued progress on student debt\u8221\'20\'1D, he said, adding:\par \par \uc2 The president is also going to call for restoring Roe v. Wade and giving women freedom over their healthcare. And he\u8217\'20\'19ll talk about protecting, not taking away, freedoms in other areas, as well as voting rights.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/joe-biden-last-state-union-address"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden to deliver final State of the Union before election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican House speaker, reportedly pleaded with his party to show \u8220\'20\'1Cdecorum\u8221\'20\'1D on Thursday, when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  comes to the chamber to deliver his State of the Union address.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDecorum is the order of the day,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said, according to an unnamed Republican who attended a closed-door event on Capitol Hill on Wednesday and was quoted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4514306-speaker-johnson-urges-gop-lawmakers-to-maintain-decorum-at-state-of-the-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by the Hill}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The same site said another unnamed member of Congress said Johnson asked his party to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4514306-speaker-johnson-urges-gop-lawmakers-to-maintain-decorum-at-state-of-the-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ccarry ourselves with good decorum\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\uc2  A third Republican was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4514306-speaker-johnson-urges-gop-lawmakers-to-maintain-decorum-at-state-of-the-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quoted}}}\uc2  as saying:\par \par \uc2 He said, \u8216\'20\'18Let\u8217\'20\'19s have the appropriate decorum. We don\u8217\'20\'19t need to be shrill, you know, we got to avoid that. We need to base things upon policy, upon facts, upon reality of situations.\par \par \uc2 Last year\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union saw {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/08/biden-sketch-state-of-the-union-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outbursts from Republicans}}}\uc2  and responses from Biden that made headlines, most awarding the president the win. Kevin McCarthy, then speaker, also asked his Republican members not to breach decorum. But in a sign of his limited authority, months before he became the first speaker ejected by his own party, such pleas fell on deaf ears.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More than a quarter of Black female voters describe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has their top issue in this year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, according to a new poll.\par \par \uc2 The findings by health policy research firm KFF reveal a significant shift from previous election years, when white, conservative evangelicals were more likely to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their biggest priority when voting, AP reported. Those voters were highly motivated in recent presidential elections to cast ballots for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Overall, 12% of voters surveyed said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the most important issue in this year\u8217\'20\'19s election. Twenty eight percent of Black women identified the issue as top of mind, as well as 19% of women living in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned, and 17% of women who are under age 50.\par \par \uc2 Of voters who said that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was their most important issue, two-thirds said they believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a complete shift,\u8221\'20\'1D pollster Ashley Kirzinger told AP.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  voters are young, Black women \u8211\'20\'13 and not white evangelicals.\par \par \uc2 Women \u8211\'20\'13 and Black women, in particular \u8211\'20\'13 were crucial to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s win over Trump in the 2020 presidential election. More than half of Black Americans live in southern states, most of which have introduced strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws since the supreme court overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the Hawaii \u8217\'20\'19s Democratic presidential contest on Wednesday with 66% of the vote, according to the Hawaii Democratic Party.\par \par \uc2 Of the 1,563 votes cast, 29% of voters chose \u8220\'20\'1Cuncommitted\u8221\'20\'1D, the highest percentage total in any statewide contest this cycle.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats have pushed for voters to cast an uncommitted ballot in states that permit it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/06/uncommitted-vote-israel-ceasefire-super-tuesday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 , as a protest vote }}}\uc2  against Biden\u8217\'20\'19s position on the war between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltr"Uncommitted" got 29% against Biden in Hawaii's caucuses {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IVr7yhvQf3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IVr7yhvQf3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Aaron Blake\uc2  (@AaronBlake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AaronBlake/status/1765713758612079061?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kate Cox, the Texas woman who had to flee her state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has described the \u8220\'20\'1Cterrifying\u8221\'20\'1D toll that politicizing health decisions takes on women and families.\par \par \uc2 Cox, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65e9d5a08f082c67eb9c0035#block-65e9d5a08f082c67eb9c0035"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is expected}}}\uc2  to attend this evening\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address as a guest of first lady Jill Biden, sued Texas after the state supreme court ruled to block her from receiving an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after her foetus was diagnosed with a fatal chromosomal condition.\par \par \uc2 Cox did not qualify for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because her doctor did not establish her symptoms were life-threatening, the court ruled, prompting her to travel to New Mexico to undergo an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Having to seek the procedure out of state \u8220\'20\'1Cadded a lot of pain and suffering to what was already the most devastating time of our lives,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in an interview with CNN aired last night. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just one,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of women and families that are suffering because of the laws in Texas today.\par \par \uc2 enltrPowerful interview from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanaBashCNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @danabashcnn}}}\uc2  with Kate Cox. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8Nb5MPVczc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8Nb5MPVczc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1765582134977159599?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/16/abortion-ban-lawsuits-pregnancy-complication-emergency-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kate Cox case reveals toll of US \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans on women in medical emergencies}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The health and human services secretary, \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , said while his agency would continue to enforce federal laws in Alabama, including laws that provide medical patients a right to privacy and the right to stabilizing emergency care, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/02/texas-emergency-abortions-ban-despite-federal-guidance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including emergency abortions}}}\uc2 , it is ultimately the courts in and politicians of Alabama who need to fix the upheaval their policies caused.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court in Alabama is the one that has to undo its wrongful decision,\u8221\'20\'1D Becerra {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/mar/07/us-health-secretary-xavier-becerra-alabama-ivf-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told the Guardian.}}}\par \par \uc2 The state legislature in Alabama should move to provide protections to families that rely on IVF \u8211\'20\'13 and serious comprehensive protections, not short-term, piecemeal protections that threaten anyone going through the process or any provider who wishes to provide quality IVF services.\par \par \uc2 Although Alabama politicians have passed a bill to give IVF providers immunity from civil and criminal suits, national associations of fertility doctors have said the law does not go far enough to address the core problem \u8211\'20\'13 the supreme court \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/alabama-ivf-frozen-embryos-legislation-immunity-68d773d6ee89107c9a2e569110e7e31f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conflating fertilized eggs with children}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClearly, this goes way beyond \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Becerra.\par \par \uc2 It would not surprise me if we also begin to see actions which undermine the ability of women to get basic family planning services.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Society for Reproductive Medicine\uc2 , which represents IVF providers nationwide, has said the new law is insufficient because it does not correct the fundamental problem \u8211\'20\'13 the court ruling that considers fertilized eggs to be children.\par \par \uc2 The bill \u8220\'20\'1Cfalls far short of what Alabamans want and need to access fertility care in their state without fear,\u8221\'20\'1D NBC cited Karla Torres, senior counsel at the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , as saying, adding that the legislation amounted to \u8220\'20\'1Cbackpedaling in the face of state and nationwide public outcry to allow politicians to save face.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although some of the clinics that paused IVF services after the state court\u8217\'20\'19s decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65e9cf6c8f08a2f90dbf47ea#block-65e9cf6c8f08a2f90dbf47ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are planning }}}\uc2  to resume treatments, the fertility clinic at the center of that case, the Center for Reproductive Medicine at Mobile Infirmary, said it will not yet be resuming IVF treatments, CNN reported. A statement said:\par \par \uc2 At this time, we believe the law falls short of addressing the fertilized eggs currently stored across the state and leaves challenges for physicians and fertility clinics trying to help deserving families have children of their own.\par \par \uc2 Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2 , acknowledged the new law was a quick fix after the court ruling and noted \u8220\'20\'1Cthere will be more work to come\u8221\'20\'1D on IVF protections.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 State of the Union guest list puts reproductive rights in spotlight\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65e9d3578f0827b1cba3ebb3#block-65e9d3578f0827b1cba3ebb3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Becerra\u8217\'20\'19s comments}}}\uc2  come ahead of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  addressing the nation in the State of the Union on Thursday night. Although the White House has not released the speech, a large number of Democratic guests suggest reproductive rights may feature heavily.\par \par \uc2 Among the guests of high-ranking Democrats are Elizabeth Carr, the first person in the US to be born via IVF; Amanda Zurawski, a Texas woman who nearly died of septic shock when she was denied a medically necessary \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; and Kate Cox, who had to flee Texas for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after she learned her fetus had a fatal chromosomal condition.\par \par \uc2 More guests include reproductive endocrinologists, an Indiana doctor who provided an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a 10-year-old rape victim, and leaders of reproductive rights groups.\par \par \uc2 Becerra\u8217\'20\'19s comments emphasizing the importance of reproductive rights, Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 guest list for the State of the Union and a recent administration officials\u8217\'20\'19 trips to states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions are the most recent evidence of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/28/democrats-statehouse-races-campaign-spending"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s election bet}}}\uc2  : that when Republicans married the motivated minority of voters who support the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, they also divorced themselves from the broader American public, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/4507514-overwhelming-majority-americans-support-keeping-ivf-legal-for-women-poll/#:~:text=An%20overwhelming%20majority%20of%20Americans,it%20should%20not%20be%20legal."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broad margins of whom}}}\uc2  support IVF, contraception and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Pandora\u8217\'20\'19s box was opened\u8217\'20\'19 after fall of Roe, says health secretary\par \par \uc2 The health and human services secretary, \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , said the US must provide federal protections for reproductive rights if Americans hope to avoid further restrictions on in vitro fertilization, contraception and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/mar/07/us-health-secretary-xavier-becerra-alabama-ivf-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an exclusive interview with the Guardian.}}}\par \par \uc2 Becerra\u8217\'20\'19s comments come in the wake of an Alabama supreme court decision that gave embryos the rights of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf#:~:text=In%20a%20first%2Dof%2Dits,Mobile%20fertility%20clinic%20to%20proceed."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and forced three of the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest fertility clinics to stop services for fear of litigation and prosecution.\par \par \uc2 He said the events in Alabama were linked directly to the \u8220\'20\'1Ctake-down\u8221\'20\'1D of Roe v Wade, a decision that provided a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  grounded in privacy and was overturned by conservative \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices in 2022. Becerra said:\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t until this new court came in\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that is, that three new supreme court justices were confirmed by former President Trump \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cthat we saw the attacks on Roe v Wade take hold, and today without Roe v Wade there are women who are trying to have babies in Alabama who are facing the consequences.\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 None of this would be happening in Alabama on IVF if Roe v Wade was still the law of the land, and no one should try to deny that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Some Alabama fertility clinics that paused IVF services last month have said they will resume services after state lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/live/2024/mar/07/trump-biden-alabama-ivf-services-republicans-latest-news-state-of-the-union?page=with:block-65e9ce058f0827b1cba3eb77#block-65e9ce058f0827b1cba3eb77"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved new legislation}}}\uc2  to protect IVF providers from potential civil and criminal liability.\par \par \uc2 The bill \u8220\'20\'1Cprovides the protections that we need to start care \u8211\'20\'13 or resume care, really,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Janet Bouknight, an IVF provider at Alabama Fertility, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/alabama-fertility-clinic-says-will-resume-ivf-services-bill-passes-pro-rcna141682"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told }}}\uc2  NBC News. The clinic is planning to resume services this week .\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s largest health care system, the \uc2 University of Alabama at Birmingham\uc2 , also said it would restart IVF services. In a video statement, Dr Warner Huh, chair of the \uc2 UAB\uc2  department of obstetrics and gynaecology, said:\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 UAB\uc2  is moving to promptly resume IVF treatments, we\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to assess developments and advocate for protections for IVF patients and our providers.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in the state legislature proposed the immunity bill as a way to get clinics reopened, but have refused to take up a bill that would address the legal status of embryos. For that reason, some legal experts and reproductive rights advocates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/03/06/health/ivf-law-alabama.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have warned}}}\uc2  the bill does not go far enough.\par \par \uc2 Barbara Collura, president of \uc2 Resolve: The National Infertility Association\uc2 , said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://resolve.org/statement-from-resolve-on-signing-of-alabama-ivf-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  statement}}}\uc2  on Wednesday evening:\par \par \uc2 While we are grateful for the actions of Alabama legislators, this legislation does not address the underlying issue of the status of embryos as part of the IVF process \u8211\'20\'13 threatening the long-term standard of care for IVF patients. There is more work to be done.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alabama governor signs IVF protection bill into law\par \par \uc2 Alabama lawmakers moved quickly to approve new legislation that to protect IVF providers from the fallout of a court ruling that found frozen embryos have the rights of children under the state\u8217\'20\'19s wrongful death law.\par \par \uc2 Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2 , signed the bill into law on Wednesday night. The law protects providers from lawsuits and criminal prosecution in the event of \u8220\'20\'1Cdamage or death of an embryo\u8221\'20\'1D during IVF services. In a statement after signing, Ivey, a Republican, said:\par \par \uc2 IVF is a complex issue, no doubt, and I anticipate there will be more work to come, but right now, I am confident that this legislation will provide the assurances our IVF clinics need and will lead them to resume services immediately.\par \par \uc2 The bill gives legal protection for fertility clinics, at least three of which paused IVF treatments after the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruled last month that three couples who had frozen embryos destroyed in an accident at a storage facility {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could pursue wrongful death lawsuits}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans in the state legislature proposed the immunity bill as a way to get clinics reopened, but have refused to take up a bill that would address the legal status of embryos.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alabama fertility services set to resume after governor signs IVF protection bill\par \par \uc2 Alabama fertility clinics that paused in vitro fertilization (IVF) treatments following a controversial state supreme court ruling last month that equated frozen embryos to children are considering their next moves after Alabama \u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/alabama-governor-ivf-provider-protection-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a bill into law}}}\uc2  aimed at protecting IVF providers from potential legal liability on Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is preparing to deliver the final State of the Union address of his presidential term, where Democrats plan to put reproductive freedom literally front and center this evening. Among the guests invited to the SoTU are guests involved in the reproductive rights movement in some way, including Kate Cox, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/11/texas-abortion-kate-cox-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made headlines}}}\uc2  in December when she fled Texas to receive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care after she was denied access to the procedure in her home state. Elizabeth Carr, the first person born via in vitro fertilization in the US, is also expected to attend.\par \par \uc2 The stakes for Biden tonight are astronomical, as the president will aim to tout his accomplishments and pitch his re-election campaign as he faces intensifying worries about his age and ability at a time when the US faces numerous challenges at home and abroad.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9am ET: Biden will receive his intelligence briefing\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9.40am: Federal Reserve chair Jerome Powell will testify to the Senate Banking committee\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am: The House will convene. The Senate will meet.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am: Treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  will hold a bilateral meeting with Germany\u8217\'20\'19s minister for economic affairs and climate action Robert Habeck.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 8.25pm: Biden, First Lady Jill Biden and Second Gentleman Doug Emhoff will depart the White House en route to the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9pm: Biden will deliver his State of the Union address to Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240307ek370023f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
