\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Far-right candidates see Super Tuesday wins at traditional Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 expense\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in Washington \par \uc2 628 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 March 2024\par 18:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Highest-profile victory goes to Mark Robinson, a Hitler-quoting anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremist who will now run for North Carolina governorUS politics \u8211\'20\'13 live updates\par \par \uc2 Far-right candidates took notable wins in state elections on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/mar/06/not-so-super-tuesday-trump-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Super Tuesday}}}\uc2 , further confirming the Republican ascendancy of supporters of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , the probable GOP nominee for president, at the expense of more traditional conservatives.\par \par \uc2 The highest-profile victory went to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/05/mark-robinson-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Robinson}}}\uc2 , the lieutenant governor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/northcarolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina}}}\uc2  who will now run for governor.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic candidate, \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2 , would be the first Jewish governor of North Carolina should he win in November.\par \par \uc2 In opposition to Stein, Robinson is a Hitler-quoting anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremist, a dedicated controversialist who once said the superhero movie Black Panther was \u8220\'20\'1Ccreated by an agnostic Jew and put to film by [a] satanic marxist \u8230\'20\'26 to pull the shekels out of your Schvartze pockets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But the candidate may find recent remarks about his views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  harder to brush off, as Democrats seek to continue a string of wins in campaigns focused on rightwing attacks on reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Robinson has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/01/17/politics/kfile-mark-robinson-abortion-ban-no-exceptions/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported}}}\uc2  total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, calling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cmurder\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cgenocide\u8221\'20\'1D and, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/01/17/politics/kfile-mark-robinson-abortion-ban-no-exceptions/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by CNN}}}\uc2 , calling the founders of the women\u8217\'20\'19s health organisation \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  satanists who practiced witchcraft.\par \par \uc2 The spokesperson for Robinson also called Stein an extremist.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/northcarolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina}}}\uc2 , a 21-year-old college student affiliated with the extremist Turning Point USA youth group scored a notable victory when he defeated an 84-year-old state representative who has served for 20 years.\par \par \uc2 Wyatt Gable beat George Cleveland in a close primary race. Earlier this year, the Jacksonville Daily News, a local paper, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jdnews.com/news/local/onslow-county-elections-nc-house-of-representatives-district-14-candidates-answer-questions/article_aa198e3f-5000-5f89-a838-fac9af2c2629.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked both}}}\uc2  men what experience they had to recommend themselves to voters.\par \par \uc2 Cleveland said: \u8220\'20\'1CI have served as a budget writer since 2010 and have chaired various House committees over the past 14 years in veterans and homeland security, general government, marine resources, and aquaculture.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gable said: \u8220\'20\'1CCurrently in the university system and only a few years removed from the public education system, I have an up-close look at our education system \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am also the Turning Point USA president at East Carolina. As president, I have stopped the school from changing the bathrooms to allow men in the women\u8217\'20\'19s room and vice versa. I have also been able to sign up almost 1,000 new members.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Further west, in Texas, a Republican civil war between Trump-aligned hardliners and establishment figures saw hardliners gain the edge in elections on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In a US House primary, Tony Gonzales, a Republican congressman from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/san-antonio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 San Antonio}}}\uc2 , was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sanantonioreport.org/bexar-county-congress-tony-gonzales-primary-election-results-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 headed for a runoff}}}\uc2  election against Brandon Herrera, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wPE5KBMBWnE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media personality}}}\uc2  and gun salesman.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Gonzales was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sanantonioreport.org/republican-tony-gonzales-statewide-censure/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 censured}}}\uc2  by his own state party, for voting in favour of same-sex marriage and gun safety reform (the latter after the massacre of 19 young children and two adults at a school in Uvalde, Texas) and for being seen as soft on immigration and border policy.\par \par \uc2 In the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  state house, the speaker, Dade Phelan, will contest a runoff with David Covey, a challenger endorsed by \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , the state attorney general, \uc2 Dan Patrick\uc2 , the lieutenant governor, and Trump himself.\par \par \uc2 Phelan supported Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2024/02/28/ken-paxton-impeachment-witness-testimony/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impeachment}}}\uc2 , a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/16/ken-paxton-texas-republican-attorney-general-acquitted"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed}}}\uc2  attempt to remove the attorney general over allegations of bribery, dereliction of duty and disregard for official duty.\par \par \uc2 Paxton, who faces a securities fraud trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2023/10/30/ken-paxton-securities-fraud-charges-trial/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 next month}}}\uc2 , also took aim on Tuesday at three judges on the highest criminal court in Texas. All Republicans, the three judges were part of a ruling that stopped Paxton fast-tracking cases of supposed voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 All three judges were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.keranews.org/politics/2024-03-06/texas-ken-paxton-endorsements-texas-court-of-criminal-appeals-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 beaten}}}\uc2  by candidates Paxton endorsed.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240306ek36002eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
