\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Group tied to anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  Trump mega-donors pours money into Alabama supreme court race\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 1,086 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 February 2024\par 15:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Organization affiliated with Richard and Elizabeth Uihlein spends half a million on candidate who believes life begins at fertilization\par \par \uc2 A group connected to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , billionaire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Business/billionaire-donors-defecting-trump-watch/story?id=93409938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump mega-donors}}}\uc2  has funneled more than half a million dollars to an Alabama supreme court judicial candidate who said \u8220\'20\'1Cembryos were human beings whose lives begin at fertilization\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court was thrust into the limelight earlier this month when eight of the court\u8217\'20\'19s nine justices ruled that embryos created for in vitro fertilization (IVF) were \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D in the eyes of the law.\par \par \uc2 The decision forced three of the state\u8217\'20\'19s eight fertility clinics to stop providing advanced treatments, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/23/fertility-doctors-reaction-alabama-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 infuriated doctors}}}\uc2 , and left hundreds of would-be parents with few options for continuing treatment. At least one company that ships frozen embryos has paused business in the state, making it difficult to ship existing embryos elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , now the presumptive Republican presidential nominee, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/tommy-tuberville-alabama-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted to back away}}}\uc2  from the Alabama supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling. Trump reportedly sees extreme {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/02/16/us/politics/trump-abortion-ban.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans as a threat}}}\uc2  to Republican victories. Republicans more broadly have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/28/republicans-alabama-ivf-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggled to respond to the decision}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The group funding the Alabama candidate, Fair Courts America, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/news/2023/09/billionaire-megadonor-couple-funding-election-denial-with-extensive-influence-machine-dark-money-network-uihlein/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 connected to}}}\uc2  anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  billionaire mega-donors Richard and Elizabeth Uihlein. Fair Courts America represents the only outside group donating in Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming primary race for supreme court chief justice, scheduled to take place next week.\par \par \uc2 The race pits the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.alreporter.com/2024/02/26/justice-stewart-leads-chief-justice-race-with-22-percent-margin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long-shot candidate}}}\uc2  Bryan Taylor, backed by the Uihlein-affiliated Fair Courts America, against the sitting supreme court justice Sarah Stewart. A recent Fair Courts America ad {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mycmag.kantarmediana.com/KMIcmagvidbin2/STSUPCT_AL_FAIRCOURTSAMERICA_RIGHT_CHOICE.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told voters}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIf you like Trump\u8217\'20\'19s judges, you\u8217\'20\'19ll love Bryan Taylor.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump confirmed three justices to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , including at least one who supported a group that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/01/amy-coney-barrett-supported-group-fertilization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposes aspects of IVF treatment}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a statement on the IVF decision, Taylor said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BryanTaylorAL/status/1761169827060752729"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he believed}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwe can uphold the sanctity of life without subjecting IVF clinics to lawsuit abuse\u8221\'20\'1D, but that resolving the legality of IVF in the state is \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin the purview of the legislature\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope they can act quickly with the dual aim to protect life and support families,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Whether the legislature can, in fact, resolve the legal status of IVF in the state is unknown. In a 2011 case, the state supreme court found fetuses had the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/02/24/health/alabama-ivf-roe-v-wade/index.html#:~:text=In%202011%2C%20a%20court%20decision,the%20fetus%20in%20the%20miscarriage."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rights of children in wrongful death suits}}}\uc2 . Further, an Alabama constitutional amendment to protect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/alabama-lawmakers-proposing-protect-ivf/story?id=107599592#:~:text=The%20court's%20decision%20had%20drawn,children%2C%22%20according%20to%20Rosen."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cthe sanctity of life\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  that was cited by the court\u8217\'20\'19s recent decision could be used to invalidate new laws meant to protect IVF, as the constitution would override laws passed by the legislature.\par \par \uc2 The Alabama supreme court seat in question now belongs to the chief justice, Tom Parker, who wrote a fiery opinion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/02/22/us/alabama-ivf-tom-parker.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laced with biblical references}}}\uc2  in the recent IVF case. Parker\u8217\'20\'19s seat is open because he hit a state mandated retirement age. Stewart, a sitting justice, voted in favor of the recent IVF decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision in Dobbs really supercharged the cycles around state supreme court elections,\u8221\'20\'1D said Douglas Keith of the Brennan Center for Justice judicial project, about the case that overturned Roe v Wade and paved the way for Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court decision. \u8220\'20\'1CThe 2022 cycle saw almost double any midterm had ever seen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Uihlein is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/news/2023/09/billionaire-megadonor-couple-funding-election-denial-with-extensive-influence-machine-dark-money-network-uihlein/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cardboard magnate}}}\uc2  whose Uline boxes are ubiquitous in commercial shipping. He is descended from the Schlitz beer fortune. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/apr/23/liz-uihlein-trump-donor-wisconsin-stay-at-home-order-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Uihleins}}}\uc2  are the second largest individual political donors in the country, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/elections-overview/biggest-donors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Center for Responsive Politics}}}\uc2 . In 2022, they donated more than $89m exclusively to Republicans.\par \par \uc2 The Uihleins are known for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activism and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/14/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-funding-donors-election-deniers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election denialism}}}\uc2 . They donated heavily to Trump in 2016 and 2022. In 2022, they donated to multiple Trump-aligned candidates. This fall, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailyherald.com/20240218/news/uihleins-spent-more-than-1-million-on-desantis-presidential-campaign-in-fall-will-they-now-back/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they backed the Florida governor, Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , in the Republican presidential primary, before he dropped out of the race. Trump is almost certain to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/18/donald-trump-megadonor-campaign-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seek their support}}}\uc2  in the upcoming general election.\par \par \uc2 The couple {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/gop-megadonor-pours-millions-into-effort-to-hinder-ohio-abortion-amendment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent millions}}}\uc2  to block a ballot initiative in Ohio that would have hindered an effort to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution. The Uihlein-backed effort failed, and the Ohio constitutional amendment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-ohio-constitutional-amendment-republicans-courts-fb1762537585350caeee589d68fe5a0d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 codifying \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights passed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Uihleins have given generously to Becket, a powerful religious law firm, the Pro-Life Action League and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/05/public-nuisance-laws-business-opioids"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American Legislative Exchange Council}}}\uc2 , which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.exposedbycmd.org/2023/08/11/alec-feeds-lawmakers-a-steady-diet-of-anti-abortion-arguments/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provides model legislation to states}}}\uc2 , including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.exposedbycmd.org/2022/07/27/abandoning-free-market-and-liberty-principles-alec-takes-on-woke-capitalism-bodily-autonomy-and-more-at-its-annual-meeting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws and information}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Uihleins were also among the top donors to Trump; have backed unfounded claims about the legitimacy of the 2020 election; and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/news/2023/09/billionaire-megadonor-couple-funding-election-denial-with-extensive-influence-machine-dark-money-network-uihlein/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported some of the activists}}}\uc2  who organized the \u8220\'20\'1CStop the Steal\u8221\'20\'1D rally immediately before the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Spending in the Alabama supreme court race has come from Fair Courts America, a Uihlein-affiliated group which has also worked on state supreme court races in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/21/wisconsin-supreme-court-primary-election-uihlein-family-campaign-finance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2 , Kentucky and Illinois.\par \par \uc2 The Brennan Center, which has tracked spending in state supreme court races for decades, said the Uihlein-connected group spent $647,900 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://u7061146.ct.sendgrid.net/ls/click?upn=u001.gqh-2BaxUzlo7XKIuSly0rC3kyN-2FTNslvlNtpWX2uRpFNs8sotjNTKhH0vXb6cNDHKrz51VAwlTP0i1-2FC-2B4poUJrnIQqkZROsN5wvT6AEQGupiEDS8NwCNxfWUVEhLEFLD__gQ_1-2FlQ5R7jXHW5rdNHc-2FQfdl7ksCXCKEYBrm8jz0sV33COnq9cqQ7UzYH5ghOoyNqbdqbml-2FOkxqtHArpP4KT1a3Hd1IixN-2F6U-2FhUFbbYD5xlsw7qxvlmNoND4RaZNisamXbQVXTOx2B0DcenETa8cL0ZcctrN3-2F-2FO1jNuUUtCvOBRtS5fuEpoQsA1n2a-2FWKDxyvHFTKNyFmKVs8BTK9YdkaecS82cpSnfGXz5PPzEwIy-2Byzp-2BK8mBkuAN1NIV4JHcn7im8dUqIW-2FyUec1oSKZmKJ-2BOBrp-2FmFVbeifrB2hgJWK40SDWl0nD1fE69FAtcoYKescWvhohlA0I2N-2B-2FpnuQMVWhQt3myOu92d-2FaMz93kQ-3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on ads}}}\uc2  in support of Taylor. By comparison, his opponent Stewart spent $273,740 of her own money on television ads. Taylor has spent $13,900 of his own cash TV ads.\par \par \uc2 What remains unclear is the motivation for spending in Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court race this year. The ad for Taylor only came to the Brennan Center\u8217\'20\'19s attention on Friday, as the race was not seen as an especially high-profile one.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere must be some motivation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Keith. \u8220\'20\'1CThe groups that are getting involved in state supreme court races are incredibly sophisticated political players. They know why these courts matter and they know how far their money can go in these races.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere must be something coming before the court or likely to come before the court that makes this group want to get involved,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Keith used a recent example from Kentucky to illustrate how detail-oriented Republican-backed court campaigns can be. In 2022, donors including Fair Courts America {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.weku.org/politics/2022-11-03/money-from-interests-groups-floods-into-kentucky-nonpartisan-judicial-races"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poured money into not only the composition of the state supreme court}}}\uc2 , but also into the race of a trial court judge in Franklin county who had repeatedly ruled against the Republican-dominated state legislature.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou really have to understand the legal system to get involved in a race that small, and I think that speaks to how strategic, at least groups on the right, are being around judicial elections,\u8221\'20\'1D said Keith.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240229ek2t001e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
