\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Supreme court will decide Trump immunity claim in 2020 election case \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now); Chris Stein and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 7,991 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 February 2024\par 23:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our full report on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court immunity case here:Supreme court to hear Trump immunity claim in election interference case\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will decide whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can be prosecuted on election interference charges. The court set an expedited schedule to hear the immunity issue, with oral arguments during the week of 22 April.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 With government funding partially expiring on Friday, House and Senate negotiators have reached an agreement to prevent a shutdown. Congressional leaders of both parties said that negotiators have already reached a deal on six full-year spending bills for agriculture, and the remaining six bills are expected to be finalized before 22 March.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  will step down as Republican leader in the Senate at the end of this year. The 82-year-old is the longest-serving Senate leader in history, a highly divisive figure in a bitterly divided country and the subject of fierce speculation, after recent public health scares.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans have blocked legislation that would protect Americans\u8217\'20\'19 access to in vitro fertilization (IVF) treatment after an Alabama supreme court ruling that frozen embryos are children led to the closure of a number of infertility clinics in the state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  continues to be \u8220\'20\'1Cfit for duty and fully executes all of his responsibilities without any exemptions or accommodations\u8221\'20\'1D, his physician has said after the president\u8217\'20\'19s annual physical exam.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A New York appeals judge has denied \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s request to pay just $100m of the $454m judgment for his New York fraud trial.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to take up the case of whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can be prosecuted on election interference charges marks a significant victory for the former president.\par \par \uc2 As my colleague Hugo Lowell writes, Trump might be the luckiest criminal defendant in the history of criminal defendants.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump might be the luckiest criminal defendant in the history of criminal defendants. And of course if he wins the election \u8212\'20\'14 the particularly perilous Special Counsel cases go away\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1762970890826907914?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , has responded to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/28/michigan-primary-election-trump-biden-government-shutdown-updates?page=with:block-65dfb1818f08e47614341c29#block-65dfb1818f08e47614341c29"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the announcement}}}\uc2  by top congressional leaders that they have reached a deal to prevent a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 In a statement posted to social media, she said:\par \par \uc2 As the President and Congressional leaders made clear at yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s meeting, we cannot allow a government shutdown. The bipartisan agreement announced today would help prevent a needless shutdown while providing more time to work on bipartisan appropriations bills and for the House to pass the bipartisan national security supplemental as quickly as possible.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs the President and Congressional leaders made clear at yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s meeting, we cannot allow a government shutdown. The bipartisan agreement announced today would help prevent a needless shutdown while providing more time to work on bipartisan appropriations bills and for the\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Yo8PnekSiV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Yo8PnekSiV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1762970744374386984?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans have blocked legislation that would guarantee Americans\u8217\'20\'19 access to in vitro fertilization (IVF) despite widespread backlash to a recent ruling by the Alabama supreme court that designated frozen embryos as \u8216\'20\'18children\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator Tammy Duckworth, who used IVF treatments to have her two children, sought an immediate vote by the Senate on Wednesday on her Access to Family Building bill.\par \par \uc2 Her move for a vote, which required unanimous consent by all 100 senators, was promptly blocked by Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 Cindy Hyde-Smith\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hyde-Smith, speaking on the Senate floor, said the bill was a \u8220\'20\'1Cvast overreach that is full of poison pills that goes way too far, far beyond ensuring legal access to IVF\u8221\'20\'1D. She added:\par \par \uc2 I support the ability for mothers and fathers to have total access to IVF and bringing new life into the world. I also believe human life should be protected.\par \par \uc2 She defended the Alabama supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, pointing out that it originated with a pair of wrongful death cases brought by three couples who had frozen embryos destroyed in an accident at a fertility clinic.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congressional leaders reach deal to avert government shutdown\par \par \uc2 Congressional leaders said they have reached a deal to advance appropriations bills in March for fiscal year 2024, averting a government shutdown for now.\par \par \uc2 A joint statement from Democratic and Republican leaders including Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and House speaker Mike Johnson reads:\par \par \uc2 We are in agreement that Congress must work in a bipartisan manner to fund our government.\par \par \uc2 Negotiators have come to an agreement on six bills: Agriculture-\uc2 FDA\uc2 , Commerce-Justice and Science, Energy and Water Development, Interior, Military Construction-VA, and Transportation-HUD. After preparing final tect, this package of six full year Appropriations bills will be voted on and enacted prior to March 8. These bills will adhere to the Fiscal Responsibility Act discretionary spending limits and January\u8217\'20\'19s topline spending agreement.\par \par \uc2 The remaining six Appropriations bills \u8211\'20\'13 Defense, Financial Services and General Government, Homeland Security, Labor-\uc2 HHS\uc2 , Legislative Branch, and State and Foreign Operations \u8211\'20\'13 will be finalized, voted on, and enacted prior to March 22.\par \par \uc2 A shutdown would have forced many federal employees to go without pay until Congress passed another funding bill, and while that disruption has been avoided for now, the threat will arise again in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  will decide whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can be prosecuted on election interference charges, indicating it will move quickly in the immunity case.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appeal to the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court marks the final challenge the former US president can make on the immunity issue related to his federal criminal case.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team had thought for months that the appeal would probably fall short on the law but would be an effective way to delay the impending trial, which had been due to begin in early March.\par \par \uc2 The court on Wednesday agreed to decide Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim of immunity on charges brought by a special counsel involving his efforts to overturn his 2020 election loss, again thrusting the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top judicial body into the election fray as Trump seeks to regain the presidency.\par \par \uc2 The justices put on hold the criminal case being pursued by special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  and will review a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s rejection of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim of immunity from prosecution because he was president when he took actions aimed at reversing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election victory over him.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers had requested a stay of that ruling, warning of dire consequences for the presidency absent such immunity.\par \par \uc2 Trump has made it no secret that his overarching legal strategy is to seek delays, ideally beyond the 2024 election in November, in the hopes that winning re-election could enable him to potentially pardon himself or direct his attorney general to drop the charges.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The supreme court \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that it will decide whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has immunity from prosecution adds a new hurdle to a trial focused on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn his 2020 election loss.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the supreme court said it will consider \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether and if so to what extent does a former President enjoy presidential immunity from criminal prosecution for conduct alleged to involve official acts during his tenure in office\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The court said it would hear arguments and issue a ruling on the immunity claim. In the meantime, the case is on hold, meaning no trial can take place.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme Court to decide Trump immunity claim in 2020 election case\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has agreed to decide \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s claim of immunity from prosecution on charges brought by a special counsel involving his efforts to overturn his 2020 election loss.\par \par \uc2 The justices\u8217\'20\'19 order maintains a hold on preparations for a trial focused on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn his election loss.\par \par \uc2 The court has agreed to expedite the case and hear arguments the week of 22 April. A decision is likely to come no later than the end of June.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  agrees to hear Trump immunity claim in the federal 2020 election interference case, oral argument set for April 22 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Lm58G1jI1v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Lm58G1jI1v}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1762962907845787777?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic Illinois senator Tammy Duckworth, speaking on the Senate floor, warned that the \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst domino has fallen\u8221\'20\'1D after an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama supreme court ruling}}}\uc2  that frozen embryos are children led to the closure of a number of infertility clinics in the state.\par \par \uc2 It could only be a matter of time before more state courts issue similar rulings, and more hospitals and organizations will have to stop providing IVF treatment, Duckworth said. She said:\par \par \uc2 Think about what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake. State courts simply can strip away access to IVF. Think about how many would-be moms might never be able to hear their child\u8217\'20\'19s first laugh.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican senator blocks vote on IVF protections\par \par \uc2 The Republican senator for Mississippi \uc2 Cindy Hyde-Smith\uc2  has blocked passage of a bill to protect Americans\u8217\'20\'19 access to in vitro fertilization (IVF) treatment.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congressional leaders have reportedly struck a deal to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/28/michigan-primary-election-trump-biden-government-shutdown-updates?page=with:block-65df9feb8f087a7b82b441ff#block-65df9feb8f087a7b82b441ff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extend funding}}}\uc2  to six agencies including the departments of agriculture, energy and water, veteran affairs with a 8 March deadline.\par \par \uc2 The House plans to vote tomorrow on the one-week stopgap measure to avert a partial government shutdown, CNN reports, citing a Republican aide.\par \par \uc2 Under the agreement, funding for six agencies including the departments of agriculture, transportation, veteran affairs, housing and urban development will expire on 8 March, a week later than planned.\par \par \uc2 Funding for the rest of the government, including defense and state departments, would be extended until 22 March.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden 'fit for duty', doctor says after annual physical\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  continues to be \u8220\'20\'1Cfit for duty and fully executes all of his responsibilities without any exemptions or accommodations\u8221\'20\'1D, his physician has said.\par \par \uc2 A summary of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s annual physical states:\par \par \uc2 President Biden is a healthy, active, robust 81-year-old male, who remains fit to successfully execute the duties of the Presidency, to include those as Chief Executive, Head of State and Commander in Chief.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats to bring bill on protecting IVF access nationwide\par \par \uc2 The Democratic senator from Illinois Tammy Duckworth will speak on the Senate floor and lead Senate Democrats in calling on Republicans to pass her bill to protect the right to access in vitro fertilization (IVF) and other fertility treatments in the wake of a ruling by the Alabama supreme court that frozen embryos are \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrTo all those Republicans who suddenly claim to support IVF\u8212\'20\'14today would be a great day to get out of the way and let the Senate pass my bill to protect access to IVF nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tammy Duckworth (@SenDuckworth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenDuckworth/status/1762867211436224544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has said he and \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  could \u8220\'20\'1Calways speak with each other honestly and put the country ahead of ourselves\u8221\'20\'1D in a statement following McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s announcement that he will step down as the Senate Republican leader in November.\par \par \uc2 Describing McConnell as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfriend\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden said he was proud that the pair have been able to work together to find common ground on behalf of the American people despite \u8220\'20\'1Cmany political disagreements\u8221\'20\'1D. He added:\par \par \uc2 Mitch has lived the American dream, overcoming polio and going on to become the longest-serving Senate leader in American history. Jill and I wish the best to Mitch and Elaine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York appeals judge denies Trump bid to pay $100m of $454m judgment\par \par \uc2 A New York appeals judge has denied \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s request to pay just $100m of the $454m judgment for his New York fraud trial.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers had asked the appeals court to halt the collection of the rest of the amount, along with the judgment\u8217\'20\'19s ban on Trump securing new loans from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  bans, until the appeal goes through.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Judge Anil Singh appeared to have some sympathy for Trump, staying the ban over Trump taking out loans from New York banks and another on him serving as an officer of a New York company, both for the next three years.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers Clifford Robert, Alina Habba and Michael Farina wrote:\par \par \uc2 The exorbitant and punitive amount of the judgment, coupled with an unlawful and unconstitutional blanket prohibition on lending transactions, would make it impossible to secure and post a complete bond.\par \par \uc2 The New York attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office said the appeals court should deny Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request as Trump has not said he does not have the assets to fulfil the judgment\u8217\'20\'19s full amount.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the news that congressional leaders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/28/michigan-primary-election-trump-biden-government-shutdown-updates?page=with:block-65df9de68f08b6f9684f411f#block-65df9de68f08b6f9684f411f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have reportedly}}}\uc2  struck a deal to prevent a government shutdown, according to Politico.\par \par \uc2 Negotiators reached an agreement on six appropriations bills, assigning them a deadline of 8 March, according to the report.\par \par \uc2 Leaders are aiming to release text by this weekend and clear the spending bills next week, the report says.\par \par \uc2 The remaining fiscal 2024 measures will get a new deadline of 22 March, according to Politico.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congressional negotiators strike deal to prevent government shutdown - report\par \par \uc2 With government funding partially expiring Friday, House and Senate negotiators have reached an agreement to prevent a shutdown, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Congressional leaders HAVE STRUCK a govt funding deal, per senior leadership source. Announcement imminent\par \par \uc2 6 approps bills next week: AG, CJS, Energy&Water, Interior, Milcon, THUD w/ March 8 deadline. Other 6 will be March 22. Vote on a CR by week's end.\par \par \uc2 StoryTK {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/politico?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @politico}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1762944254693851143?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Funding for some federal departments will expire after Friday, while the rest face an 8 March deadline. Democratic and Republican leaders in Congress met with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  yesterday at the White House, where all sides expressed their desire to avoid a shutdown that the president warned would damage the economy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In a statement marking \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to leave Senate Republican leadership, House speaker Mike Johnson made a point of mentioning McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s role in confirming conservative justices to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  rose from humble beginnings, overcoming polio to become one of the most consequential Senate leaders in history. He started his Senate career as a legislative aide and ended up in charge of the upper chamber,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo member of Congress has played a greater role in reshaping the federal judiciary than Mitch. I join my colleagues in saluting his historic contributions to the Republican party and to the Congress. His legacy will endure for generations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senators on Wednesday heard from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/16/tennessee-abortion-ban-lawsuit-allie-phillips-representative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Allie Phillips}}}\uc2 , a Tennessee woman denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the state\u8217\'20\'19s post-Roe law.\par \par \uc2 In searing testimony, Phillips told the Senate budget committee about her experience \u8211\'20\'13 almost exactly one year ago \u8211\'20\'13 of being told at an anatomy scan that her 19-week-old fetus \u8211\'20\'13 a girl she had already named Miley \u8211\'20\'13 was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot compatible with life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Phillip\u8217\'20\'19s doctor told her she could either leave the state to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or remain pregnant in Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThen the doctor warned that the longer I stayed pregnant, the worse Miley\u8217\'20\'19s condition would get and the more at risk my health would become,\u8221\'20\'1D Phillips said.\par \par \uc2 She described the disorienting scramble to find an appointment at a clinic that could care for her \u8211\'20\'13 and her family\u8217\'20\'19s struggle to scrape together the money to afford flights, a hotel, ground transportation, childcare for her daughter. Only thanks to a \uc2 GoFundMe\uc2  effort was she able to afford it.\par \par \uc2 Only patients were allowed into the clinic she found, for security reasons. After an ultrasound showed there was no longer a heartbeat, Phillips was rushed into surgery.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI went to surgery alone and I sat in recovery alone. I grieved her loss alone in a city I\u8217\'20\'19ve never been in, far away from the comfort of my home, my family, my friends,\u8221\'20\'1D Phillips said. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one should be treated this way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Phillips is now running for office in Tennessee, determined to keep telling her story until the laws are changed.\par \par \uc2 Later on the panel, a witness invited by the Republican senators suggested procedures such as the one performed on Phillips were not technically abortions and that her experience was rare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy procedure was an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is on my medical paperwork,\u8221\'20\'1D Phillips responded later.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would like to ask the people to remember my story and to remember that I am one of thousands if not millions of people in this country that need or needed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Read more about Phillips story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/16/tennessee-abortion-ban-lawsuit-allie-phillips-representative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban put her at risk \u8211\'20\'13 now she\u8217\'20\'19s running for office to change the law}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Florida Democratic congressman \uc2 Jared Moskowitz\uc2  has been a vocal critic of Republican efforts to impeach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and has been having fun mocking the process on X, including from inside the hearing room where \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is giving testimony.\par \par \uc2 The House oversight committee member linked in one post to his morning interview on MSNBC, in which he appeared in a black suit and tie resembling mourning clothes. \u8220\'20\'1CDressed today for the death of the Biden impeachment inquiry,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMoskowitz/status/1762850226128207941"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wrote}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrDressed today for the death of the Biden impeachment inquiry {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Morning_Joe?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Morning_Joe}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9GCgIO5jbk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9GCgIO5jbk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congressman \uc2 Jared Moskowitz\uc2  (@RepMoskowitz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMoskowitz/status/1762850226128207941?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Once the hearing got under way, Moskowitz had more thoughts. \u8220\'20\'1CSitting in the Depo now. BORING!\u8221\'20\'1D he added in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JaredEMoskowitz/status/1762865408506290483"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another tweet}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JaredEMoskowitz/status/1762880917062717526"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a third}}}\uc2 , he\u8217\'20\'19s posted a picture of a distraught scientist amid the smoking wreckage of an experiment that appears to have gone badly wrong\u8230\'20\'26 intended as an analogy for the effort led by Republican committee chair James Comer to turn up any damaging evidence against the president. \u8220\'20\'1CLive picture from inside the Hunter Biden Deposition,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 enltrLive picture from inside the Hunter Biden Deposition. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rBArCacp9k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rBArCacp9k}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jared Moskowitz\uc2  ?? (@JaredEMoskowitz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JaredEMoskowitz/status/1762880917062717526?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Moskowitz and Comer have a long history of clashing over the impeachment inquiry, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?c5093335/reps-comer-moskowitz-heated-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this VERY heated exchange}}}\uc2  between the pair last year, in which Comer angrily denounced as \u8220\'20\'1Cbullshit\u8221\'20\'1D allegations he had himself improperly loaned money to family members.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s an interesting Democratic primary developing in New York\u8217\'20\'19s first congressional district, a seat in the rather {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://screenrant.com/jaws-movie-location-amity-island-new-york-massachusettes/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jaws-ish bit of Long Island}}}\uc2  the party hopes will present a mortal threat to one of a number of endangered Republicans come November.\par \par \uc2 Jim Gaughran\uc2 , a state senator, has suspended his campaign and endorsed \uc2 John Avlon\uc2 , the former Daily Beast editor and CNN analyst and anchor who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/john-avlon-congress-cnn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  his own run last week.\par \par \uc2 Calling Gaughran \u8220\'20\'1Ca lifelong Long Islander who has won tough races against GOP incumbents\u8221\'20\'1D, Avlon\u8217\'20\'19s campaign released a statement in which Gaughran said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 John Avlon\uc2  is the only Democrat in this race who can build a winning coalition of Long Island families from the heart of Huntington to the tip of Montauk and bring responsible, common sense leadership to Washington. He has my wholehearted endorsement because I know he will defend reproductive rights, combat climate change, and deliver the resources our communities need to thrive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Avlon said Gaughran had \u8220\'20\'1Cdevoted his life to public service for Suffolk county and Long Island and I am so proud and honored to have his endorsement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am running for Congress because we need leaders in Washington like Jim who are focused on common sense problem solving for Suffolk county families like fixing our border, rebuilding the middle class, protecting reproductive freedom and keeping citizens safe \u8211\'20\'13 all fighting back against the Trump-LaLota extremist Maga agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nick LaLota is the Republican incumbent Avlon wants to take down. Avlon is campaigning with appeals for a return to civility in politics but the rivalry got off to a predictably testy start, after spokespeople for LaLota and congressional Republicans slammed Avlon as an \u8220\'20\'1Celitist\u8221\'20\'1D, a \u8220\'20\'1Csmug liberal hack\u8221\'20\'1D and an out-of-towner who, they claimed, really lives in Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 Avlon hit back, telling the Guardian in the interview that follows, \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re scared\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/25/john-avlon-cnn-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Avlon targets New York Republicans in US House campaign: \u8216\'20\'18They\u8217\'20\'19re scared\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 For some further further reading, here\u8217\'20\'19s Lauren Gambino\u8217\'20\'19s look at what a recent Democratic win in New York \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/14/tom-suozzi-wins-new-york-election-george-santos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the third district}}}\uc2 , the seat formerly occupied by the indicted fabulist and rare expelled congressman George Santos \u8211\'20\'13 might mean for the party and candidates such as Avlon:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/15/democrats-immigration-border-2024-election-tom-suozzi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats see New York election win as model for tackling immigration issue}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Asked for his thoughts on \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plans to depart Senate Republican leadership, \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , the top Democrat on the House oversight committee, said he blamed him for not voting to convict \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  following the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The House impeached Trump after the attack by his supporters on the Capitol, but McConnell voted against convicting him in the Senate. Seven Republicans ultimately broke ranks and voted with Democrats to sustain the charges, but McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s opposition was seen as crucial to discouraging enough Republicans that the two-thirds majority threshold for conviction was not reached.\par \par \uc2 Raskin makes that point here:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRaskin?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepRaskin}}}\uc2  on Sen. McConnell: "He didn't show the ultimate courage which would have been to vote to convict and to find enough other Senators so we that wouldn't be back in this nightmare again with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/n7gRFtHGwE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/n7gRFtHGwE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1762914142724202807?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden says he's 'sorry to hear' that McConnell is stepping down\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he was \u8220\'20\'1Csorry to hear\u8221\'20\'1D that \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  planned to leave his post as the top Senate Republican, remembering him as an antagonist who \u8220\'20\'1Cnever, never misrepresented anything\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe and I have trust, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got a great relationship, we fight like hell but he never, never, never misrepresented anything,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said at a White House event on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s crime-fighting efforts. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sorry to hear he\u8217\'20\'19s stepping down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden and McConnell served in the Senate together for 24 years.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 When Republicans controlled the Senate in 2016, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  refused to consider Democratic president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominee for a vacant supreme court seat, but later confirmed three conservative justices to the bench whom \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had nominated.\par \par \uc2 That created a six-justice conservative supermajority, which has been responsible for overturning Roe v Wade, weakening gun-safety and environmental laws, and a host of other decisions with national impact. He also killed legislation passed by Democrats when they controlled the House, and led the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s campaign against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s plans to revitalize the economy following the Covid-19 pandemic, and to fight climate change.\par \par \uc2 Despite all that, McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s record is not conservative enough for some. The Kentuckian is one of the most vocal Republican supporters of aid to Ukraine, a fact cited by the hard-right House Freedom Caucus as they bid him, essentially, good riddance:\par \par \uc2 enltrOur thoughts are with our Democrat colleagues in the Senate on the retirement of their Co-Majority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (D-Ukraine).\par \par \uc2 No need to wait till November\u8230\'20\'26 Senate Republicans should IMMEDIATELY elect a *Republican* Minority Leader.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Freedom Caucus (@freedomcaucus) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/freedomcaucus/status/1762917133929869679?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic representative Adam Schiff criticized \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s political track record following the senator\u8217\'20\'19s resignation announcement.\par \par \uc2 Pointing to McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s victory in helping to create a 6-3 conservative majority in the supreme court, Schiff said:\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  stacked the Court, undermined our democracy, and enabled \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And yet \u8211\'20\'13 in his absence \u8211\'20\'13 the @SenateGOP will invariably select someone more extreme.\par \par \uc2 With our democracy more fragile than ever, we must select and elect leaders committed to protecting it.\par \par \uc2 enltrMitch McConnell stacked the Court, undermined our democracy, and enabled \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And yet \u8211\'20\'13 in his absence \u8211\'20\'13 the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateGOP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenateGOP}}}\uc2  will invariably select someone more extreme.\par \par \uc2 With our democracy more fragile than ever, we must select and elect leaders committed to protecting it.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Schiff (@RepAdamSchiff) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAdamSchiff/status/1762903311475466661?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  on McConnell resignation: "I am very proud that we both came together"\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Democratic Senate majority leader, has responded to \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to step down from his position, saying in a statement:\par \par \uc2 During my years in the Senate, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  and I rarely saw eye to eye when it came to our politics or our policy preferences. But I am very proud that we both came together in the last few years to lead the Senate forward at critical moments when our country needed us, like passing the CARES Act in the early days of the COVID pandemic, finishing our work to certify the election on January 6th, and more recently working together to fund the fight for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 I know it\u8217\'20\'19s been a difficult year for him and his family and I wish them the very best.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  has released a statement following \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s resignation announcement, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cpassing of the torch moment \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hailing McConnell as \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the most effective leaders in the history of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, Graham said:\par \par \uc2 No one in the Republican Party has echoed the themes of peace through strength \u8211\'20\'13 the Reagan model of national security \u8211\'20\'13 better than Senator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 I look forward to continuing to work with Senator McConnell in the coming days and months as we address major challenges like securing the southern border and helping our friends in Ukraine, Israel and Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is more from the statement \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  delivered on the Senate floor regarding his resignation announcement:\par \par \uc2 I love the Senate. It has been my life. There may be more distinguished members of this body throughout our history, but I doubt there are any with more admiration for it.\par \par \uc2 After all this time, I still get a thrill walking into the Capitol and especially on this venerable floor knowing that we \u8211\'20\'13 each of us \u8211\'20\'13 have the honor to represent our states and do the important work of our country.\par \par \uc2 But Father Time remains undefeated.\par \par \uc2 I am no longer the young man sitting in the back, hoping colleagues would remember my name. It is time for the next generation of leadership \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 So time rolls on. There will be a new custodian of this great institution. Next year, I intend to turn this job over to a Republican majority leader. I have full confidence in my conference to choose my replacement and lead our country forward.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Here is where the day currently stands:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , will step down from his position in November, the 82-year-old Kentucky senator announced on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1COne of life\u8217\'20\'19s most underappreciated talents is to know when it\u8217\'20\'19s time to move on to life\u8217\'20\'19s next chapter,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The office of the House speaker, Mike Johnson, has responded to a letter from 23 global parliament leaders, urging him to allow a vote on US military aid to Ukraine. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile Speaker Johnson believes we must confront [Vladimir] Putin, and is exploring steps to effectively do so, as he said at the White House, his immediate priority is funding America\u8217\'20\'19s government and avoiding a shutdown,\u8221\'20\'1D his office said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , the top Democrat on the House\u8217\'20\'19s oversight committee, has called the Republican impeachment investigation into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ccomedy of errors\u8221\'20\'1D. Addressing reporters, Raskin said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are still waiting for our Republican friends to articulate what they think the high crime and misdemeanor is in this case.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Addressing the House oversight and judiciary committees, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  said that his father has \u8220\'20\'1Cnever\u8221\'20\'1D been involved in his business dealings. He continued: \u8220\'20\'1CFor more than a year, your committees have hunted me in your partisan political pursuit of my dad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Who will succeed McConnell?\par \par \uc2 Three Republicans are thought to be potential successors to \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  as the party\u8217\'20\'19s leader in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 They are:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  of Texas, the former whip during periods when Republicans held the majority in the Senate. In 2022, he worked with the Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/senate-breakthrough-clears-way-for-toughening-us-gun-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to pass modest gun safety reforms}}}\uc2  following the Uvalde school shooting.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Barasso of Wyoming, who currently chairs the Senate Republican Conference, making him the third-highest ranking GOP lawmaker.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Thune\uc2  of South Dakota, who, as minority whip, is McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s chief deputy in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Whoever takes over from McConnell may also end up with a different title: majority leader. In order for Democrats to maintain their current control of the chamber, incumbents representing red states of Ohio and Montana will have to win re-election, or the party will have to oust established Republicans in hostile territory like Florida and Texas \u8211\'20\'13 both tall orders.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  just ended his remarks on the Senate floor to applause.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers are coming to shake his hand, including the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s leader, Democrat \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 McConnell makes planned departure as Senate Republican leader official in floor speech\par \par \uc2 Speaking on the Senate floor, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  just formally announced his plan to depart as the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will be my last term as Republican leader. I\u8217\'20\'19m not going anywhere, anytime soon. I\u8217\'20\'19ll complete my job. My colleagues have given me until we select a new leader in November and they take the helm next January. I\u8217\'20\'19ll finish the job that people Kentucky hired me to do as well \u8211\'20\'13 albeit from a different seat,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  is speaking on the floor of the chamber now.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s expected to announce his plans to step down from his leadership position, which he\u8217\'20\'19s held longer than any other lawmaker.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  will step down in November\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican Senate minority leader who has made a lasting imprint on conservative politics in the United States, will step down from his leadership post in November, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mitch-mcconnell-senate-republican-leader-stepping-down-ba478d570a4561aa7baf91a204d7e366"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of life\u8217\'20\'19s most underappreciated talents is to know when it\u8217\'20\'19s time to move on to life\u8217\'20\'19s next chapter,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell will say in remarks from the Senate floor today, according to the AP. \u8220\'20\'1CSo I stand before you today \u8230\'20\'26 to say that this will be my last term as Republican leader of the Senate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McConnell plans to serve out his term representing Kentucky, which ends in January 2027.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats on Wednesday are moving to push through the Senate a bill that would protect Americans\u8217\'20\'19 access to in vitro fertilization after an Alabama court ruled that frozen embryos are children, which led to the closure of a number of fertility clinics in the state.\par \par \uc2 Senator Richard Blumenthal, a Connecticut Democrat, said the bill was unlikely to receive unanimous consent from the chamber to rush the bill through. While many Republican lawmakers registered disappointment over the Alabama ruling, at least one conservative senator was expected to object.\par \par \uc2 Blumenthal said Democrats would not be deterred. He would not say what the next legislative steps would be but he said Democrats, who control the Senate, would look for other ways to protect IVF and reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe IVF dilemma for Republicans is they are down a path that is not only unpopular, it\u8217\'20\'19s untenable as a matter of constitutional law and basic moral imperative and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to pursue it vigorously,\u8221\'20\'1D Blumenthal said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s vote, the effort to seek a unanimous consent, we know is unlikely to be successful. Failing today is only the prelude to a fight ahead on women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive care centered on IVF and other steps that have to be taken to protect basic rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House speaker remains noncommittal on Ukraine aid after open letter from global parliament leaders\par \par \uc2 The leaders of 23 parliaments across the world have signed a letter to Mike Johnson, the Republican speaker of the House of Representatives, urging him to allow a vote on more military aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe that thanks to your personal leadership, the Congress will demonstrate historic bipartisan unity in support of the collective effort to assist Ukraine; therefore we ask you to take the next step toward adopting a historic decision on HR815 that will secure US assistance to foreign countries and provide Ukraine with the necessary funds to continue its fight,\u8221\'20\'1D reads {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/stefanchuk.official/posts/pfbid038GY1ThTaWek3k9naA3U5koYkoaDM6HX1GWeKFW5iXTHtPr59UNzCbZ1Prh1KuZ6Zl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the letter}}}\uc2 , which was organized by \uc2 Ruslan Stefanchuk\uc2 , the chair of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s parliament, the Verkhovna Rada.\par \par \uc2 It has been signed by the leaders of several European parliaments and legislatures, including in France, Spain, Austria and Italy.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has been noncommittal about holding a vote to approve Ukraine aid after earlier this month killing a bipartisan Senate deal that would have authorized assistance to Kyiv as well as Israel and Taiwan in exchange for stricter immigration policies.\par \par \uc2 In response to the letter from the parliaments, Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s office said:\par \par \uc2 While Speaker Johnson believes we must confront Putin, and is exploring steps to effectively do so, as he said at the White House, his immediate priority is funding America\u8217\'20\'19s government and avoiding a shut down.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s deposition is happening with the oversight and judiciary committees behind closed doors, so we don\u8217\'20\'19t know what he\u8217\'20\'19s telling the lawmakers, or what they are asking him.\par \par \uc2 But Florida Democratic congressman \uc2 Jared Moskowitz\uc2  says that it has thus far been \u8220\'20\'1CBORING\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrSitting in the Depo now. BORING! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6kwtsIBG7v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6kwtsIBG7v}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jared Moskowitz\uc2  ?? (@JaredEMoskowitz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JaredEMoskowitz/status/1762865408506290483?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The top Democrat on the House oversight committee, \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , described the Republican impeachment investigation into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccomedy of errors\u8221\'20\'1D, and said the GOP has failed to prove its corruption allegations against the president.\par \par \uc2 He made the remarks as \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  testified before the committee:\par \par \uc2 enltr"This has been a comedy of errors from the beginning." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRaskin?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepRaskin}}}\uc2  says there is no evidence that President Biden was involved in \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's business dealings, that the impeachment inquiry does not meet the standard of high crimes and misdemeanors. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GDzUFBRr2I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GDzUFBRr2I}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1762865914209349897?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  took particular umbrage at the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s reliance on discredited sources to attack him and his father.\par \par \uc2 The weaknesses of some of the evidence Republicans have used to claim corruption on his part and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s became apparent earlier this month when Alexander Smirnov, a former \uc2 FBI\uc2  informant, was indicted for lying to the government, and prosecutors later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/22/fbi-informant-biden-alexander-smirnov-arrest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  that information he had provided about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  came from Russian intelligence.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Biden told the oversight and judiciary committees about that:\par \par \uc2 You have built your entire partisan house of cards on lies told by the likes of Gal Luft, Tony Bobulinski, Alexander Smirnov and Jason Galanis. Luft, who is a fugitive, has been indicted for his lies and other crimes; Smirnov, who has made you dupes in carrying out a Russian disinformation campaign waged against my father, has been indicted for his lies; Bobulinski, who has been exposed for the many false statements he has made, and Galanis, who is serving 14 years in prison for fraud. Rather than follow the facts as they have been laid out before you in bank records, financial statements, correspondence and other witness testimony, you continue your frantic search to prove the lies you, and those you rely on, keep peddling. Yes, they are lies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  says father was 'never' involved in businesses, attacks 'partisan political pursuit of my dad' - report\par \par \uc2 In his opening statement to the House oversight and judiciary committees, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  said his father has \u8220\'20\'1Cnever\u8221\'20\'1D been involved in any of his business ventures, and decried the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s campaign to impeach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over unproven claims of corruption.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am here today to provide the Committees with the one uncontestable fact that should end the false premise of this inquiry: I did not involve my father in my business. Not while I was a practicing lawyer, not in my investments or transactions domestic or international, not as a board member, and not as an artist. Never,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  said in the statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/hunter-biden-opening-statement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained by Punchbowl News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He then went on to attack the GOP for its pursuit of his father:\par \par \uc2 For more than a year, your Committees have hunted me in your partisan political pursuit of my dad. You have trafficked in innuendo, distortion, and sensationalism \u8211\'20\'13 all the while ignoring the clear and convincing evidence staring you in the face. You do not have evidence to support the baseless and MAGA-motivated conspiracies about my father because there isn\u8217\'20\'19t any.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  has arrived on Capitol Hill for his behind-closed-doors deposition before the Republican-led House oversight and judiciary committees, which are leading the impeachment of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrHunter Biden arrives on Capitol Hill for closed-door deposition. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/w5uO8lNJmX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/w5uO8lNJmX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1762856994359119907?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Republicans have for years said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  illicitly benefited from his son Hunter\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings overseas, but have yet to turn up any proof. Today, Republican oversight committee chair James Comer was asked about this, leading to a testy back and forth with a reporter:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJamesComer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepJamesComer}}}\uc2  is asked about evidence relating to the Biden investigation.\par \par \uc2 Q: "I'm asking you to back up your evidence...You're not answering my question."\par \par \uc2 Comer: "No. I am answering your question. You don't understand what we've said over and over and over..." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fgtubPWZK2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fgtubPWZK2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1762861213627642233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Democratic party chair, \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , said he expects this year\u8217\'20\'19s election in Michigan will be \u8220\'20\'1Cclose and tough\u8221\'20\'1D for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but the president will ultimately win the state:\par \par \uc2 enltrFor all the \u8220\'20\'1Cbut 2016 folks\u8221\'20\'1D, understand this\u8230\'20\'26 today\u8217\'20\'19s MI Dem Party and DNC operations and infrastructure are in stark contrast to the \u8216\'20\'1816 party operations & infrastructure. We have made great strides and improvements over the years and we will not take anything or any voter\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  (@harrisonjaime) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/harrisonjaime/status/1762841974988567038?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Democrats have long counted on support from Michigan voters, but that faith was rattled in 2016, when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the state, part of a collapse in Democratic support along the Great Lakes that was crucial in putting him into the White House. Biden won Michigan back in 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the \u8220\'20\'1Cuncommitted\u8221\'20\'1D campaign\u8217\'20\'19s success in the Michigan Democratic primary, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/laughland-oliver"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Laughland}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Standing before shimmering gold curtains on Tuesday evening, the mayor of Dearborn, Abdullah Hammoud, spoke with pride about his city.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had the audacity to choose people over political party,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had the damn audacity to put people over president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For many gathered at this sprawling banquet hall in the heart of America\u8217\'20\'19s most concentrated Muslim population, the outcome of last night\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic primary in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2  was beyond even the boldest of predictions.\par \par \uc2 Although {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  took the state, it was the hastily organized but committed grassroots campaign against the president\u8217\'20\'19s support for the Israeli government\u8217\'20\'19s war with Gaza that took the night. Organizers with Listen to Michigan, a group that urged voters to withdraw support for Biden and instead vote uncommitted, had hoped for a showing of 10,000 votes. They {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/27/biden-wins-michigan-primary-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 returned more than 100,000}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a clear demonstration of the growing fractures among the diverse coalition that brought Biden to power in 2020.\par \par \uc2 It is a warning shot to the Democratic party, and shows more signs of expanding than diminishing as the primary season wears on.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/28/michigan-uncommitted-vote-biden-israel-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Uncommitted\u8217\'20\'19 vote in Michigan a warning shot over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s support of Israel}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Also declaring victory is Abandon Biden, a group opposed to the president for his support of Israel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s primary last night, we witnessed not just a rejection of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  but a searing condemnation of his presidency\u8217\'20\'19s moral vacuity. Election results reveal that precincts with Arab and Muslim American populations have gone from supporting Biden by 90% in 2020 to thoroughly rejecting Biden,\u8221\'20\'1D the group said in a press release.\par \par \uc2 It continued:\par \par \uc2 Our call to \u8216\'20\'18Abandon Biden\u8217\'20\'19 wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just heard; it roared across Michigan, echoing our refusal to stand with a president whose policies reek of genocide.\par \par \uc2 The unprecedented support for \u8216\'20\'18uncommitted\u8217\'20\'19 in Michigan makes it clear that complicity in genocide isn\u8217\'20\'19t up for debate. It also signals that what awaits Biden in November isn\u8217\'20\'19t a guaranteed victory. And what awaits the Democratic Party is irrelevance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 One of the most prominent backers of the \u8220\'20\'1Cuncommitted\u8221\'20\'1D campaign is Abraham Aiyash, the Democratic majority leader of Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s house of representatives.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Aiyash, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AbrahamAiyash/status/1762456371084034516"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2  is the first Arab American to hold his leadership position in the country, had to say about the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s performance last night:\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump is by far the worst and most reckless candidate running for president and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hasn\u8217\'20\'19t done enough to stop the mass slaughter and suffering of the Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 We can and will demand more from POTUS. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/uncommitted?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #uncommitted}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Abraham Aiyash (@AbrahamAiyash) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AbrahamAiyash/status/1762456371084034516?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'Uncommitted' campaign backers say they sent Biden a message with success in Michigan\par \par \uc2 A group supporting the campaign to vote \u8220\'20\'1Cuncommitted\u8221\'20\'1D in Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic primary in protest of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s policy towards Israel have claimed victory and said the president must back a ceasefire in Gaza to win their voters.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Listen to Michigan, one of the groups that organized the write-in campaign, which received about 13% of the vote statewide:\par \par \uc2 enltrOur movement emerged victorious tonight and massively surpassed our expectations. Tens of thousands of Michigan Democrats, many of whom who voted for Biden in 2020, are uncommitted to his re-election due to the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 #ListenToMichigan (@Listen2michigan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Listen2michigan/status/1762672891995250774?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden has funded the bombs falling on the family members of people who live right here in Michigan. People who voted for him, who now feel completely betrayed.\par \par \uc2 President Biden, listen to Michigan. Count us out, Joe.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 #ListenToMichigan (@Listen2michigan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Listen2michigan/status/1762672916993356043?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrCount Michigan uncommitted for funding of war and genocide in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 While we\u8217\'20\'19ve noticed a small shift in language from Biden as a direct result of this campaign\u8217\'20\'19s pressure, we know that his words are not enough. This isn\u8217\'20\'19t a messaging problem, this is a funding bombs problem.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 #ListenToMichigan (@Listen2michigan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Listen2michigan/status/1762672958084985098?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Strong showing by Gaza protest vote adds to Biden's headaches in swing state Michigan\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. On the surface, things went {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/27/biden-wins-michigan-primary-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about as expected}}}\uc2  in Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s primary last night. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  was the overwhelming pick of the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republicans, who gave him more than 68% support compared to his sole challenger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nearly 27%. Among Democrats, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  won 81% of the vote \u8211\'20\'13 no surprise for a sitting president. But more than 13% of the party\u8217\'20\'19s voters opted not to vote for Biden and rather write in \u8220\'20\'1Cuncommitted\u8221\'20\'1D as part of a campaign to protest his administration\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel and refusal to press for a ceasefire in its invasion of Gaza. In Dearborn, home to large communities of Arabs and Muslims, the write-ins {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cityofdearborn.org/documents/city-departments/city-clerk/elections/election-results/2024-election-results/8308-february-27-2024-primary-election-unofficial-results-as-of-10-15-p-m/file"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 beat the president}}}\uc2  by more than 50 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 The general election is eight months away, but the protest was nonetheless another worrying sign for Biden, whose re-election campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/2024/michigan/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been rattled by polls}}}\uc2  showing him down against Trump in several swing states, including Michigan. The president now seems tasked with not just winning over a state that was crucial both to his victory in 2020 and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s in 2016, but winning back a community whose support could prove pivotal to deciding the election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  will finally give behind-closed-doors testimony before the House committees trying to impeach his father, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/hunter-biden-contempt-congress-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after much drama}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A government shutdown still looms, despite a meeting at the White House yesterday between Biden and the leaders of Congress, where all sides pledged to ensure it does not happen. They have until Friday to make good on that.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House press secretary, duels with reporters at 2.30pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240228ek2s0028n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
