\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Alabama IVF ruling leaves Republicans stuck between their base and the broader public\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 1,022 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 February 2024\par 19:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Amid a lack of popular support for fetal \u8216\'20\'18personhood\u8217\'20\'19, GOP seeks to support IVF without drawing attention to its record of undermining it\par \par \uc2 Republicans have been forced to stake an uncomfortable position between their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  base and the wider American public, as fallout from an Alabama supreme court ruling that embryos are \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D continues into a second week.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Democrats have seized on the issue as the forewarned conclusion of decades of Republican policies to restrict reproductive rights, and pointed to contraceptives as the next frontier for restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans are in a pretty tough spot, because not only have they aligned themselves with the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, but they really need the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a legal expert on the history of reproduction, and the \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2  professor of law at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey can\u8217\'20\'19t win without anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  base voters,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The fallout is likely to continue through the week as the US senator Tammy Duckworth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/02/27/duckworth-ivf-senate-vote-00143509"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeks to force a vote}}}\uc2  on a bill to enshrine protection for IVF in federal law, a prospect that has been met with palpable Republican squirming.\par \par \uc2 In one example, when the Republican US senator \uc2 Joni Ernst\uc2  was asked whether she believed embryos were children, she told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/ivf-alabama-republicans_n_65de30c5e4b005b85831e99b?a7f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Huffington Post}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to say they\u8217\'20\'19re not children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There has also been strong grassroots pushback. On Wednesday, families and advocates are expected to rally at the Alabama state capitol against the state supreme court ruling. The US health and human services secretary, \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 , is expected to appear in Alabama on Tuesday evening alongside families harmed by the decision.\par \par \uc2 A growing number of Americans say they know someone who has received fertility services, and an overwhelming majority of American women say they have received advice on fertility, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2023/09/14/a-growing-share-of-americans-say-theyve-had-fertility-treatments-or-know-someone-who-has/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew Research Center}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrats are also seeking to make the connection between Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s IVF decision and birth control restrictions, which are likely to alienate voters. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/02/26/us/politics/republicans-birth-control-ivf.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 All but eight Republicans}}}\uc2  opposed a bill to protect contraception that was proposed immediately after Roe v Wade was overturned in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have been \u8220\'20\'1Canti-family and anti-women at every turn, and that has proven to be a losing issue for Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D, said the Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee chair, Suzan DelBene, in a press call on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CCome November, we\u8217\'20\'19ll take back the House of Representative to enshrine the protections of Roe once and for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Alabama supreme court threw assisted-reproductive treatments in the state into chaos last week when it issued a decision that said embryos created for IVF were \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D. The decision forced three in eight clinics to pause treatments, and left would-be parents who were undergoing expensive and taxing treatment with few options.\par \par \uc2 By bestowing embryos with the rights of children, the core idea of fetal \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonhood\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/31/opinion/abortion-fetal-personhood.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed by the anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  movement}}}\uc2 , justices threw into question multiple stages of the IVF process.\par \par \uc2 Among myriad questions, it was no longer clear whether parents had the right to destroy genetically abnormal embryos or whether that would be considered \u8220\'20\'1Cwrongful death\u8221\'20\'1D; whether doctors could be held liable for embryos that failed; or whether a person could be forced to have all created embryos implanted in their uterus.\par \par \uc2 Clinics that paused treatments cited the potential for civil and criminal liability for doctors, if they were to continue. Additionally, at least one company that ships frozen embryos said it would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/news/2024/02/companies-that-transport-frozen-embryos-stop-operations-in-alabama.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pause business in Alabama}}}\uc2 , making it more difficult for couples to move embryos out of state.\par \par \uc2 The fallout \u8211\'20\'13 upheaval in the industry, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/24/us-infertility-patients-ivf-alabama-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sorrow among families}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/23/fertility-doctors-reaction-alabama-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rage among doctors}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 has been cheered by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, the fiercest proponents of fetal \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonhood\u8221\'20\'1D, and met by backpedaling from Republicans, who have tied themselves intimately to the movement despite a lack of popular support.\par \par \uc2 The powerful Christian legal group \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  described Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s decision to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-68366337"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BBC}}}\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Ctremendous victory for life\u8221\'20\'1D. The president of one of the largest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy groups in the country, Lila Rose of Live Action, said the decision is \u8220\'20\'1Can important step towards applying equal protection for all\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have flailed in response to the decision, seeking a middle ground that voices support for IVF without drawing attention to their own record of undermining its legality.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers on the right in Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/27/fetal-personhood-ivf-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 postponed a \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonhood\u8221\'20\'1D bill}}}\uc2  in light of the fallout. The Republican Alabama senator Tommy Tuberville {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/tommy-tuberville-alabama-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 floundered when asked}}}\uc2  about the IVF decision.\par \par \uc2 Republican governors \uc2 Bill Lee\uc2  of Tennessee, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  of Georgia and \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2  of New Hampshire all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/02/22/ivf-ruling-embryos-alabama-00142625"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voiced support for IVF}}}\uc2  following the decision, as did former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the presumptive Republican presidential nominee. Republican and Democratic Alabama lawmakers said they were working on a bill to protect IVF treatments.\par \par \uc2 But Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 attempt to put daylight between themselves and the decision is complicated \u8211\'20\'13 not least because all of Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court justices are Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe strongest Trump voters are self-professed evangelical Christians who often believe in personhood\u8221\'20\'1D, or the idea that fertilized eggs should have the same rights as people, said Ziegler.\par \par \uc2 Trump himself nominated and confirmed three of the conservative \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices who ultimately overturned Roe v Wade, which paved the way for the Alabama decision. One of those justices, \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/01/amy-coney-barrett-supported-group-fertilization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 publicly supported an organization}}}\uc2  that said the discarding of embryos in IVF ought to be criminalized.\par \par \uc2 Virtually every Republican who has spent significant time in office, at either the state or federal level, has offered material or rhetorical support for the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. As a party, Republicans have done so knowing there are reliable and motivated voters energized by the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. Any strong rebuke of the core tenets of the ruling \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonhood\u8221\'20\'1D in particular \u8211\'20\'13 could imperil that support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a scenario where Republicans can say: \u8216\'20\'18Hey, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to cut it out on this personhood stuff because you\u8217\'20\'19re killing us,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ziegler.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240228ek2s0025u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
