\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  extremists in the US are waging a holy war against women\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,306 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 February 2024\par 14:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republicans aren\u8217\'20\'19t content with just forcing women to give birth, they are intent on controlling all facets of reproductive healthcare, as we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing in Alabama\par \par \uc2 The holy war on IVF\par \par \uc2 Friends, Romans, frozen extrauterine children, lend me your ears. Except for the extrauterine children, that is \u8211\'20\'13 they obviously don\u8217\'20\'19t have ears. Nor do they have fully formed brains, nervous systems or organs. Nevertheless, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 in a decision which has which paved the way for two wrongful death suits to proceed against a fertility clinic \u8211\'20\'13 frozen embryos are \u8220\'20\'1Cchildren\u8221\'20\'1D and should be treated as such.\par \par \uc2 So what does this mean? Well, in the immediate term it means that if you\u8217\'20\'19re going through fertility treatments in Alabama your life just got upended. Numerous embryos tend to be created and then frozen during the IVF process because it maximizes the chances of success, is more cost-effective and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2024/02/23/1233023637/ivf-alabama-frozen-embryo-personhood-abortion-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reduces the health risks}}}\uc2  of the procedure. Surplus embryos are then disposed of or donated. If every frozen embryo is suddenly deemed a child, it means that disposing of the embryo \u8211\'20\'13 or having a machine malfunction and accidentally ruin an embryo \u8211\'20\'13 would be a criminal act. It even throws into question the standard practice of freezing embryos. After all, you wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t stick a child in a freezer, would you?\par \par \uc2 In short, a handful of Republican judges in Alabama have effectively made IVF too legally dangerous to practice in the state. Already at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/university-alabama-pauses-ivf-services-court-rules-embryos-are-childre-rcna139846"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three fertility providers}}}\uc2  in Alabama have said that they are pausing IVF because of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/23/fertility-doctors-reaction-alabama-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 risks}}}\uc2 . This is unbelievably cruel to people currently going through fertility treatments that, even in the best of times, can take a major emotional, physical and financial toll.\par \par \uc2 While the Alabama decision is unprecedented and shocking, it\u8217\'20\'19s far from surprising. It has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/sep/24/republicans-ivf-abortion-week-in-patriarchy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clear for a while now}}}\uc2  that IVF could be at real risk because of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists. Several \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonhood\u8221\'20\'1D bills, which define life as beginning at the moment of fertilization have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-us-supreme-court-health-government-and-politics-constitutions-93c27f3132ecc78e913120fe4d6c0977"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced across the US}}}\uc2 , resulting in a mess of thorny legal questions about what it means to treat fertilized eggs, embryos and fetuses as people. For example: can you claim a fetus as a dependent on your tax return? In Georgia, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/08/02/1115204443/georgia-fetus-pregnant-dependent-taxes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has a fetal personhood law}}}\uc2 , you can! Pregnant people can also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wabe.org/georgia-hov-lanes-now-open-for-pregnant-people-state-officials-confirm/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drive in the high-occupancy lane}}}\uc2 , which requires two or more passengers, to be in the car. The Alabama ruling is a major victory for the growing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/health-law-and-business/alabama-embryo-ruling-gives-boost-to-fetal-personhood-movement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fetal personhood movement}}}\uc2  : expect IVF to come under scrutiny in many more states.\par \par \uc2 But hang on a minute, you might say. I thought all these anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists wanted more kids in the world. Why would they force people who don\u8217\'20\'19t want children to give birth and then also try and strip fertility treatments from people who desperately want children?\par \par \uc2 There are a lot of answers to this question. The politest one is that many of the people arguing that embryos are people have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/23/fertility-doctors-reaction-alabama-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 zero understanding of reproductive medicine}}}\uc2 . Certainly the Alabama supreme court justices seem more concerned with theology than biology. Their ruling seems to have been heavily influenced by the Bible and repeatedly references God and biblical scholars. Chief Justice Thomas Parker, for example, wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CHuman life cannot be wrongfully destroyed without incurring the wrath of a holy God \u8230\'20\'26 even before birth, all human beings bear the image of God, and their lives cannot be destroyed without effacing his glory.\u8221\'20\'1D (If this is true, by the way, then God must have incurred a lot of wrath towards Alabama: the state has one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eji.org/alabama-executions/#:~:text=Alabama%20consistently%20has%20one%20of,voted%20for%20a%20life%20sentence."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highest execution rates in the}}}\uc2  US and recently made headlines for executing a prisoner with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2024/jan/26/official-describes-untested-nitrogen-hypoxia-execution-of-kenneth-smith-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nitrogen gas}}}\uc2 , an untested method that the \uc2 UN\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-68371430"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned as cruel}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 While IVF care in Alabama is currently in a state of turmoil, there is some good news. A few prominent Republicans, spooked by the fallout from the Alabama ruling have gone {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/tv/something-is-totally-wrong-matt-gaetz-reacts-to-alabama-decision-imperiling-ivf/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 into damage control mode}}}\uc2  and are trying to get the law\u8217\'20\'19s impact on IVF clarified. Even Donald Trump has stepped in to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-ivf-abortion-alabama-republicans-8215336740a5963b57bbd970b47bb3a7?taid=65d8f6cf436cd10001530a90&utm_campaign=TrueAnthem&utm_medium=AP&utm_source=Twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 say he supports IVF}}}\uc2 . The Alabama attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office has also said it won\u8217\'20\'19t prosecute IVF {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/02/23/us/alabama-ivf-embryos-supreme-court-ruling-legislation/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 families or providers}}}\uc2 . Still, that\u8217\'20\'19s little comfort when you look at the bigger picture: Republicans aren\u8217\'20\'19t content with just forcing women to give birth, they are intent on controlling all facets of reproductive healthcare. Bill by bill, ruling after ruling, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement in America is chipping away at everything from access to fertility treatments to birth control. There may be a lot of uncertainty around the ruling in Alabama but one thing is very clear: anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists in the US are waging a holy war against women.\par \par \uc2 The weird way Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s embryo ruling takes on artificial wombs\par \par \uc2 The Alabama ruling specifies that an embryo is a child \u8220\'20\'1Cregardless of its location\u8221\'20\'1D. As the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.technologyreview.com/2024/02/23/1088851/alabama-court-embryo-artificial-wombs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MIT Technology Review notes}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis could have implications for future technologies in development, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/artificial-wombs-for-premature-babies-might-soon-begin-human-trials-180982949/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 artificial wombs}}}\uc2  or synthetic embryos made from stem cells.\u8221\'20\'1D The ruling doesn\u8217\'20\'19t just threaten current fertility treatment, it threatens the future of reproductive technology.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley tries to walk back comments on Alabama ruling\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, embryos, to me, are babies,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4481497-haley-on-alabama-ivf-ruling-embryos-to-me-are-babies/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Haley told NBC following the Alabama ruling}}}\uc2 . After realizing this may not have been the smartest thing to say for her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/why-nikki-haley-is-continuing-her-seemingly-hopeless-2024-gop-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hopeless presidential election campaign}}}\uc2 , she walked the comments back and said that she didn\u8217\'20\'19t mean to imply she agreed with Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Some landlords are enforcing no-sex clauses\par \par \uc2 Vice takes a look at the British landlords who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/n7ema8/no-sex-tenancy-clauses-landlords"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t want unwed tenants having sex}}}\uc2 . (RIP to Vice, which has become the latest media company to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/feb/22/vice-media-layoffs-cease-publishing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announce mass layoffs}}}\uc2  and will stop publishing on its site.)\par \par \uc2 Can AI porn be ethical?\par \par \uc2 Betteridge\u8217\'20\'19s law of headlines states: \u8220\'20\'1CAny headline that ends in a question mark can be answered by the word no.\u8221\'20\'1D I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/feb/18/ethics-ai-porn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fascinating piece in the Guardian}}}\uc2  is an exception.\par \par \uc2 New York governor apologizes after implying Israel is justified to destroy Gaza\par \par \uc2 Did you perhaps labor under the delusion that women are always more compassionate leaders than men? \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  is here to disabuse you of that notion! The New York governor seems to think that dead and starving children in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2024/jan/30/how-war-destroyed-gazas-neighbourhoods-visual-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  are something to laugh about and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/new-york-governor-apologizes-after-implying-israel-is-justified-destroy-gaza-2024-02-17/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made a joke at a recent event in New York suggesting Israel was right to destroy Gaza}}}\uc2 . She\u8217\'20\'19s now apologized. Still, I urge Hochul to spend some time looking at the devastating videos coming out of Gaza and ask herself why she thinks it\u8217\'20\'19s OK to make light of a situation so traumatizing that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/msf-slams-us-gaza-un-says-children-young-5-want-die-2024-02-22/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kids as young as}}}\uc2  five have told aid workers they want to die.\par \par \uc2 Searching for a \u8216\'20\'18male\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18female\u8217\'20\'19 brain is a waste of time\par \par \uc2 Stanford recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newscientist.com/article/2417690-ai-can-tell-a-persons-sex-from-brain-scans-with-90-per-cent-accuracy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 generated a ton of headlines}}}\uc2  with a study that found AI can distinguish between male and female brain scans with around 90% accuracy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/feb/22/male-female-brains-different-centuries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Neuroscientist Gina Rippon looks in the Guardian}}}\uc2  at why scientists have long been obsessed with trying \u8220\'20\'1Cto find a nice set of biologically programmed, sex-specific differences in the brain\u8221\'20\'1D. Rippon stresses that there is \u8220\'20\'1Clittle or no consistent and conclusive evidence that any brain differences found can be solely attributed to biological sex. Essentialist assumptions like these have negative consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a ruff week in the world of canine world records: Bobi the Portuguese mastiff has been posthumously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/feb/22/bobi-the-portuguese-mastiff-stripped-of-record-as-worlds-oldest-ever-dog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped of his record as the world\u8217\'20\'19s oldest ever dog}}}\uc2  due to insufficient evidence. Record or not I think we can all agree that Bobi was a very good boy.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240224ek2o001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
