\par\par \uc2 Society\par \b \uc2 Doctors shocked and angry as Alabama ruling throws IVF care into turmoil\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 1,441 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 February 2024\par 18:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 29\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Declaration that IVF embryos are \u8216\'20\'18extrauterine children\u8217\'20\'19 means \u8216\'20\'18literally criminalizing standard medical care\u8217\'20\'19, physicians say\par \par \uc2 Doctors are reacting with shock and fury to an Alabama supreme court decision that has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/university-alabama-ivf-embryo-care-paused-supreme-court-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shut down in vitro fertilization}}}\uc2  at the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest infertility clinics.\par \par \uc2 Physicians said the decision, which ruled embryos are \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D, grossly misunderstood reproductive medicine and was \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating\u8221\'20\'1D for infertile patients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe made the impossible decision to pause new IVF treatments at our center, which is devastating for our patients and the state,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Mamie McLean, a fertility specialist at Alabama Fertility, which performed about 700 rounds of IVF in 2023.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur legal team is telling us that, as the ruling is written, that modern fertility treatments cannot continue in the state of Alabama because of the risk to physicians and embryologists, given that embryos are now considered children,\u8221\'20\'1D said McLean.\par \par \uc2 The chief legal officer and general counsel for the \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (ACOG)\uc2 , Molly Meegan, said she expected confusion about how to implement the decision to make IVF \u8220\'20\'1Ceither completely unavailable or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/issue-brief/coverage-and-use-of-fertility-services-in-the-u-s/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 too expensive for most patients}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in Alabama.\par \par \uc2 The Alabama supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision ruled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embryos are \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in a case that arose out of an incident at a Mobile fertility clinic. In December 2020, a patient at the clinic wandered into cryogenic embryo storage, lifted an ultra-cold vessel out of storage, and immediately dropped it when it burned her hand \u8211\'20\'13 destroying the embryos inside.\par \par \uc2 Three couples sued under the state\u8217\'20\'19s wrongful death of a minor statute. A lower court threw out the case, because courts have repeatedly held that embryos are considered property, not people, thus \u8220\'20\'1Cwrongful death\u8221\'20\'1D would not apply. The couples appealed to the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, where a majority of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/alabama-ivf-embryo-extrauterine-children-ruling#:~:text=Alabama's%20supreme%20court%20ruled%20embryos,IVF%20patients%20are%20worried&text=Alabama,The%20Guardian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 justices ruled in their favor}}}\uc2 , deciding that the wrongful death statute applies to \u8220\'20\'1Call unborn children, regardless of their location\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re literally criminalizing standard medical care,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Serena Chen, vice-president of the grassroots group Doctors for Fertility and a reproductive endocrinologist in New Jersey, where she is director of advocacy at CCRM Fertility and a founder of the Institute for Reproductive Medicine and Science.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re legislating malpractice \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19re saying, \u8216\'20\'18You don\u8217\'20\'19t use your normal medical principles, all the training you went through, all your experience\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19re just tossing it out to this arbitrary idea that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have a biological basis,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chen.\par \par \uc2 Already, the decision has forced Fertility Alabama and the \uc2 University of Alabama at Birmingham\uc2  to stop administering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/university-alabama-ivf-embryo-care-paused-supreme-court-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most stages of IVF}}}\uc2 . While other infertility treatments may continue, such as intrauterine insemination, none are as effective as IVF.\par \par \uc2 Doctors said the decision shows a fundamental misunderstanding of reproductive medicine \u8211\'20\'13 with several portions wholly ungrounded in reality. For instance, justices introduced the idea that a \u8220\'20\'1Cfull-term infant or toddler\u8221\'20\'1D could be \u8220\'20\'1Cgestated to term in an in vitro environment\u8221\'20\'1D, when there is no way to gestate an embryo outside a human uterus for longer than roughly seven days.\par \par \uc2 The justices \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly don\u8217\'20\'19t understand IVF at all and clearly don\u8217\'20\'19t understand what these couples are suffering from\u8221\'20\'1D, Chen said. \u8220\'20\'1CAren\u8217\'20\'19t they supposed to learn about the topic before they make these decisions?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Today, about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nccd.cdc.gov/drh_art/rdPage.aspx?rdReport=DRH_ART.ClinicInfo&rdRequestForward=True&ClinicId=9999&ShowNational=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2% of all babies}}}\uc2  born in the US are conceived through in vitro fertilization. To perform a round of IVF, doctors stimulate a patient\u8217\'20\'19s ovaries to produce several eggs. Those eggs are retrieved and fertilized with sperm in vitro, Latin for \u8220\'20\'1Cin glass\u8221\'20\'1D (hence the expression {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2018/jul/08/ivf-in-vitro-fertilisation-louise-brown-born"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ctest tube baby\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  ), creating embryos that consist of a group of a few hundred cells and are called blastocysts. Doctors typically implant one or two of the embryos in a patient\u8217\'20\'19s womb around the sixth day of the embryo\u8217\'20\'19s development.\par \par \uc2 At each of these stages, it is expected that some number of embryos will fail to develop. There are eggs that may not fertilize, fertilized eggs that may not become embryos and embryos that will never produce a healthy baby. Doctors often refer to this as the \u8220\'20\'1Cinefficiency of reproduction\u8221\'20\'1D, and it is why IVF typically relies on the creation of multiple embryos to succeed.\par \par \uc2 There are other points of failure in the process as well: embryos may be discarded because of irregular genetic test results; others may not survive the freeze-thaw process of cryogenic storage, which allows couples to save embryos for potential future rounds of IVF.\par \par \uc2 Meegan said calling an embryo \u8211\'20\'13 any embryo \u8211\'20\'13 a \u8220\'20\'1Cchild\u8221\'20\'1D calls multiple stages of the IVF process into question. \u8220\'20\'1CCan you freeze an embryo at all? Do you need to implant every embryo that exists in Alabama?\u8221\'20\'1D she asked.\par \par \uc2 There are more questions. Must frozen embryos be maintained in perpetuity? That\u8217\'20\'19s an expensive proposition given the cost of storage. Must all embryos be implanted into a patient\u8217\'20\'19s womb at once? That increases the odds of multiples, which are risky for both mother and child. And, if every embryo\u8217\'20\'19s failure could lead to a wrongful death suit, how can doctors possibly carry enough liability insurance to practice?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is what you get when you have non-medical individuals, who don\u8217\'20\'19t really understand what they\u8217\'20\'19re talking about, making decisions like this,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Jennifer Bakkensen, an endocrinologist and assistant professor of obstetrics and gynecology at the Warren Alpert Medical School of Brown University in Rhode Island.\par \par \uc2 Fertility is of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ama-assn.org/medical-residents/medical-resident-wellness/ama-backs-resident-physicians-access-fertility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 special concern to female physicians}}}\uc2 . Residents typically finish training at 31.6 years of age, which are prime reproductive years. Female physicians {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamanetworkopen/fullarticle/2807657?resultClick=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suffer infertility at twice the rate}}}\uc2  of the general population, because demanding careers push many to delay starting a family.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis not only affects patients but also colleagues who rely on these kinds of technologies to build their families,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bakkensen. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you have legislation or decisions like this, basically if this decision holds, [it] would prohibit the practice of modern fertility care as we know it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Alabama supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to grant embryos the rights of \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jul/25/states-using-fetal-personhood-laws-to-criminalize-mothers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stems directly from anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  activism}}}\uc2 , and is part of a nationwide push to establish {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/21/us/abortion-anti-fetus-person.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fetal personhood}}}\uc2 . Doctors in Oklahoma are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kfor.com/news/oklahoma-legislature/efforts-to-adopt-personhood-at-conception-convict-abortion-pill-orders-as-drug-trafficking/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 actively fighting a proposed ballot measure}}}\uc2  that, if passed, would enshrine the idea that life begins at conception in the state constitution. Eleven states, including Alabama, have personhood language in their laws, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pregnancyjusticeus.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/fetal-personhood-with-appendix-UPDATED-1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Pregnancy Justice}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision is one in a series of decisions that have been attempting to create {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/clinical-information/policy-and-position-statements/position-statements/2022/acog-statement-on-personhood-measures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this concept of personhood}}}\uc2  around an embryo that is likely to have additional downstream ramifications over months and years to come,\u8221\'20\'1D said Meegan. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pregnancyjusticeus.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/fetal-personhood-with-appendix-UPDATED-1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concept}}}\uc2  could have far-reaching implications on everything from criminal and family law to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/04/us/georgia-abortion-law-fetus-tax-dependent.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tax}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/09/13/texas-personhood-laws-abortion-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 traffic violations}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Personhood has been a goal of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/the-personhood-movement-timeline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly the moment}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was legalized nationally in 1973 in the Roe v Wade case. For nearly 50 years, the rights granted in that decision protected against \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonhood\u8221\'20\'1D statutes and decisions.\par \par \uc2 But Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise in June 2022 cleared the way for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14 states}}}\uc2  and pushed fetal personhood to the forefront, paving the way for the Alabama decision.\par \par \uc2 Meegan said the \uc2 ACOG\uc2 , the \uc2 American Medical Association\uc2  (AMA) and the \uc2 Society for Maternal-Fetal Medicine\uc2  (SMFM) have all been in \u8220\'20\'1Crapid response\u8221\'20\'1D mode since the Dobbs decision, writing briefs to state courts to fight \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 The Alabama Medical Association argued forcefully against such an outcome in an amicus, or \u8220\'20\'1Cfriend of the court\u8221\'20\'1D, brief in the Alabama case. In an email to the Guardian, a spokesperson for the association said the group had \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave concerns\u8221\'20\'1D about how the decision will affect reproductive medicine in the state. Similarly, the \uc2 American Society for Reproductive Medicine\uc2  (\uc2 ASRM\uc2 ) called the decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.asrm.org/news-and-events/asrm-news/press-releasesbulletins/asrm-condemns-dangerous-court-decision-alabama/?_t_tags=siteid:01216f06-3dc9-4ac9-96da-555740dd020c,language:en&_t_hit.id=ASRM_Models_Pages_ContentPage/_452aa234-8e02-4a48-9f63-24d32882ed03_en&_t_hit.pos=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cprofoundly misguided and dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , a statement the SMFM supported, saying it stood in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MySMFM/status/1760324753317896639?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong opposition\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s been a real drawing together of the house of medicine, and an understanding that the ramifications here are severe\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D, said Meegan. For McLean, the only \u8220\'20\'1Csilver lining\u8221\'20\'1D is the support she has received from other doctors within and outside the state.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, not all doctors feel the medical community has been aggressive enough. Chen said there was \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely not enough\u8221\'20\'1D action from the medical community to meet the moment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs doctors, we\u8217\'20\'19re trained to try to be apolitical, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has such violent connotations \u8211\'20\'13 literally physicians have been killed over this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D Chen said. However, \u8220\'20\'1CIf we as doctors and healthcare providers don\u8217\'20\'19t do something, say something, we are not serving our patients.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240223ek2n001ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
