\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden calls \u8216\'20\'18disregard\u8217\'20\'19 for reproductive rights in conservative push \u8216\'20\'18outrageous\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 4,964 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 February 2024\par 21:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on fallout in Alabama after the court\u8217\'20\'19s IVF decision, read our latest report:Second Alabama provider stops IVF care after court deems embryos \u8216\'20\'18children\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Democrats channeled their outrage over an Alabama supreme court ruling that has curbed IVF care in the state, with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign saying \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d778118f086f23f6db1368#block-65d778118f086f23f6db1368"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is to blame}}}\uc2 . Republican strategists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d788428f089db0bc972b65#block-65d788428f089db0bc972b65"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are reportedly nervous}}}\uc2  about the decision targeting the procedure many people rely on to start families, and warn it could blow back on the party ahead of the November elections. Biden has meanwhile found himself in hot water {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d756578f0877292bb3594a#block-65d756578f0877292bb3594a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with progressives}}}\uc2  after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d74b4c8f086f23f6db107e#block-65d74b4c8f086f23f6db107e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports emerged}}}\uc2  that he is considering implementing policies to stop migrants from crossing the border with Mexico. The president spent the day in San Francisco, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d7a11b8f089db0bc972c78#block-65d7a11b8f089db0bc972c78"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he met}}}\uc2  with the wife and daughter of Russian opposition figure \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 , and pledged new sanctions against Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A second Alabama IVF provider{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d77c498f089db0bc972ab0#block-65d77c498f089db0bc972ab0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paused their treatments}}}\uc2  after the state supreme court ruling.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Washington{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d7a1ff8f089db0bc972c7e#block-65d7a1ff8f089db0bc972c7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also plans}}}\uc2  to sanction Iran for selling weapons to Russia, which it has used in its invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d7853b8f086f23f6db1460#block-65d7853b8f086f23f6db1460"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he has no problem with IVF.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Byron Donalds, a rightwing Florida congressman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d7741a8f0877292bb35b48#block-65d7741a8f0877292bb35b48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened}}}\uc2  to shut down the government if tougher immigration laws weren\u8217\'20\'19t passed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moscow{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d7a1a58f089db0bc972c7c#block-65d7a1a58f089db0bc972c7c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received a warning}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 US government\uc2  amid reports that it is planning to launch a nuclear-armed anti-satellite weapon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke briefly to reporters in San Francisco about his meeting with \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s family, and said the sanctions he will announce tomorrow will target \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden noted that he blamed the Russian leader for Navalny\u8217\'20\'19s death. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden: "This morning I had the honor of meeting with \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 's wife and daughter...we're going to be announcing sanctions against Putin, who is responsible for his death, tomorrow." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5JSWRssnUY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5JSWRssnUY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1760768344276255068?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  was none too pleased with comments \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  made about him while in San Francisco, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/pjotr-sauer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pjotr Sauer}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has described as \u8220\'20\'1Crude\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments in which the American president called the Russian leader a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazy SOB\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden was talking about the climate crisis on Wednesday when he said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a crazy SOB like Putin and others, and we always have to worry about nuclear conflict, but the existential threat to humanity is climate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, after a flight onboard a strategic bomber that is capable of carrying nuclear warheads, Putin responded \u8220\'20\'1Cyes, rude\u8221\'20\'1D to a reporter who said Biden had made a rude remark about him.\par \par \uc2 Referring to earlier remarks in which the Russian leader {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/feb/15/vladimir-putin-tucker-carlson-interview-footage-sharp-questions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said Biden was a preferable president}}}\uc2  for Russia than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Putin joked: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not like he can say to me, \u8216\'20\'18Volodya, thank you, well done, you\u8217\'20\'19ve helped me a lot\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added with a smile: \u8220\'20\'1CYou asked me which is better for us. I said it then that, and I still think I can repeat it: Biden.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin earlier in the day said Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments were a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgrace\u8221\'20\'1D for the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe use of such language against the head of another state by the president of the United States is unlikely to infringe on our president, President Putin,\u8221\'20\'1D the Kremlin spokesperson, Dmitry Peskov, said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it debases those who use such vocabulary.\u8221\'20\'1D The remarks were \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably some kind of attempt to look like a Hollywood cowboy\u8221\'20\'1D, Peskov added.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/22/joe-biden-vladimir-putin-crazy-sob-donald-trump-alexei-navalny"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vladimir Putin says Joe Biden was rude to call him a \u8216\'20\'18crazy SOB\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Daily Mail reports that protesters demanding \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  support a ceasefire in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza have entered the hotel where the president is in San Francisco:\par \par \uc2 enltrGaza Ceasefire protestors have got into Biden's hotel in San Francisco. Chanting: Biden Biden you can't hide, we charge you with genocide ' {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DnnALEot1m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DnnALEot1m}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rob Crilly (@robcrilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/robcrilly/status/1760759193362133022?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden has repeatedly had his speeches and events interrupted by protesters upset over his administration\u8217\'20\'19s policies towards Israel in the wake of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 7 October attack:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/31/biden-pro-palestine-protest-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pro-Palestinian protesters at Biden events cast shadow on his re-election effort}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has released photos of his meeting with \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wife and daughter in San Francisco:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, I met with Yulia and Dasha Navalnaya \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Aleksey Navalny\uc2 's loved ones \u8211\'20\'13 to express my condolences for their devastating loss.\par \par \uc2 Aleksey's legacy of courage will live on in Yulia and Dasha, and the countless people across Russia fighting for democracy and human rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aiCcgTrws3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/aiCcgTrws3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1760752933866512580?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden expressed 'heartfelt condolences' in meeting with Navalny family, pledged new sanctions\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  offered his condolences to the wife and daughter of Russian opposition figure \uc2 Aleksey Navalny\uc2  in a meeting today, and pledged stricter sanctions on \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s government in Moscow, the White House announced:\par \par \uc2 President Biden met with Yulia and Dasha Navalnaya today in San Francisco to express his heartfelt condolences for their terrible loss following the death of \uc2 Aleksey Navalny\uc2  in a Russian prison. The President expressed his admiration for \uc2 Aleksey Navalny\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s extraordinary courage and his legacy of fighting against corruption and for a free and democratic Russia in which the rule of law applies equally to everyone. The President emphasized that Aleksey\u8217\'20\'19s legacy will carry on through people across Russia and around the world mourning his loss and fighting for freedom, democracy, and human rights. He affirmed that his Administration will announce major new sanctions against Russia tomorrow in response to Aleksey\u8217\'20\'19s death, Russia\u8217\'20\'19s repression and aggression, and its brutal and illegal war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US set to unveil new sanctions on Iran over arms to Russia\par \par \uc2 The White House is promising to unveil new sanctions on Iran in the coming days in retaliation for its arms sales that have bolstered Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, and threatening a \u8220\'20\'1Cswift\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csevere\u8221\'20\'1D response if Tehran moves forward with selling ballistic missiles to Moscow, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 National security council spokesman John Kirby said Thursday that the US will be \u8220\'20\'1Cimposing additional sanctions on Iran in the coming days\u8221\'20\'1D for its efforts to supply Russia with drones and other technology for the war against Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 And he issued a new warning to Iran that providing ballistic missiles to Russia for use against Kyiv would be met with even more sanctions and actions at the United Nations.\par \par \uc2 The US has been warning for months of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to acquire ballistic missiles from Iran in return for providing Tehran with enhanced military cooperation.\par \par \uc2 We have not seen any confirmation that missiles have actually moved from Iran to Russia \u8230\'20\'26 [but] we have no reason to believe that they will not follow through.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said that if Iran moves forward:\par \par \uc2 I can assure you that the response from the international community will be swift and it will be severe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said the US would take the matter to the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council, where Russia has a veto.\par \par \uc2 We will implement additional sanctions against Iran and we will coordinate further response options with our allies and partners in Europe and elsewhere. We have demonstrated our ability to take action in response to the military partnership between Russia and Iran in the past. We will do so in the future. In response to Iran\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing support for Russia\u8217\'20\'19s brutal war. We will be imposing additional sanctions on Iran in the coming days. And we are prepared to go further if Iran sells ballistic missiles to Russia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US is set to announce a new set of sanctions Friday against Russia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The United States has directly warned Russia against launching a new nuclear armed anti-satellite weapon, a US official said on Thursday, speaking on condition of anonymity, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 The US official\u8217\'20\'19s comments came two days after a source familiar with the matter told Reuters that the United States believes Russia is developing such a weapon.\par \par \uc2 The detonation of a weapon of this kind, the source said, could disrupt everything from military communications to phone-based ride services.\par \par \uc2 The US official said that Washington had cautioned Russia against launching such a weapon.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal first reported the warning, saying that the United States told Russia that such a weapon would violate the Outer Space Treaty and jeopardize U.S. national security interests.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the Biden-Harris re-election campaign issued a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d778118f086f23f6db1368#block-65d778118f086f23f6db1368"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slamming}}}\uc2  the Alabama court decision over frozen embryos for IVF. Now there\u8217\'20\'19s more from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as he weighs in directly from the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here is the full statement from the US president moments ago:\par \par \uc2 Today, in 2024 in America, women are being turned away from emergency rooms and forced to travel hundreds of miles for health care, while doctors fear prosecution for providing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And now, a court in Alabama put access to some fertility treatments at risk for families who are desperately trying to get pregnant. The disregard for women\u8217\'20\'19s ability to make these decisions for themselves and their families is outrageous and unacceptable.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake: this is a direct result of the overturning of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 I know that folks are worried about what they\u8217\'20\'19re seeing happening to women all across America. I am too. I hear about it everywhere I go. My message is: The Vice President and I are fighting for your rights. We\u8217\'20\'19re fighting for the freedom of women, for families, and for doctors who care for these women. And we won\u8217\'20\'19t stop until we restore the protections of Roe v. Wade in federal law for all women in every state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is campaigning heavily for reproductive rights and against Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 determined crusade against those right. Harris is visiting Grand Rapids, Michigan, today, where the White House said she will continue her nationwide \u8220\'20\'1CFight for Reproductive Freedoms\u8221\'20\'1D tour by convening a roundtable conversation with medical providers, patients, reproductive rights advocates, and state and local leaders. Expect remarks later.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden calls 'disregard' for reproductive rights in conservative push 'outrageous'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has issued a statement sharply criticizing the Alabama state supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision declaring}}}\uc2  embryos kept for IVF as \u8220\'20\'1Cchildren\u8221\'20\'1D, and saying that this and other restrictions from the right on reproductive choice are \u8220\'20\'1Ca direct result of the overturning of Roe v Wade\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a first-of-its-kind decision, the Alabama supreme court ruled last Friday that frozen embryos are \u8220\'20\'1Cchildren\u8221\'20\'1D, allowing two wrongful death suits against a Mobile fertility clinic to proceed. The decision has sweeping implications for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/black-women-infertility-ivf-iui-surrogate-birth-success-story"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 people seeking in vitro fertilization (IVF)}}}\uc2  or other assisted reproductive technology treatments and could increase criminalization of expectant people, my colleague Adria Walker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 The US president issued a statement from the White House on Thursday afternoon saying: \u8220\'20\'1CA court in Alabama put access to some fertility treatments at risk for families who are desperately trying to get pregnant. The disregard for women\u8217\'20\'19s ability to make these decisions for themselves and their families is outrageous and unacceptable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden added: \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake: this is a direct result of the overturning of Roe v Wade.\u8221\'20\'1D The supreme court, as stacked to the right during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, in 2022 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tossed out}}}\uc2  the national right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, almost 50 years after the landmark federal right was granted by a previous court bench.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s more, see next post.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Democrats are channeling their outrage over an Alabama supreme court ruling that has curbed IVF care in the state, with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign saying \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d778118f086f23f6db1368#block-65d778118f086f23f6db1368"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is to blame}}}\uc2 . Indeed, Republican strategists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d788428f089db0bc972b65#block-65d788428f089db0bc972b65"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are nervous}}}\uc2  about the decision against the procedure many people have used to start families, and warn it could blow back on the party ahead of the November elections. Biden has meanwhile found himself in hot water {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d756578f0877292bb3594a#block-65d756578f0877292bb3594a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with progressives}}}\uc2  after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d74b4c8f086f23f6db107e#block-65d74b4c8f086f23f6db107e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports emerged}}}\uc2  that he is considering implementing policies to stop migrants from crossing the border with Mexico. Republican House speaker Mike Johnson, who has repeatedly demanded tougher immigration policies, called Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposals \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d78c3d8f0877292bb35caa#block-65d78c3d8f0877292bb35caa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election year gimmicks}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A second Alabama IVF provider{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d77c498f089db0bc972ab0#block-65d77c498f089db0bc972ab0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paused their treatments}}}\uc2  after the state supreme court ruling.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d7853b8f086f23f6db1460#block-65d7853b8f086f23f6db1460"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he has no problem with IVF.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Byron Donalds, a rightwing Florida congressman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/22/biden-border-crackdown-migrants-us-latest-trump-republicans-congress-updates?page=with:block-65d7741a8f0877292bb35b48#block-65d7741a8f0877292bb35b48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened}}}\uc2  to shut down the government if tougher immigration laws weren\u8217\'20\'19t passed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Johnson says immigration actions Biden is reportedly considering are 'election year gimmicks'\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson is none too impressed by reports that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is considering using his powers under existing law to curb migrants crossing into the United States from Mexico.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Johnson demanded Biden take tougher actions, such as forcing asylum seekers to remain in Mexico while their claims are processed. He also said the reports that the president is wiling to act unilaterally prove that there\u8217\'20\'19s no need for Congress to pass new laws to curb undocumented migrants:\par \par \uc2 Americans have lost faith in this President and won\u8217\'20\'19t be fooled by election year gimmicks that don\u8217\'20\'19t actually secure the border. Nor will they forget that the President created this catastrophe and, until now, has refused to use his executive power to fix it.\par \par \uc2 These reports also underscore just how brazenly and intentionally President Biden misled the public when he claimed he had done everything in his power to secure the border. Specifically, the President\u8217\'20\'19s alleged desire to invoke Section 212(f) of the Immigration and Nationality Act, which the White House dismissed using for months, is particularly telling.\par \par \uc2 If these reports are true and the President intends to take action, he can show he\u8217\'20\'19s serious by changing more than asylum policy. He should begin by reinstituting the \u8216\'20\'18Remain in Mexico\u8217\'20\'19 policy and ending his administration\u8217\'20\'19s abuse of the parole system, along with other critical reforms.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Johnson and his fellow House Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/feb/05/ukraine-israel-aid-border-security-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 torpedoed}}}\uc2  a bipartisan Senate deal that would have authorized another round of military assistance to Ukraine as well as Israel, while also imposing hardline immigration policies. Among Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s objections were his belief that Biden didn\u8217\'20\'19t need any new legislation to stop people from entering from Mexico \u8211\'20\'13 but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also encouraged him to reject the deal, reportedly so he can use frustration with migrants in his campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican strategists are growing worried the Alabama supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision that greatly complicates access to IVF care in the state could harm the party\u8217\'20\'19s candidates nationwide, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/02/21/alabama-ivf-abortion-00142536?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt certainly intersects, badly, with general election politics for Republicans,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Stan Barnes\uc2 , a former Republican state senator from Arizona who is now a political consultant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen a state, any state, takes an aggressive action on this particular topic, people are once again made aware of it and many think: \u8216\'20\'18Maybe I can\u8217\'20\'19t support a Republican in the general election.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Former Donald Trump White House official Kellyanne Conway in December shared polling with congressional Republicans that found IVF care to be widely popular, including with evangelicals, a group that is traditionally anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCandidates for Congress \u8211\'20\'13 and certainly those already serving there \u8211\'20\'13 can bank significant political currency by advocating for increased access to and availability of contraception and fertility treatments,\u8221\'20\'1D Conway\u8217\'20\'19s team told lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 According to Politico, \u8220\'20\'1CThe survey found that 86 percent of all respondents supported access to IVF, with 78 percent support among self-identified \u8216\'20\'18pro-life advocates\u8217\'20\'19 and 83 percent among Evangelical Christians.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While he refrained from commenting on the Alabama ruling, Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , said he supported IVF, noting many people \u8220\'20\'1Cwouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have children if it weren\u8217\'20\'19t for that\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 From an interview with Politico:\par \par \uc2 enltrDays after the \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2  made waves by ruling frozen embryos are children under state law, Georgia Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  voiced his support for IVF.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people out there in this country... wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have children if it weren\u8217\'20\'19t for that,\u8221\'20\'1D he told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POLITICOLive?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POLITICOLive}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/18BAuyb4yb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/18BAuyb4yb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 POLITICO (@politico) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/politico/status/1760714890111557899?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Besides \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , other Democrats are piling on Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court for its decision that curbed IVF care by finding embryos are \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Illinois senator Tammy Duckworth :\par \par \uc2 enltrThe fall of Roe was about so much more than \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u176\'00\'B0\u176\'00\'B0With the future of IVF access at stake, we need to pass my bill to protect fertility care for every American who needs it to start or grow their family.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tammy Duckworth (@SenDuckworth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenDuckworth/status/1760488565337944513?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And her colleague from Virginia, Tim Kaine :\par \par \uc2 enltrAlabama Republicans want to ban IVF.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma Republicans want to ban the morning after pill and certain IUDs.\par \par \uc2 Republicans were never going to stop at banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This was always about controlling women's reproductive health care choices\u8212\'20\'14we can't let them succeed.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tim Kaine (@timkaine) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/timkaine/status/1760382668812775814?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Democrats have campaigned on restoring nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access ever since Roe v Wade was overturned two years ago, and voters appear receptive. The party has performed well in special elections and in state legislative races, and limited its losses in Congress in the 2022 midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The aftershocks from the Alabama supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that IVF embryos are children continue to reverberate across the state, the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 A second Alabama provider announced that it will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/university-alabama-ivf-embryo-care-paused-supreme-court-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pause its in-vitro fertilization (IVF) treatments}}}\uc2  on Thursday, just days after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state supreme court ruled}}}\uc2  in a first-of-its-kind decision that embryos are \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have made the impossibly difficult decision to hold new IVF treatments due to the legal risk to our clinic and our embryologists,\u8221\'20\'1D Alabama Fertility said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/C3pzimqrixc/?next=%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post to its Instagram account}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe are contacting patients that will be affected today to find solutions for them and we are working as hard as we can to alert our legislators as to the far reaching negative impact of this ruling on the women of Alabama.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The clinic said it does not plan to close entirely, and urged people to check back in for \u8220\'20\'1Cadvocacy opportunities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Alabama Fertility is at least the second IVF provider to announce that it would suspend its IVF procedures after the \uc2 University of Alabama at Birmingham\uc2  Wednesday said it would pause treatments in the wake of the court ruling. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/university-alabama-ivf-embryo-care-paused-supreme-court-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spokesperson}}}\uc2  for the university, the largest healthcare provider in the state, said the institution is \u8220\'20\'1Csaddened that this will impact our patients\u8217\'20\'19 attempt to have a baby through IVF, but we must evaluate the potential that our patients and our physicians could be prosecuted criminally or face punitive damages for following the standard of care for IVF treatments\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/22/alabama-fertility-pause-ivf-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Second Alabama provider stops IVF care after court deems embryos \u8216\'20\'18children\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign blames Trump for Alabama court ruling curbing IVF access\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign is attempting to link last week\u8217\'20\'19s Alabama supreme court ruling curbing IVF care in the state to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , saying that the decision only came about after the downfall of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Trump appointed three of the conservative \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices who overturned the 49-year-old precedent in 2022, allowing states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely. In a statement, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager Julie Chavez Rodriguez said the recent ruling by Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s top court, which has allowed wrongful death suits to proceed against IVF care providers in cases where embryos have been destroyed, was a side-effect of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s end:\par \par \uc2 What is happening in Alabama right now is only possible because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Supreme Court justices overturned Roe v. Wade. Across the nation, MAGA Republicans are inserting themselves into the most personal decisions a family can make, from contraception to IVF. With their latest attack on reproductive freedom, these so-called pro-life Republicans are preventing loving couples from growing their families. If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is elected, there is no question that he will impose his extreme anti-freedom agenda on the entire country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Conservatives in Congress have long clamored for tighter border restrictions to keep migrants from entering the United States from Mexico, with some going as far as to threaten to shut down the government over the issue.\par \par \uc2 Rightwing congressman Byron Donalds reiterated the threat today at the Conservative Political Action Conference, ahead of a 1 March deadline for lawmakers to agree on new government funding measures, or face a partial shutdown of federal operations:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Byron Donalds (R-FL): \u8220\'20\'1CMy position to my colleagues on Capitol Hill is...you either secure the border or you get no money for the government. Now the press would say, \u8216\'20\'18Oh my gosh, Rep. Donalds, you\u8217\'20\'19re talking about the government being closed\u8230\'20\'26\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 CPAC crowd: \u8220\'20\'1CShut it down!\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nrlGQdlPKO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nrlGQdlPKO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1760695148147618190?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More progressive lawmakers are criticizing Biden\u8217\'20\'19s potential use of presidential authority to limit asylum seekers at the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 Abdullah H Hammoud, the mayor of Dearborn, Michigan, said that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s potential actions mimic Trump\u8217\'20\'19s infamous \u8220\'20\'1CMuslim ban\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 From Hammoud via X:\par \par \uc2 enltrFYI that \u8220\'20\'1Csweeping presidential authority\u8221\'20\'1D was called the \u8220\'20\'1CMuslim Ban\u8221\'20\'1D under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MI1l4mFYD5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/MI1l4mFYD5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Abdullah H. Hammoud (@AHammoudMI) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AHammoudMI/status/1760673752898236533?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 If Biden attempts to implement executive action policy to limit asylum, his administration would probably face legal challenges, CBS News reported.\par \par \uc2 Lee Gelernt\uc2 , a lawyer with \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 , told \uc2 CBS\uc2  that Biden could face lawsuits similar to Trump, when the former president attempted to issue an asylum ban.\par \par \uc2 Gelernt previously helped halt Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ban in federal court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn executive order denying asylum based on where one enters the country would just be another attempt at the exact policy Trump unsuccessfully tried and will undoubtedly end up in litigation,\u8221\'20\'1D Gelernt said to \uc2 CBS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Recent polling shows that more Americans are concerned about issues at the border, but a majority still view immigration as central to what makes the country unique.\par \par \uc2 The latest polling comes as Biden weighs unilateral action limiting the ability to seek asylum at the border.\par \par \uc2 From PBS News:\par \par \uc2 For a majority of Americans, the United States\u8217\'20\'19 openness to people from all over the world remains essential to the fabric of the nation. Yet, just as Congress wages a battle over the border and the future of immigration, support for that bigger idea has been eroding, according to the latest PBS {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maristpoll.marist.edu/polls/the-road-to-the-general-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NewsHour/NPR/Marist poll}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Welcoming others makes the country what it is, 57 percent of U.S. adults said in this poll, including 84 percent of Democrats and 55 percent of independents. That\u8217\'20\'19s a significant downward shift in attitudes since July 2021, when 66 percent of U.S. adults supported openness to others.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, 42 percent of Americans overall \u8211\'20\'13 including 72 percent of Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 said they felt that if the U.S. is too open, it runs the risk of losing its identity.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/where-voters-stand-on-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2 , chair of the Congressional Progressive Caucus, said that Biden would be making a \u8220\'20\'1Cmistake\u8221\'20\'1D if he took executive action to stop migrants from seeking asylum at the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis would be an extremely disappointing mistake,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RepJayapal/status/1760435318744920392?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jayapal said}}}\uc2  on X of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s potential unilateral action.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCruel enforcement-only policies have been tried for 30 years and simply do not work,\u8221\'20\'1D Jayapal added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats cannot continue to take pages out of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s playbook \u8211\'20\'13 we need to lead with dignity and humanity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden is facing mounting backlash from progressives over reports that he will attempt to curtail migration by using Trump-era federal law.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ocasio-Cortez calls Biden weighing action to restrict migrants from asylum 'outrageous'\par \par \uc2 Top progressive lawmaker \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  criticized Biden for reportedly considering executive action that would restrict migrants from seeking asylum in the US.\par \par \uc2 The New York representative called out Biden for potentially using federal laws previously implemented by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to crack down on migration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDoing Trump impressions isn\u8217\'20\'19t how we beat Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AOC/status/1760487315590242324?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a post to X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSeeking asylum is a legal right of all people. In the face of authoritarian threat, we should not buckle on our principles \u8211\'20\'13 we should commit to them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe mere suggestion is outrageous and the President should refuse to sign it,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House considers bypassing Congress to crackdown on migration at US-Mexico border \u8211\'20\'13 reports\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his White House team are considering using various aspects of federal immigration law \u8211\'20\'13 that were repeatedly utilized by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  during his hardline, anti-immigrant presidency \u8211\'20\'13 to unilaterally initiate a sweeping crackdown on migrants crossing into the US across the Mexico border uninvited, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 The administration, stymied by Republican lawmakers who rejected a negotiated border bill earlier this month, has been exploring options that the US president could deploy on his own without congressional approval, multiple officials and others familiar with the talks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/white-house-immigration-law-us-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the Associated Press last night.\par \par \uc2 But the public is warned that plans are not finalized and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how the administration would draft any such executive actions in a way that would survive the inevitable legal challenges.\par \par \uc2 Biden has hardened his rhetoric and policy intentions over the course of his presidency so far and the issue of irregular migration at the southern border \u8211\'20\'13 chiefly migrants crossing the border between official ports of entry into the US, because they can\u8217\'20\'19t get an appointment or gain permission to enter for an asylum interview, and turning themselves in to border patrol, hoping then to be able to file an asylum claim.\par \par \uc2 The notion of a crackdown on asylum seekers by Biden goes against international human rights laws and a tradition of being able to request shelter after reaching US soil and will enrage progressives and immigration advocates, probably provoking legal challenges and political uproar. But voters have consistently told pollsters they disapprove of the White House\u8217\'20\'19s handling of border security.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden reportedly weighing unilateral crackdown on migration at US-Mexico border\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s a very busy week considering that Congress isn\u8217\'20\'19t even in full session, but there\u8217\'20\'19s news out of the White House and on the campaign trail and we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring it to you as it happens.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s afoot:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is strongly considering taking executive action to crack down on undocumented migrants crossing the US-Mexico border to request shelter in the United States, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 With Congress stalled on legislative action to reform immigration laws and toughen asylum rules at the southern border, the White House is now reportedly weighing unilateral action.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US president is considering using provisions of federal immigration law repeatedly tapped by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during his hardline presidency, but Biden would be likely to run into immediate legal challenges from immigrant rights groups and outrage on the left of his party.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Irregular immigration is a huge election year topic and opinion polls show that a strong majority of American voters disapprove of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s handling of migration issues at the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Reverberations are widening from the Alabama court decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/alabama-ivf-embryo-extrauterine-children-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to declare that}}}\uc2  frozen embryos used in IVF are human babies and to destroy them would be a crime. Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  has weighed in behind the ruling but it\u8217\'20\'19s thrown the healthcare sector and would-be parents into a conundrum.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazy SOB\u8221\'20\'1D (son of a bitch) during a fundraiser in San Francisco, warning there is always the threat of nuclear conflict but that the existential threat to humanity remains the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate crisis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240222ek2m00234\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
