\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump privately backs 16-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban with exceptions, report says\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 576 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 February 2024\par 20:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ex-president favors ban with exceptions for rape, incest and to save mother\u8217\'20\'19s life, NYT says, but won\u8217\'20\'19t discuss until after primary\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump likes the idea of a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 16 weeks of pregnancy with exceptions for rape, incest and to save the life of the mother, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/02/16/us/politics/trump-abortion-ban.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reported on Friday morning}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump has veered away from taking a firm stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  during his presidential campaign. He has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/donald-trump-abortion-election-republicans-iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taken credit}}}\uc2  for the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2022 overturning of Roe v Wade, since he appointed three of the justices who took part in that decision, but he has also suggested that Republicans who take extreme stances on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lose elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKnow what I like about 16?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told one individual, according to the Times, which based its report on two people with knowledge of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s thoughts. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s even. It\u8217\'20\'19s four months.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump is waiting until after the conclusion of the Republican primary to publicly discuss his position, the Times reported.\par \par \uc2 Since Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise, voters have repeatedly rejected attempts to curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and supported state-level ballot measures to protect the right to the procedure. Outrage over Roe is also widely credited with defeating the promised \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D in the 2022 midterms and leaving Republicans with fewer victories than anticipated.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Virginia Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/01/republicans-abortion-ads-virginia-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaigned in a state election}}}\uc2  on a pledge to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 15 weeks, as a kind of \u8220\'20\'1Ccompromise\u8221\'20\'1D position. Their efforts to retake control of the state legislature failed.\par \par \uc2 However, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, with its coterie of high-powered activists, has made it clear that they would like to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/22/roe-v-wade-abortion-anniversary-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see the procedure totally outlawed}}}\uc2 . Although most Americans consider themselves \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D, polling shows they are far less supportive of abortions past the first trimester.\par \par \uc2 After publication of the Times article, the Trump campaign sent out a statement dismissing it as \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs President Trump has stated, he would sit down with both sides and negotiate a deal that everyone will be happy with,\u8221\'20\'1D said Karoline Leavitt, the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s national press secretary. Leavitt then celebrated Trump\u8217\'20\'19s role in overturning Roe and falsely accused Democrats, among other things, of supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cafter birth\u8221\'20\'1D, which is infanticide and already illegal in the United States.\par \par \uc2 The vast majority of abortions take place in the first trimester of pregnancy. However, someone may have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  later on in pregnancy due to a medical emergency.\par \par \uc2 More than a dozen states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enacted near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2 , several of which do not have exceptions for rape or incest. And doctors have repeatedly said that carve-outs for abortions in cases of medical emergencies have proven so vague as to be unworkable; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/28/texas-supreme-court-hears-extreme-abortion-ban-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dozens of women}}}\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/feb/01/abortion-ban-tennessee-texas-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now come forward}}}\uc2  to say that they were denied medically necessary abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, after being the one responsible for taking away women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom, after being the one to put women\u8217\'20\'19s lives in danger, after being the one who has unleashed all this cruelty and chaos all across America, Trump is running scared,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said in a statement on Friday afternoon. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s afraid that the women of America are going to hold him responsible for taking away their rights and endangering their rights at the ballot box in November. That\u8217\'20\'19s exactly what\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240216ek2g002uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
