\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Tennessee advances bill to ban people from helping minors obtain  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 824 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 February 2024\par 12:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Proposed bill that could see prison sentences of up to 15 years for breaching rules moves forward in state legislature\par \par \uc2 Tennessee state legislators moved on Tuesday to advance a bill that would ban people from helping minors procure an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without parental permission \u8211\'20\'13 an act that the bill has dubbed \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If someone illegally \u8220\'20\'1Crecruits, harbors, or transports a pregnant unemancipated minor\u8221\'20\'1D for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they could face three to 15 years in prison under the proposed law, which has now advanced out of a statehouse subcommittee after a hearing.\par \par \uc2 Although Tennessee already bans almost all abortions, as do more than a dozen states across much of the southern and midwestern United States, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents remain frustrated that people have continued to procure abortions since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in 2022. Some individuals have fled across state lines for the procedure, while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates continue to give out \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in a grey market so that people may \u8220\'20\'1Cself-manage\u8221\'20\'1D abortions at home.\par \par \uc2 Medical experts widely agree that, early on in pregnancy, it is safe to use pills to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on one\u8217\'20\'19s own.\par \par \uc2 In the Tuesday hearing, the bill\u8217\'20\'19s sponsor, Republican state representative Jason Zachary, said he saw the bill as an important shield for \u8220\'20\'1Cparental rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the state of Tennessee, you cannot take a child to an emergency room or any medical facility to obtain treatment without their parents\u8217\'20\'19 permission if they\u8217\'20\'19re under 18,\u8221\'20\'1D Zachary said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo this legislation simply says that if you are an adult, you are not allowed to take a minor who is not your child for any procedure related to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without parental consent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At another point in the hearing, Zachary clarified his position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m never good with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Period. End of story.\u8221\'20\'1D He later added: \u8220\'20\'1CMy intent was to protect every life \u8211\'20\'13 every life and every unborn child.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bill would allow individuals to sue for \u8220\'20\'1Cwrongful death\u8221\'20\'1D after an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 language that suggests that a fetus is legally considered a person. Establishing the legal personhood of fetuses is a longtime goal of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement and could have sweeping implications for vast swathes of US law, as it could leave pregnant women pitted against the rights of the fetuses they carry.\par \par \uc2 Rapists would not be allowed to sue for wrongful death under the proposed legislation. However, during the Tuesday hearing, which lasted nearly an hour, state lawmakers tussled over other complications posed by rape.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat is the situation if the sole parent or guardian is the rapist of the young lady who\u8217\'20\'19s carrying the child?\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic state representative John Ray Clemmons asked Zachary.\par \par \uc2 The minor could go to court and get a court order that would erase the guardianship rights, Zachary said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThen if a child or an unemancipated minor, in this statute, wanted to seek health care, and their only sole parent or guardian was their rapist, that child would have to go to court to petition a court to get help?\u8221\'20\'1D Clemmons asked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D has become something of an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bogeyman since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe. Last year, Idaho enacted a bill that also barred people from taking minors across state lines for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without their parents\u8217\'20\'19 permission, an act legislators in the state also labeled as \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D. A judge subsequently put that law on hold.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny woman who\u8217\'20\'19s ever had to decide whether or not to terminate a pregnancy, I would say, has been in a conversation with herself about the sanctity of life,\u8221\'20\'1D Kacey Cardin, a Tennessee woman who has worked as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doula and is now considering having children in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt bothers me when I hear as lawmakers talk about: \u8216\'20\'18All life is sacred!\u8217\'20\'19 But there\u8217\'20\'19s very little care given to how sacred a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life is and how sacred the decision about a woman\u8217\'20\'19s future is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cardin, who is now in her 40s, was raped, became pregnant, and got an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when she was just 16, she said to the Guardian ahead of the Tuesday hearing. She considers herself privileged because her parents were supportive and able to help her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo think about the amount of girls who already can\u8217\'20\'19t afford the procedure \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s such a stretch for so many people \u8211\'20\'13 and then to have to take time off to have to find a safe person they trust, someone who would keep their confidence,\u8221\'20\'1D Cardin said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think about the amount of cases where young girls are raped by a family member \u8211\'20\'13 how do you find support to help take care of this when the people who are supposed to be taking care of you are the ones hurting you? That is so much more common than I think people realize.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240214ek2d00003\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
