\par\par \uc2 Life and style\par \b \uc2 Rate of US babies born prematurely has grown 12%, analysis says\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza in New York \par \uc2 733 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 February 2024\par 09:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Report adds to evidence of a maternal and infant health crisis, which experts expect will be exacerbated by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans\par \par \uc2 The rate of babies born prematurely in the US grew 12% from 2014 to 2022 to nearly 8.7%, with pronounced racial and age disparities among the mothers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/data/nvsr/nvsr73/nvsr73-01.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new analysis}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 National Center for Health Statistics (NCHS)\uc2  found.\par \par \uc2 Black mothers were almost twice as likely as white mothers to give birth before babies reached full term, 12.5% versus 7.6% respectively. Similarly, women older than 40 had a greater risk of preterm birth compared with women aged 20-29, 12.5% versus 8.23%.\par \par \uc2 The report adds to the evidence of a maternal and infant health crisis in the US, one experts expect will be exacerbated by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans across the US south}}}\uc2  and in some western states. The US has one of the worst maternal mortality rates among developed democracies, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonwealthfund.org/blog/2022/us-maternal-mortality-crisis-continues-worsen-international-comparison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Commonwealth Fund}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s important here is, with all of the research we\u8217\'20\'19ve done to try to decrease preterm birth, we still have not found the solution,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cynthia Gyamfi-Bannerman, a maternal-fetal medicine specialist and president-elect of the \uc2 Society for Maternal-Fetal Medicine\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s because we actually don\u8217\'20\'19t know what instigates preterm birth in many cases.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The new \uc2 NCHS\uc2  report is significant for a few reasons. First, it reinforces data showing the stubbornly high rate of preterm birth in the US. It also highlights the potential risks of starting families later in life \u8211\'20\'13 in the past decade, there has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/social-trends/2018/01/18/theyre-waiting-longer-but-u-s-women-today-more-likely-to-have-children-than-a-decade-ago/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a shift toward}}}\uc2  women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/motherhood-deferred-us-median-age-giving-birth-hits-30-rcna27827"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 giving birth in their early 40s}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lastly, it highlights glaring and ongoing racial disparities between Black women and their white and Hispanic counterparts. Researchers have hypothesized that these disparities may be attributable to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2741514/#:~:text=These%20results%20support%20the%20%E2%80%9Cweathering,that%20increases%20preterm%20delivery%20risk."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weathering}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, or premature ageing attributable to the stress of racism and deprivation. Gyamfi-Bannerman said that although weathering may be part of the problem, preterm birth is probably \u8220\'20\'1Cmulti-factorial\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Preterm birth, or birth anytime before 37 weeks, is the leading cause of death and of health conditions, or \u8220\'20\'1Cmorbidities\u8221\'20\'1D, for infants and children. In general, the earlier a baby is born, the greater the risk of death, serious health complications and disabilities. Similarly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/clinical/clinical-guidance/committee-opinion/articles/2019/02/avoidance-of-nonmedically-indicated-early-term-deliveries-and-associated-neonatal-morbidities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 studies have found}}}\uc2  that even babies born \u8220\'20\'1Cearly term\u8221\'20\'1D, particularly at 37 weeks, suffer increased health risks.\par \par \uc2 Researchers at the \uc2 NCHS\uc2  examined birth records from 2014, the most recent low point in premature births, to 2022, accounting for all births. The analysis was restricted to births involving one baby, or \u8220\'20\'1Csingletons\u8221\'20\'1D, as multiples tend to be born earlier.\par \par \uc2 Researchers found that rates of preterm birth increased about 2% each year with some fluctuation during the Covid-19 pandemic, indicating that the social and economic stressors that are believed to drive many preterm births could be worsening.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know there\u8217\'20\'19s a link between stress and preterm birth, and that\u8217\'20\'19s something that\u8217\'20\'19s been studied in the literature but very challenging to mitigate,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gyamfi-Bannerman. \u8220\'20\'1CWe see it time and time again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Importantly, another highly publicized preterm birth statistic from the March of Dimes put the preterm birth rate at 10.4%. That statistic, while also based on \uc2 NCHS\uc2  data, includes births of multiples, which have a higher overall rate of preterm birth. In November, the infant advocacy organization {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/11/16/health/preterm-birth-march-of-dimes/index.html#:~:text=Despite%20slight%20downtick%2C%20the%20preterm,up%20from%209.8%25%20in%202012."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave the US a grade of D+}}}\uc2  for its high rate of preterm births.\par \par \uc2 The report covers the very beginning of the post-Dobbs era. The supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , which guaranteed a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in July 2022. More than a dozen states, especially in the south, rapidly outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . By June 2023, a survey of obstetricians and gynecologists reported the effect of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrictions and bans}}}\uc2  as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/06/21/obgyn-abortion-poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelmingly negative}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Experts believe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2023/03/15/1163365018/premature-birth-abortion-bans-pregnancy#:~:text=The%20U.S.%20has%20a%20high,bans%20could%20make%20that%20worse&text=Limited%2FGetty%20Images-,Physicians%20say%20roughly%20half%20of%20all%20preterm%20births%20are%20preventable,access%20to%20prenatal%20health%20care."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans could worsen preterm birth}}}\uc2  trends, particularly in southern and some western states, by pushing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/08/abortion-roe-v-wade-maternal-care-deserts-louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doctors who care for pregnant women and new mothers}}}\uc2  to leave for places where their livelihoods and liberties are not threatened by criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 2 February 2024. An earlier version incorrectly described how a statistic in a March of Dimes report on preterm births was calculated. It was based on all births, including singletons and multiples, rather than only singletons.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240131ek1v001jr\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 atleast5(abortion) OR atleast3("reproductive justice")\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/30/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Source\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 The Guardian (U.K.)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 